{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.337386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00e4d994c89b545307b1ad2681dc65c7c21e32a770f0d024237688e4fec56f26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Dynamic programming) of arXiv:2506.15037, '2BSDE with uncertain horizon and application to stochastic control in erratic environments'] Assume that $\xi$ is an $\mathcal G_{T\wedge \tau}-$measurable random variable such that $\|\xi\|_{L_{0,\hat\chi}^{2}}<\infty$. Then, any solution $(Y,Z,U,M,K)\in  \mathbb S^2_{0, \hat{\chi}}(\mathbb G^{\mathcal P_0+})\times \mathbb H^2_{0, \hat{\chi}}(\mathbb G^{\mathcal P_0+})\times \mathbb J^{2}_{0, \hat{\chi}}(\mathbb G^{\mathcal P_0+}) \times \mathbb I^2_{0, \hat{\chi}}((\mathbb G^{\mathbb P +})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0})\times \mathbb M_{0, \hat{\chi}}((\mathbb G^{\mathbb P +})_{\p\in \mathcal P_0})$ to the 2BSDE \eqref{2bsde:eq}
