{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.190634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00f99323eb5255f3fd6c791b4f4ebac7efe36bfdfb8420b8aeb26c78b602cb78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 44 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$ and $d\neq 6$, there exist $\Cl,\Cl, \Cl,\cl>0$ such that for any $v\neq v'\in \widetilde{B}(\Cref{const_additional_lemma_four_point1})$, any sufficiently large $N\ge 1$, and $w,w'\in \widetilde{B}(10N)\setminus \widetilde{B}(N)$ with $|w-w'|\ge N$, 
