{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.295755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00fe8d2aab5e092b1bc2942af065c4790c43eae623c78e9d4169281fdd7d9a64","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def eq2 of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] We call  a stochastic process
\begin{align*}
\tilde y\in L_{{\mathbb{F}}}^2(\Omega;C([0,T];L^2_{\rm loc}(G)))\cap L_{{\mathbb{F}}}^2(0,T;H^1_{\rm loc}(G))
\end{align*}
a solution to the equation (system-sp1 of the paper) if for any
$t\in[0,T]$, $\widehat G\subset\!\subset G$ and $\rho\in H_0^1(\widehat G)$, it holds that
\begin{align} \notag
& \int_{\widehat G}\tilde y(t,x)\rho(x)dx-\int_{\widehat G}\tilde y(0,x)\rho(x)dx
\\ \notag
& = \int_0^t\int_{\widehat G} \!\Big[\!-\!\sum_{j,k=1}^n b^{jk}
\tilde y_{x_j}(s,x)\rho_{x_k}(x) \!+\!\tilde a_1\cdot \nabla \tilde y(s,x)\rho(x)
\!+\! \tilde a_2     \tilde y(s,x)\rho(x)     \Big]dx ds
\\
& \quad +\int_0^t\int_{\widehat G} \tilde a_3 \tilde y(s,x)\rho (x) dx dW(s), \quad ~ \text{${\mathbb{P}}$-a.s.}
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.595157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_010439b9de38f4e96f14daea5e252c9ba1e54bfcf82dfdde5bdf5d4fb845cabb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 (Predictive stability for GPs) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Let $P$ and $Q$ be Gaussian process laws on $L^2(\bP_X)$. Then there exists an absolute constant $L_{\cM}>0$ such that
