{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.952669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_012fa4691b80edde119fc5b3f4e0d44e3ba99baca89717fdcf8347234b0f4705","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:mgf-comparison of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[corollary]{cor:mgf}
Let $G$ be any $m\times m$ correlation matrix, let
$\xi\sim\mathcal N(0,G)$, and let
$\xi^\triangle\sim\mathcal N(0,G_\triangle)$.  Then
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i\right\}
  \leq
  \mathbb E\exp\!\left\{\lambda\max_i\xi_i^\triangle\right\}
  \qquad(\lambda>0).
\end{equation}
If $G\neq G_\triangle$, then (equation eq:mgf-comparison of the paper) is strict for every
$\lambda>0$.  Equivalently, equality for any one $\lambda>0$ holds if and
