{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.654528+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01988d6dc71cc5355d2c3fc970c80d3873b07d3be49a3dd80adafbcdcb71fb03","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2609.03713, 'A Sharp Mass Threshold for Boundedness in a Critical Quasilinear Chemotaxis Model with Ind'] Introducing
\begin{equation}
    \mu_{M,\bar{M}} := \inf_{(u,w)\in \mathcal{I}_{M,\bar{M},rad}(\mathbb{B}_R)} \mathcal{L}(u,w) \in [-\infty,\infty)\,, \quad \bar{M}\ge M>0\,, 
\end{equation}
with $\mathcal{I}_{M,\bar{M},rad}(\mathbb{B}_R)$ defined in~\eqref{IS}, there holds:
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
    \mu_{M,\bar{M}} & = -\infty \;\;\text{ for }\;\; \bar{M}\ge M>M_c\,,\\ 
    \mu_{M,\bar{M}} & > -\infty \;\;\text{ for }\;\; M\in (0,M_c] \;\text{ and }\;\bar{M}\ge M\,.
\end{split}
\end{equation}
More precisely, in the second case, there is $c_0=c_0(d,R)>0$ such that, for all $(u,w)\in \mathcal{I}_{M,\bar{M},rad}(\mathbb{B}_R)$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
    \mathcal{L}(u,w) \ge \frac{1}{2} \left( 1 - \left( \frac{M}{M_c} \right)^{2/d} \right) \|\nabla\mathcal{K}[w-\langle w\rangle]\|_2^2 - c_0 \frac{M\bar{M}}{|\mathbb{B}_R|} - \frac{mM}{m-1}\,. 
\end{split}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.425795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01a01e2ee1645520d1550b334c4f906e213b3c124ca667f95791694c84656258","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 169 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under the conditions of Proposition~\ref{Proposition_hex_hole_offcrit}, $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}$ has exactly two bands and $q^-(z)$ factorizes as:
