{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.482796+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01a748cbcda6698298ed546d46da1f0f3b24646969b644057ff27b3e7c2587b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 35 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Consider $\ind_{\Ns_{\varepsilon}(A)}$ the Lebesgue measure on 
$\Ns_{\varepsilon}(A)$ (indicator function).
It satisfies the following asymptotic expansion:
for every $N\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}

\ind_{\Ns_{\varepsilon}(A)}
=
\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}
\sum_{k=0}^{N} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{\psi_{2k+1,A}}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}
~+~R_{N,\varepsilon},
\end{equation}
where the error term $R_{N,\varepsilon}$ satisfies, as $\varepsilon \to 0$,
\begin{displaymath}
\forall \eta >0,~
\E\big[\Vert R_{N,\varepsilon} \Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\big]^{1/2}
=\, o (\vert\log \varepsilon\vert^{-(N+1/2)}).
\end{displaymath}
As for the Lebesgue measure on $\widetilde{\Ns}_{\varepsilon}(A)$,
fix a deterministic smooth cutoff function $f_{0}:D\rightarrow [0,1]$, compactly supported in $D$.
Then  $\ind_{\widetilde{\Ns}_{\varepsilon}(A)}f_{0}$ satisfies the following asymptotic expansion:
for every $N\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}

\ind_{\widetilde{\Ns}_{\varepsilon}(A)}f_{0}
=
\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}
\sum_{k=0}^{N} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{f_{0}\,\tilde{\psi}_{2k+1,A}}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}
\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}
~+~\widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon, f_{0}},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

\tilde{\psi}_{2k+1,A} = 
\sum_{j=0}^{k} \dfrac{(2k+1)!}{2^{j} j! (2(k-j)+1)!}
\,\Big(\dfrac{1}{2\pi} \log \CR(z,D)\Big)^{j}\,\psi_{2(k-j)+1,A},
\end{equation}
and the error term $\widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon, f_{0}}$ satisfies, as $\varepsilon \to 0$,
\begin{displaymath}
\forall \eta >0,~
\E\big[\Vert \widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon, f_{0}} \Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\big]^{1/2}
=\, o (\vert\log \varepsilon\vert^{-(N+1/2)}).
\end{displaymath}
Further assume that
\begin{eqnarray}

\forall \beta >0,~
\operatorname{Leb}(\{ z\in D \vert \,d(z,\partial D)<\varepsilon\}) 
= o(\vert \log\varepsilon\vert^{-\beta})
\text{ as } \varepsilon\to 0.
\end{eqnarray}
Then for every $N\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}

\ind_{\widetilde{\Ns}_{\varepsilon}(A)}
=
\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}
\sum_{k=0}^{N} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{\tilde{\psi}_{2k+1,A}}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}
\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}
~+~\widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon},
\end{equation}
where the error term $\widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon}$ satisfies, as $\varepsilon \to 0$,
\begin{displaymath}
\forall \eta >0,~
\E\big[\Vert \widetilde{R}_{N,\varepsilon} \Vert_{H^{-\eta}(\C)}^{2}\big]^{1/2}
=\, o (\vert\log \varepsilon\vert^{-(N+1/2)}).
\end{displaymath} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:36:16.062580+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01a7f36c81945e5fafa7f20b0bec5cacc83c1cd2c60bc3c3536965fa7b53da92","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_Gronwall_bounded of arXiv:2606.28067, 'Ergodic approximation for the invariant distribution: An abstract framework for law-depend'] Let $(\gamma_k)_{k\ge 1}$ be a nonincreasing
