{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.707087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_023c1e4ef172d6838941a6154f6036ed30afc7210f214abaffac19c4230e6910","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:main of arXiv:2510.24424, 'On the Fourier Coefficients of Critical Gaussian Multiplicative Chaos'] Let $\mathcal{F}_{n,t}$ be defined as in Equation (equation eq:def_Ft of the paper). Then there exists a constant $C(A)=C>0$ such that for large enough $t,n>0$,  $\mathcal{F}_{n,t}(\Delta)$ satisfies the bound
