{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0246d9e7f9f8f557fb1b9f728a1f8eb542a4bb21ed99520c2ab6ac494ea36fe1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 50 (Tree-graph inequality) of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$ and $\beta\geq 0$. Then, for every $x,y,z \in V$, 
