{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.239036+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02fdba23a0d5d4711febab5027d446025e330b26600bf0d9a20febb19966caf3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:upper_bound_on_width of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] Suppose that we have the same setup described above.  Then,  there exists a universal constant $c>0$,  and a constant $\varepsilon_0 \in (0,1)$ depending only on $a,\delta,N$ and $\theta$ such that
