{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.432621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03858fee016cd2cbc8468affb75a1c2568915a89667f4360356fe85213de6f69","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:centered-lyapunov-moment-equivalence of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let \(p\geqslant2\). Under the parameter conditions of (assump:admissibility of the paper), the strict positivity of the equivalence constants \(c_1^{(2)}>0\) and \(c_1(a_p,p)>0\) is guaranteed. Define the constant \(K_{p,\gamma} := \max\{1+2^{p-1}\gamma^{-p}, \, 2^{p-1}\}\), and set
\begin{equation}
    C_{p,1} := \frac{1}{K_{p,\gamma}} \begin{cases} c_1^{(2)}, & p=2,\\ c_1(a_p,p), & p>2 \end{cases}, \qquad
    C_{p,2} := K_{p,\gamma} \begin{cases} c_2^{(2)}, & p=2,\\ c_2(a_p,p), & p>2 \end{cases}.
\end{equation}
Then the pathwise functional satisfies
\begin{equation}
    C_{p,1} \left( \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal X^J_{t}}} + \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal V^J_{t}}} \right)
    \leqslant L_p(t) \leqslant
    C_{p,2} \left( \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal X^J_{t}}} + \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal V^J_{t}}} \right).
\end{equation}
Consequently, taking expectations yields
\begin{equation}
    C_{p,1} \mathbf{E}\left[ \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal X^J_{t}}} + \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal V^J_{t}}} \right]
    \leqslant \mathcal L_p(t) \leqslant
    C_{p,2} \mathbf{E}\left[ \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal X^J_{t}}} + \momentp{p}{\mu_{\mathcal V^J_{t}}} \right].
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.005426+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0391b79fc015cbb5fcb7e168722e27cf26698ec1e8d2894b4a1423b68b142d71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop instP gau LB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exists a deterministic constant $c \in (0, \infty)$ such that,
