{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.917045+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_03c34e5753a66b1b11b687a7aae115c74d9bba1700a95f68351d55bc4b481d86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Integral one-sided color expansion) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every fixed $n\ge2$ and every zero-framed knot $K$, there are Laurent
polynomials
\begin{equation}
 b_k^{(n)}(K;q)=\varepsilon_n a_{(k)}(K;q^2)
