{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:47:53.344145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0421949bebafcf679e4049d7f75dd42c9278f2b967007b9637eedc8bafda9f06","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 27 (Du, 2025) of arXiv:2607.14948, 'Graph alignment in sparse inhomogeneous models via self-overlap'] Fix $\lambda_1, \lambda_2 > 0$, $\beta \in (0, 1)$. Let $G^\uparrow \sim \mc{G}(n, \frac{\lambda_1}{n^\beta})$ and $s \sim \lambda_2n^{-\left(\frac{1-\beta}{2}\right)}$, and consider a correlated inhomogeneous graph system $(G, H)$ obtained by subsampling $G^\uparrow$ with parameter $s$. In particular,

    \begin{equation}
        I \sim \mc{G}(n, \frac{\lambda_1 \lambda_2^2}{n}); \qquad U \sim \mc{G}(n, \frac{\lambda_1 \lambda_2 (2-o(1))}{n^{\frac{1+\beta}{2}}})
    \end{equation}

    Then, for any $\eps > 0$: 

    \begin{itemize}
        \item there exists an estimator recovering $\sigma^*$ on at least $|V_{\geq (\beta^{-1} + \eps)}|(1 - o_\Proba(1))$ vertices;
        \item any estimator must be wrong on at least $|V_{\leq (\beta^{-1} - \eps)}|(1 - o_\Proba(1))$ vertices.
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.584755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_042abe27dbcf2bf24323d72566e745149ed04d2e3c00665c76540615ee632b18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:random1 of arXiv:2411.09716, 'Stable Tables'] The probability $f^*(n)$ that a given person is unmatched in a table with $n$ people under random matching is
