\item[\rm(C)] There exist $U\in\mathcal U_\kappa^2$ and constants $c_0,C_0>0$ such that, for every $R\ge1$, the following holds. The dilated potential $U_R(x)=R^2U(x/R)$ also belongs to $\mathcal U_\kappa^2$, the kernel $Q_{h,\gamma}^{U_R}$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$, and there is an initial state $z_R\in\mathbb R^4$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
