{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.626773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05128aedcd6d478b9b02ef723a3bf2da65f21efdd5a15bbed7bab66bdb43e98b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:VolumeGrowthEstimate of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $A_0 \subset A_1 \subset A_2 = \mathbb R^s$ be affine subspaces of dimension $d_0 < d_1$ and $d_2 = s$ equipped with the Euclidean distance. Let $X_i \subset A_i$ be compact subsets with $\operatorname{diam}(X_0) \leq \delta_0$ and $\operatorname{dist}(X_{i-1}, X_i) \leq \delta_i$ for $i = 1, 2$. Then
