{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:16:46.133582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05262fcb09b50e14d06a6deb3168b0989b7a0f1659ee2605ad3ec3eafa847ad4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:matroid of arXiv:2605.01444, 'From second moments to pairwise negative correlation: \\applications to minimal and unifor'] A matroid ${\ensuremath{\mathscr M}} =(E,{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} )$ consists of a finite ground set $E$ and a collection ${\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} \subset 2^{E}$ of independent sets satisfying:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item[(1)] $\emptyset\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} $;

		\item[(2)] if $A\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} $ and $B\subset A$, then $B\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} $;

		\item[(3)] if $A,B\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} $ and $|A|<|B|$, then $\exists e\in B\setminus A$ such that $A\cup\{e\}\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}} $. 
	\end{enumerate}
The rank function $r:2^E\to{\ensuremath{\mathbb Z}} _{\;\geqslant\;0}$ associated ${\ensuremath{\mathscr M}} $ is given by 
\[
r(S)\coloneq \max\left\{ |A|  \,\,\big|\,\, A\subset S,A\in{\ensuremath{\mathcal I}}   \right\}\,.
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.422987+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_052a60963a80bc442fd7abb4906ae136b453bace4501b0e402520d890c9af1cf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:minimal-m of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:moment-thresholds}
For every \(p\ge3\), matching only the mean and variance suffices for the regularized bulk-pressure conclusion (equation eq:pressure-univ-weak of the paper).  The least matching order sufficient for the ratio conclusion is
\begin{equation}
 m_\star(p)=\left\lfloor\frac{2}{p-2}\right\rfloor+2
 =\begin{cases}
 4,&p=3,\\
 3,&p=4,\\
 2,&p\ge5.
