{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.645626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05af8e30347c73c331a415513030d2e199fd753208673f65d387f0e19b9b6741","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Balls around a rooted tree of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] For $T$ a rooted tree and $a>0$, define by $\mathcal{B}_{a}(T)$ the open ball of radius $a$ around $T$ in the local topology, i.e.,
