{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.629845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_062ac61936f4f5ed3cc5127e55764d9737ff6eea4d2a794c35c62e3d433565f6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lower_bound_alpha_stab of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\bm{X}$ be a L\'evy process that differs in law from the $\alpha$-stable process~$\bm{Z}$, $\alpha\in(0,2]$. Let $\psi_{\bm{X}}$ and $\psi_{\bm{Z}}$ denote their L\'evy--Khintchine exponents. Pick any $q\in(0,1]\cap(0,\alpha)$ and $\bm{u}_*\in \mathbb{R}^d\setminus\{\bm 0\}$ for which $C_*\coloneqq 2^{q-1}|\bm{u}_*|^{-q}|\psi_{\bm{X}_1}(\bm{u}_*)-\psi_{\bm{Z}_1}(\bm{u}_*)|> 0$. Then, we have
