where $\p V:= \{ x\in V : \exists x'\in V' \setminus V \text{ with } xx' \in E' \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.874985+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0677475d829ad8ff8d8d27b55fb40295201185f49ca5c4dd2e5ef2f1ab5d5714","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 (\textsf{Uniform truncation principle}) of arXiv:2609.02064, 'Coalescence and fluctuations of O'Connell--Yor polymers\\ via the free-energy correlation '] Let $K\subset\R$ be compact and $q>0$.  Then
