{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.066402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_069f5e748c107c4813a628d886c0281251503e5d15be59cc91a8cfa1bdd19cb9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Scaling limit for $X^{(N)}/N$) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] Assume that $X_0^{(N)}/N\to X_0$ in distribution as $N\to\infty$ for some random variable $X_0$. Then, as $N\to\infty$, the space-scaled process $(X_t^{(N)}/N)_{t\ge 0}$ converges in $D_{[0,1]}([0,\infty))$ to the process $X=(X_t)_{t\ge 0}$ having state space $[0,1]$, whose generator $L^X$ acts on test functions $f\in C^2([0,1])$ via
   \begin{equation} 
   L^Xf(x)
   \ =\ \Lambda(\{0\})(1-2x)f'(x)+\int_{(0,1]}
        \big(f(x(1-t))+f(x(1-t)+t)-2f(x)\big)
        \frac{\Lambda({\rm d}t)}{t},
   \end{equation}
   where $\Lambda$ is the finite measure on $[0,1]$ uniquely determined via (\ref{lambda_rep}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.222409+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06a2ee70d74e1881eadbee8cb18b894de4723a0c7f3639c710e93dc944e2c8a4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lowergeneral of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] Fix $\alpha\in(0,2),$ $\delta>1$, and let $N,n$ be integers such that $N\geq \delta n$. Let $(x_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq N,1\leq j\leq n}$ be i.i.d. random variables with a symmetric distribution and satisfy (equation stablelaw of the paper). Fix $0<A_1<A_2$ and let $(a_{ij})_{1\leq i\leq N,1\leq j\leq n}$ be fixed real numbers such that $$A_1\leq a_{ij}\leq A_2\quad \forall i=1,\cdots,N, j=1,\cdots,n.$$ 
    Let $A=(a_{ij}x_{ij})$ be an $N\times n$ random matrix
and let $B$ be any deterministic $N\times n$ matrix. We do not make any assumption on $B$.
Then for any $D>0$ we can find $C_3>0$ and $N_0\in\mathbb{N}_+$ such that,
whenever $N\geq N_0,$ 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}(\sigma_{min}(A+B)\leq C_3N^\frac{1}{\alpha}(\log N)^\frac{2(\alpha-2)}{\alpha})\leq N^{-D},
\end{equation}
 where $C_3$ and $N_0$ depend only on $D,\delta,\alpha,C_\ell,C_u,A_1,A_2$, and notably do not depend on $B$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.068337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06a5ab18074d24d50cbdfdc3b8733db0f3e0e0b6eba5c0e453755c28e3a5f69e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2606.27774, 'Variational Formulas for the Spectrum of\\ Block Wishart Matrices'] Fix integer $k \ge 1,$
let $\alpha \in (0,\infty)$, and $\nu\in\cuP_0(\sa{k}{\C})$. Define   
$\cU_-\equiv \cU_{-}(\alpha,\nu)\subseteq \sa{k}{\C} $ via
