{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.477324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e72eb7e0733d5b9c6cd9cef5d3fd9cf0b806ab6acf4ea97713a9c7949c866e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convexbifurcation of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] After some arbitrarily $C^\infty$-small perturbation of $\xi$, there exists finitely many times $0 < t_1 < \dots < t_N < 1$ such that 
    \begin{itemize}
