    Moreover, when a pair of characteristics is born (in forwards time), a $\flat$ annulus appears between them, and when a pair of characteristics dies, a $\sharp$ annulus disappears between them (see \zcref{fig:birthdeath}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.355068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e84e2f417e6966609a72c9e90e252a32309b45eb7cfb712f5acd51bb4a05f5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] There are \(n_0\geq 1\), \(c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\),
