{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.456391+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0815156be50c217d2ab90a2cbbfd16dd054fff28abc21d9677fe3ba9e15a5f0d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 16 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Assume Hypothesis \ref{hypnonlin}. Then, there exists some $\delta_1 \in (0, \;1]$ and some bounded function $g: \mathbb{N} \mapsto \mathbb{R}$, such that
