{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.728373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_081d531d4a80a48c0b7fff93bb6f86f78a23a1401a7bdabdbaf03b187b6efb97","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 21 of arXiv:2605.02002, 'Glauber dynamics for random field Ising models on bounded degree graphs and MLSI'] (Second-order correlation matrix) Let $\mu$ be a distribution on $\{0,1\}^V$ and $G=(V,E)$ be a graph. Then for $u,v\in V$, denote by $uv$ the event that 
$$
uv:=\{\sigma\in\{0,1\}^V\mid \sigma_u=\sigma_v=1\}.
$$ Then we define the second order correlation matrix $\operatorname{Cor}_\mu^{(2)}\in\mathbb{R}^{E\times E}$ via
$$
\forall (u,v),(w,z)\in E,\quad \operatorname{Cor}_\mu^{(2)}(uv,wz):=\begin{cases}
    \mu(wz\mid uv)-\mu(wz),&\text{ if }\mu(uv)>0,\\0,&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.028651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_081ebdb3977a2f6e7b4f9625928e52d35aa207186894121023fea311f2321ee1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:main_corollary of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Fix a bounded open set $U \subseteq \mathbb{C}$, $\ell>0$ and $\nu>0$. Set $\varepsilon_n = 2^{-n}$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Fix also $q>0$. Then almost surely, the following holds for all $n$ large enough. For all $\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z} \in (\varepsilon_n^{q} \mathbb{Z}^2) \cap U$ and all $w \in U$ satisfying $w\notin \mathcal{B}_{\tau_{16\ell}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})}^\bullet(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})$, and every geodesic $\Gamma_{\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z},w}$, there exists $(z,r) \in \mathbb{C} \times [\varepsilon_n^{1+\nu} , \varepsilon_n]$ such that 
\begin{align}

B_{\lambda_4 r}(z) \subseteq \mathcal{B}_{\tau_{2 \ell}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})}^{\bullet}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z}) \setminus \mathcal{B}_{\tau_{\ell}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z})}^{\bullet}(\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z}), \quad  \Gamma_{\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z} ,  w} \cap B_{\lambda_2 r}(z) \neq \emptyset \quad \text{and} \quad \mathfrak{C}_r^{\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z} ,  w,\Gamma_{\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z},w}}(z)\quad  \text{occurs}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.311027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0823fac32cf85d4be963e24eb1a89f616642c406bac58889fd275a155ecf225d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.28505, 'Quagmires and large Suslin forests'] Silver's principle $W_\kappa(\lambda)$ asserts that there exist a $\kappa$-Kurepa tree $T$ with $|T_\kappa| = \lambda$ and a sequence $\langle W_\alpha : \alpha < \kappa\rangle$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item for every $\alpha < \kappa$, $W_\alpha$ is a subset of $\mathcal{P}(T_\alpha)$ of cardinality  $<\kappa$,
\item for every $X \in [T_{\kappa}]^{<\kappa}$, there exists $\alpha < \kappa$ such that $\pi_\beta[X] \in W_\beta$ for every $\beta$ with $\alpha \le \beta < \kappa$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.702813+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0829aefcfeb3465dc6a84d66ec1c4f43b0a26ac57b4ee1d7275aad60f3320479","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2608.06038, 'Efron type identities\\ for stopping sets and Poisson hulls'] Let $f\colon \bN\times[0,\infty]\times\bar{\N}_0\to\R_+$ be a
