  where $C_0$, $C_1$ and $C_2$ are constants and the sets $\mathscr{Q}_{\pm\pm}$ are explicit parameter-dependent regions. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.799108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08fef05e83b72081b9fd8a6dd2f8b3795103d00e45aab46e7bf6957aa654452a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:trajectory of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Let $g_0 \in L^2(\pi)$ satisfy the centering condition $\langle g_0, \mathbf{1} \rangle_\pi = 0$. The \emph{relaxation trajectory} generated by $g_0$ is the sequence
\begin{equation}
g_k := P^k g_0, \qquad k = 0,1,2,\dots
\end{equation}
The \emph{energy} of the trajectory at step $k$ is
\begin{equation}
E_k := \|g_k\|_\pi^2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.759904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09065a2f7a3eeb4b75e513f83787a518d2557c2ab1bd2880ec64c336f4d3e6e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor-p-mom-L of arXiv:2604.24914, 'SPDEs with time-independent\\ L\'evy colored noise'] If $p\geq 2$ is such that $m_p<\infty$, then for any function $\varphi \in L^2(\mathbb{R}^d)$,
