\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{B}_p$ is the constant from Theorem (rosenthal of the paper) and $\mathcal{C}_p=\mathcal{B}_p (m_2^{1/2} \vee m_p^{1/p})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.760330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_090ca467421bfe1488e6f83da3ba0e191c5b09918dafcaf127fa7fbbb04d228d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Fubini-v of arXiv:2604.24914, 'SPDEs with time-independent\\ L\'evy colored noise'] Suppose that Hypotheses A to E hold. 

Let $\{\widetilde{Z}^{(t,x)}(s)\}_{s \in [0,t]}$ be a jointly measurable modification of the process $\{Z^{(t,x)}(s)\}_{s \in [0,t]}$ defined in (equation def-Y of the paper). Then, for any $(t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_{+} \times \mathbb{R}^d$, the function
