{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.641052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_090fcbf22d27e2acd916eb08c22561b8860593a0daaea4470f5a677916f3deab","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem PI-3 of arXiv:2411.13788, '\bf Gradient bounds and Liouville property for a class of hypoelliptic diffusion via coupl'] Let $f\in C^1\left(\mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}\right)$ be a globally Lipschitz bounded function. Then for any $t\ge0$, $x=(x^{(1)},\cdots,x^{(r+1)})\in \mathbb{R}^{m_0}\times\cdots\times\mathbb{R}^{m_r}$,  we have
\begin{align}
P_t(f^2)-(P_tf)^2&\le P_t\left(\left\langle \int_0^tE(-(t-s))AE^*(-(t-s))ds\nabla f,\nabla f\right\rangle\right).
\end{align}
For $t>0$, the following reverse Poincar\'e inequality holds for any bounded function $f$:
\begin{align}
P_t(f^2)-(P_tf)^2&\ge \left\langle \mathcal{C}(t)\nabla P_tf,\nabla P_tf\right\rangle.
\end{align}
Where $E(t)=\exp(-tB^*)$ and  $\mathcal{C}(t)$ is defined in (equation C-M of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.246909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_091132744ca8d539e3974e9268b5e248fd9bc71980f0c56c22a6184921cf506b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mainwedge of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp There exists a choice of initial data for (equation eq:curr of the paper)-(equation eq:phi of the paper) such that Assumption (assump:noneq of the paper) for small {\small$\gamma_{\mathrm{data}}>0$} is satisfied, such that the estimates in (equation eq:mainI of the paper) hold, and such that the following holds for some deterministic {\small$\mathcal{T}_{N}\in\R$}:

