\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.764666+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_093c868d2389040455a4757e2e0d280d37132c60b46f0b1acd9bdb20b451942d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c2 of arXiv:2411.19433, 'Singular mean-field backward stochastic Volterra integral equations in infinite dimensiona'] Let condition $(A_{2})$ hold. Then, for any \( \Psi(\cdot) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}_b}(\delta, b; H) \), singular MF-BSVIE (equation 3.7 of the paper) admits a unique adapted M-solution

\[
(X(\cdot), \aleph(\cdot, \cdot)) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}}(\delta, b; H) \times L^2(\delta, b; L^2_{\mathcal{F}}(\delta, b; L_0^2)).
\]

Moreover, if \( \bar{\eta} \) also satisfies $(A_{2})$, \( \bar{\Psi}(\cdot) \in L^2_{\mathcal{F}_T}(\delta, b; H) \), and \( (X(\cdot), \aleph(\cdot, \cdot)) \) is the unique adapted M-solution of (equation 3.7 of the paper) with \( (\eta, \Psi) \) replaced by \( (\bar{\eta}, \bar{\Psi}) \), then

\begin{align}
&\quad \mathbb{E} \left[ \sup_{t \in [\delta, b]} \vert X(t) - \bar{X}(t)\vert_H^2 + \int_{\delta}^b \vert \aleph(t, s) - \bar{\aleph}(t, s)\vert_{L_0^2}^2 \, ds \right] \nonumber\\
&\leq C \mathbb{E} \left[ \vert \Psi(t) - \bar{\Psi}(t) \vert_H^2 + \int_t^b \vert \eta(t, s, \aleph(t, s),\mathbb{E}\aleph(t, s)) - \bar{\eta}(t, s, \aleph(t, s),\mathbb{E}\aleph(t, s)) \vert_H^2 \, ds \right],
\end{align}
for \( t \in [\delta, b] \), where \( C \) is a constant depending on the problem's parameters. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.678317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_094844c52cee3620eb94b32c86b771bcf6f976924efa9751d441507e60e67500","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:walk of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Fix $N,l\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$ and $M_{1},\ldots,M_{l}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, $M_1+\ldots+M_l=M$. For each sequence of monomials $\{P(s)\}_{s=0}^{M}$, coming form the action $\frac{1}{\mu_{+}(N)^{M}}\left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{l}}}{N}\right)^{M_{l}}\cdots \left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{1}}}{N}\right)^{M_{1}}G_{N}(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta)|_{\vec{x}=0}$, let $E(t):[0,M]\rightarrow \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$ be a C\'adl\'ag function defined by 
        \begin{equation}
        E(t)=\operatorname{Deg}(P(\lfloor t\rfloor)).
        \end{equation} 
        We refer to $E(t)$ as a walk.","status":"unverified"}

