{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.751855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0960920709084505afed36c95c360261b3ec09bdc8ca51f2d0358f10a180a0f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:radial-L2-local-mass-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Let \(\nu\) be a finite Borel measure on \(\mathbb S^1\). There exist constants \(c,C>0\) such that for every \(x_0\in\mathbb S^1\) and all sufficiently small \(r>0\), if \(\Lambda=r^{-2}\), then
