{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.812798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09609368cfac03f431b52401104b53b7a614f4babf62619fafa17daf588c0162","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 5 of arXiv:2608.12804, 'Scaling Limits for Ising Models on Inhomogeneous Random Graphs and Applications'] Let us consider $f,g \in L^2[0,1]$. Define the following \emph{rank-one operator} $\opb{g}{f}:L^2[0,1] \to L^2[0,1]$ as,
