\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.249680+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0981f66d8378aef6ec1faa8280ce25ec37750b05d58fedd2a3375e2909e4b10b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 42 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Adopt the notation of \Cref{thm:therecursion}. For every $i\le i_{max}-1$ and for every initial condition, the following holds off of an event of probability at most  $N^{-2L}+2\epsilon_{i+1}$ (with $L$ the same constant as in  \Cref{rem:whoisL}):
  for all times $t$ in the interval
  \begin{eqnarray}

I^N_i=    [\mC N_i^{2+\delta}+t_{\rm mix}^{N_{i+1}}(\epsilon_{i+1}),N^5],
  \end{eqnarray}
 we have that { $\mathcal{H}_{-q_0} (z) \le H^{N_i}_t (z) \le \mathcal{H}_{q_0} (z)$} for all $z \in \mathfrak{X}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.881774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_098217364c33ac957c7ec201d2f1cca3e80afa7d913488b75750e3fb6ca9d0b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Gbranch of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] {Yel16}}] We have
