{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.077814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09a3eeda00177fc8bbae3fa36e3dce4142f4b08703f72a19edef18ac33b0da4c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $(X,\psi)$ be a metric space and let $A\subset X$. Then $A$ is $\sigma$-porous if and only if $A=\bigcup_{n\in\N}F_n$, where each $F= F_n$ satisfies:
