{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.032885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09a3f47dbd1cea01036575222fd4b9243f79a66cd74966e72220f7d2f742563c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:muckenhoupt_maximal of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] If $\rho\in A_2$, then there exists a constant $C(d)>0$ such that for $u\in L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\rho)$,
\begin{align*}
\|\mathfrak{M}(u)\|_{L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\rho)}\leq C(d)[\rho]_{A_2}\|u\|_{L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\rho)},
\end{align*}
where $\mathfrak{M}$ denotes the \emph{Hardy-Littlewood maximal} function given by
\begin{equation}
\mathfrak{M}(u)(x): = \sup_{x\in B,\;B\;\textup{ball}}\frac{1}{|B|}\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}|u(y)|\, dy,\quad x\in\mathbb{R}^d.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:28:33.894765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09ab69be7a7be3592f978474a3cdcfe49cbf087b3e30022ab8faf10d8e871484","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-CondRW of arXiv:2504.20963, 'Exponential moments of truncated branching random walk martingales'] Let $(S_{n}^+)$ denote the Doob $h$-transform of the  $(S_{n})$ and  $(Q_{n})$ be a random sequence such that for all non-negative, measurable function $f$,
  \begin{equation}
