\E[\exp(\la h(X))\ind\{X\in\us\}]&\leq C(R, \Cf).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.321272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09ad2cb3b340bcf7acdf4c05878633ce3e11cb0ca6eaddee05da0de27a54c852","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem uniftotallybounded of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $\delta>0$. Let $N^p_n(\delta,m,Q)$ be the minimum number of $\delta$-balls in the metric $d^{{\mathrm {path}}}_{Q,n}$ needed to cover $\mathcal{X}^{(m)}_{Q,n}$. Let $N'(\delta)$ denote some integer-valued function of $\delta$. Let $E_n(N')$ be the event that for all $\delta>0$, $m\in\mathbf N$, and $Q\in\mathcal{Q}$, we have $N^p_n(\delta,m,Q)\leq N'(\delta)$. Then for all $\varepsilon>0$, there exists a function $N'_{\varepsilon}$ such that for all $n$,
