{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:19.216721+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_09fb8984c0184bd7dbb709477f5c8e8399c2d2910b1939911af814f84af34907","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2602021059 of arXiv:2609.02626, 'Comparison principles and symmetry for subquadratic fractional $p$-Laplacian equations'] Let $N\ge 1$, $s\in (0, 1)$, $1<p<2$, and $u\in \widetilde{W}^{s,p}(U)\cap\widetilde{W}^{s,p}(\mathcal{T}(U))\cap  L^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^N)$ where $U\subset  \mathbb{R}_+^N$ is a bounded open set.  If $w=u-u^*\ge 0$ a.e. in $\mathbb{R}^N_+\backslash U$, there holds 
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
