then $\theta(\lambda) >0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.971733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a4a58fc219a4f9163150ea4e14446c46fc8fa9a53955b1b950a3b5413664da8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:scaledlabeledgraft of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2\in\boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$, and $n\in N(\underline{\tau}_1)$. 
