{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a4eb92f1c229eab35adeb17359cf7d048af3e673b6d8d1564f605c2c07e7f0a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 25 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>4$. There exists $C_1>0$ such that the following holds. For every $\beta<\beta_c$, and every $n\geq C_1(\beta_c-\beta)^{-1/2}$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_{n/2}$ containing $0$ such that
