{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.692891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a506c47574fbbeca97489ca1588e46082403e1b22d73f67dce060946cba69e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop p:300.5 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For each $u \geq 0$, there exists a constant $C'_u \in (0,1]$ such that, uniformly over all measurable $f: {\rm D} \to \mathbb{R}$ with $\|f\|_\infty \leq 1$,
