{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a57f9d3061a5f4b5a41f3a153b7ee51cce9646db3fd2d5629675584b56c50b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop4.2 of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] There exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that, for all $1\leq i\leq N$,
