{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.356492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a5818948ccdc6f2cb33d1189695ad0a3d47841a910e4e6b60caa0d35c843834","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:NSE_cutoff of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R,\mu,\varepsilon>0$ and $q,p\in (2,\infty)$ satisfying (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper). Let $u_0\in \mathbb{B}^{1-2/p}_{q,p}(\mathbb{T}^3)$ and 
$$
w_{{\rm cut,d}} \in L^{2p}({\mathbb R}_+;\mathbb{L}^{2q}(\mathbb{T}^3))\cap L^2_{{\rm loc}}([0,\infty);\mathbb{H}^1(\mathbb{T}^3))\cap C([0,\infty);\mathbb{H}^{-\varepsilon}(\mathbb{T}^3)) .
$$
We say that $w_{{\rm cut,d}}$ is a weak $(p,q)$-solution to the {{\normalfont{3D NSEs}}} with cutoff (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff_det of the paper) if for all divergence-free vector fields $\varphi\in C^{\infty}(\mathbb{T}^3;{\mathbb R}^3)$ and all $t\in {\mathbb R}_+$, it holds that 
\begin{align*}
\langle w_{{\rm cut,d}}(t),\varphi\rangle
&=\int_{\mathbb{T}^3} \varphi\cdot (u_0-\overline{u}_0)
+\Big(1+\frac{3\mu}{5}\Big)\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}
\, w_{{\rm cut,d}}\cdot\Delta \varphi \,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} s\\
&+\int_0^t\int_{\mathbb{T}^3}
\big[ (w_{{\rm cut,d}}\otimes \overline{u}_0)+ \phi_{p,q}^R(\cdot,w_{{\rm cut,d}})\,(w_{{\rm cut,d}}\otimes w_{{\rm cut,d}})\big] : \nabla \varphi\,\mathrm{d} x \,\mathrm{d} s.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.829101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a5adeae22299ecf07baf46ffc9843795a1dffd47b46c24afa1944b0ff2ed5e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm mamporia of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] {mamporia2004}}]
Let $\phi\in {\mathcal H}_{Q}(L(({\mathscr{F}}(U),{\mathscr{F}}(U))))$, and $L_{\phi}: ({\mathscr{F}}(U))^{\ast}\rightarrow {\mathscr{F}}(U)$, $x^{\ast}\mapsto \int_{0}^{t}\int_{\Omega}\phi(s,w)Q\phi^{\ast}(s,\omega)x^{\ast}{\rm d} s{\mathbb{P}}(\omega)$ belongs to $\mathscr{R}_{2}({\mathscr{F}}(U))$. Then there exists the stochastic integral $\int_{0}^{t}\phi {\rm d} W_{s}^{Q}$, and
\begin{align}
  {\mathbb E}\norma{\int_{0}^{t}\phi {\rm d} W_{s}^{Q}}_{{\rm BL}}^{2}<+\infty.  
