and that $\bigl(q_j^{(MF1,l)}(0)\bigr)_{j,l}$ are i.i.d. with finite mean. Then for all $i \in [1;N]$,
\[
\bigl(q_i^{(K,1)}(t)\bigr)_{0 \leq t \leq T}
\xrightarrow[K \to \infty]{d}
\bigl(q_i^{(MF1,1)}(t)\bigr)_{0 \leq t \leq T}.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.678427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a64fa9417a7d4e6652cde89fd09eb7b9079dbc3daab0f5e5bc174b32eefa638","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:block of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] Fix $N,l\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$ and $M_{1},\ldots,M_{l}\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, $M_1+\ldots+M_l=M$. For each sequence of monomials $\{P(s)\}_{s=0}^{M}$, coming form the action $\frac{1}{\mu_{+}(N)^{M}}\left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{l}}}{N}\right)^{M_{l}}\cdots \left(\frac{\mathcal{D}_{i_{1}}}{N}\right)^{M_{1}}G_{N}(x_1,\ldots,x_N;\beta)|_{\vec{x}=0}$, let $q_{i}(t):[0,M]\rightarrow \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$ be a piecewise function, which is C\'adl\'ag on $[0,M]\setminus\{C_{0},\ldots,C_{l}\}$, defined by 
        \begin{equation}
            q_{i}(t)=\begin{cases}
                \operatorname{Deg}_{i}(P(\lfloor t\rfloor)),\quad & t\in [0,M]\setminus \bigcup\limits_{j:i_{j}=i}(C_{j-1},C_{j}]\\
                0,\quad &\text{otherwise}.
            \end{cases}
        \end{equation}
        Let $$q(t)=\sum_{i=1}^N q_{i}(t),\quad t\in [0,M].$$
         We call $\vec{q}(t)=(q_{1}(t),\ldots,q_{N}(t))$ the blocks of $\{P(s)\}_{s=0}^{M}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.661424+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a686e3ff06a08653a66b5dcbc78a5d338dff36649e3a4b00a45d562179ef33f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:switching of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] For any set of vertices $A\subset D_\delta\backslash \partial D_{\delta}$,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb E^+_{\delta, \beta}\left[\prod_{v\in A}\tau_\delta(v)\right] = \mathbf{P}^{\textup{w},\mathrm{DRC}}_{\delta, \beta}\left(\hat{\mathbf{n}}_\delta\in\mathfrak F_A\right)
    \end{equation}
    where $\mathfrak{F}_A$ is the event that every cluster of $\hat\mathbf{n}_\delta$ intersects $A$ (resp. $A\cup\{\partial D_\delta\}$) an even number of times if $|A|$ is even (resp. $|A|$ is odd). The dual statement with free boundary conditions also holds. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.366760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a6a0d731bd3c3d1510c02aa35f4e8029db897f6340c05e1d66792b1c5e82086","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem two-arm-vs-one-arm of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] For every $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $\delta=\delta(\varepsilon)>0$ and $n_0=n_0(\varepsilon)$ such that for all measurable $A\subset Y$ and $n\geq n_0$, we have
