{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.872684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a6bdcc01cf36a9d50f19ccbd608d10773894e5384f2e48115ff2227f359fb70","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:cap of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $(X,d,\mu, \mathcal{E}_p,\mathcal{F}_p, \Gamma_p)$ be a $p$-Dirichlet space, where $p \in (1,\infty)$. Then  for any sequence of subsets $(A_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ of $X$, we have 
