{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.539502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a72c4cc61815d4ae43ebc52b53de4c6427aa6f132dd739b528e3968d92d08d0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:CT-TASEP-propagator of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The propagator $B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}$ satisfies:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)},
leftmargin=*]
\item For all $i > j$ and $r, r' \in \mathbb{Z}$,
\begin{equation}
[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r{+}1, r'{+}1)
= [B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r').
\end{equation}

\item For all $i > j$ and $r, r' \in \mathbb{Z}$,
\begin{align}
[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r')
- [B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r')
= \sum_{j < \mu < i}
[B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{i\mu}(r, a_\mu{+}1)
[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1},\mathbf{n}}]_{\mu j}
(a_\mu{+}1, r').
\end{align}

\item The propagator is $t$-independent and
invariant under uniform shifts of the particle
labels: replacing each $n_i$ by $n_i + 1$ leaves
$[B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r')$ unchanged.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.836532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a76239a8ed2dcb9e1834fb0a83f80837969d1ed3e4678ddd69fd1089c26a199","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $p \geq 2$ and $\beta > 0$. We say that the fast variable $(Y_t)_{t \ge 0}$ is \emph{$p$-dissipative (with constant $\beta$)}, if for all $x\in \R^{d_1}$ and $y_1,y_2 \in \R^{d_2}$
