{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.645133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ad0f3e9ba5e4df534a4e5f6fb65f63ace8cf191ad307044e1bdcff377621181","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ES-XOR of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] {spin-perc-height}}, {[DRC-1]}]
    Let $D$ be a Jordan domain with discrete domain approximation $D_\delta\subset \delta \mathbb Z^2$. The XOR-Ising model $\tau_\delta$ with free/free boundary conditions in $D_\delta$ can be written as 
    \begin{align*}
        \tau_\delta = \sum_{k=1}^{N} \xi_{k}^\delta \mu_{k}^\delta,
    \end{align*}
    where $(\mu_k^\delta)_{k=1}^N$ is a collection of measures with pairwise disjoint supports $(C_k^\delta)_{k=1}^N$, and $(\xi_k)_{k=1}^N$ are i.i.d. symmetric signs. 

