{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b6fa2ad80adf3e4d749853cf9f8dcd3c1bc17a2e2efcf4ca4f54e7935018356","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] For local $f:\Omega\to\C$,
\begin{equation}
\left\langle f,f\right\rangle =\lim_{N\to\infty}\frac{1}{\left|\Lambda_{N}\right|}\mu\left(\left|\sum_{x\in\Lambda_{N}}\left(\tau_{x}f-\mu(f)\right)\right|^{2}\right),
\end{equation}
where $\Lambda_{N}=\left([-N,N]\cap\Z\right)^{d}$.

For a local admissible flow $\phi$,
\begin{equation}
\left\langle \phi,\phi\right\rangle =\frac{1}{4}\sum_{z\in\Z^{d}}\mu\left[c(0,z;\eta)^{-1}\left|\sum_{x\in\Z^{d}}\tau_{x}\phi(\eta,\eta^{0,z})\right|^{2}\right].
\end{equation}
By completion both formulas hold for any $f\in\cH_{1}$ and $\phi\in\cH_{2}$.","status":"unverified"}

