{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.732546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c5610c5da35bcc4ca65d236f37b769eb10adb5dcb67654230062ae4f2c2596f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:buser-isoperimetric-bound of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] If the Ricci curvature of $\mathcal M$ is bounded below by $-(N-1)\delta^2$ for some $\delta>0$, then 
