{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.762003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c8086d46d1f59e5bd28317a535881b289f83ee78e61ad1efc5a9dd205f1be59","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:L4bound2 of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Let $X$ be a solution of (equation eq:main_d of the paper) and suppose that the conditions (equation eq:localLipschitz of the paper) and (equation eq:monotone_fg of the paper) of Assumption (assum:FG_bounds of the paper) hold for some $p\geq 2$. Then, if $\alpha_1$ is the constant in (equation eq:monotone_fg of the paper), we have
