{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.782204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c8f8b7d2dd9392dce9437ce8c9debc2c0e7366cd907406a706bd10f47b06034","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cor:mixing-from-other-temp of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $h_0$ such that for all $\beta'$ and all $h\ge h_0$, if $X_t$ is continuous-time Glauber dynamics run at $\beta>\beta_c$ on $\mathbb{T}_n^2$, initialized from $x_0 \sim \pi_{\beta',h}$, with probability $1-o(1)$, $x_0$ is such that 
