{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856313+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c99dc2d65d69a8e14b7bef46f4fca6d7546557bb959fa5cadf518798f90d1bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] Suppose that $u$ and $f$ are related via~\eqref{eq.u}. There exist $\kappa, c_M>0$ depending only on $\Lambda$ such that 
