{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.321506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0d0182c8abf37da7aebac54093a5a2239cdb3699f154f36388c1326dbe950c0c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 35 (Bilateral sub-Gamma class) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\sigma, \alpha > 0$. A random variable $X$ belongs to the class $\SG(\sigma^2, \alpha)$ if
\begin{align}
    \E\left[e^{\lambda X}\right] \le \exp\left(\frac{\sigma^2\lambda^2}{2\left(1 - \alpha|\lambda|\right)}\right)
