{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.618971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e06514fa5ca5e3328acaef10eba5fc2a3a07d1512800f0758461387546ef744","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 165 (Decomposition of various components of the energy-momentum tensor) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $f$ be a scalar function, and let $\enmomem$ be the corresponding energy-momentum tensor
