{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.951270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0e4a71305286dd37aa5b089d7cc3264fa2168d6a827968991f0d50c437ea2a3a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:regeneration of arXiv:2608.15344, 'A Harris recurrent continuous-time Markov process without wide-sense regenerative structur'] The process $X$ is said to be \textit{wide-sense regenerative} if there exist randomized stopping times $0\leq R_0<R_1<\dots<\infty$ such that:
