{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.665592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0edc5b32b0d19ee0a73a8fa7b9b26824ca05fa1761cb47cee6c950b7a132e309","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem cmj-ell-tree-coupling of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Let $h_\ell\to\infty$, $h_\ell=o(\log\ell)$, and $t_\ell^\star=O(h_\ell)$.
Fix $0<\gd<1/2$, and set
\begin{align*}
 N_\ell:=\ell^\gd,
 \qquad
 r_\ell:={N_\ell}/{\ell}.
\end{align*}
Then the limiting CMJ tree and the $\ell$-spread-out tree can be coupled up to
time $t_\ell^\star$ so that there is a high probability event $\mathcal{E}_\ell$ satisfying the following properties.
On $\mathcal{E}_\ell$, there is an injective ancestry-preserving map
\begin{align*}
 \Phi_\ell:\mathcal{N}_{t_\ell^\star}\to \mathcal{N}_{t_\ell^\star}^{(\ell)}
\end{align*}
such that $\Phi_\ell(\varnothing)=\varnothing$ and, for every $u\in\mathcal{N}_{t_\ell^\star}$,
$
 \mathsf{t}_\ell(\Phi_\ell(u))=\mathsf{t}(u),
$
and 
$
 |\mathsf{p}_\ell(\Phi_\ell(u))-\mathsf{p}(u)|\leqslant r_\ell .
$
Moreover, on $\mathcal{E}_\ell$,
\begin{align*}
 \operatorname{dist}
 \left(
 \mathsf{p}(u),\{0,h_\ell,h_\ell+1\}
 \right)>3r_\ell
\end{align*}
for every non-root $u\in\mathcal{N}_{t_\ell^\star}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.733132+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0edeee3f33f4d3a75f9e2806f753ebc26a7995024b7d69a081875c41197b52e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] For any $\tau \in \tilde{\cT}$, we have that
