	\end{align*}
	where $K_\varrho$ denotes the number of kernel edges appearing in the tree $\varrho$ and $\mathfrak{n}_\varrho$ denotes the node decoration of $\varrho$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.257341+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ef1bce91e6ed1613bfb522a5f3ec8b97a4f039552789d25c1389e6c535fe11a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 62 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Let $\kappa,\;E,\;E_1,$ and $E_2$ be in \cref{hkest}, and $x\in F,\;x_n\in F_n$ be points satisfying
