{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.081665+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ef6061cf8b04b5ff4acadbed428026b20635307a76527a63f60c73cd60ff25d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition PropMartingaleProperty of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] Let $Y$ be a jointly measurable and $\mathcal{F}^-$-adapted process such that 
