{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.466461+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fa04d8d9281d01b63c831aea0e82a42ca479a9a29c9b39aa2850a4dfc7041d0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem MHnp1 of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] The handover frequency in multi-speed case with set of speeds $v_{[n]}$ is given by:

\begin{enumerate}
\item  The pure handover frequencies are 
\begin{equation}
     \Lambda_i= \frac{4v_i\sqrt{\lambda}}{\pi}\left(\frac{\lambda_i}{\lambda}\right)^2, \text{ for }i\in [n].
\end{equation}
\item   For any pair $i\neq j\in [n]$, the mixed handover frequencies satisfies, $\Lambda^{(1)}_{i,j}=\Lambda^{(2)}_{j,i}$ and $\Lambda^{(2)}_{i,j}=\Lambda^{(1)}_{i,j}$.

\item    For any pair $j<i\in [n]$ and $k\in \{1,2\}$, 
\begin{align}
\Lambda^{(k)}_{i,j}&= 4\lambda_i\lambda_j v_i v_j\int_{0}^{\infty}\left[\int_0^{h_j}\int_{t^*}^\infty e^{-\lambda\pi\hat h^2_k(t, h_j, h_i)}   \,{\rm d}t \, {\rm d}h_i +\int_{h_j}^{\infty}\int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-\lambda\pi\hat h^2_k(t, h_j, h_i)}   \,{\rm d}t \, {\rm d}h_i\right] {\rm d}h_j,

\end{align}

\end{enumerate} 
where 

\[
\hat h^2_k(t, h_j, h_i)= v_j^2 \left(\frac{v_i^2 t+ (-1)^k \Delta^{{\frac{1}{2}}}_{i,j}}{v_j^2-v_i^2}\right)^2\!\!\!\!{+} h_j^2 \text{ and } \Delta_{i,j}\equiv \Delta_{i,j}(t, h_j, h_i)= v_j^2v_i^2 t^2- (h_j^2-h_i^2)(v_j^2-v_i^2),
\]

both of them as a function of $t, h_j, h_i$. The quantity
$t^*\equiv t^*(h_j,h_i):=\frac{1}{v_j v_i}(h_j^2-h_i^2)^{\frac{1}{2}} (v_j^2-v_i^2)^{\frac{1}{2}}$, is the non-negative solution of $\Delta_{i,j}(t, h_j, h_i)=0$ in the variable $t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.370732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fa07edc433e9268d58a47fb56c1fd5d08ed281e9f190d97e977d389374ce298","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem one but not other of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $(B_t)_{t\geq 0}$ denote a standard Brownian motion on
