{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.344971+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0fb0e7ad4c5e414bf8843f7a95f4adad589d48ae42d7403356f57c753c9442c9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $ f $ be a random variable. If $ f $ is Bochner integrable with respect to the probability measure $ \mathbb{P} $, then we denote 
