{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.328505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_10408ec7263007ce10b9bbb46ecb44c7946ff7409444a486112657aa445dfc97","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a $n$-dimensional stochastic process. Then the autocovariance at time $t\ge0$ 
and lag time $\tau\ge0$ is defined as 
\begin{align}
    V_t(\tau):=\E[\mathbf{x}_t\overline{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\tau}^{\text{T}}]-\E[\mathbf{x}_t]\E[\overline{\mathbf{x}}_{t+\tau}^{\text{T}}],
\end{align}
where $\overline{\mathbf{x}}$ is the complex conjugate and $\mathbf{x}^{\text{T}}$ is the transpose.
For $\tau=0$ we recover the variance of the process. For $n=1$ we can also define the autocorrelation function
\begin{align}
    AC_t(\tau):=\frac{V_t(\tau)}{V_t(0)}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

