{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.285979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1069389c0e4190138ffe6dfabd4da645f689d30b0daa978c53798a278f5a53c3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn mild solution of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] We say that $(u,v)$ is a mild solution of system ((main of the paper)) if $(u,v)$ is a progressively measurable stochastic process with values in $C(\bar{\mathcal{O}})\times W^{1,\infty}({\mathcal{O}})$ that satisfies:
