{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.544301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_110aa1093f17ca619e771aa9c073768c260c059710b904b89cf27bd205334fbd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 35 of arXiv:2603.28734, 'Free energy analyticity of the disordered XY model and Debye screening in the 2D Coulomb g'] A point $(t,x) \in L  \cdot (\Z_{\leq 0}\times\Z^d)$ is said to be $(L  ,\delta)$-good is the following three conditions are satisfied:
\begin{itemize}
