{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_118a2f95be6f460aa60ecfeebf4fc8aa1194e90aa482c5fb1058c56bf93228fb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 42 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Assume that the condition \eqref{Eq cond small boundary} holds:
the area of the $\varepsilon$-neighborhood of $\partial D$
decay faster than any power of $1/\vert \log\varepsilon \vert$.
Fix $\eta>0$. Let $b$ depend on $\varepsilon$, $b=b(\varepsilon)$,
with values in $[(2v)\vee(2\lambda),+\infty)$.
We further assume that as $\varepsilon\to 0$,
\begin{equation}

\dfrac{\vert \log \varepsilon\vert}{b(\varepsilon)^{2}}\gg \log \vert\log\varepsilon\vert,
\end{equation}
that is to say
