Then, if the condition
\begin{equation}G_1(x)\leq V(x)\leq G_2(x),\end{equation}
holds for all $x\in[x_I,x_S]$, the DG  of Definition (def:dg of the paper)
has value function $V(x)$ in (equation eq:ve of the paper), and optimal stopping rules given by
\begin{equation}\sigma^*=\inf\{t\geq 0\colon X_t\leq x_I\}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\tau^*=\inf\{t\geq 0\colon X_t\geq x_S\}.\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:48:25.153610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_119a0768dfbe559b9ca99ac457e65323164478106fea56f1fe4c83988232c0bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pr:psi of arXiv:2607.05345, 'The local product condition implies cutoff'] If $\mu_0 \ll \pi$, then
