When the limit exists, set \(\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n}=\lim_{L\to\infty}\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n,L}\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.890480+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_120142ea29feec68f5c485aa2ad734bbc0a1efed0abac892f4ed6c2efa1bb7ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 29 (Lyapunov) of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] Let $\ a_{ij}:=(\sigma \sigma^T)^{ij} \in W^{1,p}_{loc}(\mathbb{R}^n) \cup C(\mathbb{R}^n)$ 
    and $\mu \in L^p_{loc}(\mathbb{R}^n), p \in (n,\infty).$ A sufficient condition for the martingale problem associated with the infinitesimal generator $ L$ to be well-posed is that, for every $ T > 0$, there exists a number $ M = M_t > 0$ and a non-negative function $\phi \in C^{1,2}(\mathbb{R}^n \times [0,T]) $ such that $\phi$ is a Lyapunov function on $\mathbb{R}^n \times [0,T]$. In this case, the solution process is non-explosive and, for every $ (x,t) \in \mathbb{R}^n \times [0,T]$, the following holds
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{E}_x[\phi(X_t,t)] \leq \exp(Mt) \phi(X_0,0).
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.965758+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_120680bf76c1baa88c0544acde98df045be965b1ea1474ff7a867c4ea627ea61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop Camrud of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Under Assumptions~(assu:regularity of the paper) and (assu:moments of the paper), setting $a$ as in~(equation eq:a of the paper), for all $n\in\mathbb N$ and $N\geqslant 1$,
