{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.518788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12072082a705b32baf7f42a41753b5f4c1a2da31fd93368ad1256a1907d7db76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Samuels' conjecture) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every integer $n\geq1$, ordered mean vector $0\leq\mu_1\leq\cdots\leq\mu_n$, and $\lambda>\sum_{i=1}^n\mu_i$,
\begin{equation}
c(\bm{\mu},\lambda)
=
\min_{1\leq i\leq n} q_i(\bm{\mu},\lambda)
=
\min_{1\leq i\leq n} \prod_{j=i}^n \left( 1- \frac{\mu_j}{ \lambda-\sum_{k=1}^{i-1}\mu_k } \right).

\end{equation}
The bound is sharp and is attained. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.803020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12080dc10b73ecf28320a571b594054bf39fc23053a5fc02741661ba6ea4b3f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj GW:vertex of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] For $n\in\{1,\ldots,5\}$ and curve class $\beta = [C_1]+\cdots+[C_n]$, the equivariant Gromov--Witten theory of $Z_n$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

