    \end{equation}
    where $\overline{M}_{0}(Z_n,\beta)$ denotes the moduli space of genus-zero stable maps to $Z_n$ in curve class $\beta$. (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.303590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1208509277cdf18e1cef6ff483031ac23803df3ec986bf8394a15cb1c3be4a96","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition sumeq of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] For any $k\leq m <  n$ and $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$, we have
\begin{align} 
