\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.972847+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1208b5aa002a4a78fbf110edbfe90121f6b18a39b4bc40bb4de909b9164c4429","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:propB of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $\mu \in[0,1]$, $\tau_i \in \mathfrak{T}$, and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau_i]\,$ for $i = 1,2$. The most important property of the grafting $\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^\tau$, upon which we rely extensively, is that for every $N\in\N$, uniformly in $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_i}$ and $\mu\in(0,1]$ we have
    \begin{equs}
        \|K_{N,\mu}^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}&\big(\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\graft^\mu\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\big)^\tau\|_{L^\infty_t L^1_{s^\tau}}\\&\lesssim \|   \mathcal{P}_{2N,\mu} \dot G_\mu\|_{\mathcal{L}^{\infty,\infty}}
\|K_{N,\mu}^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau_1)}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_1}\|_{L^\infty_t L^1_{s^{\tau_1}}}
\|K_{N,\mu}^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau_1)}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau_2}\|_{L^\infty_t L^1_{s^{\tau_2}}}    \,.\textcolor{white}{a}    
    \end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.868121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_120d5c82424c60361d1ef4e6135e16dcc3c83930205db0f9e665ffa616403c9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq_1819 of arXiv:2605.10479, 'Poisson approximation of random lattices'] Let $S \subseteq \mathbb R^n$ be a measurable set with $S \cap (-S) = \emptyset$ and $0 < { \rm Vol }_n(S) < \infty$. Let $f: \mathcal F(S) \rightarrow \mathbb R$ be a bounded, measurable
	function such that $f(X) = 0$ if $|X| \geq n$. Then,
	\begin{equation}  \mathbb E \sum_{X \subseteq L \cap S}
		f (X) \cdot \iota(X) =
		\mathbb E \sum_{X \subseteq S \cap P }
		f (X),
		 \end{equation}
	where the sum runs over all subsets $X$ of $L \cap S$ on the left-hand side, and of $S \cap P$ on the right-hand side. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_120f19aaef6fe957d27613c2d6b082f505dd609f6e04f716abb05e3b802bf50b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition analytic R transform of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $x=u+u^*$.  For $\|b\|<1/2$,
