{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.321550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12ac0d257b64e5705e3edd07a28b01e4c7fb515c07a2808753a61e713fb77a55","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem perfectbounds of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $B\in\mathcal{B}^R_{k,n}$ and let $B^{(i)}$ be one of its superboxes. There exists a constant $c=c(\delta)>0$ such that for all $R$ sufficiently large, $k\geq 2$, $0\leq i<k$ and $n> R^k$,
\begin{equation}
