{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12f7d0d538a9e8d359c102ea487f4b8ed312d8aaf925880ae42268605bc2815c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 15 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$. Let $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^E$, $\mathsf{h}\in \mathbb R^V$, and $A\subset V$. Then, for every $x\in V$,
