{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.588814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1315b66a7b9d376fdf8a1ff92734b6adb3f97ab659b90b2ebae06c994ad8c26b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-iteration-expectation of arXiv:2608.30548, 'Finite speed of propagation and waiting time phenomena for stochastic porous media equatio'] Let $u$ be the unique kinetic solution to (equation Eq_SPME_intro of the paper) with initial value $u_0$, $x_0 \in \mathbb T^d$ as constructed in [Fehrman_Gess_ARMA]. For $i\in \left\{1,2,3\right\}$, there exist constants $\ell_i \geq 0$ and $\kappa_i>1$ such that for any stopping time $\tau \geq 0$, the following holds for every $\frac{1}{2}>R\geq s+\delta >s \geq 0$:
