    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_131a21b1761c9d39cdd8655c15dba83d2442908061da3dfcaef154f8e5466b84","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro advanced geographic ineq coupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $n\in \mathbb N$ be such that $\tau_{K}/n\leqslant \delta$ and $n(1-\varepsilon-\delta)\geqslant 1$, let $T\in \mathbb N$ be such that $n+r\tau_{K}\leqslant T\delta$, and let\footnote{This choice of $N$ satisfies $T\geqslant Nn+Nr\tau_K$.}
