{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.775955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_131b3408e1b380de7455237ea825f58d3c0c40215aa104602fca175c80d1b6f6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:FP-pKP of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] At every $(t, \mathbf{x}, \mathbf{a})$ with $t > 0$,
