{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.368803+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1322ecf1eb8db26fe684b27f54070a084348ad0cdb09f34b9beb5e9b46cf95a5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Suppose we are in the set-up of Theorem (thm:convbls of the paper) with $a > 0$. Consider the boundary cluster that is given by the closed union of all critical Brownian loop soup clusters that intersect at least one boundary to boundary excursion, denote it by $\widetilde C_{a}^{m}$ for the metric graph, and by $C_{a}$ for the continuum.

