{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.039262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1335ac2eac109b2bceaa9071631b32ab7525d31f64b4fafb4970feacce93f8bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Markov chain tree theorem) of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $X^N_t$ be a continuous-time Markov chain with transition graph $(V,E)$ and positive transition rates $r_N$.
