{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.576431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_133ddf6a3a22d914ad45ee3d3ce7aa7a4a5554bf897adc0dc67e36dc50e99bfe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:F_tht of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] \begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]
    \item If $s_1 = s_2 = s$, then $F_{\theta}(s,s)$ is convergent if and only
