{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.464575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1343eea8dd403165ca3e45f0fa48f4fea655156db7129b978d9a52cdf8599ebb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop single-location master loop equation in the 't Hooft limit of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Let $\Lambda_N$ be an increasing sequence converging to $\mathbb{Z}^d$. Suppose that there exists a subsequence of $N$ such that $\phi_{\Lambda_N,N,\upbeta}(s)$ converges to $\phi_{\infty}(s)$ for all strings $s\in\mathcal{S}$.  Then, for every fixed non-empty string $s$ and every fixed edge $\mathbf{e}$ in $s$,
\begin{align}
	\phi_{\infty}(s) &= \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') - \sum_{s'\in \mathbb{S}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') \notag
	\\&+ \upbeta\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_-(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s') - \upbeta\sum_{s'\in \mathbb{D}_+(\mathbf{e},s)}\phi_{\infty}(s').
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.189614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13461520ba0ad25568093dda1c03e1ab861e27ccc3704afedc9a00c6ac113a95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2606.31133, 'Level-dependent quasi-birth-and-death processes: Application to cost analysis of multi-ser'] We have,
\begin{eqnarray}
