{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.573201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_13619124becabf9cde7296fc566d847828a096aa85fdfbd1d66d1c500abf2578","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cmt-sharpness of arXiv:2511.01851, 'Percolation on graphs of polynomial growth is local:\\analyticity, supercritical sharpness'] Let $\mathscr{G}\in\mathfrak{G}$ and $p_0\in (p_c(\mathscr{G}),1]$. Then, there is a constant $c>0$ such that the following holds:
