{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.432956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_138fd78fa565c63a4ff3c21759ea5b4bc6deb4d6e25534408de89fbcc00cb042","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:qvar-centered-noise of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] For all $j \in \{1, \dots, J\}$, the quadratic variation of the centered noise process $M^{j,\mathrm{center}}$ satisfies, in the sense of symmetric semi-definite matrices:
