{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.575694+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_147b5ccb23e02c7625671b04eefd7bdc70ad71bc119de78be1f7bde63e8bfaa3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:X:smallball of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Let $I \subset \mathbb{R}$ be a compact interval and $X=\{X(t): t\in I\}$ be a centered
  Gaussian process. Suppose there exist constants $\rho\in(0,1)$ and $c_1, c_2,
    c_3\in (0,\infty)$ such that
  \begin{align}
    c_1 |t-s|^\rho \le \mathbb{E}[(X(t)-X(s))^2]^{1/2} \le c_2 |t-s|^\rho \quad \text{for all $t,s\in I$}
  \end{align}
  and $X$ satisfies one-sided strong local nondeterminism:
  \begin{align}
    \ensuremath{\mathrm{Var} }(X(t)|X(t_1),\dots,X(t_n)) \ge c_3 \min_{1\le i \le n}(t-t_i)^{2\rho}
  \end{align}
  uniformly for all integers $n \ge 1$ and for all $t,t_1,\dots, t_n\in I$ with
  $\max\{t_1,\dots, t_n\} \le t$. Then there exist constants $0<C_1\le C_2
    <\infty$ such that for all $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$,
  \begin{align}
    \exp\left(- \frac{C_2}{\varepsilon^{1/\rho}} \right) \le \mathbb{P}\left\{ \sup_{t\in I}|X(t)| \le \varepsilon \right\} \le \exp\left( - \frac{C_1}{\varepsilon^{1/\rho}} \right).
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.969600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_148451cd106a5075f08214bf72f261c0aeb2fca291bea80b63838617062865fc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 37 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] For every $\mathcal{I}=[t_1,t_2]\subset[0,\infty)$ and $\mathcal{J}=[\underline{a},\overline{a}]\subset(0,1)$ it holds that $x\mapsto V_\infty(t,x)$ is differentiable, and
