	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.759010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14d440a00c6def333aac10fc19ccaf92e9659effec7c559b2847d1c12971fdc1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:grid-annular-estimate-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C,c,\eta>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\),
