{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.568846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14d5a8ae5f2428b6bfefdbf5eff985ac441bd9b50af46e3a7d9c3ac5e3d6e3a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm:BesovLog of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] Let $s, \beta \in \mathbb{R}$ and $0 < p,q\leq \infty$ and $p'$ the conjugate exponent of $p$. We have the following embeddings
\begin{itemize}
\item if $q<+\infty$
\begin{equation}
\widetilde{B}^s_{p,q,\vert \log \vert^{\beta - r_1/q}}(\mathbb{R}^2) \hookrightarrow B^s_{p,q,\vert \log \vert^{\beta}}(\mathbb{R}^2) \hookrightarrow \widetilde{B}^s_{p,q,\vert \log \vert^{\beta +r_2/q}}(\mathbb{R}^2)
\end{equation}
where $$r_1 = \begin{cases}q(\frac{1}{p}-1)+ \max(q-1,0) & \text{ if } p \le 1 \\ 
\max( \frac{q}{\min(p,p')}-1,0) & \text{ if }p>1 \end{cases}$$
and
$$
r_2 = \begin{cases}1  & \text{ if } p < 1 \\ 
\max(1- \frac{q}{\max(p,p')}-1,0) & \text{ if }p\ge 1 .\end{cases}$$

\item if $q=+\infty$
\begin{equation}
\widetilde{B}^s_{p,\infty,\vert \log \vert^{\beta - \max(1/p-1,0) -1}}(\mathbb{R}^2) \hookrightarrow B^s_{p,\infty,\vert \log \vert^{\beta}}(\mathbb{R}^2) \hookrightarrow \widetilde{B}^s_{p,\infty,\vert \log \vert^{\beta }}(\mathbb{R}^2)
\end{equation}

\item if $q=2$, the Sobolev spaces $H^{s}_{2,\vert \log \vert^{\beta}}(\mathbb{R}^2)$ coincide with the classical Besov spaces $B^{s}_{2,2,\vert \log \vert^{\beta}}(\mathbb{R}^2)$ and with the hyperbolic Besov spaces $\widetilde{B}^{s}_{2,2,\vert \log \vert^{\beta}}(\mathbb{R}^2) $.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14e2942a36c66b1758662026df235e57e6edaa2d6688e6fea0bca7b605704158","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 3 (Cumulants and endpoint behavior) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] For every integer $n\geq1$ such that
$\int |x|^{n+2}\nu(\dd x)<\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \E R_X^n=\frac{2\kappa_{n+2}(X)}{(n+1)(n+2)V}.

\end{equation}
In particular, when the third cumulant is finite,
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X)\geq\pos{\frac{\kappa_3}{3V}},
 \qquad
 \cminus(X)\geq\pos{-\frac{\kappa_3}{3V}}.

\end{equation}
The MGF boundaries give
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X)\geq\frac{1}{\tplus(X)},
 \qquad
 \cminus(X)\geq\frac{1}{\tminus(X)}.

\end{equation}
If $\kappa_4$ is finite, then both directional objectives have the same
one-sided derivative at the origin:
\begin{equation}
 \Psi_+'(0+)=\Psi_-'(0+)
 =\frac{\kappa_4}{12V}-\frac{\kappa_3^2}{9V^2}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:04:59.433903+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14ee175503959faa5ef42aaa118badd65790cb4565a73afde9ad0d869868d099","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:concentration-ineq of arXiv:2605.20697, 'Uniform-in-time propagation of chaos for \\ Second-Order Consensus-Based Optimization'] Let the objective function \(f\) satisfy
    (assumption:bounded,assumption:lip of the paper), and let \(q>2\). Consider the
    second-order CBO dynamics where the initial positions and velocities are sampled
    i.i.d.\ from some \(\overline\rho_0\in\mathcal P_{2q}(\mathbb R^{2d})\).
    Assume that the parameter conditions in
    (prop:ito-centered-lyapunov-differential of the paper) hold for \(p=2\) and \(p=2q\).
    Let
    \[
        0<\kappa<\min\left\{\lambda_{2},\frac{\lambda_{2q}}q\right\}.
    \]
    For brevity, write
    \[
        c_{1,2q}:=c_1(a_{2q},2q).
    \]
    Then there exists a finite constant \(C_{\mathrm{Bad}}>0\) such that, for any
    threshold \(A>0\) and \(J\in\mathbb N_+\), the pathwise empirical Lyapunov
    functional \(L_2(t)\) satisfies
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P\left[
            \sup_{t\geqslant0}
            \e^{\kappa t} L_2(t)
            \geqslant
            \mathcal L_2(0)+A
        \right]
        \leqslant
        \frac{C_{\mathrm{Bad}}}{A^q}
        J^{-\frac q2}\,
        \mathcal L_{2q}(0).
    \end{equation}
    Consequently, by norm equivalence result (equation eq:psi2-norm-equivalence of the paper),
    \[
        c_1^{(2)}\mathfrak M_2(\mu_{X_t^J})\leqslant L_2(t),
    \]
    the empirical spatial moments satisfy
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P\left[
            \sup_{t\geqslant0}
            \e^{\kappa t}
            \mathfrak M_2(\mu_{X_t^J})
            \geqslant
            \frac{\mathcal L_2(0)+A}{c_1^{(2)}}
        \right]
        \leqslant
        \frac{C_{\mathrm{Bad}}}{A^q}
        J^{-\frac q2}\,
        \mathcal L_{2q}(0).
    \end{equation}
    In the above, \(C_{\mathrm{Bad}}:=C_{\mathrm{Bad},q,\kappa}\) is given by
    \begin{align}
        C_{\mathrm{Bad},q,\kappa}
        &:=
        2^q\widetilde C_{\mathrm{MZ},q}
        +
        C_{\mathrm{Mart}},
        \\
        \widetilde C_{\mathrm{MZ},q}
        &:=
        \frac{
            2^{3q-2}C_\phi^q(C_{{\rm MZ},q}+C_{{\rm MZ},2q})
        }{
            c_{1,2q}
        },
        \\
        C_{\mathrm{Mart}}
        &:=
        \frac{
            2^{q+1}C_{\mathrm{BDG},q}C_{\sigma,q}
        }{
            \lambda_{2q}-q\kappa
        }
        \left(
            \frac{q-2}{\lambda_{2q}-q\kappa}
        \right)^{\frac q2-1}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.903096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_14efcc315d32ecf73af0707a0debb0f0b0c5935710167dbe9cc5718b5817783c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def SCR of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A \textbf{stochastic choice rule} (relative to $\cal G$) is a map $c : {\cal G} \rightarrow \Delta(\Omega)$, which we will also write as $G \mapsto c_G(\cdot)$ for $G \in {\cal G}$, satisfying:
