$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.250576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15f81df267ca042d01b995bbb03f28629868f2dc18e48a30000e53d99389d457","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: loops to be inserted in STEP1 of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For any $\omega \in \mathcal{A}$ and $\boldsymbol{x}\in \mathcal{R}(\mathcal{L}_{\boldsymbol{F}}^{\beta_N}(\omega))$, we define
    \begin{equation}

        \beta_{\boldsymbol{x}}=\beta_{\boldsymbol{x}}(\omega)=
        \begin{cases}
            \beta(\boldsymbol{x},\mathsf{Near}(\omega,\boldsymbol{x}))&\text{if $\boldsymbol{x} \neq \mathsf{Near}(\omega,\boldsymbol{x})$},\\
            \beta_{i}(\boldsymbol{x})&\text{if $\boldsymbol{x} = \mathsf{Near}(\omega,\boldsymbol{x})$ and $\mathsf{Dir}(\omega,H_{\beta_N}(\omega,\mathsf{Near}(\omega,\boldsymbol{x}))-1)=i$},
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation}
    where $\mathsf{Dir}(\omega,k)=i$ if $\omega(k+1)-\omega(k)=\pm e_i$ for a path $\omega$ and $k \geq 0$. 
    Moreover, we define 
    \begin{equation}

        B(\omega)=\{\beta_{\boldsymbol{x}}(\omega)\,:\, \boldsymbol{x} \in \mathcal{R}(\mathcal{L}^{\beta_N}_{\boldsymbol{F}}(\omega))\}
    \end{equation}
    as the collection of loops to be inserted in the first step.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.956670+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15fb201042ac9558bfc2bdf26e146e79e4f914e444874804f419f84f7b849534","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 51 (Metric transfer does not control deterministic response) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] There exist a profile-admissible bounded target transform \(f\), a bounded transform \(h\) with the same unshifted centering and normalization, and a delocalized spike sequence such that
