{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.473250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_162e4fdac1549ff4dd32fe980ded25154d8b77d7f49ab8d898dcf9f4c478f913","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:multi-derivative of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:multiplicative-Lindeberg}
Let \(X_1,\ldots,X_M\) and \(Y_1,\ldots,Y_M\) be two independent families.  Assume that, for each \(i\), \(X_i,Y_i\) satisfy the hypotheses of (lem:one-coordinate-Lindeberg of the paper) with the same constants and match through order \(m\).  Let \(F:\mathbb R^M\to(0,\infty)\) be \(C^{m+1}\).  Suppose that for each coordinate \(i\), every \(z\in\mathbb R^M\), and \(r=1,\ldots,m+1\),
