\end{enumerate}
Consequently Claims~\ref{conj:A} and~\ref{conj:B} are both false. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.939574+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16737192e4c6ed8714ee8e7c5c47ac2e3349d0d440c0b77ca259d55b239a9ce1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm2ndResult of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Suppose that Assumption~(Assumptions of the paper) holds and that (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) admits an invariant measure $\mu$. Let $\mathbf{X}_0 \sim \mu$ be independent of $\mathbf{W}$, let $\mathbf{X} = (\mathbf{X}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ be the corresponding solution process to (equation eqGenSDEIntro of the paper) with $d$-th component $X = (X_t)_{t \geq 0}$, and assume that the ergodicity condition (equation eqErgoCond of the paper) is fulfilled. Then it holds that
\begin{equation}

