{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.738202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16d42d87ca9eaf9232641988f54822d7c06af516c807eda3168ae19a0c57ab97","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:double_bound_given_pts of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1,a' > 0$. Then for each $\underline{z} \in \mathcal {D}_k^m$, $\underline{r} \in \mathbf{R}_+^m$ with $r_u > 2^{-k(1-a_1)}$ for each $u$ we have
