{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.251290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_173040549dd59f771b946727f709a8b819e5e15a79ddec975aeff0974a45012a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 of arXiv:2605.23222, 'On global solutions to the semidiscrete stochastic heat equation'] For $\beta$ sufficiently small, the following holds: For every $\sigma \in (0,1)$ there exists $\theta = \theta(\sigma) > 0$ such that for all $x,y\in\Z^d$ and $s < t$ with $\| x - y \| < (t - s)^{\sigma}$, the partition function $Z_{x,s}^{y,t}$ has the representation 

