{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.181193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_175f9ef9c5cd80297be98bbf4502dfe697cc8e35ddff7b8c05235bf566ebe550","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2608.22636, 'Q-Learning with Stable Infinite-Dimensional \\Linear Function Approximation'] Under Assumptions~\ref{assump:mdp} and \ref{assump:stable_kernels}, the operator
$\cG=\mrm{K}\mathcal T\Phi$ maps $\Theta$ into itself and is a $\gamma$-contraction on $\Theta$.  Hence $\cG$
