{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.532310+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_19163d0b8257349ea9729e3207612f36b3aa9dc3200834166e3bf0fb1fa27e24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Generalised Theorem of arXiv:2411.07671, 'Long Time Behavior of General Markov Additive Processes'] Let $((\xi,\Theta),\mathbb{P})$ be a MAP such that Assumptions 1,2,3, and 4* satisfied. Then, 
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
