\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.476959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_192c3639e51061d9b4bd7470ed663da4f55be23418ea5d0465bc1086417ebef9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (Exact two-population location) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] For every $\delta\in(0,1)$,
\begin{equation*}
 \mathcal M_{n,2,1,\delta}
