{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.734115+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1932be77d17ce70d9d32544ffa9314fd6ec0bfd49cf2a7bcef3d61e5aade231e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemm_sp_ER_RRG of arXiv:2503.24372, 'A criterion on the free energy for log-Sobolev inequalities in mean-field particle systems'] Let $\E_N$ denote the expectation associated with a random regular graph with degree $d_N$ or an Erd\"os-R\'enyi random graph with mean degree $d_N$ and assume $\lim_{N\to\infty}d_N/\log N=+\infty$. 
