\] 
satisfies
\[
	\nucnorm{\mathbf{X}^+-\mathbf{X}_\star}
	\geq \left(1-\frac{220 r}{d}\right)\nucnorm{\mathbf{X}-\mathbf{X}_\star}.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.098316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1946b54b544d30562b2986e5e9f37cc3d8c8990e48a12803e84d0960da756a84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Critical Noise Threshold for Demographic Survival) of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] The condition $C_t(\gamma) \ge 1$ is guaranteed as soon as the mechanism's noise scale satisfies the explicit lower bound $\gamma \ge \gamma_c$. Given an $\ell_2$ clipping bound $R=\Omega(\sqrt{d})$, the critical threshold $\gamma_c$ is defined as:
\begin{equation}
    \gamma_c \triangleq
    {\Omega} \left(\frac{\sqrt{dN_{t-1}}}{N_{t-1}-1}
    \left(
    \frac{\Phi_{q,r}^{-1}
    +\sqrt{(\Phi_{q,r}^{-1})^2+2\tau}}
    {2\tau}
    \right)\right)
\end{equation}
where $\Phi_{q,r}^{-1} \triangleq \Phi^{-1}\left( \frac{q}{q+r} \right)$ is the probit function (the inverse of the standard normal cumulative distribution function) evaluated at the performative survival threshold. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.245286+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1947bbaa5f4f6a2b7e5193bfb370b707792c246ffb23b897113743bc26df9d16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: dimension bound of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $\lambda\vdash n$, and $r:=n-\lambda_1$. Then, we have
