{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.355169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_199b2f0706dbfb38d03440adfcff35976d5b70fa7f0fce4e82d1acff37aef756","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor.duality.fbsde of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Let $p\in[2,\infty)$ and $\delta\in[0,\infty)$, and write $q=p/(p-1)$ for the conjugate exponent. The unique optimizers $\alpha$ and $Y$ of the problems $V_{p,\delta}^{\infty}$ and $P_{q,\delta}$ are given by
    \begin{align*}
        \alpha(t) = - \lambda(t) Y(t),\quad t\in(0,1),\qquad Y=Y(1),
    \end{align*}
    where $(X(t),Y(t),Z(t))$, $0\leq t \leq 1$, is the unique strong solution of the forward-backward stochastic differential equation
    \begin{equation*}
        \left\{
            \begin{alignedat}{2}
                dX(t) &= -\min\bigg(\frac{c_0}{\|Y(t)\|_2},\, \frac{1}{\delta}\bigg) Y(t)\,dt + dB(t),\qquad&& X(0) = 0,\\
                dY(t) &= Z(t)\, dB(t),\qquad&& Y(1) = \frac{X(1) |X(1)|^{p-2}}{\|X(1)\|_p^{p-1}},
            \end{alignedat}
        \right.
    \end{equation*}
    and $\lambda:(0,1)\to[0,\infty)$ is defined as in (equation eq:primal-optimizers-finite-p:def-lambda of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.756613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_199dd4abfc7a50bdca6bf8a0a5f6b8323aa6e80df51c7368b0b5cd6885fba889","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma5 of arXiv:2411.02362, 'Limit theorems for random Dirichlet series: boundary case'] Let $(s_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be as defined in Lemma (lemma4 of the paper), where $\gamma\in (0, 1/2)$, and $M(s)=\lfloor \log 1/s/\log\log 1/s\rfloor$ for $s\in (0,{\rm e}^{-{\rm e}})$. For $s\in [s_{n+1},s_n]$, the following limit relation holds
