{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.329192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a49682c7700a82cd0c18419aa09addc0efe3701ff6454d1ef0593bfa1bdaf8c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 13 of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $p \in [1, \infty)$ and assume that $\{X^n_s : s \in S_n, n \ge 1\}$ is $(\nu_n)$-$\CUI(p)$ in the sense of  \cref{def:CUI-uniform}. Assume that for each $n \ge 1$ there exists $D_n \in \cS_n \otimes \cS_n$ such that:
