{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.215230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1a97f861eaf508acb2d051eb7ffb2b9b10f8bb4b79f5ff31a93cf13ce6a1a1fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lpineq of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Consider a probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P})$ on which a scalar valued Wiener process is defined.  Suppose $f(s,\omega)$ for $\omega \in \Omega$ is an $\mathcal{F}_t$-adapted process.  Then the following inequality holds for $q > 1$

