    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1aa526d28487561d55f3111bd1f9d85f83c65405e0b49c08c5db388c184cb040","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $M\sim CP(\lambda, F)$, $f$ be a Bernstein function (see \eqref{definizioneFunzioneBernstein}) and $\mathcal{H}_f$ be the corresponding Bernstein subordinator.
\begin{itemize}
