{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.354421+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1acb1e19b916e13c5a97406b1bf50aa329bc4b04f3001d4d15bc7ca14e4c75d8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.glivenkocantelli of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Suppose that $\bm{x}^n = (x^n_1,\dots,x^n_n) \in {\mathbb R}^n$, and $h^n \in {\mathbb R}_+$ are such that
    \begin{align*}
        m_{\bm{x}^n}^n \xlongrightarrow{\mathbf{d}_p} m, \qquad h^n \longrightarrow h,
    \end{align*}
    for some $m \in \mathcal{P}_p({\mathbb R})$ and $h \in (0,\infty)$. Suppose moreover that for each $n$,
    \begin{align*}
        \bm{G}^n = \big(G^n_1,\dots,G^n_n \big) \sim \gamma_{h^n}^{\otimes n}.
    \end{align*}
   Then,
