{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.188793+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ae5f446463a49220ecc9a69d586f616ef5b03d7721de12daf6326585dbebe56","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumptions~\ref{assump-PDE} and \ref{assump-particles} hold, with $\sigma=0$. Let us further assume that $F \in L^\infty([0,T]; H^\gamma_{2}(\T^d\times \R^d))$, for some $\gamma>0$. Then there exists $C>0$ depending on $d,\gamma,\vartheta^1,\vartheta^2$ as well as on $\lVert \langle v\rangle^{2k} F^\circ \rVert_{L^2_{x,v}}$, $\lVert F \rVert_{L^\infty_{t} H^\gamma_{2}}$ and $ \lVert u \rVert_{L^\infty_{t}L^\infty_{x}}$, such that for any $N\in \N^*$,
\begin{equation*}
\rateone=  \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \big\| \langle v \rangle^{k} (F_{t}- F_{t}\ast \vartheta^{N}) \big\|_{L^{2}_{x,v}} \leq C N^{-\frac{1}{2} \beta(\gamma\wedge 1)} .
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:11.642019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ae688b98207c7b94a269a49209364133eead40e56ec64d21d51b1ee1fd5bf3c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2605.31374, 'Multi-point functions of a full-plane two-state\\ fuzzy $4$-Potts model'] Fix $n\in2\N$ and $d\in(0,1)$. Let $\rho$ be a function satisfying $\rho(t)\to0$ as $t\downarrow0$. There exists
$\eps(\delta)\in(0,d/2)$ such that we have, as $\delta\to0$,
\begin{align*}
    \eps(\delta)\to0,\qquad \tfrac{\delta}{\eps(\delta)}\to0,\qquad
    \eps(\delta)^{\rho(\delta/\eps(\delta))}\to1,
\end{align*}
and, for every $\tau\in4\Z\cap[-n,n]$ and every $\xi\in\Xi_\tau$, the convergence in
\emph{\eqref{e.GFF_compute}} holds with $\eps$ replaced by $\eps(\delta)$, uniformly in $x\in X(n,d)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.282726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ae7fefb5570d1e7daa2ddc0000ccc5542ce85d1d7294cab69dc2127d5a121cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2604.25336, 'Central limit theorem for slow-fast system under mixed fractional Brownian motion'] Let \(p\ge 2\) and \(\alpha\in(0,H)\). Under \textbf{H1}--\textbf{H3}. Then for all \(\epsilon\in(0,1]\),
\begin{eqnarray}
\mathbb{E}[\|x^\epsilon\|^p_{\alpha}] \le C_{x_0,T}, \quad \|\bar x\|_{\alpha}\le C_{x_0,T}
\end{eqnarray} 
where the constant \(C_{x_0,T}>0\) only depends on \(x_0\) and \(T\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.286230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1aea0a7bf6c5c7ce24fca170ea69b21a6276434f33de8f7077011e25ba8cd69c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma det asymp of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Let $\zeta$ be a probability measure on $[0,1]$ with prefix $\{0,q\}$ with $q\in (0,1)$. Let $f\in \mathbb{R}$. There exists $C_\varepsilon>0$, depending only on $\varepsilon$, $f$, and $\xi$, with $C_\varepsilon\to 0$ as $\varepsilon\to 0$, such that the following holds uniformly over $\mathbf{m}\in \mathrm{SUSY}_1(\zeta,\varepsilon)$: Letting $\mathcal{B}:=\{\nabla F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}(\mathbf{m})=0,\, F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}(\mathbf{m})=Nf\}$,
		\begin{equation*}
			\left| \log \mathbb{E}\bigl[ |\det\nabla^2 F_{\mathrm{TAP},\zeta}(\mathbf{m})|\mid\mathcal{B}\bigr]
			- \log\prod_{i=1}^N\partial_{mm}h_\zeta(q,m_i)
			- \frac{N}{2}\xi''(q)\left(\int_q^1 \zeta([0,t])\,\mathrm{d} t\right)^{\!2}
			\right|
			\leq C_\varepsilon N.
		\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.770965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af1ec8ccf41888611517c7c229dbefbb9a8cc71d70caa69c406981ae92dc79a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma drift term convergence of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Let $T > 0$ and $0 < \epsilon' < 1$ be fixed. Then, whenever $r \geq R(\epsilon)$ that satisfies ((eq: 4.1.46 of the paper)), it holds that
