\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.088187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af2257180676fb4dc1e9740be5c1fa3f2b8891ffb2402f3d1f60f83536319be","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:C2 of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Suppose that $(\sigma,b)$ satisfy Assumption~(assu:H of the paper) and conditions~(item:1a of the paper)--(item:1d of the paper) on $I$. Let $N\ge 2/|I|+1$. Then there exists a sequence $(\sigma_n,b_n)_{n\ge N}$ satisfying Assumption~(assu:H of the paper) and conditions~(item:1a of the paper)--(item:1d of the paper) on ${\mathbb R}$, such that,
    \begin{align}
        b_n(x,t)=b(x,t)\ \text{ and }\ \sigma_n(x,t,\cdot)=\sigma(x,t,\cdot), \quad \forall x\in I_n,\, t\in {\mathbb R},
    \end{align}
    where $I_n:=\bigl(\inf I+\tfrac{1}{n},\, \sup I-\tfrac{1}{n}\bigr)$, with the convention $-\infty+c=-\infty$ and $+\infty-c=+\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.375351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1af43cb3d48f1b5fe338fd3adb40fd4b39539b0d20d35f015c08d89a70a7df67","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition cor:moments of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $\beta\in\mathbb{R}$, $N\in\mathbb{N}$, $k\in\mathbb{N}$, and
	$\mathbf x=(x_1,\ldots,x_k)\in\mathbb{Z}^k$. Recall $\mathscr E_{\beta,k}$ from (equation eq:G-beta-k of the paper). Then, for every $t\ge0$ and every
	$\phi_1,\ldots,\phi_k\in\ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b(\mathbb{R})$,
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{aligned}
		&\mathbb{E}\bigg[
			\prod_{i=1}^k
			\mathfrak H_{\beta,N}(t,x_i,\phi_i)
		\bigg]
		=
		\mathbf E_{\mathbf x}^{(\beta,k)}
		\bigg[
			\mathscr E_{\beta,k}(tN)
			\prod_{i=1}^k
			\phi_i(N^{-1/2}\tttonde{R_{tN}^i-tN\sinh(\beta)})
		\bigg]\; \text{.}
		\end{aligned}
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:40.043135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1afa07cf0e1462736a04bc82b177d9f0c209790710e2bc55406cb16572e22dff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2510.24244, 'Statistical properties of Markov shifts: part II-LLT'] Let Assumptions \ref{MixAss}, \ref{Assss}, \ref{Ball Ass} be in force.
 If $(f_j)$ is irreducible then  with  $\sigma_n=\|S_nf-\bbE[S_nf]\|_{L^2}$ and $S_n=S_nf$,
   \begin{equation}

\sup_{t\in\bbR}\left|\bbP((S_n-\bbE[S_n])/\sig_n\leq t)-\Phi(t)-
  \frac{\bbE[(S_n-\bbE[S_n])^3](t^3-3t)}{6\sig_n^3}\varphi(t)\right|=o(\sig_n^{-1})
