{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.327909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b6ce5e1ae28d1e3b2c5b62d019afe366be6610422a82b7c75e403d99e3c6ddd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 (\cite{GGT25}) of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $\{X^n_s : s \in S_n, n\ge 1\}$ be a collection of $\cX$-valued random elements such that $(\omega, s) \mapsto X^n_s(\omega)$ is $\cF\otimes \cS_n/\cB(\cX)$-measurable for all $n \ge 1$. Let $p \in (0, \infty)$. Then, the following assertions are equivalent:
