{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.356822+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1be87c7d49d609788990e154b81016f13d8a70137451c52d30df73fdba638234","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumption {\rm\ref{A2}} holds. Then, for any $t\in \RR$ and $x\in\RR^n$, there exists $\mu^x_{t} \in \mathscr{P}_1(\RR^m)$ such that for any $s\le t$ and $y\in\RR^m$,
