{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.781941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c2e81ef7af9f64e0a5e934add92e2933b1926745e0a4bbf00787c1a2f3bf040","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $p_0<1$ such that for all $p>p_0$ and all $\beta>\beta_c(2)$ the following holds. 

