{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.747255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c5e290f540c1b1286929a5b772bda2d68492709df116aedb64a629169de72e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 21 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Let $\{X_n;n=1,2,\cdots\}$ be a sequence of $m$-dependent and linear stationary random variables in a sub-linear space $\sles$ satisfying condition (CC). If there exists $M$ such that 
