{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c6c1e8c581ea8851a599afef3c85d1c811b646d7770806e43833c3645c30ddb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:codiff-asymp of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Under Assumptions~(ass:params of the paper) and~(ass:limits of the paper), for fixed
$s \in \mathbb{R}$ and as $t \to +\infty$:
\begin{equation}

\tau\!\bigl(X^{(n)}_H(s),\, X^{(n)}_H(t)\bigr)
\sim C(s)\, t^{(\alpha-1)H_+ + H(s) - n},
\end{equation}
where the constant $C(s) > 0$ is given by
\begin{equation}

C(s)
= \frac{\alpha\,|\kappa_\infty|^{\alpha-1}\,|C_n(s)|}
{n - (\alpha-1)H_+ - H(s)},
\end{equation}
with
\[
\kappa_\infty := \frac{\binom{H_+-1/\alpha}{n}}{\Gamma(H_++1-1/\alpha)},
\]
and $C_n(s)$ is the leading tail coefficient of $f_n(s,\cdot)$ from
Lemma~(lem:kernel-asymp of the paper)(iii). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.888134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c7504123e88059c8791c6df2d287afc76df40aea4e89bb39eb03b62d199806e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2607.17087, 'Transportation-cost inequalities for invariant measures of stochastic reaction-diffusion e'] Let $\{\sigma(s,y): (s,y)\in\mathbb{R}_+\times [0,1]\}$ be a progressively measurable random field such that the following stochastic integral is well-defined. Then for any $\alpha>0$, $T\geq 0$, and $p>2$,

  \begin{align}
     \sup_{t\in [0,T]} \mathbb{E} \sup_{x\in [0,1]}\left|\int_0^t\int_0^1 e^{-\alpha (t-s)}p_{t-s}(x,y)\sigma(s,y)\,W(ds,dy) \right|^2
    \leq   \frac{K_p}{\alpha^{\frac{p-2}{2p}}} \sup_{s\in [0,T]} \mathbb{E}\sup_{y\in[0,1]}| \sigma(s,y)|^2,

  \end{align}

where the constant $K_p$ is independent of $T$ and defined by
\begin{align}
  K_p:=\min_{\frac{1}{2p} < \theta< \frac{1}{4}} \left\{\left|\frac{\sin\pi\theta}{\pi}\right|^2 (2\pi)^{-\frac1{p}} \left(\frac{p-1}{p}\right)^{\frac{p-1}{p}}  2^{2\theta - \frac{1}{2}} \left( \Gamma\big(\theta - \frac{1}{2p}\big) \right)^2 \times \frac{p-1}{2\sqrt{\pi}} \Gamma\big(\frac{1}{2} - 2\theta\big) \right\},
\end{align}

where $\Gamma(\cdot)$ is the gamma function. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

