{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.317156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ca3e9535140ad1eed55ff850f1ae55d6f9d28a99e7b5ce99d37604102782f0c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-convergence of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $d^{{\mathrm {geo}}}$, $d^{{\mathrm {res}}}$, and $\mu$ be suitable multiples of the geodesic CLE$_6$ metric, the CLE$_6$ resistance metric, and CLE$_6$ gasket measure, respectively. There exist sequences $({\mathfrak{q}}_n^{{\mathrm {geo}}})_{n\in\mathbf N},({\mathfrak{q}}_n^{{\mathrm {res}}})_{n\in\mathbf N}$ such that for all $m$,
