{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.254215+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1cc6eb778e4380f11686f7898a5b8e46a26ec86610a4400ebef0f3c1844e9597","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 14 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For $\calX=(X,d^X,\rho_X,\mu_X),\;\calY=(Y,d^Y,\rho_Y,\mu_Y)\in\frK_{\bullet}(\tau)$, we define
