{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.293292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1de3eeb605ca6165ed24391250ed41b7acf6998a902c06e661703927b67ed34d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem teo:2 of arXiv:2601.00291, 'The probability of connection between two vertices cannot be monotone with the distance fo'] For every $d \geqslant 2$, there exists a critical value $\lambda_c(\mathbb{Z}^d) \in (0,\infty)$ such that
