 \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:08.987689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ec0192bcf928ce799c24be71fe19bd01c42f644e35eb4a7e4ba439fdeee786e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem_Slepian of arXiv:2608.17463, 'Persistence probabilities of fractional L\'evy fields indexed by hyperbolic space and othe'] Let $(E,d)$ be a metric space and let $(X_t)_{t\in E}$ and $(Y_t)_{t\in E}$ denote two real-valued, separable, centred Gaussian processes, such that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{E}\left[X_t^2\right] & = \mathbb{E}\left[Y_t^2\right], \quad \forall t\in E,
        \qquad\qquad
        \mathbb{E}\left[X_s X_t\right]  \leq \mathbb{E}\left[Y_s Y_t\right], \quad \forall s,t\in E.
    \end{align*}
    Let $f: E\to \mathbb{R}$ be a measurable function that is continuous except for countably many points. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb{P}\left(X_t \leq f(t) \quad \forall t\in E\right) \quad \leq \quad \mathbb{P}\left(Y_t \leq f(t) \quad \forall t\in E\right).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.900983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ec1359507b03fc1b16ac33bb73268d0bacab77cd3bf5539cf4ac6abad6d7ac7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma epscontrol of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] Let $\mathbf{X}_\star,  \mathbf{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2}$. Assume that the measurement operator $\mathcal{A}: \mathbb{R}^{d_1 \times d_2} \longrightarrow \R^m $ satisfies the NSP of order $r$ of (def:NSP:statement of the paper) with constant $\eta_r <1$.
