    denote the \textbf{locus of rational curves} on $(X, I)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.727188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f182fe605e0448b7761d2e475e0b1ca828c800aeebb8a91ad55130536e9766f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmas3.1 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] For every fixed \(\delta>0\),

\begin{equation}
D\to K_\delta(D)-I,
\qquad
D\to S_\delta(D)

\end{equation}
are globally Lipschitz maps from \(H\) to the Hilbert--Schmidt
operators on \(H\).  More precisely,

\begin{equation}
\|K_\delta(D)-K_\delta(E)\|_{\mathrm{HS}}
+\|S_\delta(D)-S_\delta(E)\|_{\mathrm{HS}}
\le C_{K_0}\delta^{-1}\|D-E\|_H,

\end{equation}
where $C_{K_0}>0$ only depends on $K_0$.
Furthermore,

\begin{equation}
\|K_\delta(D)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le1,
\qquad
\|S_\delta(D)\|_{\mathrm{op}}\le1,
\qquad
K_\delta K_\delta^*+S_\delta S_\delta^*=I.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.057350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f2841ac43f54651afc418cc5934bfc7d105a036f51976bb8e5ea2067baf4f06","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:occupation-current-geometry of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Under Assumptions~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper) and
(ass:bochner-regularity of the paper), the identities
