{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.861587+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f3e59de660a6100d9c01350463daee1848203d51fb9dcd7dc681268a75f57d4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2605.21424, 'A dice game, a multinomial walk, and the inverted Dirichlet distribution'] The winning probability has the form  
 \begin{align*}
 \pi_1&=\mathbb{P}(A_k<n_k,  2\leq k\leq m).
 \end{align*}
where $(A_2,\ldots,A_m)$ has a negative multinomial distribution (see e.g.~\cite[Chapter 36]{JohnKotzBal97}) with parameter set 
