{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.779785+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fa7fb62086f3ad8c6b6a9439b25fce9e4c43343c60c828fa0ea9c35269fcf45","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma JTtrapRF of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] Fix $ \beta \in (0,\infty) $. Then as $ N\to\infty$, under the measure $ \mathbb{P}_{{\mathfrak m},N,W}^{\ssup{{\rm sym}}} $ the empirical path measures $ L_N $ satisfy a Large Deviations Principle on $ {\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal C }_\beta) $ with speed $ N $ and rate function $I_{W,{\mathfrak m}}:{\mathcal M }_1({\mathcal C }_\beta)\to \mathbb{R} \cup \{\infty\}$ given by
\begin{equation}
\hat{I}_{W,{\mathfrak m}}(\mu)=\begin{cases}
    H(\mu_0|{\mathfrak m})+H(\mu_{0,\beta}|\mu_{0}\otimes\mu_{\beta})+{\mathcal S }_W(\mu),\text{ if } \mu_0=\mu_\beta\\
