{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.935607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fb2c64e7eb5c06d63455c9a3a36c91b1edc6a6be7b8b904ffdcfa6c8025873f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.H1TwoScaleDeg2 of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a finite positive constant $C(c_{-},c_{+},\mathbf{r},\rho)$ such that for every $\lambda\in(0,\tfrac{1}{2})$, the following estimates about the expectation and variance of the carr\'e du champ of $\widetilde{G}_\lambda$ hold:
