{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.118248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fbe4d96e36221b6e89e8414d129c8614bb925ab24b48df818618c09f31e4740","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: cle outermost singularity of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] For any $\iota>0$, there exists a constant $N_0=N_0(\iota)>0$ and an absolute constant $c>0$ 
     such that for any integer $N>N_0$ and disorder strength ${\epsilon}=N^{-\frac{7}{8}}$, we have \begin{equation}
        {\mathbb{E}}\left[ \frac{1}{2}\sum_{\tau\in\{0,1\}^n}\Big|\mu^+_{\Lambda_N,0}(\mathcal{E}_\tau)-\mu^+_{\Lambda_N,{\epsilon} h}(\mathcal{E}_\tau)\Big|\right]\ge 1-c^{-1}\iota^{c}.
