{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.268953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fbf8027223e6ed056be47af43a40b5494ec6c6419003c7810b404953696dc8b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: main result of arXiv:2411.05924, 'Non-negative Martingale Solutions to the Stochastic Porous Medium Equation with Sticky Beh'] There exists a stochastic basis $(\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P)$ supporting processes $u \in \bigcap_{\delta\in(0,1)} \Xi^\delta_{\mathfrak u}$, $u_n \in C([0,T], L^2)$ for $n\in\mathbb N$ and $Q$--Wiener processes $W$ and $W_n$ for $n\in\mathbb N$, s.t.~$((\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P), u, W)$ is a non-negative martingale solution to the stochastic porous medium equation (equation eq: intro1 of the paper)--(equation eq: intro3 of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def: solution of the paper), satisfying for any $p \geq 1$
    \begin{equation}

        \mathbb E\left[\sup_{r\in[0,T]} \left\| u(r) \right\|_{H^{(\alpha-2)/\alpha}_0}^p \right] + \mathbb E\left[\int_0^T \left\| u(r) \right\|_{H^1_0}^p \mathrm d r \right] < \infty.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, for any $n\in\mathbb N$ the triples $\left((\Omega, \mathcal F, \mathbb F, \mathbb P), P_n(u_n), W_n \right)$ are martingale solutions to (equation eq: discrete dynamics Rn of the paper) in the sense of Proposition (prop: existence for discrete systems of the paper), and there exists a subsequence of $u_n$ converging to $u$ $\mathbb P$-a.s.~in $\Xi_u$. Furthermore, if for some $\varepsilon > 0$ the pre-limiting systems satisfy
    \begin{equation}

        \limsup_{n\rightarrow\infty} \mathbb P (\mathcal S(u_n) \geq \varepsilon) > 0,
    \end{equation}
    then the system (equation eq: intro1 of the paper)--(equation eq: intro3 of the paper) exhibits sticky behavior (equation eq: limiting stickiness condition of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.592076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fc012cbaffe6d9e941c8727cecc6bb958d7503455c8972eeb902e18d750d725","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition DUFJ-INT-SJ-A of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] A random function $v\left( {x} \right)$ is said to be intermittent, if for two positive exponents ${p_1} > {p_2}$, there exists an increasing function $\mathfrak{h}_1\left( r \right)$ such that
\begin{equation}
\frac{{{{\left\| {v} \right\|}_{{L^{{p_1}}}}}}}{{{{\left\| {v} \right\|}_{{L^{{p_2}}}}}}}  \sim  \mathfrak{h}_1\left( r \right) \to  \infty , \ \ \mbox{as}\ r \to  \infty  , \ \mathbb{P}\mbox{-a.s.},
\end{equation}
where $r$ is the cutoff wavenumber associated with the Fourier transform of $v\left( {x} \right)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:30:36.801531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fc4add7cc1f14ec3f77468b42fc0ded869c058d848aa84996e4cf347511a182","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 55 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $\bX_n \to \bX $ in $\bZ_T$. Suppose $z \in \mathscr{V}$. Then       
