{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.877040+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1fc67c4bc75922a814065eaea25a1d320f3a6c514c7b3c0928fa22f4368b23d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 (Polynomial colon-ideal criterion for classwise realizability) of arXiv:2609.02449, 'Finite Directional Coefficient Modules over Euler Fibers of $A$-Hypergeometric Systems'] Let $\Lambda\in\mathfrak{L}_{\bm{\beta}}$ and $K\in\mathcal{A}_{\bm{w}}(\Lambda)$.
