{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.581096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21346a1c1b14cfcc232f1731753656b62f1b4d03d730e58dcbede1577503cb36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 5 (Kernel-density score rate) of arXiv:2609.01319, 'Matched Queries for Curvature and Density at Branching Junctions'] Assume a fixed finite query design, a positive lower bound on local tangent mass, bounded branch jets, and the conditions of \cref{thm:perturbation}. For $N$ independent samples and fixed $\lambda>1$, the score of the empirical Gaussian kernel density estimate (KDE) gives, with probability at least $1-\delta$,
\begin{equation}
\norm{\widehat\theta-\theta}
