{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.161388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_224e1e114f6199e722cbca6009ecca54458442bc81339265a9ed3c2b5139af5e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.17302, 'Elephant random walk with attributed steps and extractions of random sizes'] When we are in Scenario \eqref{Scenario_1}, and the samples are drawn with replacement, the sequence $\left\{\left(n^{-1}A_{n},n^{-1}B_{n}\right)\right\}$ converges, almost surely, to a (possibly sample path dependent) compact connected internally chain transitive invariant set, contained in $\mathcal{S}$, corresponding to the autonomous ODE:
