{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.899462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2255bcf1fead5426e5ec7909d171f0f2832b7319db1c19ee9e9f187e0243c9b6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 24 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Given a weight $w_h(x)$ as in \eqref{eq_ansatzw} and $h\in[H]$ we define two holomorphic functions $\Phi^{\pm}_h(z)$ of $z \in \amsmathbb{M}_{h}$ satisfying
\begin{equation}

\forall x \in [\hat a_h,\hat b_h]\qquad \frac{w_{h}\big(\N x+\frac{1}{2}\big)}{w_{h}\big(\N x-\frac{1}{2}\big)} =
 \frac{\Phi^+_h(x)}{\Phi^-_h(x)}.
\end{equation}
They are specified by
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}

\Phi^+_h(z) & := e^{-\N[U_h(z+\frac{1}{2\N})-U_h(z-\frac{1}{2\N})]} \cdot \prod_{j=1}^{\iota_h^+} \bigg(\hat b_h - z-\frac{1}{2\N} + \frac{\rho^+_{h,j}}{\N}\bigg), \\
\Phi^-_h(z) & := \prod_{j=1}^{\iota_h^-} \bigg(z-\hat a_h -\frac{1}{2\N}+ \frac{\rho^-_{h,j}}{\N}\bigg).
\end{split}
\end{equation}
We also define holomorphic functions $\phi^\pm_h(z)$ of $z \in \amsmathbb{M}_{h}$ satisfying a $\N=\infty$-version of \eqref{eq_ratio_weights} (although they may still be $\N$-dependent as $V_h$ can depend on $\N$)
\begin{equation}
 \forall x \in [\hat{a}'_{h},\hat{b}'_{h}]\qquad
\frac{\phi^{+}_{h}(x)}{\phi^{-}_{h}(x)} = e^{-\partial_x V_h(x)}.
\end{equation}
They are specified by
\begin{equation}

\phi^+_h(z):= e^{-\partial_zU_h(z)} \cdot \big(\hat b'_h - z\big)^{\iota_h^+},\qquad
\phi^-_h(z):= \big(z-\hat a'_h\big)^{\iota_h^-}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.187661+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_226224ea0d70b3076b8e537f7d4a72e0e7b112ae344ddcd683a08c8833d9a999","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 7$ and $\epsilon>0$, there exist $\Cl(d,\epsilon),\cl(d,\epsilon)>0$ such that for any $n\ge  \Cref{const_highd_avoid_box_twopoint1}$, $N\ge \Cref{const_highd_avoid_box_twopoint1}n$, $\psi\in \Psi(n,N)$, $i\in \{ 1,2\}$, and any $x\in \mathfrak{B}_{m_{\diamond},100}^{\diamond}$ satisfying $|z_i^{\diamond}- x | \ge \frac{m_\diamond}{100}$,  
