{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:16:53.569531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_228946744d8e75e49dbc59344c3d385f4ef8cd8f3d99d7f9211f5054052ff20e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cox2charac of arXiv:2412.04589, 'Inverting the Markovian projection for pure jump processes'] Let $X$, $\mathbb{G}$, $(J_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}^*}$, $(\tau_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $(\lambda^k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}^*}$ be given by Theorem~(thm:cox of the paper). Furthermore, suppose that each $\lambda^k$ is predictable with respect to $\mathbb{G}$. Let $h: \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be a truncation function. Then, $X$ is a $\mathbb{G}$-It\^o semimartingale whose differential characteristics associated with $h$ are
