{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.086777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_229b948c77e9b37b101eb1e4d68365de842f6ca5fa3fe193a7256a2640ef324c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume that Hypotheses \ref{H0}, \ref{H0.5} and \ref{H1} hold and let $\vartheta\in [0,1)$. For every $n\in\N$, $\varphi\in C^\vartheta_b(H_n)$ and $t>0$ we have
