Moreover,  \smallskip

\noindent 1.  the eigenfunction $M_\eta$ converges to the equilibrium $M$ in $L^2(\mathbb{R}^d,\mathbb{C})$ when $\eta$ goes to $0$.  \smallskip

\noindent 2.  If furthermore we assume (a3 of the paper) and (a5 of the paper) then, the  eigenvalue $\mu(\eta)$ satisfies
 \begin{equation}
