{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.207076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2322eae5bad79feb12e893e13d6eb87db484a2a9c67e3ce627854083e5e329a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 (Variance bound on a finite chaos) of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] Let \(\delta(\varepsilon)>0\) be such that \(\delta(\varepsilon)\xrightarrow{\varepsilon\to 0} 0\) and \(\varepsilon/\delta\to 0\) as \(\varepsilon\to 0\). For \(\varepsilon\) small enough,
