{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.671493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23efb3a1484128863f8f400bf375ece106488cd30935b601d4b66fba74840d09","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 (Bounded-entry pencil limits) of arXiv:2608.04824, 'Strong Convergence for a General Class of Random Matrix Models'] There is a probability-one event on which, simultaneously for every
\(q\geq1\), all self-adjoint coefficient matrices in
