{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.377333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24f2567a0a424194dfceaa989af4384db9b38832b8284a3c5b8e21dbb261ba69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma vprocess of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix  $k \geq 2$, a finite-support function $h:\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{R}$, and a sequence $\beta=\beta_N\to 0$ as $N\to \infty$. Consider $\mathbf x^N\in \mathbb{Z}^k$ such that $N^{-1/2}\mathbf x^N\to \mathbf z \in \mathbb{R}^k$ as $N\to \infty$. Then, for all $1\le i,j\le k$, $i\neq j$, the pair
     \begin{equation}
