{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.777375+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_251c165f7e9f6a387d3c721ff3fd9bfa9eebc1a2a787f3f911237d3a10bb419e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma_modification_of_shift of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] For any $1\le k\le DN/2$, suppose that $\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}$ satisfies the condition (equation eq:condA2 of the paper). Defined $z_1$ and $\Delta_{\text{\rm{ev}}}$ as in (equation eq:z1 of the paper) and (equation definition_shift_eigenvector of the paper) for a constant $\varepsilon\in\left({0,1}\right)$.

Then, we have 
\begin{equation}
            \begin{aligned}
                \Delta_{\text{\rm{ev}}}(z_1)=\gamma_k-\gamma_{k}^{\text{\rm{sc}}}+\mathrm{O}\pa{\left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle^2+\left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle\sqrt{\kappa(\gamma_k)+\eta}}=\gamma_k-\gamma_{k}^{\text{\rm{sc}}}+\mathrm{O}\bigg(\frac{\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^4}{N^{2}}+\frac{k^{ 1/ 3}\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2}{N^{4/ 3-{\varepsilon}/{2}}}\bigg).
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation}
where $\kappa(\gamma_k)=|E^+-\gamma_k|\wedge|\gamma_k-E^-|\sim {k^{2/3}}/{N^{2/3}}$ by (equation eq:kappa_gamma_k of the paper).
The shift $\Delta_{\text{\rm{e}}}$ in (equation definition_shift_eigenvalue of the paper) satisfies a similar bound:         \begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\Delta_{\text{\rm{e}}}(k,\eta)=\gamma_k-\gamma_{k}^{\text{\rm{sc}}}+\mathrm{O}\pa{\left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle^2+\left\langle \Lambda^2 \right\rangle\sqrt{\kappa(\gamma_k)+\eta}}=\gamma_k-\gamma_{k}^{\text{\rm{sc}}}+\mathrm{O}\bigg(\frac{\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^4}{N^{2}}+\frac{k^{ 1/ 3}\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2}{N^{4/ 3-{\varepsilon}/{2}}}\bigg). 
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}













        In particular, if we take $\varepsilon<\varepsilon_A$, the errors in these two estimates are bounded by $N^{-2/3-{\varepsilon}_A}k^{-1/3}$. 

        The corresponding results also hold for $DN/2<k\le DN$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.650888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_251d52df5077e8eb104e11d4f0fa6f711281a4a7561eb930c44053310107b6f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm domain-mon of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D, \tilde D\subseteq\mathbb C$ be two simply connected domains such that $D\subseteq\tilde D$. Let $\phi$ and $\tilde\phi$ be two GFFs in the respective domains. We have that:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
