{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.127300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_255af329c0802ea7af66040fd7c90cb99000cc178f3e5e4837c7da617bb13cf0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem NormalisedDist of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] Let
$\gamma:\left[\tau_{1},\tau_{2}\right]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{2}$
be a continuous BV path. There exist  $\delta_1,\delta_2,r\in(0,1)$ such that the following properties hold true. Let $a<b<d$ be elements
of $\left[\tau_{1},\tau_{2}\right]$ such that $\gamma_{a}\neq\gamma_{b}$ 
\[
\left|\gamma_{b}-\gamma_{c}\right|<\delta_{1}\left|\gamma_{b}-\gamma_{a}\right|.
\]for all $c\in[b,d]$. 

