{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.588602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26972b719ccc6a4ff934f6e6b107337be5c9e3542443cf53fbb1de5514001ea9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 603 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] We have uniformly in $\zeta \geq 0$,  $\beta \in \mathbb{R}$ and $0\leq t_1<t_2$, 
