{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.340723+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2697c94158644c32d7c4459957ebe77cd4f54a1d7a726c3e060fbf9e31314b15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:one_step_improvement of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Suppose that Assumption (ass:forcing_regularity_iteration of the paper) holds. Let $\mu>0$, $r\in (1,\infty)$, $p_0\in (2,p)$, and fix $0<\gamma_0< (1-\frac{2}{p}-\frac{d}{q})\wedge (1-\frac{2}{p_0})$. 
Then there exist constants 
$$
L_0\geq 1\qquad \text{ and } \qquad \eta\in (0,1/4],
$$ 
depending only on $\mu,p,q,r,p_0,d$ and $\gamma_0$ for which the following assertion holds whenever $\delta\in (0,1]$ and $N\geq 1$ satisfy 
$$
(\delta N)^{-1}\leq L_0^{-1}.
