        \SM_\SCT(B_\varepsilon(z; d_\SCT)) \ge \varepsilon^{2 + \zeta}, \quad \forall z \in B_1(o; d_\SCT), \ \forall \varepsilon \in (0, \varepsilon_\ast]. 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.474049+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27f5f7ea7024bda9ed477598290e700b1b3bbf5ac8695772f2342a8d49f02f0b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:intercondi of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] [Intertwining condition] 
    Suppose that $\mathcal{P}_t$ is a $\sigma$-KMS detailed balanced with generator $\mathcal{L}$. There exists operators $\{V_j\} = \{V_j^*\}$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal{L} = - \sum_{j \in \mathcal{J}} \partial_j^\star \partial_j 
    \end{align*}
    where $\partial_j(\cdot) := [V_j, \cdot]$ with the adjoint
    $\partial_j^\star$ with respect to the KMS inner product. We say $\mathcal{P}_t$ satisfies the $\kappa$-intertwining condition for some $\kappa \in \mathbb{R}$ if for any $j \in \mathcal{J}$,
    \begin{equation} 
        \partial_j \mathcal{P}_t = e^{-\kappa t} \mathcal{P}_t \partial_j\,,\quad \text{equivalently, }\    \partial_j \mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L} \partial_j - \kappa \partial_j\,. 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27f9670762603fa4893ee588498c21c55633fb5fb9c5a275266c2fc5d6fa01c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:unif_bound of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $x\in\Omega$ and $D_x=\mathbb B(x,r_x/2)$ where $r_x=d(x,\partial\Omega)$. Then,
		\begin{align}
			\inf_{x\in \Omega}\mathbb{P}_x\left(B^{(\alpha)}_{\tau_{D_x}}\in\Omega^c\right)>0.
