         Then, $\pi \in \mathcal{T}_{bc}\deln{\mathbb{W}^d, \mathbb{W}^d}$.
        \item If $\pi$ is induced by a bicausal Monge map $T$, then $\rho$ is $\mathcal{O}^d$-valued and there exists a strong solution to (equation eqn:extendedbrowniansde of the paper). 
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

