{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329067+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c533613ce413124bca4f3dc0c1b4a96cb770917000c9905ce63dd9d2743d5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] A fractional Brownian motion (fBm) $\left(\mathbf{W}^{H}_t\right)_{t\geq 0}\subset \R^n$ with Hurst index $H\in(0,1)$ is a centered Gaussian process with covariance 
\begin{equation}

\left(\E \left[\mathbf{W}^H_t \left(\mathbf{W}^H_s\right)^\textnormal{T}\right]\right)_{j_1,j_2\in\{1,\dots,n\}}=\frac{1}{2} (t^{2H} +s^{2H} -|t-s|^{2H}) \delta_{j_1,j_2},
 \end{equation}
for $\delta$ that indicates the Kronecker delta. Specifically, the fBm in $\R^n$ is composed by i.i.d. scalar fBms with Hurst index $H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c66b1d38d481d703b9c6fb00ade91fa19d13de5d819e095752cdcb4b9b9f35","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma ONCS of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] Let $f:\ {\mathbb{R}^m}  \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}$ and $u:\ {\mathbb{R}^n} \longrightarrow {\mathbb{R}^m} $ be two smooth functions. There then exists a positive constant $C\left( {n,m,N} \right)$ such that
