{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.288066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c793f4813a0626bd5a9f7ea4d6e14fb6f15dae49f46814478dc1066d6005cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:max_fluct of arXiv:2604.21142, 'Gaussian fluctuations for Internal DLA on cylinders'] Let $(A(t))_{t\geq 0}$ denote an IDLA process on the cylinder ${\ensuremath{\mathbb G}} _N$ starting from $A(0) = R_0$. For every $\n > 0$ and every $m \geq 1$ there exists a constant $C = C(\n, m) < \infty$ such that, with
	\[ T^\sharp \coloneqq N \sqrt{\t_{mix}} \,(\log N)^2\,, \qquad \Delta_N \coloneqq C \max\!\left\{\, \log N,\; \sqrt{\frac{T \wedge T^\sharp}{N}\,\Big( \log N + \log_+\!\big( T/N \big) \Big)} \,\right\}\,, \]
