{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.755223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_298987228910678bfd3812a391897e74e99b69a14b89d5d0e36e05e7a644bc4f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lil of arXiv:2411.02362, 'Limit theorems for random Dirichlet series: boundary case'] Assume that $\mathbb{E}[\eta]=0$, $\sigma^2=\mathbb{E} [\eta^2]\in (0,\infty)$ and let $\alpha>-1/2$. Then, almost surely,
