{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.471005+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29933c61f637ea2133061ead7e9c1a5efd47731e218dc5b24d5085dfe0dd37d4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 95 (The blow-up weight) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] We define the \textbf{blow-up weight} $\weight$ to be the function defined in double-null coordinates as: 
