{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.677570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29d063734120e2f89359cf9f4b1f526bf4c8c90d4b0d27f58392d1c0be8dfb4e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] For $\ell \geq 0$, let $Z_\ell \coloneqq |\cT^\dom_\ell|$ be the total number of vertices in the branching process after $\ell$ generations. Then, \(Z_\ell\) has a probability generating function, defined recursively by
    \[
