{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.889916+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ab12da4523727360af890798b9f0c075f83de45571324a62b705c8b9e5d6795","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:log:Hanson:Wright of arXiv:2607.04047, 'Top Singular Value in Sum-Products of Random Matrices'] There exists some universal constant $c > 0$ such that for every $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ and $\theta \in \mathbb{R}^n \setminus \{0\}$, 
