{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:11.413526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2aec8d944509e57bd39922b753b06671e8c7a20ec50257897e6ee5ff9558975c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2606.08115, '2606.08115'] Let sequences $\{a_n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, $\left\{\delta_{n, m}\right\}_{n, m \in \mathbb{N}}$, $\left\{b_{n, m}\right\}_{n, m \in \mathbb{N}}$ be such that the equality $a_n = \delta_{n, m} + b_{n, m}$ takes place for every natural $n, m$. Assume that the following conditions are valid:
