{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.671762+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c1bcab7f05421af80871627f7f564341448ba1684381cefefc39c6a2160bae7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Gaussian:process:moments of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( \gamma \) be a Gaussian measure on \( (\mathbb{R}^T,\mathcal{C}(\mathbb{R}^T)) \).
