{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.750780+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c7a4b2f36324ce662276aff5f0a32cf0054f03ab11bc12cec3cc61f3eff5046","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:circle-uniform-cylinder-upper-bound-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. If \(0<\beta<A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\), then, almost surely, there exists a finite random constant \(C_\beta\) such that
