{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c9227b08010ac9b82e1317126e092ba143eac6fa2604e79fc61c63f1162668a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:unif_prob_bound of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $(B_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ denote the hypoelliptic Brownian motion on $\mathbb{G}$. If $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is a bounded, open set satisfying the intrinsic exterior cone condition, there exists a constant $c=c(\Omega)\in (0,1)$ such that 
