{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.848536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2c92b4852584ee4331d55eb6ef4272d521c900601ba6ea70b6f03c18108b8409","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:central-bound of arXiv:2606.27073, 'Retention Profiles and KL Contraction Bounds in Finite Markov Chains'] For any $\mu\neq\pi$,
\[
  \frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu P\|\pi)}{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu\|\pi)}
  \;\le\;
  M\cdot\frac{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu\|\pi)+H(\mu)}{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu\|\pi)}
  \;-\;
  \frac{I_\mu(X;Y)}{D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu\|\pi)},
\]
where $H(\mu)=-\sum_x\mu(x)\log\mu(x)$ is the Shannon entropy.
Equality holds if and only if $r(x)=M$ for all $x$ in the support of $\mu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.301181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ca43b2a41068bdf7096006e9868c9f1fa51c7a8a2b59ea704f3e2062b5681fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem prob:testingunknown of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Given a matrix $M$, distinguish the following two hypotheses. 
