{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:57.004086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ca5334fe482fcdc7fe0cb112bdd0752143b543577b7c2e0e7990f90315a30fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:E[multi-edges] of arXiv:2604.05921, 'Simplicity of random hypergraphs'] Let $\forall e \in E: \delta_e \leq \frac{1}{2} n \mathds{E}[d_U]$ and let $R(\cdot)$ be as in (equation def:B of the paper). Then the expected number of multi-hyperedge pairs in a uniformly random undirected hypergraph with degree sequence $\vb*{d}$ is
    \begin{align}

        \mathds{E}[M_n]&= \frac{1}{2} \sum_{e \in E} \sum_{\substack{e' \in E\backslash\{e\}:\\\delta_{e'}=\delta_e}}\frac{(n\mathds{E}[d_U]-2\delta_e)!}{(n \mathds{E}[d_U])!}\sum_{\substack{\vb*{a} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}:\\\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} ia_i = \delta_e}}  \frac{\delta_e!^2}{\prod_{k=1}^{\delta_e} k!^{2a_k} }\sum_{\alpha(\cdot) \in R(\vb*{a})} (-1)^{\sum_{\vb*{x} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}} (\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} x_i - 1)\alpha(\vb*{x})} \\
     &\hspace{1cm}\times 
    \prod_{\vb*{y} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}} \Bigg( \frac{1}{\alpha(\vb*{y})!} \Big(\frac{n\mathds{E}\big[\prod_{i=1}^{\delta_e} (\mathds{1}_{\{d_U \geq 2i\}}\frac{d_U!}{(d_U-2i)!})^{y_i} \big]\big(\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} y_i-1 \big)!}{\prod_{i=1}^{\delta_e} y_i!} \Big)^{\alpha(\vb*{y})} \Bigg). \nonumber
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.411282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ca9d1cd7b44401a66e653ad1119a1500159c54910a1976fb9d43c18fe679a64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2601.07808, 'Supercritical long-range percolation on graphs of polynomial growth: the truncated one-arm'] \label[lemma]{prop:one_arm_connection}
    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = O(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.  

    For $r \in \mathbf{N}$, $b \geq 2$, and $\mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)$, there exist $c_1 = c_1(G,J) > 0$ and $c_2 = c_2(G) > 0$ such that 

    \begin{multline}        
        \sum_{\substack{
            \mathbf{r} \in \mathcal{R}(b,\mathbf{m},r)
            \\
            \mathbf{A} \in \mathcal{A}(b,\mathbf{m})
        }}
        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            P(\mathbf{A},\mathbf{r})
            \subseteq
            \mathcal{H}^*(\mathbf{A})
        \right)
        \\
        \leq 
        c_1 
        r^{d(1 - \alpha)}
        (b-2)^{d \alpha - d + 1}
        \mathbf{E}_{\beta}\left[\deg(o)\right]^{b-1}
        \prod_{i=0}^{b-1} 
        \exp
        \left(
            c_2 \beta m_i
        \right)
        .
    \end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.608475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ca9f4f92ed891d4927f40014c4db9935a4c967865b7996cb49cf0b935004adb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.25772, 'Propagation of Chaos and Gaussian Fluctuations for Mean-field Coupled Maps'] Under the assumption \textup{\textbf{(A1.1)}}, let $\bar{\rho}_t,t=0,1,\dots$ be a solution to \eqref{eq:mf-dynamics}. Then there exists some constant $C>0$, depending on $\Delta,\mathrm{Lip}(F)$ and $\Vert h\Vert_{C^1}$, such that
