for all $x>0$, $y\ge1$, and $n\in\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.033322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cb063a4de6327fb20ca9a57c8d18022e41d7cdf6fb3b605544f3cda60e3e403","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:SIR_monotonicity of arXiv:2607.29409, 'The Zombie Infection Model'] Let $G_{1} = (V_{1}, E_{1})$ and $G_{2} = (V_{2}
		, E_{2})$ be countable, locally bounded and connected graphs. Assume that the
		following conditions hold:
		\begin{enumerate}[label=\roman{*}.]
			\item $\lambda_{1}\leq\lambda_{2}$ and $\mu_{1}\geq\mu_{2}$ 

			\item $V_{1}\subseteq V_{2}$ and $E_{1}\subseteq E_{2}$ 

			\item $\Delta_{1} \Subset V_{1},\Delta_{2} \Subset V_{2}$ with $\Delta_{1}
				\subset \Delta_{2}$ 
