{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:11:57.341602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e0db41af3a83212fd065f7d18eb05454e2faeb124dd49c16885c3ecb69296b9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] The functions $f_+$ and $f_-$ are strictly convex, satisfying
\begin{equation}
 f_+(0)=f_-(0)=0,\qquad f_-(1)=0,\qquad
