{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.671047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e14055f744f00cbb477e62e12fd4b8d674c5cffa8e859b77e72b0d764e8bfac","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:gaussian:measure of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] A probability measure \( \gamma \) on \( (X,\mathcal{C}(X)) \) is called a \emph{Gaussian measure} if the characteristic functional of \( \gamma \) has the form
