{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.467684+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e6c19df4197d5e1223fc7ff9b3f05ff829beed142a756ea443d2219a907aee9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 (Exact reflection) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] Let $T(p)=1-\delta-p$. Then, for every $n,k,t$ and $p\in[0,1-\delta]$,
