{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.589788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ecfd397fec6bd8da7651bb4b2bc1bb2180778606f70e75f10965c12c383f162","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Fourier-isometry of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $M_\alpha$ be a real S$\alpha$S random measure on $\mathbb{R}$
with Lebesgue control measure, and $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ a complex
isotropic S$\alpha$S random measure on $\mathbb{R}$ with Lebesgue
control measure. For $f \in L^\alpha(\mathbb{R})$ with Fourier transform
