{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.275335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2fdb0659fa669d1a5d0c78b6dfbdc2ba8017d4e3c66d642f4e3bc40773284c74","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.06246, 'The smallest singular value for rectangular random matrices with Lévy entries'] For fixed $\theta>0,m>0$ we define subsets $\mathbb{S}_p^{n-1}(\theta)$ and $\mathbb{S}_a^{n-1}(m)$ of $\mathbb{S}^{n-1}$ via
    \begin{enumerate}
