{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:44:24.744944+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ffb66d22a8148f7c2ff84c6dd883a7317c3a1b229ed62ca4a3cf999bac295a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PropFiniteDimProperties of arXiv:2605.06429, '\large \bf $\mathsf{GL}_N(\mathbb{C})$ BROWNIAN MOTION AND STOCHASTIC PDE ON ENTIRE FUNCTI'] Let $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$. The SDE (equation GLinitial of the paper) has a unique strong solution  from any initial condition in $\mathbf{W}_{N;+}$. Moreover, for $\mathsf{x}^{(N)}(0)\in \mathbf{W}_{N;+}^\circ$ we have almost surely for all $t\ge 0$, $\mathsf{x}^{(N)}(t)\in \mathbf{W}_{N;+}^\circ$. Furthermore, the semigroup $(\mathsf{P}_{t;N})_{t\ge0}$ associated to $\mathsf{x}^{(N)}$ is $\mathrm{C}_0$-Feller continuous on $\mathbf{W}_{N;+}$ and the space of smooth symmetric  functions with compact support on $\mathbb{R}^N$ restricted to $\mathbf{W}_{N;+}$ forms a core for the generator $\mathsf{L}_N$ of $(\mathsf{P}_{t;N})_{t\ge0}$ and is moreover invariant under the action of $\mathsf{L}_N$. Finally, the transition kernel of $\mathsf{P}_{t;N}$ is given explicitly by, for $t>0, \mathbf{x}\in \mathbf{W}_{N;+}^\circ, \mathbf{y}\in \mathbf{W}_{N;+}$,
\begin{equation}
\mathsf{P}_{t;N}(\mathbf{x},\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y})=\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda_Nt}\frac{\prod_{1\le i <j \le N}(y_i-y_j)}{\prod_{1\le i <j \le N}(x_i-x_j)}\det\left(\mathsf{q}_t^{(N)}(x_i,y_j)\right)_{i,j=1}^N\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y},
\end{equation}
where $\lambda_N=N(N-1)(3\theta+2-4N)/12$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.386735+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ffd6b7fb06f652be25d564eb60efccb0bd43934c0beabd8879b5143817a6683","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2609.03962, '$L^p$ isomorphisms for the fractional Laplacian on $\mathbb{R}^n$ and their application'] Let $n\ge2$, $0<s<2$, $p\in(1,\infty)$, and let
$f\in\Lambda^{-1,p}(\R^n)^n$, $g\in\Lambda^{s-2,p}(\R^n)$. Then
\eqref{fstokes} admits a solution $(u,P)\in V_{s,p}^n\times L^p(\R^n)$ if
and only if
\begin{equation}
  f\perp\mathcal P_{[1-n/p']}
  \qquad\text{and}\qquad
  g\perp\mathcal P_{[2-s-n/p']}.
\end{equation}
In this case the pressure $P$ is unique, and the solutions are precisely
the pairs $(u+\lambda,P)$ with
$\lambda\in(\mathcal P_{[s-1-n/p]})^n$; thus the solution is unique
whenever $s-1<n/p$, in particular for all $0<s\le1$, and unique up to an
additive constant vector when $s-1\ge n/p$. Moreover every solution
satisfies
\begin{equation}
  \norm{P}_{L^p}
  +\inf_{\lambda\in(\mathcal P_{[s-1-n/p]})^n}
   \norm{u-\lambda}_{\Lambda^{s-1,p}}
  \le C\big(\norm{f}_{\Lambda^{-1,p}}+\norm{g}_{\Lambda^{s-2,p}}\big).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.355679+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ffdd2a24048feadd41bab444a93a79f7deab2f16990731396277b965d722bea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem.optproperties of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] For any $0 < T \leq 1$, the problem
