{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.834737+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30177890ad9200f04a7f7e2769212dd72571cef7801f525f404b8bdcca532602","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:exp-log-differentials-app of arXiv:2609.00556, 'Higgs--Demailly System and Positivity of Higgs Bundles'] For a Hermitian endomorphism $u$ and an endomorphism-valued one-form $X$,
\begin{align}
 e^{-u}\mathcal D(\exp)_u(X)
 &=\int_0^1e^{-su}Xe^{su}\,ds,
 \\
 \mathcal D(\log)_G(B)
 &=\int_0^\infty(G+\rho\operatorname{Id}_E)^{-1}B(G+\rho\operatorname{Id}_E)^{-1}\,d\rho.

\end{align}
If $u=\operatorname{diag}(\ell_1,\ldots,\ell_r)$ at a point, then
\begin{equation}
 \bigl(e^{-u}\mathcal D(\exp)_u(X)\bigr)_{ab}
 =\chi(\ell_b-\ell_a)X_{ab},
 \qquad \chi(s)=\frac{e^s-1}{s},
\end{equation}
with $\chi(0)=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.631941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_301a00907820c1692fecf484f6c04952d85eee31b0f34e490bfb86b8c54fa92a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:capacity of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Let $W$ be a simple random walk on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ for $d\geq 3$ and denote by $\mathbb{P}_y$ the law of $W$ with $W(0)=y\in\mathbb{Z}^d$. For a set $A\subset\mathbb{Z}^d$, the capacity of $A$ is defined as
\begin{equation}
    \Ca(A):=\lim_{\|y\|\rightarrow\infty}\frac{\mathbb{P}_y(W[0,\infty)\cap A\neq\varnothing)}{G(0,y)}=\sum_{a\in A}\mathbb{P}_a(W[1,\infty)\cap A=\varnothing),
\end{equation}
where $G$ is the SRW Green's function on $\mathbb{Z}^d$ and $\|y\|$ denotes the Euclidean norm of $y$.","status":"unverified"}

