{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.757828+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3102b3f2af5c43d1603f5ceb10552776ff1f6d0b072b438353ff3b87fbf9aa67","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_regular_estimate_localized_eigenvector of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under the assumptions of (theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of the paper), the following bounds hold for any $a\in [\![{D}]\!]$ and $\mathsf M_0\in\ha{M_{\text{\rm{sc}}}(z_0),M_{\text{\rm{sc}}}^*(z_0)}$, $\mathsf M_1\in\left\{{M(z_1),M^*(z_1)}\right\}$:   \begin{align}
