{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.985058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_314de9328f0948bbd736b7eaef6091be19fc440854d38dbcba74e0a281cd9dd2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition inversibilite de A of arXiv:2412.00865, 'On the spectral problem and fractional diffusion limit for Fokker-Planck with(-out) drift '] Let $\eta_0>0$ and $\lambda_0>0$ small enough. Let $\eta \in [0,\eta_0]$ and $\lambda \in \mathbb{C}$ fixed, with $|\lambda|\leqslant \lambda_0$. 
For all $F \in \mathcal{H}_\eta'$,  equation (equation formulation fable of the paper) admits a unique solution $\psi^{\lambda,\eta} \in \mathcal{H}_\eta\subset  \mathcal{H}_0$, satisfying the following estimate
\begin{equation}
\| \psi^{\lambda,\eta} \|_{\mathcal{H}_0} \leqslant \| \psi^{\lambda,\eta} \|_{\mathcal{H}_\eta} \leqslant C \| F \|_{\mathcal{H}_\eta'} ,
