{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.460010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3180402d5f16a55796c58f8d604e952ba5549a8043fd98b87fff026bcaabfc89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 (Kinetic formulation) of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] Let $u_{\alpha,n}$ be the weak solution of \eqref{eq:penalized-viscous} and $f_{\alpha,n}:=\one_{\{u_{\alpha,n}(x,t)>\xi\}}$. Then $f_{\alpha,n}$ satisfies, for every $\varphi\in C_c^2(\mathbb T^N\times[0,T)\times\mathbb R)$,
\begin{align}
&\int_0^T \langle f_{\alpha,n}(t),\partial_t\varphi(t)\rangle\dd t+\langle f^0_{\alpha},\varphi(0)\rangle+\int_0^T\langle f_{\alpha,n}(t),a(\xi)\cdot\nabla_x\varphi(t)+\alpha\Delta_x\varphi(t)\rangle\dd t\\
&=-\sum_{k\geq1}\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}g_{k,\alpha}(x,u_{\alpha,n})\varphi(x,t,u_{\alpha,n})\dd x\dd\beta_k(t)\nonumber\\
&\quad-\frac{1}{2}\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{T}^N}G_\alpha^2(x,u_{\alpha,n})\partial_\xi\varphi(x,t,u_{\alpha,n})\dd x\dd t\nonumber\\
&\quad+q_{\alpha,n}(\partial_\xi\varphi)-\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}\varphi(x,t,\psi(x,t))
\dd\nu_{\alpha,n}(x,t),\qquad\text{a.s.},\nonumber
\end{align}
where $f^0_{\alpha}(x,\xi)=\one_{\{u^0_{\alpha}(x)>\xi\}}
$, $\nu_{\alpha,n}$ is defined by \eqref{rs-33} and $q_{\alpha,n}$ is defined by \eqref{eq:def-q-eta-epsilon}.","status":"unverified"}

