{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.317859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3307f466b6d5417e875239bdc08c0f6679e700c5a01b083e0d6ea98e0aef81a5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm3.3. of arXiv:2411.09005, 'On Time-Changed Linear Birth-Death Process with Immigration at Extinction'] The Laplace transforms of the state probabilities of TFLBPwI are given by
	\begin{equation}
		\tilde{\bar{p}}^\nu(n,z)=\begin{cases}
			\displaystyle \frac{z^{\nu-1}}{z^\nu+\alpha},\ n=0,\vspace{0.1cm}\\
			\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{n}\binom{n-1}{k-1}\frac{(-1)^{k}\alpha}{k\lambda-\alpha}\left(\frac{z^{\nu-1}}{z^\nu+k\lambda}-\frac{z^{\nu-1}}{z^\nu+\alpha}\right),\ n\ge1.
