{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:52:23.575556+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3345099fdcd068ac84d06d6dd120df1e20275adfc7965b0e746fd9c81f1a2cab","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma L:LX23cond of arXiv:2602.05317, 'Strong local nondeterminism for stochastic time-fractional\\ slow and fast diffusion equat'] Let $\alpha > 0$, $\beta \in (0, 2]$, $\gamma \ge 0$, $H \in [1/2, 1)$ and
  $\ell \in (0, 2d)$. Assume Dalang's condition
  (equation E:main of the paper), and suppose $\rho \in (0, 1)$ and $\theta \in (0, 1)$. Then
  the following estimates hold:
  \begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]

    \item If $\beta \in (0,1]$ and $\gamma \in [0,1-\beta]$, for any compact interval $I = [S, T]$ in $(0,
            \infty)$ and $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^d$, there exists a positive finite constant $C$
          such that for all $t, t' \in I$ and $a_0 := 1 \vee (1/S^\rho) \le a < b \le \infty$,
          \begin{align}
            \| v_1([a, b), t', x_0) - v(t', x_0) - v_1([a, b), t, x_0) + v(t, x_0) \|_{L^2}
            \le C \left( a^{\frac{1}{\rho} - 1} |t'-t| + b^{-1} \right)
          \end{align}
          and
          \begin{align}
            \|v_1([0,a_0),t',x_0)-v_1([0,a_0),t,x_0)\|_{L^2} \le C |t'-t|.
          \end{align}

    \item If $\beta \in (0,2]$ and $\gamma \ge 0$, for any compact rectangle $J$ in $\mathbb{R}^d$ and $t_0 > 0$, there exists
          a positive finite constant $C'$ such that for all $x, x' \in J$ and $0
            \le a < b \le \infty$,
          \begin{align}
            \| v_2([a, b), t_0, x) - v(t_0, x) - v_2([a, b), t_0, x') + v(t_0, x') \|_{L^2}
            \le C' \left( a^{\frac{1}{\theta} - 1} |x-x'| + b^{-1} \right).
          \end{align}

  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_334967a4fa2e2c8cae202682636a551ce5e1031587d6e5c21c9767afa796db15","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:covariances of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Recall the random variables $S_j^X(n), S_j^Y(n)$, and $S_j^Z(n)$, $j=0,1,\ldots,\ell$ just defined, and assume they satisfy~(equation eq:gdcondvars of the paper). Then  there is an $m\in \N$ depending only on  $\ell, N, (K_j)_{j=0}^\ell$, and $\alpha$, such that for 
