{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.578429+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_343706e890a8ea169cf3b54016dab239a55260d1cc5acc90a41680263be315a2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, and $p\in [1,2)$,
