              The  error terms are as in \Cref{rem:B80}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.252126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3490f9df2bf8a250e6b9eb89b9e6a7c92799476639111575e68fdc01c16c85a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let $x,y\in X$, $p\in[1,\infty]$, $C,t>0$, $r_2\geq r_1\geq 0$. Assume that for $z\in\{x,y\}$, all $\delta\in(0,1)$ and all $\omega\in\ell^\infty(X)$ we have
\[
\left(\fint_{t/2-\delta r_1^2}^{t/2+\delta r_1^2}\| {B_z(r_1)}P_\tau^\omega\|_{2,2p}^{2p}\drm \tau\right)^\frac{1}{p}
\leq C(z)\delta^{-\frac{n}{2}}(1+\delta r_2^2 h(\omega))^{\frac{n}{2}+1}\fint_{t/2-\delta r_2^2}^{t/2+\delta r_2^2}\| P_\tau^\omega\|_{2,2}^2\drm \tau.
\]
Then we have 
