{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.586405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34c9dbbc4f5ae5392631bda9161b662c80bf0089e0094b5b5f9a4871d0d2f2b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Prop.703 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] There exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $f_1,f_2\in L^\infty_{\rm loc}(\mathbb{R}_+;\mathbb{R})$ and $t\geq 0$,
