{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:26:52.671570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34f57eb7b3d2f2953e89ae88a9eae267477cd09b0d49d9ff4abf700f81a988e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 41 (Gauss--Chebyshev quadrature) of arXiv:2609.03736, '2609.03736'] For every $N\geq2$, there is, up to relabeling, exactly one positive
