{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.029766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3506bd4735b2c59d690a957360cfc5975b6dd32c224728f28d01dbc654118542","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[The 21 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let \( \phi\in\text{\rm SCL}(\T^n) \) and $H:\T^n\times\R^n\to\R$ be a Tonelli Hamiltonian. Then we have
