{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.580697+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3560bc9470c3ec3da06eab458884dca497062e261a0da5398c96be15af005566","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma-Marcus-n of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let $l\in\mathbb R$, $s\ge0$ and let (Hypo-Qi of the paper) hold. Let $\mathcal Q_{2,n}$ denote the regular approximation of  $\mathcal Q_2$ provided by Lemma (Lemma:Qn of the paper). Consider the following regularized Marcus flow
		\begin{equation}
			\wp_n(r)\triangleq  \wp_n(r,l,f),\quad  \frac{{\rm d}}{{\rm d}r}\wp_n(r)= l\cdot \mathcal Q_{2,n}\wp_n(r),\quad r\in[0,1],  \quad \wp_n(0) = f\in H^s.
		\end{equation}
		Let $C_{2,1} > 0$ and $C_{2,2} > 0$ be the constants introduced in  (Q-n cancel of the paper) of Lemma (Lemma:Qn of the paper). 
		Let $V\in \mathscr{V}$ $($see (equation SCRV of the paper)$)$.
		Define
		\begin{equation}
			V_s^{\wp_n,f}(r,l)\triangleq V(\|\wp_n(r,l, f)\|_{H^s}^2) - V(\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{H^s}^2),\quad r\in[0,1],\quad f\in H^{s}.
		\end{equation}
		Then we have that for $l\in\mathbb R$
		\begin{align}
			\sup_{n\ge1}\Abs{V_s^{\wp_n,f}(r,l)}
			\leq \left({\rm e}^{2C_{2,1}|l|r}-1\right) V(\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{H^s}^2),\quad r\in[0,1],

		\end{align}
		and
		\begin{align}
			\sup_{n\ge1}\left\{V_s^{\wp_n,f}(1,l)-2l\cdot V'(\|f\|^2_{H^s} )\bIP{\mathcal Q_{2,n}f,f}_{H^s}\right\}\leq \frac{C_{2,2}}{2C_{2,1}^2}\left({\rm e}^{2C_{2,1}|l|}-2C_{2,1}|l|-1\right)V(\|f\|^2_{H^s}).

		\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.726384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35614fd64a9079f6ba4eb919f4eadddac0dbfdb760d85d900859928cad997359","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:tightness_bdry_good_fl_refl of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] There exists $\zeta>0$ such that the following is true. Fix $M,p > 0$, $r \in (0,1)$, and suppose $\delta < r$. Let $h$ be a GFF on $r\mathbf{D}$ with boundary values as in Lemma~(le:reflected_fl_law of the paper). Let $\eta_1,\overline{\eta}_2$ be as defined in Lemma~(le:reflected_fl_law of the paper). Let $z_1 \in \partial B(0,r/2)$, $w_1 \in B(0,3r/16)$, and let $E_\delta$ denote the event that the following hold. 
Let $\eta_{z_1}$ be the flow line starting at $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(0,3r/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}$ be the flow line starting at $w_1$, reflected off $\eta_{z_1}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(0,r/4)$. Then
\begin{itemize}
 \item $\eta_{w_1}$ intersects the right side of $\eta_{z_1}$ with angle difference $0$ (before reflecting off), and they do not intersect in any other way.
 \item Let $U$ be the region bounded between $\eta_{w_1}, \eta_{z_1}$, and sample the internal metric in $U$. There exist $x,y \in \eta_{w_1} \cap \eta_{z_1}$ such that if $U_{x,y} \subseteq U$ denotes the region between $x$ and $y$, then $\mathrm{diam}(U_{x,y}) \le \delta$ and
\[ D_\epsilon^{\partial U_{x,y}} \ge \delta^\zeta+\epsilon^{a_0} . \]
 \item The angle $\pi$ flow line $\eta^{\pi}_{w_1}$ starting from $w_1$ exits $B(0,3r/4)$ without intersecting $\eta_{z_1}$.
 \item The conditional probability given $\eta_{z_1}$, $\eta_{w_1}$, $\eta^{\pi}_{w_1}$, $X_r^0$, $X_r^{\pi}$, and the values of $h$ on these sets is at least $p$ that
 \begin{itemize}
  \item $\eta_1$ merges into $\eta_{z_1}$ before entering $B(0,r/4)$.
  \item The continuation of $\eta^{\pi}_{w_1}$ does not intersect $\eta_1$ before it hits $\partial B(0,r)$.
 \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
Then
\[ \mathbf{P}[E_\delta] = o^\infty(\delta) \]
uniformly in the choice of $z_1,w_1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.373998+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3565522e035e4813da09a4f869b032735e67f651b75d5362e335948e9277db39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma maximizing first binomial coefficient of arXiv:2507.10294, 'Guessing Strategies for Shelf-Shuffling Machines'] We have
    \begin{equation}\max_{i\geq 1}\frac{\binom{i-1}{j-1}}{2^{i}}=\frac{\binom{2j-2}{j-1}}{2^{2j-1}}\end{equation}
    and this maximum is achieved if and only if $i=2j-1$ or $i=2j-2$.
    \begin{proof}
        Arguing as in the proof of Proposition $(middle terms strategy of the paper)$, we let 
            \[a_i=\frac{\binom{i-1}{j-1}}{2^i}\;\;\;\text{and}\;\;\;R_i=\frac{a_{i+1}}{a_i}=\frac{i}{2(i-j+1)}\]
        We observe that $R_i>1$ when $i<2j-2$, $R_i=1$ when $i=2j-2$, and $R_i<1$ when $i>2j-2$. A similar argument as in Proposition $(middle terms strategy of the paper)$ implies Equation $(maximum of first binomial coefficient of the paper)$.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.850937+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3572b9fd6590ade1303b223f6ead96c55484fb2a18e5b5192296e77159fcb886","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2511.11189, 'Sharp asymptotics for the maximal distance from the boundary to the nucleus of a typical P'] Let \(c\in\VO\) be a vertex of \(\CO\) determined by the points 0 and \(\m X_1,...,\m X_d\) of \(\Phi\), and let \(\Urm_0,...,\Urm_d \in\Sp_{\R^d}\), where \(\Sp_{\R^d}\) denotes the \((d-1)\)-dimensional unit sphere, be the unit vectors
		\begin{equation*}
			\Urm_0 = \frac{c}{\|c\|} \; , \; \Urm_i = \frac{\m X_i-c}{\|\m X_i-c\|}.
		\end{equation*}
		Then the vertex \(c\) is pointy if and only if
