{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.487970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3585f78f675a51fb316775abc75d0586b727aed90982fdd5f9335a2199bdea27","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Deff def:strong of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Fix $r \in [2,\infty), \theta \in \mathbb{R}$, a stopping time $\tau$, and assume $x \in L^p(\Omega;C([0,T];B))$. 
   We say a process $x_t$ is a strong solution in $\mathcal{B}_{\theta,r}$ to (equation eq:gefx of the paper) up to time $\tau$
    if for all $T > 0$:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item $\mathbb{E}[\int_0^{T\wedge \tau} \|x_t\|_{1+\theta, r} dt] < \infty$
        \item $F: B \to \mathcal{B}_{\theta, r}$ and $\mathbb{E}[\int_0^{T\wedge \tau} \|F(x_t)\|_{\theta,r} dt] < \infty$
        \item $G: B \to \gamma(\mathcal{U},\mathcal{B}_{\theta, r})$ and $\mathbb{E}[\int_0^{T\wedge\tau} \|G(x_t)\|_{\theta,r}^2dt] < \infty$
    \end{enumerate}
    (see (fractional-domains-deff of the paper) for the definition of the norms) and furthermore
    \begin{equation}
    x_{t \wedge \tau} = x_0 + \int_0^{t \wedge \tau} Ax_s + F(x_s)ds + \int_0^{t \wedge \tau} G(x_s)dW_s \,.    
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":["Rare events have positive probability","Polish state space for weak-convergence criterion","No assertion that the toy process is percolation"],"created_at":"2026-10-10T08:06:45.814101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_358a09f18cc575b995f83aeac9ef59b9d258fa8f4b9da339f3bfd50dc8c5cd1c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"AUTHOR-CHECKED; independent w346 audit PENDING. Unconditional convergence, even almost sure convergence, and an exact
