{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.571923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_35f2d932e6152d413c6096fceefed1a8b558196fae742f42726a435890f0a8ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 10 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d=3$. Assume that the critical exponent $\eta$ defined in \eqref{eq:def eta} exists. Then, for every $n\geq 1$,
