{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.256761+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37344a91d12f4e2f1e27ffc2602e99a486eea4e489c41acbb773fddbcbc7a17e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:loglogfail of arXiv:2609.04101, 'Endpoint Estimates for Stein's Purely Quadratic Carleson Operator'] Suppose $\Phi(t)=o(t \log_2 t)$. Then ${\mathcal C}_{2,\mathsf{lac}}$ does not satisfy a $\Phi$-modular estimate. In particular, for any $0 < \kappa < 1$, there exists an $f_\kappa$ so that
