{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.245905+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_375f065771792f4ef2f339056ccbb0a2a2ebb34655ba6ccb00e290d61b5befcc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm limiting profile_main thm of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $n=ml$, such that $m,l\ge 2$, and $l=\omega(1)$. Suppose 
$$t=\frac n2\left(\log n-\frac 12\log l+c\right),$$ 
where $c\in \mathbb{R}$ is an absolute constant. Then, we have 
$$d_{TV}(\sim_l\backslash P_{n}^{*t},\sim_l\backslash U_{\mathfrak{S}_n})=\begin{cases}
