{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.493856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_37c7662d1aa3827a31cff621947d3309b9299efde1644721879606f9780865db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 17 of arXiv:2512.02538, 'On the spectral geometry of Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $N(\lambda) = \sum_{n=0}^\infty 1_{\{\lambda_n \le \lambda\}}$ denote the eigenvalue counting function. Then 
