{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.304865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_380d6e60d54047628ca0d13535e1d70a265bc7a8aebcd7eb435427c204dd345a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:linear_seat of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\eta \in \Omega$. Then, for any $k \in {\mathbb{N}}$ and $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, we have
                    \begin{align}
                        \zeta_{k}\left(T\eta, i +  k + o_{k}\left(\eta\right) \right) = \zeta_{k}\left(\eta, i \right),
                    \end{align}
                where the offset $o_{k}\left(\eta\right)$ is given by 
                    \begin{align}
                        &o_{k}\left(\eta\right) \\
                        &:= s_{\infty}\left(\eta,0\right) - s_{\infty}\left( T\eta,0\right) + 2\sum_{y = s_{\infty}\left(0\right)+ 1}^{0} \sum_{\ell = 1}^{k}  \eta^{\downarrow}_{\ell}\left(y\right) - 2\sum_{y = Ts_{\infty}\left(0\right)+1}^{0}\sum_{\ell = 1}^{k}  T\eta^{\uparrow}_{\ell}\left(y\right).
                    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

