{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.239417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3963626c33799d25cc138ac9f4bece78afadd78631b84b28c5bcf7d6180cf692","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: good paths prop of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] For $F \subset \mathbb{T}_N$, we say a path collection $\mathcal{A} \subset \Omega_{T_3}$ is $(F,\varepsilon,M_0)$-good if for all $\omega \in \mathcal{A}$,
    \begin{subequations}

        \begin{gather}

            \mathbb{T}_N \setminus F \subset \omega[0,T_3];\\

            \boldsymbol{r}_{x}(\omega) \leq l_N \text{ for all } x \in  \mathcal{L}_{F}^{\beta_N}(\omega);\\

            2d\cdot\mathsf{Mdist}\big(\mathcal{L}_{F}^{\beta_N}(\omega)\big)\leq J(F,M_0),
        \end{gather}
    \end{subequations}
    where 
\begin{equation}

        J(F,M_0)\overset{\rm def.}{=} 2d M_0\cdot|F|N^{-d\gamma}.
    \end{equation}
