{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.284575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_39eb8463caa73203ff89a7c03537758d8a4a65a99d8f0dd0662308c3a7b24f8e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Complex array normal distribution) of arXiv:2608.21551, '\bf Sparse Separable Factor Analysis in the Complex Domain with an Application to Local Fi'] Let $\Mcal\in\CC^{c_1\times\cdots\times c_d}$, and let $\Vb_j\in\CC^{c_j\times c_j}$ be Hermitian positive definite for $j=1,\ldots,d$. A $d$-mode array $\Ycal$ follows a proper complex array normal distribution with mean $\Mcal$ and mode-specific covariance matrices $\Vb_1,\ldots,\Vb_d$ if
