{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.889548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a11b1ed99f69132c82af2ff706ba12aee48257533b9f05f63d98df52d30dae3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 21 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] Let $ V=(Y,C,\tau,H)$ be a stochastic infinitesimal transformation. Then $ V$ is an infinitesimal symmetry of $ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ if and only if $ V$ generates a one-parameter group on $ M$ and the following conditions hold:
\begin{equation}
    Y(\mu) - L(Y)  - \sigma  H + \tau \mu=0, \ \ \ \ \  [Y, \sigma] + \frac{1}{2} \tau \sigma + \sigma C=0.
\end{equation}
where $\ [Y, \sigma]^i_{\alpha}=Y(\sigma^i_{\alpha}) - \partial_k(Y^i)\sigma^k_{\alpha}= Y^k \partial_k (\sigma^i_{\alpha}) - \partial_k(Y^i)\sigma^k_{\alpha}. $","status":"unverified"}

