{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.651212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3a8079e8d61ebb4cf36a4daf6fb2fec14229afc54b8295ceae9cb24e1469afa2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop bdy-expect of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$. Let $D$ be a bounded, simply connected domain. Fix any $A\subseteq \partial D$ to be a (deterministic) closed subset of the boundary such that $\dim_M(A)<2-\alpha^2/2$. 
