{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.030322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3aff7bcc49dc63640e90becc2f39214e2cbb1f952ec94e980d5dec3740941756","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[The 27 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $H$ be a Tonelli Hamiltonian on $\T^n$, $\phi\in\SCL(\T^n)$, and $u$ be the viscosity solution of \eqref{eq:HJephi pre}. Then there exist $C_1>0$ and $C_2>0$ (depending on the local $C^2$ modulus and the Tonelli modulus of $H$ and the Lipschitz and semiconcavity constants of $\phi$) such that for any $(u,H)$-calibrated curve $\gamma:[0,T]\to\T^n$ and $(u,H)$-generalized characteristic $\xi:[0,t]\to\T^n$ satisfying \eqref{eq:GC} with $0\leqslant t<T$,
	\begin{equation}
		e^{-C_1 T}(T-t)^{C_2}\cdot d(\xi(0),\gamma(0))\leqslant d(\xi(t),\gamma(t))\leqslant e^{C_1 T}(T-t)^{-C_2} \cdot d(\xi(0),\gamma(0)).
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.133759+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b009db225d1035df7fd73eb4b956d2e9e7e466dfe16b1c25609526ec5e54bd1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.10515, 'Limiting Law of Local Fields for the Mean Field Ghatak-Sherrington Model'] Let $\beta\le \beta_0$ and $h,D\in\R$. Let $U:\R\to\R$ be smooth, with derivatives of moderate growth. For a cavity field $l$ and $r=\langle l\rangle$, with Gaussian reference variance $p-q$, we have, for every positive integer $k$,
\begin{equation}
  \E\left[\frac{\langle U(l)W(\beta l+h)\rangle}{\langle W(\beta l+h)\rangle}
  -\frac{\E_\xi[U(\xi+r)W(\beta(\xi+r)+h)]}{\Wtil(\beta r+h)}\right]^{2k}\le \frac{K}{N^k}.
\end{equation}
Here $K$ is uniform over the system size and over $0<\beta\le\beta_0$, by the uniformity of \eqref{eq:known-overlap-estimate}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.366169+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b029b52dceac2ed157f29829bb86800d7644e162026c37157c139317f335c9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 32 of arXiv:2506.20146, 'Parabolic Anderson Model in the Hyperbolic Space. Part I: Annealed Asymptotics'] For each $R>0,$ one has
