{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.252530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b1ffbee6e86e6129af742aa114bb95e9df65f98788df15d551ed7f65c2cba34","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 76 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any point $z \in \mathfrak{X}$ and integer $m \in [0, (q-q') / u(z)]$, the following two statements hold w.o.p., for each $t \in [\mathsf{t}'+mN^{10K\delta+2} u(z), N^5]$. First,
