{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.471946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c5c315d62e6a44d3585473a34b6bc31702c9ff8011bcffe302f3d54e958d6a4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 107 (Quasilinear system satisfied by $Z\ubar$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\newuL$ be the vectorfield defined in \eqref{E:DOUBLENULLEIKONALFUNCTIONNORMALIZEDNULLVECTORFIELDS}. If $\ubar$ is a solution to the eikonal equation $(\gfour^{-1})^{\alpha\beta} \p_\alpha \ubar \p_\beta \ubar = 0$ with $\Lunit \ubar > 0$, then the scalar functions $\Lunit \ubar, \, \muX \ubar,  \, \geop{x^A} \ubar$ solve the following quasilinear system of equations for $A =2,3$:
