{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.267468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3cffa2d205bcc93e5253a91db04a6ce39e8f2abe094297349c7326dee44afead","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma qstabilitywedge of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp Suppose {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}:[0,\infty)\times\Z\to\R$} satisfies the following \abbr{SDE}, where {\small$\mathscr{T}_{N}$} is from Proposition (prop:s-sde of the paper):

\begin{align}
\d\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}=\mathscr{T}_{N}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}\d\t+\sqrt{2}\lambda N^{\frac12}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,\x}\d\mathbf{b}_{\t,\x}.
\end{align}

Suppose also that the initial data is non-negative, possibly random, and satisfies the deterministic bounds

\begin{align}
\sup_{\x\in\Z}\mathrm{e}^{\t\mathscr{T}_{N}}[\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\cdot}]_{\x}\lesssim\t^{-1/2}\quad\mathrm{and}\quad N^{-1}\sum_{\x\in\Z}\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\x}\lesssim1.
\end{align}

Next, suppose that for any {\small$\t>0$} fixed, the function {\small$\X\mapsto\mathrm{e}^{\t\mathscr{T}_{N}}[\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{0,\cdot}]_{N\X}$} converges uniformly in {\small$\X\in\R$} to {\small$\mathbf{H}_{0,\t,\X,0}$}. Then, there exists a coupling between {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}$} and the narrow-wedge solution {\small$\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{nw}}$} to (equation eq:she of the paper) so that for any fixed and small {\small$\tau>0$}, we have {\small$\wt{\mathbf{Q}}^{N}_{\t,N\X}-\mathbf{Z}^{\mathrm{nw}}_{\t,N\X}\to0$} locally uniformly on {\small$[\tau,1]\times\R$} in probability.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:12:13.584569+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d0813fb3f64e977879324b839f9470e662790711cc632d05e481ece5d0049fd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 37 (Propagation of $T_2$ for the nonlinear law) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target}, \ref{ass:W2}, and
