{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.487602+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d58558ae9d7c96154cacd498f8f2a179a8f5cbc7d3201cbce65b75af3778d43","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 11 of arXiv:2607.03360, 'Smoluchowski-Kramers Approximation Meets Khasminskii Averaging Principles in Nonequilibriu'] Let the function $u$ and $f$ be continuous on the interval $[0,1]$ and let the function $\CK$ be continuous and non-negative on the triangle $0\leq s \leq t \leq 1$. If 
\beq{eq-uf}
u(t)\leq f(t)+ \int_0^t \CK(t,s) u(s)ds, \quad 0\leq t\leq 1,
\eeq
then 
\beq{gron-uf}
u(t) \leq f(t)+ \int_0^t \CH(t,s)f(s)ds, \quad 0\leq t \leq 1,
\eeq
where 
$\CH(t,s)=\sum_{n=1}^\infty \CK^{*,n}(t,s), 0\leq s \leq t \leq 1$, is the resolvent kernel, and the $\CK_n\,(n=1,2,\dots)$ are the iterated kernels of $\CK$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.187399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d5d197deb94815face0bbb7b9cc94764763d14c3c75b5b1c3641ad3f1d349df","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 133 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] If  
