{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.465568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d774df6045a1a14d95509cddf48adc823d684a20bc2c1ebb6877a25d98ef001","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that \eqref{t1-2-1} holds for some $\beta>0$. Let $\Upsilon_\e^2 f(x,y)$ be defined in \eqref{e3-3a}. Then there exists a positive constant $C_4:=C_4(\beta)$ such that for every $f\in \M_\beta$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
