where the supremum is over the real Hilbert space $L^2(\mu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.028334+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3db3177217f60dc6815e4b25383472a12a41a46ecd2e87564146a8605ce81988","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:legendre of arXiv:2607.29330, 'Large deviations for the maximum of\\ the generalized TAP free energy'] Fix a regular \(f\in(f_{\mathrm{eq}},f_1)\). Let \(\theta_f\in(0,1)\) be the
		unique minimizer defining \(\Sigma(f)\), let \(\zeta_f\) be the
		corresponding constrained Parisi minimizer, and let \(q_f\) be its first
		positive contact point. Let \(X^f\) be the Auffinger--Chen process
		associated with \(\zeta_f\). Assume the strict Plefka condition
		\begin{equation}
			1-\xi''(q_f)\mathbb{E}\left[
			\left(
			\partial_{xx}\Phi_{\zeta_f}(q_f,X^f_{q_f})
			\right)^2
			\right]>0.
		\end{equation}
		Then
		\begin{equation}
			\begin{aligned}
				\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\liminf_{N\to\infty}
				\frac1N\log\mathbb{P}\bigl(\mathcal E_{N,\varepsilon}(f)\bigr)
				&=
				\lim_{\varepsilon\downarrow0}\limsup_{N\to\infty}
				\frac1N\log\mathbb{P}\bigl(\mathcal E_{N,\varepsilon}(f)\bigr)\\
				&=
				\Sigma(f)
				=
				\inf_{\theta\in(0,1)}
				\bigl[\Lambda(\theta)-\theta f\bigr].
			\end{aligned}
		\end{equation}
		Moreover,
		\begin{equation}
			\lim_{N\to\infty}
			\frac1N
			\log
			\mathbb{E}\exp\left\{
			\theta_f\max_{\mathbf{m}\in[-1,1]^N}F_{\mathrm{TAP}}(\mathbf{m})
			\right\}
			=
			\Lambda(\theta_f).
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.338010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dbfc9dfbb134d126ce4f19ad7767e94292ddbbfbc4ef08bf125350c21756ca9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 3 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] Let $u\in \R$. 
For functions $F=F(\eta)$ and $G=G(\eta) \in C^2(\R^N)$, if all integrals
in the following converge, we have
\begin{align*} 
 \int_{\R^N} GL_0F d\mu_u & = \int_{\R^N} FL_0G d\mu_u  \\
& = -\frac12 \int_{\R^N} \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \partial_{\eta(x)} -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} \big) F \cdot
\big( \partial_{\eta(x)} -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} \big) G\, d\mu_u, \\
\int_{\R^N} G L_1 F d\mu_u &= -\int_{\R^N} F L_1 G d\mu_u.
\end{align*}
For the carr\'e du champ of the $\eta$-process, we have
\begin{align} 
\Ga(F)  = \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \partial_{\eta(x)} F -\partial_{\eta(x-1)} F \big)^2 
= \sum_{x\in \T_N} \big( \nabla^*D_\eta F(x) \big)^2 
=: |\nabla_{\T_N}^* D_\eta F|^2,
\end{align}
recall Remark \ref{rem:1.3} for $\nabla^*$ and $D_\eta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.726474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dc23fa18b93b834a40104051a508ed7c4002954c8b7848251e01a5e9895fd7c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2609.01190, 'Rough differential equations on manifolds via natural bundles'] There exist constants $\delta\in (0,1)$ and $L\in (0,\infty)$ such that for every interval $[U,V]\subseteq [S,T]$, we have 
