{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.041200+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dc95d41d678e42859c1fbd1642c24f2d813c9043dc03cf8348e20544490c422","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 42 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] For any Borel $g\geq0$, $\rho\leq\rho_{b}$ and $\cF_{\tau}$-measurable $\bR^{d}$-valued $y$
