{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.755669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e04b01f644bc1c8fc3529d1b74dc6b65634fefdc501eb1db0d39608256bde54","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:abstract-simple-response of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] If $\Lambda_n^\mu$ is simple, then for every $f\inH_{\mathrm{reg}}$ the two one-sided
