    with $C_{\gamma,\delta}$ being a normalizing constant corresponding to the sum over $k\in\mathbb Z$ of the exponential term. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.860287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e181a9e6bb9be23c4a1d5a3749abe739f5b3cd7af84074e15406da29d7c82c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Fix $\chi \in[0,1]$ and $A$ satisfying~\eqref{A_assumptions}.  Let $u$ be a solution to~\eqref{main_eq} with ``steep initial data'' $u_0$ 
