{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.561355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ecd505ebcf17fbb6ca064baa0dca0592f331b02bdc3be57c5d2249d3b8f2d4f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $m\in \N$. Let $a,b\in \R\cup\{\pm \infty\}$, with $a<b$, and let $F:(a,b]\to \R_+$ be a continuous, non-decreasing function such that $\lim_{r\to a^+}F(r)=0$. Let $\lambda_i\in (0,1)$ satisfy $\sum_{i=1}^m\lambda_i=1$ and set $\lambda=(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_m)$. 

