    Moreover, $\KM^\nu \deq \lim_{t\searrow 0} \KM^\nu_{t\gets}$ exists in $L^2(\gamma)$, and $(\KM^\nu)_\sharp \gamma = \nu$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.658019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f0bfef9abe0bc23ce5ea3bc91e1c70ddb236f7e0d4ed058131874160e508ff2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:recursion of arXiv:2608.24830, 'Motion helps the contact process: survival below\\ the percolation threshold on Poisson Br'] Let $s\in(0,s_\ast)$, $\theta_\ast:=\tfrac d2-2s-\tfrac{2sd}\kappa>0$ and $\mathsf N:=(d+2)^2$. There
