{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.963197+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40f15d7a8c392bc0a1cf2355ab10dea66c7f3894e4dd5b411b9fe003448240ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lvl_sets_kendall_williamson of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C$ be a $d$-dimensional Archimedean copula with generator $\psi$ and Williamson measure $\gamma$. 
