{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.488912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40f6f7a7df34f0f546e2e919c5fc48a4ec4e1c378c4d4eb56ced5f503e100582","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm of arXiv:2505.14762, 'Multiple radial SLE($\kappa$) and quantum Calogero-Sutherland system'] Under the neutrality condition $\int \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+}+ \int \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}=-2$ , the value of the differential $C_{\mathbb{H}}\left[\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{+}, \boldsymbol{\sigma}^{-}\right]$ in the identity chart of $\mathbb{H}$ (and the chart $z \mapsto-1 / z$ at infinity) is given by

