{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:48:49.895925+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4106b5eb61b10c8d362f00d32d9ff6a246d0aff664cfc6ccefba4d7e05607e36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo steeptheo2 of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] With the notation above:

(1) The limit
\begin{equation}
\lim_{N\to \infty}G^{(0,-p)}_{\lambda(N)}(\mathbf z, 1^{N-n})N^{\frac d2}\prod_{i=1}^k\frac{(\tilde \chi_i+p)^{\lambda(N)'_i}}{(1+\tilde \chi_i)^N}
\end{equation}
does not depend on $\lambda(N)'_i$ with $\beta_i<p$. When $\beta_i<p$ for all $i$ the limit above is $1$.

(2) When $\beta_1,\dots, \beta_k>p$:
\begin{equation}
G^{(0,-p)}_{\lambda(N)}(\mathbf z, 1^{N-n})N^{\frac d2}\prod_{i=1}^k\frac{(\tilde \chi_i+p)^{\lambda(N)'_i}}{(1+\tilde \chi_i)^N}\to
Z\ (2\pi)^{-\frac{k}{2}}\prod_{i=1}^{k}\frac{e^{-\frac{y_i^2}{2}}}{\sqrt{\beta_i(1-\beta_i)}}\prod_{\substack{i<j\\\beta_i=\beta_j}}\frac{y_i-y_j}{\sqrt{\beta_i(1-\beta_i)}}\prod_{i=1}^n\Phi^{\varnothing, \mathcal B}(z_i),
\end{equation}
where
$$
 Z=\frac{\prod_{\chi} (\chi+p)^{\binom{m(\chi)+1}{2}}\prod_{\substack {i<j:\\ \chi_i>\chi_j}}(\chi_i-\chi_j) }{\prod_{i=1}^k\chi_i^{k-i+1}},\qquad \Phi^{\varnothing, \mathcal B}(z)=\prod_{i=1}^k\left(1+\frac{\beta_i-p}{1-p}(z-1)\right)  .
$$
Moreover, this convergence is uniform over sequences $(\lambda(N))_N$ such that $\mathbf y\in C$ for a compact subset $C\subset\mathbb R^k$ and $\lambda(N)'_i-N\beta_i-\sqrt{N\beta_i(1-\beta_i)}y_i$ are bounded by a uniform constant $M$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.861095+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_410af355301edd6f4434bc61cd5a37942f7f5f9ce52ad3a1af98119534c78807","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Let $0 < s < t$. Then, under the assumptions of \Cref{main_result_theorem},
