{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.308394+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4163a991e1d16dd60dca29b8545ae8cf967b213262c786dc05927acbd6744d13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:st_cor_3 of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] Suppose that $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}$ and ${\mathbb{E}}_{\nu_\mathbf{q}}\left[ {s_{\infty}\left(1\right)}^2 \right] < \infty$. Then for any $k, \ell \in {\mathbb{N}}$ with $k < \ell$ and $u, v \in {\mathbb{R}}$, we have 
                \begin{align}
                    &\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{1}{n} \sigma^{\left( \left\lfloor n u \right\rfloor \right)}_{k,\ell}\left({\eta}, 0\right) = f_{k,\ell}\left(\mathbf{q}, u\right), \quad \nu_{\mathbf{q}}\text{-a.s.,} \\
                    &\varlimsup_{L \to \infty} \varlimsup_{n \to \infty}\nu_{\mathbf{q}}\left( \left| \frac{1}{n} \sigma^{\left( \left\lfloor n u \right\rfloor \right)}_{k,\ell}\left(0\right) - f_{k,\ell}\left(\mathbf{q}, u\right) \right| > \frac{L}{\sqrt{n}} \right) = 0 ,
