{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.318019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_433d0297f0f5464c2eb7e165760648f0d4abe3d668c6c269d8bc75298f7a49e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 2 of arXiv:2609.01498, 'A Tight Erd\H{o}s-Stone Bound for All Graph Densities'] For every $r \ge 2$, $0 < \epsilon < 1/r$ and every $n>n_0(r,\epsilon)$ we have
