{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.889690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4340ed40fe31beac2d28368d20ed5615fa65dc086bb319ac93032a29ef89e4e3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Teorema 23 of arXiv:2506.11937, 'Random rotational invariance of integration by parts formulas within a Bismut-type approac'] A stochastic symmetry $\ T=(\Phi, B,\eta,h) \in S_m(M)$ is a $\mathcal{G}-$weak symmetry of $\ SDE_{\mu,\sigma}$ if and only if
