        \liminf_{t\uparrow+\infty,x\in M} \frac{\ln \mathbb{E}[\abs{u(t,x)}^p]}{t}\geq p\max\left(\sup_{0<r<+\infty}Q(r),C\right).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.681893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44027ead73a2e572e2426cc8715a7b5970d91f9505bd78d263e8727bdfd0278d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition c:cltsharp of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] Let \(\mathcal{P}\) be a simple, stationary point process on \(\mathbb{R}^d\) with summable exponential mixing correlations as in Definition (def.A2 of the paper), and assume that the (reduced) Palm intensity function of the ground process \(\mathcal{P}\) is bounded at all orders, as specified at (equation bdedreduced of the paper). Let \(\Psi = \Psi(\cdot)\) be a stabilizing interaction graph on finite windows with respect to \(\mathcal{P}\) as per Definition~(d:stabilizing-graph of the paper),
