{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.871436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_442cfd2c4696c2e44b0e99ab2685ff07eec5a78f7296cc0193b8b3e024905abe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:dr-current of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] [DR] Let $T_1=\vec{T_1} \norm{T_1}, \ldots, T_n= \vec{T_n} \norm{T_n}$ be one-dimensional normal currents on $\mathbb{R}^n$ such that there exists a positive Radon measure $\nu$ on $\mathbb{R}^n$ with the following properties:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item $\nu \ll \norm{T_i}$ for $i=1,\ldots,n$;
			\item For $\nu$-a.e.~$x \in \mathbb{R}^n$, $\operatorname{span}\{\vec{T_1}(x),\ldots,\vec{T_n}(x)\}=\mathbb{R}^n$.
		\end{enumerate}
		Then $\nu \ll \mathcal{L}_n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.238336+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_442e40f054ac97c27dcfeb4fb024db38a398cb87eeddf51355a94a6eb698fabc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 119 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] Let $\pi$ be a separable representation of $\G$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[a.] If $\pi$ is cyclic and disjoint from $\l$, and if $\rmh^0(\pi) > -\infty$, then for every $\eps > 0$ there is a representation $\rho$ on $H_\pi\oplus H_\l$ such that $\rho \simeq \l$ and
\begin{equation}
\sum_{s \in S\cup S^{-1}}\|(\pi\oplus \l)(s) - \rho(s)\|^2_{\rm{HS}} \le 4(\eps - \rmh^0(\pi)).
\end{equation}
\item[b.] If $\rmh^0(\pi) > -\infty$, then $\pi$ is contained in a Hilbert--Schmidt perturbation of an inflation of $\l$.
\item[c.] If $\rmh^0(\pi) = 0$, then $\pi \lesssim_{\rm{a}} \l$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.899076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44319ea02144e817dacde28298befb92ed00a478435b9b675a100ed11d142f1b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Rank-uniform integer-valued coefficients) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every zero-framed knot $K$, there is a unique sequence
$G_k(K;A,q)\in\Z[A^{\pm1},q^{\pm1}]$, $k\ge1$, such that
\begin{equation}
 \HH_r(K;A,q)
 =1+\sum_{k=1}^{r}
 \qbinom{r}{k}\{r+k-1;A\}_k\{-1;A\}G_k(K;A,q)
 \qquad(r\ge0).
\end{equation}
Set
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf H_0(K;A,q)=1,\qquad
 \mathsf H_k(K;A,q)=\frac{\{-1;A\}G_k(K;A,q)}{\{k\}!}
 \quad(k\ge1).
\end{equation}
Then, for every $k\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf H_k(K;A,q)\in\mathscr I_q^{\ge2},\qquad
 \mathsf H_k(K;q^n,q)=H_k^{(n)}(K;q)
 \quad(n\ge2).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.246004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_443bbb66476143868e9a5f3591c5cb1f29f9797db8379b0cea2f18e01874e2db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] Let  $C,r_0>0$ and $n>2$ and assume that, for all $B(r)\subset  X$, $r\geq r_0$, and all $U\subset B(r)$, we have the Faber-Krahn inequality
\begin{equation*}
