{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.087535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_444a0fe37e5eb79c2ddc4f4828869c886ff6cea71217c819c966fdc5bbf5aba4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lm:conv_sigma of arXiv:2606.12143, 'Continuous stochastic flows driven by white noise and their duals'] Fix $(a,r)\in{\mathbb R}^2$ and assume that the coefficients $(\sigma_n,b_n)_{n \ge 1}$ and $(\sigma,b)$ satisfy the conditions in Proposition~(thm:conv_appro_1 of the paper). Suppose further that, almost surely, $\mathcal W^n \to \hat{\mathcal W}$ in $H^{-d}_{\mathrm{loc}}({\mathbb R}^2)$ and $X^n \to X$ in $C([r,\infty))$, where $X^n$ is the unique strong solution to
