{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.200658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44eaca47247d885b1f17e694b9f1e3de3f8c127d9ccc07cdae7e9a0c60ecf667","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:growth-bound-partition-functions of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] For any $A', B'$ in $Q$, we have
