{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.799985+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_452992e70e1bddd8184061919d43ccdc14c87f46a76e30e4771e233bb6909bdf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:six-observables of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] With $u_k := v_k$ the normalized power-iteration vector of (sec:power-iteration of the paper) and $\rho_k := E_{k+1}/E_k$ the energy retention ratio of (thm:observable-variance of the paper), define
\begin{align*}
G_k &:= \|u_k - \operatorname{sign}(c_2)\phi_2\|_\pi^2, & &\text{(geometric/iterate error)}\\
I_k &:= 1 - \langle u_k, \phi_2\rangle_\pi, & &\text{(direction deficit)}\\
R_k &:= \langle u_k, P u_k\rangle_\pi - \lambda_2, & &\text{(Rayleigh quotient error)}\\
