{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.202357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4572de5b73ecb3b6e06bf48130f3c919409b7f24a37e82194a01fffe05cb8612","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:gradphi-large-deviations of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] There exists a constant $C=C(p)>0$ such that the following holds for any domain $V$ that contains $\ensuremath{\mathcal B}_R(o)$, where $R = Ch^{p-1}$ for $1 < p < 2$ and $R = Ch$ for $2 < p < \infty$. Let $z$ be such that $\ensuremath{\mathcal B}_{R+1}(z) \subset V$. Then there exist absolute constants $c_0,c_1,c_2,c_3,c_4>0$ such that
    \begin{align}
		\exp\Big[-c_0 \beta h^{(p-1)\,\wedge\, 1}\Big] \leq \frac{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h)}{{\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h-1)} &\leq \exp\Big[-c_1 \beta h^{(p-1)\,\wedge\, 1}\Big]\,,\\
		\exp\Big[-c_2 \beta h^{p \,\wedge\, 2}\Big] \leq {\widehat\pi}^{(p)}_V(\phi_o = h) &\leq \exp\Big[-c_3\beta h^{p \,\wedge\, 2}\Big]\,,\\        
