{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.121192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45b385ec124cbb072e2ee46c767492878cf90f37edb7ab89296217e96e044307","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cancellation-of-excellent-clusters in cle of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] For any boundary condition $\xi\in\hat\Sigma_i$, we have
\begin{equation}
\langle R\sigma^I\rangle_{\Lambda_M}^\xi=\langle \mathbf 1_{\mathtt{NoEx}} R\sigma^I\rangle_{\overline{\Lambda_M}}^\xi,\quad
\langle S\sigma^I\rangle_{\Lambda_M}^\xi=\langle \mathbf 1_{\mathtt{NoEx}} S\sigma^I\rangle_{\overline{\Lambda_M}}^\xi.
\end{equation}
Here, the subscript $\overline{\Lambda_M}$ indicates that the expectation is taken with respect to the extended Ising measure. Moreover, on the left-hand side, the quantities $R\sigma^I$ and $S\sigma^I$ depend only on the spin configuration, so it is equivalent to work with the classical Ising measure. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.056386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45c354abbbe46359cb61e9746f359d01fd059107cf0b59af8150a2a83c18f96e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:positive-time-local-density-equivalence of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Under Assumption~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper), there is a function
$\varrho\in C((0,T]\times\mathbb R^d)$, locally H\"older continuous on $Q$, such
that
\begin{equation*}
 \mu_t(\,\mathrm d x)=\varrho(t,x)\,\mathrm d x,
 \qquad \varrho(t,x)>0,
 \qquad (t,x)\in(0,T]\times\mathbb R^d.
\end{equation*}
For every $0<\varepsilon<T$ and $K\Subset\mathbb R^d$,
\begin{equation}
 0<\inf_{(t,x)\in[\varepsilon,T]\times K}\varrho(t,x)
 \leq\sup_{(t,x)\in[\varepsilon,T]\times K}\varrho(t,x)<\infty.

\end{equation}
Consequently, Lebesgue measure and the occupation measure $\mathfrak m$ are
locally equivalent on every positive-time cylinder.","status":"unverified"}

