{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.365933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46246f7b06ff1fa5ed38da46021a999d0659a00a95b940e917b79a84fc631a49","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:moment variance X of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] For $u_1 , u_2 \in \{0,\ldots,M\}$ and $k\in \N$ with $M+1 \leq e^{k^2}$ and $n \geq e^{(k+1)k^2}$,  define the random variable 
    \begin{align*}
        X_k(u_1, u_2) = \frac{1}{k} \sum_{j=1}^{k} \frac{1}{k^2} \left( U_{jk^2,(j+1)k^2}^{T_n^1}(u_1) - U_{jk^2,(j+1)k^2}^{T_n^2}(u_2) \right)^2.
    \end{align*}
    Then, for each fixed $\varepsilon > 0$ and for $k$ large enough,
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E} \left[ X_k(u_1,u_2)\right] \in \left( 2\left(1 - \alpha \mathbbm{1}_{u_1 = u_2}\right) - \frac{\varepsilon}{10}, 2\left(1 - \alpha \mathbbm{1}_{u_1 = u_2}\right) + \frac{\varepsilon}{10} \right)
    \end{equation}
    and
    \begin{equation}
        \Var \left( X_k(u_1,u_2) \right) \leq \frac{\Bar{C}}{k} 
    \end{equation}
    for some $\Bar{C} < \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4624a49b4e9c31de8fd9f978485bf4a729871bc69e5d192b6df61aa3dbcdfd13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Ikeda-Watanabe of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\geqslant 0}$ be a Feller process defined on a locally compact separable metric space $(M,d)$. Assume that there exists a positive kernel $\Pi(x,E)$, $x\in M$, $E\in\mathcal{B}(M)$ such that 
	\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
		\item  $\Pi(x,E)<\infty$ if $d(x,E)>0$, 
		\item  for any bounded $f\in C(M)$ and a bounded open set $D$ with $d(D,\operatorname{supp}(f))>0$, 
		\begin{align*}
			\frac{P_t f(x)}{t} \mbox{ is uniformly bounded in $x\in D$, $t>0$},
		\end{align*}
		and 
		$\lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{P_t f(x)}{t}=\int_M f(y)\Pi(x,dy)$ for every $x\in D$,
	\end{enumerate}
	then for any open set $\Omega\subset M$, $E\in\mathcal{B}(M)$ satisfying $d(E,\Omega)>0$, and $\lambda>0$,
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{E}_x\left[e^{-\lambda \tau_\Omega}, X_{\tau_\Omega}\in E\right]=\int_\Omega G^\lambda_\Omega(x, dy)\Pi(y,E),
	\end{align}
	where $G^\lambda_\Omega(x,E)=\int_0^\infty e^{-\lambda s} p_\Omega(s,x,E)ds$. Therefore, the joint distribution of $(\tau_\Omega, X_{\tau_\Omega})$ on the event $\{X_{\tau_\Omega}\neq X_{\tau_\Omega -}\}$ is given by 
	\begin{align*}
		\mathbb{P}_x\left(\tau_\Omega\in ds, X_{\tau_\Omega}\in dz\right)=\int_\Omega p_\Omega(s,x,dy)\Pi(y, dz).
	\end{align*} 
	Moreover, (equation eq:Laplace_transform of the paper) holds for $\lambda=0$ if $\mathbb{E}_x[\tau_D]<\infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.823209+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_462b309ef91106e371f1daa52f7dfc2d987997f9deec7d075a161881e26a9862","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm intro local curve GW g formula of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] Suppose that $\mathsf{T}$ acts on the fibers of the local curve $Z$ with weights $\epsilon_2,\ldots,\epsilon_5$ satisfying the Calabi--Yau condition $\sum_i \epsilon_i=0$. If (conj:GW:vertex of the paper) holds for $n=1$, then
