{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.713187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_465b64ec4c977ae648880fcb5b09df14bd760c7ba9d07e3734ac1cfa11171d31","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For the grids of Proposition~\ref{prop:dyadic-grid-diagonal}, define
\begin{equation}
  \Lambda_{n,k}:=\{h_n(j-k):0\leq j\leq M_n\},
  \qquad 0\leq k\leq M_n,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  Q_{n,k}:=\mathcal L\left(
    B\,\middle|\, B_t\leq0\text{ for every }t\in\Lambda_{n,k}
  \right),
  \qquad
  p_{n,k}:=\PP(B_t\leq0:t\in\Lambda_{n,k}).

\end{equation}
Then
\(p_{n,k}=\PP(K_n=k)>0\),
\(\sum_{k=0}^{M_n}p_{n,k}=1\), and
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal L(\Xi_n^{\mathrm{grid}})
  =\sum_{k=0}^{M_n}p_{n,k}Q_{n,k}.

\end{equation}
Write
\begin{equation}
  L_{n,k}^-=h_nk,
  \qquad L_{n,k}^+=h_n(M_n-k).

\end{equation}
For \(0<k<M_n\), the component \(Q_{n,k}\) is
\(Q_{h_n,L_{n,k}^-,L_{n,k}^+}\) from \eqref{eq:pure-wall-law}.  The endpoint
components \(k=0,M_n\) retain their direct conditional definitions in
\eqref{eq:mixture-components}; they are full-path laws constrained on only
one side of the pin and are not covered by the positive-two-horizon
definition \eqref{eq:pure-wall-law}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.669135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_465dfe668d55d5b291312dbb1aa45833c618103dfc18013a966da73fc586b71e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem finite-n-uniform-renewal of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] By enlarging $n_0$ if necessary,
