Under the Galerkin-state condition in Assumption~\ref{ass:time}, the same estimate holds with the supremum over $\Lambda$ inside the $L^p$ norm, with a constant depending additionally on the uniform finite-state bound $L_{\rm cut}$.  For each fixed dyadic triple,
\begin{equation}
 B^{\circ}_{\Lambda,N,Q,M}
 \longrightarrow B^{\circ}_{\infty,N,Q,M}
 \quad\text{in }L^p\bigl(\Omega;C(\Delta_T;\cL(L^2_q,L^2_n))\bigr).
