{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.784228+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46b5cccc9b1169b586a4118117cfebaafcd0b05d436bc4838ff88b3db48c7283","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 (Consequences of the dominant energy condition) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Given a Navier--Stokes potential~$\chi$ as in \autoref{def-pot-hyperbolic}, one has the following inequalities between components in the orthonormal coframe $e^m$: for $m,n=0,1,2,3$,
