{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4737cc1f2bcf901fe3ec3b5ea982c57d298c29a19b123e501655cb3164d7ca1e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:nprefix of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Fix $n\geq 1$ and set $q_0=0$. Given a strictly increasing sequence
		$(q_i)_{1\leq i\leq n}$ in $(0,1)$ and a strictly increasing sequence of
		weights $(u_i)_{1\leq i\leq n}$ in $(0,1)$, we write
		$\mathrm{Prefix}_{n+1}\!\bigl((u_i)_{1\leq i\leq n},(q_i)_{1\leq i\leq n}\bigr)$
		for the collection of probability measures $\zeta$ on $[0,1]$ satisfying
		\begin{equation*}
			\mathrm{supp}(\zeta)\cap[0,q_n]=\{q_0,q_1,\ldots,q_n\}
			\qquad\text{and}\qquad
			\zeta([0,q_{i-1}])=u_i \;\text{ for all }\; i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}.
		\end{equation*}
		We say that such $\zeta$ has an \emph{$(n+1)$-atom prefix} $\{0,q_1,\ldots,q_n\}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.755370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4738dc878b642c37f0f9c5b9c673c6d71c6f19211c14786322f3111c0c9a96d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:abstract-cluster-response of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For $f\inH_{\mathrm{reg}}$, there are $\varepsilon>0$ and real-analytic branches
$\lambda_j:(-\varepsilon,\varepsilon)\to\mathbb R$, $1\le j\le r$, listing the
eigenvalues of $\widehat A_{\tau,f}$ issuing from $\Lambda$.  In the basis
$(\phi_i)$,
\begin{equation}
 \left(\inner{B_f^\Lambda(\mu)\phi_j}{\phi_i}_{L^2(\mu)}\right)_{i,j}
 =-\kappa\Lambda
 \left(\int f\phi_i\phi_j\,d\mu\right)_{i,j}.

\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \{\lambda_1'(0),\ldots,\lambda_r'(0)\}
 =\Spec(B_f^\Lambda(\mu))

\end{equation}
as multisets.  The statement is independent of the basis.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_473d2ca77a0834f3fefb55083737f2d60e4f4f6775448e5eaf24674c881ffc59","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:mgf_bound of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] For $A\in\{\rho,J\}$, $k\in\mathbb{R}$, $t\ge0$, and any initial law $\nu\ll\mu$,
\begin{align}
  \E^\nu\bigl[\mathrm{e}^{kA_t}\bigr]
  \leq\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \mathrm{e}^{t\Lambda^A(k)}.

