{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.672425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_488378d80cf2b97dfb079bf04d53b16a5840b7cb5d160aa0df3bd06a484cbcb7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cameron:martin of arXiv:2605.28106, 'Gaussian Processes with Sample Paths in Reproducing Kernel Banach Spaces'] Let \( R : X^* \to X \) be a symmetric positive operator.
