{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.763207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_489cbca01e5e2c173a692623121acec58e49773a5f59ce334b70f66efffd7948","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:linnonlin of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Suppose the solution $X\equiv 0$ of the linear system (equation eq:SDEgenLinKh of the paper) is globally a.s.~asymptotically stable (or asymptotically stable in probability), and there exists $\varepsilon,\gamma>0$ sufficiently small that the drift and diffusion coefficients of (equation eq:main_YSDE of the paper) satisfy 
