{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.488337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48c2cde8b127b8f7d5114e0f8bde95abe72d556b187d9707823c4a457eee41b9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] Let $m\geq2$, and let 
\begin{equation}
\Omega_{m}=\left\{ 0,\ldots,m-1\right\} ^{\mathbb{N}}
\end{equation}
with its product Borel structure. If $E$ is a POVM on $\Omega_{m}$,
write 
\begin{equation}
E_{w}=E\left(\left[w\right]\right),\qquad H_{w}=\overline{ran}\,(E^{1/2}_{w})
\end{equation}
for each finite word $w$ in the alphabet $\left\{ 0,\ldots,m-1\right\} $.
Then, for every $w$, there are unique positive contractions 
\begin{equation}
A^{\left(0\right)}_{w},\ldots,A^{\left(m-1\right)}_{w}\in B\left(H_{w}\right)
