{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.759575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48e405f37025932a9f7f3a374acde726d15c64e154b2b07e4ab2f6c4368c9183","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Time-fractional compound Poisson process) of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $M\sim CP(\lambda, F)$, $L_f$ be the inverse Bernstein subordinator and  $p_f$ be the probability function of $M\circ L_f$. Let assume Condition I and that $\mathcal{D}_t^f p_f(t,\dif x) = \int_0^\infty p(s,\dif x) \mathcal{D}_t^f l_f(t,s)\dif s\ \forall t,x$. Then, $p_f$ satisfies
