{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.580938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_498a9a734670024edbb52dc701fcfc0e191803bf20c1dc0fb38143aa1deff1a4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition solution definition (q u) of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let $\tau^*$ be a stopping time with $\mathbb P(\tau^*>0)=1$, and let $(X,\tau^*) \triangleq (X(t))_{t\in [0,\tau^*)}$ be a progressively measurable process on $\mathbb H^s$.
		\begin{enumerate}[label={{\rm (\arabic*)}},leftmargin=0.79cm]\setlength\itemsep{0.2em}
