{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.592335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_49e9239f6e9ac4e67c095bff4c44fb97cab8183d0ca2562275fd0101ecf0910d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition COR-WIEJDUHFJ-HUD of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] Suppose that the exponents ${p_1}$ and ${p_2}$ obey $1 \leqslant {p_2} < {p_1} $. Then, the building block ${\mathbb{W}_\xi } \left( {t, x } \right)$ satisfies the intermittency
