{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.375445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0cc6595b2e031ffe3c3609b1cc73e729aaad4fa899bed85a9214418abedb79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] Let $V_{l}$ be the space of admissible flows $\phi\in\cH_{2}$ such
that $\left\langle \div\phi-j_{l},\div\phi-j_{l}\right\rangle =0$.
Then 
\begin{equation}
\left\langle j_{l},\cL^{-1}j_{l}\right\rangle =\sup_{\phi\in V_{l}}\left\{ -\left\langle \phi,\phi\right\rangle \right\} .
\end{equation}
The (formal) expression $\left\langle j_{l},\cL^{-1}j_{l}\right\rangle $
is defined as the term $-\int_{0}^{\infty}\dd t\sum_{x}\mu\left[\tau_{x}j_{l}\ e^{t\cL}j_{l}\right]$
appearing in the Green-Kubo formula (\ref{eq:green-kubo}).","status":"unverified"}

