{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700237+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c577b5f0dfdb005c178de1e517a73c034b6949a98234fcddc18f13d51333f9e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop coupling1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is chosen sufficiently small then, for any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \tfrac{1}{2}$ small enough (depending only on $\gamma$), if $k$ is sufficiently large then, for any $2k \leq T \leq {\rm e}^{\frac{1}{2}k^\gamma}$, we have that
