{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.116999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cde9539b1673c333f68df354eb8d8a00d5e8d255d11ae203c9d869219da0861","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: DHX input for specific rare event in sle of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] There exists a constant $c_6>0$ such that 
