{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.621306+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d13901d763ceadf2cdb8a3cf02cf3381e615fba20555115524f3ef6ce656a9e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 177 (The master controlling quantity) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] For $(\ubar,u) \in [\leftubar,\ubarboot)\times[\moreinterestingu_1,\moreinterestingu_2]$, we define the \emph{top-order master controlling quantity} 
	by:
	\begin{align}
		\begin{split}
			 \mastercontroltop(\ubar,u) & =  \totalfluxcontrolvelocity_N(\ubar,u) +
				\frac{1}{2} \strongangularcontrolvelocity_N(\ubar,u) + 2\blowupratetoporderwave \weakspacetimetransvelocitycontrol_{\Ntop}(\ubar,u)  +\frac{\blowupratetoporderwave}{2}  \weakspacetimeangularvelocitycontrol_{\Ntop}(\ubar,u) \\
				& \ \  + \totalfluxcontrolprecisefullymodifiedchi(\ubar,u) + \blowupratetoporderwave \totalbulkcontrolprecisefullymodifiedchi(\ubar,u)  \\
			&  \ \ + \totalfluxcontrolimprecisefullymodifiedchi(\ubar,u) + (\blowupratetoporderwave + 1) \totalbulkcontrolimprecisefullymodifiedchi(\ubar,u) \\
