Finally, the solution $(\theta_{\eps,},\tilde{R}_{\eps,})$ is continuous in the data $(\tilde{F}_{\eps,},\Tilde{I}_{\eps,})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.568829+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4d1bd4a2097094a25c29092fbac53411e363c9fe90df7db5b633cd3e0f653b86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 46 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $A\subset \mathbb{S}^n$ be a measurable set with positive measure. Then,
