{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.377904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4da1614b3ea0b122ad8e6e4bb8511aef641f8cd3d42786c968d1b50dec73ea13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:HKUB-collisions of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $A>0$, $k\ge 3$, $\delta\in (0,\frac14)$, $0<t_0<T$, and $r\ge 1$. Then, for some $C>0$, and all $\mathbf x\in\mathbb{Z}^k$, $N\in \mathbb{N}$, $|\beta|\le AN^{-1/8}$ and $t\in[t_0,TN]$,
