{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.736025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4da369584aef852902894fbac23cd34f5d25155e483563c69d6fc382bdae8636","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-Ward of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Let $\mathcal A$ be a Hermitian matrix. Define its resolvent as $R(z):=(\mathcal A-z)^{-1}$ for any $z= E+ \mathrm{i} \eta\in \mathbb{C}_+$. Then, we have 
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
\sum_x \overline {R_{xy'}}  R_{xy} = \frac{R_{y'y}-\overline{R_{yy'}}}{2\mathrm{i} \eta},\quad
\sum_x \overline {R_{y'x}}  R_{yx} = \frac{R_{yy'}-\overline{R_{y'y}}}{2\mathrm{i} \eta}.
\end{split}
\end{equation}
As a special case, if $y=y'$, we have
\begin{equation}
\sum_x |R_{xy}|^2 =\sum_x |R_{yx}|^2 = \frac{\im R_{yy}}{ \eta}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.547693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4dad07dca86f743cb89c7cf0a74a3dca892b709744e92cf8f8723b83b289e47f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:H+H- of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For $\alpha \in [0,1]$ and $H \in (0,1)$, we set
\begin{equation}
H_\alpha^+ := (1+\alpha)H \quad \text{ and } \quad H_\alpha^- := (1-\alpha)H    
\end{equation} 
and we define the Gaussian field $\{X^{\alpha,H}_{(x_1,x_2)}\}_{(x_1,x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2}$ by 
\begin{equation}
X^{\alpha,H}_{(x_1,x_2)} :=  \int_{\mathbb{R}^2}  \frac{(e^{i x_1 \xi_1}-1) (e^{i x_2 \xi_2}-1)}{\phi_{\alpha,H}(\xi_1,\xi_2)}  d\hat{\bf{W}}({\boldsymbol{\xi}}) 
\end{equation}
where the function
\[\phi_{\alpha,H}(\xi_1,\xi_2)=\min(\vert \xi_1 \vert, \vert \xi_2 \vert)^{H_\alpha^- +\frac{1}{2}}\max (\vert \xi_1 \vert, \vert \xi_2 \vert)^{H_\alpha^++\frac{1}{2} }\]
denotes the square root of the inverse of the spectral density of the field.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.069505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4db6ef361f600a5bd964c8206e77b299e116a63deab524ea68b6282d48fb6afc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.01742, 'Large deviation principles for SPDEs with locally Lipschitz coefficients'] Assume that Hypotheses \ref{cond-initial}, \ref{cond-dif}  and  \ref{3} hold. If $L_{\sigma}>0$, then
