{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.585720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e23b281045b27a32efe27b81f759b953df8d4c5a964b204abbdb4b89463b9c1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem second_moment_interpol of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with $\int \xi(\Lambda_1)^2\mathsf{P}_i(d\xi)<\infty$ and  $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1).$ Set $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$ and  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$. Then for $0\leq t\leq 1$ and $n\in \IN$ 
