{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.282979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e3f7a2c94ec448f424b95f41d6054fd1b8ac16753c40c6b2d85b1716a30da66","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:pureweak-nonstrong of arXiv:2507.14676, 'On the critical parameters of branching random walks'] {cf:BZ17}}]
Let $(X,K)$ and $(X,K^*)$ two irreducible continuous-time BRWs such that $k_{xy}=k^*_{xy}$ for all $x \in X \setminus A$
