{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.311974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ead01faa3b2d2446c7bb78e8bf9de3e4e12166c4725f7c70c0422b4d051e4a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sep of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For $\mathbb{P}_{\vec x}$-almost  every $\mathcal{W}$, there exist $\delta_1(\mathcal{W})$, $\delta_2(\mathcal{W})>0$ such that for any closed subset $\mathcal{A}\subseteq\mathcal{W}$ and all $x\in B(0,1/2)\setminus \mathcal{A}$, we have 
