{"assumptions":["$F:\mathbb{R}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}^{+}$ convex and nondecreasing","$A=(a_{ij})$ diagonal-free","$\xi_1,\dots,\xi_n$ independent, $(\tilde\xi_i)$ an independent copy of $(\xi_i)$"],"created_at":"2026-10-12T16:00:40+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ed298efb7395ec4f31e577779851f026061749c9cf1f772e5afc0a879ba1bbb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Theorem 3.1.1 in \cite{de_la_Pena_Book}) of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $F: \mathbb{R}^{+}\to \mathbb{R}^{+}$ be a convex nondecreasing function and $A=(a_{ij})_{n\times n}$ be a diagonal-free matrix. If $\{\xi_{i}, i\le n\}$ is a sequence of independent random variables and $\tilde{\xi}_{i}$ is an independent copy of $\xi_{i}$, then there exists a universal constant $C$ such that
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{E}F\Big(\big\vert\sum_{i,j}a_{ij}\xi_{i}\xi_{j}\big\vert   \Big)\le \mathbb{E}F\Big(C\big\vert\sum_{i,j}a_{ij}\xi_{i}\tilde{\xi}_{j}   \big\vert\Big).
	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.249845+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ed33be0dfbd324c9fb62b0351ddd9a540838eff2df18476df2d9702dd9a6fef","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 44 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Assume that there exists a sequence of  boundary  height functions $f^{(n)} : \partial \mathfrak{X} \rightarrow \mathbb{R}$, for each $n \ge 1$, such that $\Adm(\mX;f^{(n)})$ is not empty (recall \Cref{def:Adm}) and
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item [(A)] $\lim_{n\to\infty}\sup_{z\in \partial\mathfrak X
    }|f^{(n)}(z)-f(z)|=0$

  \item [(B)] the limit shape  $\mathcal H^{(n)}$ in $\mathfrak X$ with boundary condition $f^{(n)}$ {(cf. \Cref{th:limshapeD})}
    has the property that $\nabla \mathcal H^{(n)}\in \mathcal T$ and $\dist(\nabla \mathcal H^{(n)},\partial\mathcal T)\ge 1/(2n)$ hold almost everywhere in $\mathfrak{X}$, where $\mathcal T$ was defined in \eqref{e:cT}.
  \end{enumerate}
  Then, for the Glauber dynamic in $\mathfrak X$, for every $\delta,L,\omega>0$ there {exists $C<\infty$} such that, for every $N$,
  \begin{eqnarray}

    \max_{\eta\in \Omega^N}\mathbf P_\eta\Big(\exists t: C N^{2+\delta}\le t\le N^{L}, z\in \mathfrak X, |H_t(z)-\mathcal H(z)|\ge \omega\Big)\le CN^{-L}.
  \end{eqnarray}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.539748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ed69e2b1fdf668baf72dbe7d20f2b18337108354408a70c9f13df171eb09924","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:CT-TASEP-dressing of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The kernel $K_{t,\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}$ is dual dressing
compatible (Definition~(def:sc-dual-dressing of the paper)) with
