{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.144350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f39c713968172a22535e9b29ca4036e16d5ec8b742aed0939becf717f2eab6d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.11071, 'Scaling Laws for Majority-based Opinion Dynamics in the Presence of Stubborn Agents'] Suppose that $N_0^n=N_1^n=\ceil{n\gamma}$ for some $\gamma\in(0,1/2)$. Let $X^n$ and $\bar X^n$ be two chains, each following the rates in~\eqref{eq:uprate}-\eqref{eq:downrate} and started at $x\in \mc S^n$ and $\bar x\in \mc S^n$, respectively. Assume without loss generality that $|x-1/2|\geq |\bar x -1/2|$. Then we have
