{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.925591+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f67599d13f49804a8315d8187c35911ffa3f3c31aec411958ac81a06b269072","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 21 (\Cref{thm: restate of pnkt and nu} in the text) of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] For $n=\omega(1)$ and $k\ge 2$, the following holds. Let $t':=t-\frac{n\log n}{k}$. Let $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ be defined as in \Cref{defi: Pnk and its convolution}, and $\nu_{n,k}^t$ be defined as in \Cref{defi: construction of nu}. 
