{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.376738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fb346e7f10bd3e02451186b8fad87aae3743e8a33c581ac794fdc8bebcdb6ab","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:secondorder of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] Fix $x^0 \in \partial \Delta$ with $x^0_1=\dotso=x^0_k=0$,  $x^0_{k+1},\dotso,x^0_d > 0$, and $\sum_{j=k+1}^d x_j^0<1$. Taking $r= (1-\sum_{i=k+1}^d x^0_i)/{(2d)}$,  there exist two positive constants $c_1(x^0)$, $c_2(x^0)$ such that for any $x_1,\dotso, x_k \in (0,r)$,
    \begin{align*}
    c_1(x^0) Diag(1/x^2_1,\dotso,1/x^2_k, 1,\dotso, 1) 
  &\leq \nabla^2 g(x_1,\dotso, x_k, x^0_{k+1},\dotso,x^0_d) \\
