{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.399004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4fc7303b940da205be3773202c958860df5111db8c8da5f93b953ef4707a0d7a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi deflich of arXiv:2608.25865, 'Instability of Böhm's Einstein metrics'] The Lichnerowicz Laplacian is the linear operator $\Delta_L:\mathscr{T}^0_2(M)\to \mathscr{T}^0_2(M)$ defined by $$\forall T \in \mathscr{T}^0_2(M),~~\Delta_L T=\overline{\Delta} T+\mathfrak{R} T,$$
