{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.558539+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_501dd41ef6867088dbb83b2cffa4c5cd7233f763edf9689842a1119651afd05c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:first-counter-example-2-general of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] For every choice of $a>0$, $n\in\N$, and $\theta\in(0,1/2)$, the functions
