{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.429411+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50564ed8fa3f855a7307ca584c773bf41480549249cc71dfd62b223924f90353","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 195 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The \emph{even} Green function is defined for any two points $p_1,p_2 \in \Sigma^{\textnormal{half}}$
\begin{equation}

\textnormal{Gr}^+(p_1,p_2) = \textnormal{Gr}(p_1,p_2) + \textnormal{Gr}(\overline{\varsigma}(p_1),p_2).
\end{equation}
where $\textnormal{Gr}$ is the usual Green function for $\Sigma^{\textnormal{half}}$ and $\overline{\varsigma}$ is the anti-holomorphic involution on $\Sigma^{\textnormal{half}}$ that sends a point $p \in \Sigma^{(q,\textnormal{L})}$ with coordinate $z$ to the point $\overline{\varsigma}(p)$ with coordinate $z^* \in \Sigma^{(q,\textnormal{R})}$. We define the \emph{even Gaussian free field} to be the centered (generalized) Gaussian field with covariance $\textnormal{Gr}^+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.988460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5058fb8cdf4d74aa14932e630b942b5bcfb17e0ef74596ab00418a8be2f3f0a2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gaus_tail_beyond_window of arXiv:2607.04514, 'Boundary-layer asymptotics for Gaussian-smoothed singular measures'] Let \(F\in\mathfrak G_s\) on \(\mathcal D_{\infty,A, \mathcal{K}_{\mathcal{S}},\sigma_0}\) for an integer
