\inf \left\{ v(D') \middle|
\begin{gathered}
 \text{$D'$ is a $\Q$-Cartier $\Q$-divisor on $f^{-1}(S^0)$} \\
 \text{such that $D|_{f^{-1}(S^0)} \equiv_{S^0} D' \geq 0$}
\end{gathered} 
\right\}, 
\end{equation*}
where $S^0$ runs through all open neighborhoods of $c_{X}(v)$ in $S$.
By definition, $v_{\num}(D/S)$ only depends on the $f$-numerical equivalence class of $D$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.800464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_50b74d431ac862f595a9e4ff2c407643a2afd4038cd1b91ea358d21d9ef88481","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme 79 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\bs{x}_N\in \R^N$ have pairwise distinct entries. The matrix $\op{A}(\boldsymbol{x}_N)$ introduced in \eqref{definition matrice A2}
