{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.214215+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5104a00b46b131a7fe64ce5ca43ce48b512b4f9caccb8830261bd4b5d93b07e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:meanfieldproc of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Consider the multivariate linear-Gaussian setting, $g(x) := Gx, \enskip h(x):= Hx$ and a mean-field SDE of the form 
    \begin{align}

        d\bar{X}_t = \underbrace{G\bar{X}_t + \Sigma^{1/2}dW_t}_{\text{mutation}}  \quad + \underbrace{dI_t}_{\text{observation update}} 
    \end{align}
    with $\bar{X}_0 \sim \mathcal{N}(x; m_0, C_0)$ and the stochastic observation update term 
    \begin{align}

        dI_t = &-\frac{s}{2}K_t H (\bar{X}_t - m_t)dt + \underbrace{ (r-s) K_t \left(dZ_t - H\bar{X}_t dt  + \left(\frac{2}{r-s}\Xi\right)^{1/2} d\bar{B}_t\right)  }_{\text{Stochastic Kalman Innovation}} 
    \end{align}
    or the deterministic observation update term 
    \begin{align}

	d I_t = \left( \frac{r}{2} - s \right) K_t H (\bar{X}_t - m_t)dt   + \underbrace{\enskip  (r-s) K_t\left( dZ_t - \frac{1}{2} \left(H\bar{X}_t + Hm_t  \right) dt \right)}_{\text{Deterministic Kalman Innovation}} 
\end{align}
where $\bar{B}$ is a scalar Wiener process independent of $W, B$. The time evolution of the conditional density of $\bar{X}_t$ given $\mathcal{Z}_t$ for (equation eq:basemf of the paper) with either (equation eq:mfinfla of the paper) or (equation eq:mfinflabias of the paper) observation update terms is given by the limiting non-local replicator-mutator equation or modified Kushner equation (equation eq:modifiedkushner of the paper).  Similarly, consider observation update terms driven by piecewise smooth in time observations, 
\begin{align}

	d I_t =    - \frac{s}{2} K_t H \left( \bar{X}_t - m_t \right)dt + \enskip (r-s) K_t \left(\frac{dZ_t^d}{dt} - \frac{1}{2}H\left( \bar{X}_t + m_t  \right)\right)dt 
\end{align}
or the stochastic version 
\begin{align}

	d I_t = -\frac{s}{2}K_t H (\bar{X}_t - m_t)dt + (r-s) K_t \left(\frac{dZ_t^d}{dt} - H\bar{X}_t  \right)dt + \sqrt{r-s} K_t \Xi^{1/2} d \bar{B}_t  
\end{align}
The time evolution of the conditional density of $\bar{X}_t$ given $\mathcal{Z}_t$ for (equation eq:basemf of the paper) with either (equation eq:mfstochode of the paper) and (equation eq:mfdetode of the paper) observation update terms is given by the non-local replicator-mutator equation (equation eq:repmutlineargauss of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

