{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.278760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5196f9050962fbc0acd0ad4e84758fa16fc99d20802ec54003cda1fe17c64274","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 3 (Optimality of Theorem~\ref{Theo_main2} when $p_{1}=\cdots=p_{2}=1$) of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $\eta_{1}, \cdots, \eta_{n}\stackrel{i.i.d.}{\sim}\mathcal{W}_{s}(\alpha)$ and $A$ be a symmetric diagonal-free matrix. Then for $0<\alpha\le 1$ and $t\ge 0$
