(Here we use the standard convention: $(-1)!!=1$.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.468582+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_51a3f8e8d189b7a78f887473a0943933755d9864a9ae580a2f2f7ab39daef74a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lower of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Suppose that the QMS $\exp(t \mathcal{L}_\gamma)$ is a lift of $\exp(t \mathcal{L}_O)$ in the sense of (def:2ndlift of the paper). Let $C \ge 1$ and $\nu > 0$ be the prefactor and the convergence rate in the estimate (equation ex:expdecay of the paper) for $\exp(t \mathcal{L}_\gamma)$, and $t_{rel}$ be the relaxation time (equation eq:trelax of the paper) of $\exp(t \mathcal{L}_\gamma)$. Then, 
     \begin{align} 
        \nu \le (1 + \log C) \sqrt{\widetilde{s_{\rm m}}^{-1} \lambda_O}\,,\quad
            t_{\rm rel} \ge  \frac{1}{2 \sqrt{\widetilde{s_{\rm m}}^{-1} \lambda_O}}\,,
