{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.728672+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52087c7ae9c8e2e651fa9ee8a51b70e99adfa2d9ede4d37c4b35e41e58829640","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 (Lemma 2.9 \cite{Grigoryan2024}) of arXiv:2609.02732, 'Conservation of mass for solutions of Leibenson's equation on Riemannian Manifolds'] Let $u=u\left( x,t\right) $ be a non-negative bounded subsolution to \emph{(\ref{dtv})} in $M\times I$  with non-negative initial function $u(\cdot, 0)=u_0\in L^{1}(M)\cap L^{\infty}(M)$. If $\sigma\geq 1$, including $\sigma=\infty$, then the function 
