{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.161866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_526a75c3e7cf4b9771899ae4fd84729dc390b2b9a29e0170a070b014d1fa4ee0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 of arXiv:2606.29512, '2606.29512'] A real-, vector-, or tensor-valued function
on $\Omega\times[0,T]\times\mathbb \cR$
is called admissible if
$f=f^M+f^B$  
for some $\cO\otimes\cB(\mathbb\cR)$-measurable 
functions $f^M$, $f^B$, and 
a constant $\hat f>0$ and a nonnegative optional process
$\bar f=(\bar f_t)_{t\in[0,T]}$ exist such that 
\begin{equation}

\left(
\dashint_{B_\rho}{\bf1}_{\cR}|f^M(t,x)|^r\,dx
\right)^{1/r}
\le
\hat f\,\rho^{-1} \quad \text{for $\mathbb{P}\otimes dt$-a.e 
$(\omega,t)\in\Omega\times[0,T]$}
\end{equation}
for all $B_\rho\in\mathbb B_\rho$, $\rho\leq1$, 
and
\begin{equation}

\operatorname*{ess\,sup}_{x\in\cR}
|f_t^B(x)|
\leq \bar f_t \,\, \text{(a.s.)},
\quad
\sup_{\omega\in\Omega}
\int_0^T \bar f_t^2\,dt<\infty.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.301950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_526af85edc4db84a2b931616daab1f18001e259b8077af384352a65bce15a1e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<1$, let $0<\epsilon<1$ small enough, for any $i$ take $x$ such that $x =  i^{1-\epsilon}$ (note that we do not add a notation for the integer value of $i^{1-\epsilon}$), 
