{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.618052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_528581b8774110421dc451927c0d39da40b0a656d5af2dcc3f57863885cca006","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$\sigma\in(0,1/10)$ and let~$\gamma_{n,a}$ be as in \eqref{E:6.34ii}. For each~$a\ge0$ there exists a constant~$c'>0$ such that for all $n,k\ge1$ with $2k\le n$, all $s\ge 0$, all $u\le s$ and all $v>0$,
