{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.915100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52891c845e1073a5f003b7ed878bc2f6b6d52be0618108ff2bda0d8cbb32c14b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop prop_no_g2 of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] There exists a consistent APS $S$ satisfying the following conditions:
