{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.912023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5289dd0af992c0809cd4e2c3338c2ab162e40ff4277c0af4c434bd31f807b7c3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Abstract provability structure (APS) of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] A structure $S = \langle L, \leq, \top, \bot, \Box, \boxtimes\rangle$ is called an \emph{abstract provability structure} (APS) if the following conditions hold: 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $L$ is a nonempty set.
        \item $\leq$ is a partial order on $L$.
        \item $\top$ and $\bot$ are elements of $L$.
        \item $\Box$ and $\boxtimes$ are unary operations on $L$ satisfying the  following conditions for all $x, y \in L$:
        \begin{description}
            \item[(C1)] If $x \leq y$, then $\Box x \leq \Box y$ and $\boxtimes y \leq \boxtimes x$;
            \item[(C2)] $\top \leq \boxtimes \bot$;
            \item[(C3)] If $x \leq \Box y$ and $x \leq \boxtimes y$, then $x \leq \boxtimes \top$;
            \item[(C4)] $\boxtimes x \leq \Box \boxtimes x$.
        \end{description}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:03.893363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_528f35c08e5f10371963b2f1d7766d02657ff956d63fcf42404fc6933adcd372","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2606.18877, 'Ergodic Properties of Non-Linear Density-Dependent Perturbations of the Ornstein--Uhlenbec'] The stationary density \(\pi\) satisfies 
