{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.598328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53105727a57938d846bd51932e3534efce680743f04f3f84c95c9f0f9557c27a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:resolventconvergence of arXiv:2608.11603, 'Continuous-time directed polymers to the Critical SHF via moments'] {}
	 Fix $\alpha, \alpha' \in \mathsf{Pair}[\![n]\!]$ with $\alpha \neq \alpha'$. Then, there exists a $\theta_{\star} \in \mathbb{R}$ for which the following holds: for every $\lambda \gtrsim e^{2\theta+ 4\pi\mathfrak{K}} + 1$, there exists $\varepsilon_{0}(\lambda) > 0$ such that for all $\varepsilon < \varepsilon_{0}(\lambda)$, the prelimiting resolvents satisfy the following:
	\begin{subequations}
	\begin{align}
	\normop{\mathcal{G}_{\varepsilon\alpha}(\lambda)}  & \lesssim \lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}} \qquad \qquad \qquad   \text{ and } \qquad \qquad \quad \normop{\mathcal{G}_{\varepsilon\alpha}(\lambda) -\mathcal{G}_{\alpha}(\lambda)} \to 0,    \\ 
	\normop{\mathcal{G}^{\ast}_{\varepsilon \alpha}(\lambda)} & \lesssim \lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}} \qquad \qquad \qquad   \text{ and } \qquad \qquad \quad \normop{\mathcal{G}^{\ast}_{\varepsilon \alpha}(\lambda) -\mathcal{G}^{\ast}_{\alpha}(\lambda)} \to 0,  \\
	\normop{\mathcal{G}_{\varepsilon \alpha\alpha'}(\lambda)} & \lesssim 1 \qquad \qquad \qquad  \quad \, \text{  and } \qquad \qquad \quad \normop{\mathcal{G}_{\varepsilon \alpha\alpha'}(\lambda) -\mathcal{G}_{\alpha\alpha'}(\lambda)} \to 0,  \\
	\normop{\prediag{\theta}{\alpha}(\lambda)} & \lesssim (\log\lambda - \theta )^{-1}  \quad \quad \,   \text{ and } \qquad \qquad \quad \prediag{\theta}{\alpha}(\lambda) -\diag{\theta_{\star}}{\alpha}(\lambda) \to 0 \, \, \text{strongly}\, \, . 
