{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.311815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5333014b5c797b48f1699522ad366cd11febefed9f2752daab418d687dde3942","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:cltsmooth of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] (CLT for Sobolev statistics)

Let ${\mathcal X}$ be a simple stationary point process on $\mathbb{R}^d$ with truncated correlations satisfying Assumption (asmpt:integrationofrhokT of the paper).  Assume that for all $m \geq 2$, there exists $d_m \geq m$ such that for all $l_1,\ldots,l_{m-1} \in \mathbb{Z}_+$ with $\sum_i l_i \leq d_m$,

\begin{align}
    \int_{(\mathbb{R}^d)^{m-1}}  \prod\limits_{i=1}^{m-1} |z_{i}|^{l_i}\; |\kappa_{m-1}|(z_1,\ldots ,z_{m-1}) \, \mathrm{d} z_1\ldots \mathrm{d} z_{m-1} < \infty,
