{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.590980+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53a6072b9604bb0579c195606f99411c33a199b5107f0061edfde2c8fca2de1e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition StoFubiniThm of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Let $T\geq 0$, $m(dt)$ be a $\sigma$-finite measure on $\mathbb{R}_+$ and $h$ be a measurable function on $\mathbb{R}_+$ satisfying that 
