{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:05:37.778018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_53c583b0161b66f3eea123eaeb0f199638484afe18737c2677cdf791544350a7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4.1 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Assume that $\xi$ and $\xi'$ are two terminal values, $g$ and $g^{\prime}$ are two generators, and $(Y_\cdot, Z_\cdot)$ and $\left(Y_\cdot^{\prime}, Z_\cdot^{\prime}\right)$ are, respectively, solutions of BSDE$(\xi,\tau,g)$ and BSDE$\left(\xi^{\prime}, \tau, g^{\prime}\right)$. If $(Y_\cdot-Y_\cdot^{\prime})^+\in S_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R})$ and $\xi \leq \xi^{\prime}$, and either of the following conditions is satisfied:\vspace{0.2cm}

