{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.470233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5448fac7e7bcb564927e5eda1394469573e6bdae743859dd69f18800686d7623","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 86 (The frame components of $\deform{Z}$) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\zetatan$, $\zetatrans$, $\angktan$, and $\angktrans$ be the $\ell_{t,u}$-tensorfields defined in \eqref{E:CONNECTIONCOEFFICIENTDECOMPOSITIONS}. Then the following identities for the frame components of the angular deformation tensor $\deform{Z}$ of $Z \in \comder = \{\Lunit,\muX,\Yvf{A},\Yvf{B}\}$:
\begin{subequations} 
	\begin{align}
		\deformarg{L}{L}{L} & = 0, & & \deformarg{L}{\muX}{X} = 2 \Lunit \upmu, & & \deformarg{L}{L}{\muX} = - \Lunit\upmu \\
		\angdeformarg{L}{L} & = 0, & & \angdeformarg{L}{\muX}  = \angrmD \upmu + 2 \zetatrans + 2 \upmu \zetatan,  & & \\
