{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.563326+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54cbd7fb0ab15716f465a26db9c3ae3bc1dd7ac3696c868f05bb783e5e616076","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2605.30560, 'Projected McKean--Vlasov Dynamics for Entropic Weak Optimal Transport'] Suppose $(\X_n)_{n \in \mathbb N} \in \rm FP_2(\mu,\nu)$. If $\AW_2(\X_n, \mathbb X) \to 0$ for some $\mathbb X \in \rm FP_2(\mu,\nu)$, then we have 
