{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:02:11.269699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54e90f4d1be62aa8f81fde13d6625d69c45426a7ae662b321eaf6f3104d65512","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lil-rw2mc of arXiv:2509.10225, 'Phase Transitions for Elephant Random Walks \\ with Two memory Channels'] {The rates of almost sure convergence of the fluctuations around the almost sure limit in the appropriate regimes are as follows.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[a)] For $p \in \left(0, \frac{11}{16}\right)$,
\begin{align}
    &\limsup_{n \to \infty} \sqrt{\frac{n}{2\log\log n}}\left(\frac{S_n}{{n}} - \Lambda_p\right) \\
    =-&\liminf_{n \to \infty} \sqrt{\frac{n}{2\log\log n}}\left(\frac{S_n}{{n}} - \Lambda_p\right) 
    {= \sqrt{\Sigma^{(1)}_p}}, \nonumber
