{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.224848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_554360b23be78fab50e09a9ad1a2f0e14a5d1e0f3c59d8176d0f2510542c1abc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: RI second moment of arXiv:2411.16398, 'Large Deviations of Cover Time of Tori in Dimensions $d\geq 3$'] There exist constants $C>0$ and $c_1>1$ such that for all $u\geq 0$, $N\in \mathbb{N}$ and $F \subset Q(0,2N-1)$, 
