{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.261231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_555486d1d496afff8e8bf05d6a17678b36d35c2eedc9989f7bc42d25d4306265","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Erd\H{o}s \cite{Erdos}) of arXiv:2609.01114, 'Unbalanced spectral Tur\'an problem for color-critical graphs with prescribed large maximu'] Let $\mathcal F$ be a family of graphs with $\chi(\mathcal F)=p+1\ge2$.	Then there exists $c=c(\mathcal F)>0$ such that
