energy.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.859441+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5590c9d00e5ce1c30fdd423bab333f4b76f8f98f4ae4cfbb81030e37265fd28d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm superlinear of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Suppose that $(\mathcal{T}_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$ is a generalised preferential attachment tree, with deterministic values $(f(j))_{j \in \mathbb{N}_{0}}$. Moreover, assume that, for some $\kappa > 0$, we have 
