{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.758693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_566d53a6c376536d568e64d86d2dfe3bd5b674ca219d0e72688b49c722a3a728","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $X, Y$ two stochastic processes on $\mathcal{D}[0,\infty)$. Assume that $X(t)\stackrel{d}{=}Y(t), \ t\ge0$. 
