{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.310494+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_566d5b5acc1c257c4a2d3f0c31410e60949b3daf47efd57ddc8a2f0c24d07944","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.28505, 'Quagmires and large Suslin forests'] A $(\kappa, \lambda)$-forest is \emph{Suslin} if the following conditions hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item for every $x \in [\lambda]^{< \kappa}$, $|\{f \in F : \mathrm{dom}(f) = x\}| < \kappa$,
\item for every $A \in [\lambda]^\kappa$ and $f : A \rightarrow 2$, there exists $x \in [A]^{< \kappa}$ such that $f \upharpoonright x \not\in F$,
\item the forest $F$ ordered by reverse inclusion is $\kappa$-cc.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

