{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.597578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56f1aee4220f72de5618df50a363e2d0400b25cc4c53d34a794e90c5cdb4fab0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:DCM of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] Consider MMPPs $(B,X),(B',X')$ with possibly different initial distributions for $B$ and $B'$ but with the same arrival rate vector $\alpha$ and generator matrix $T$. The MMPP with $\alpha,T$ is called \emph{downward conditionally monotone} if $v^*\preceq \mathcal{L}(B_0)\preceq\mathcal{L}(B'_0)$ implies, for all $t>0$,
	\begin{equation*}
		v^*\preceq\mathcal L(B_t\mid X_s=0 ~\forall s\leq t)\preceq\mathcal L(B'_t\mid X'_s=0~\forall s\leq t).
	\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.742266+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56f26d7df33d5bc7f8c00075b2c4c3252d9b0322f80846fcf2928bcf14ededc1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:ito of arXiv:2411.19192, 'Characteristic function and Esscher transform of a switching Levy model for the temperatur'] The solution of equation ((eq:tempdyna of the paper)) is:
\begin{eqnarray} 
  T_t&=&C_1(t, \alpha)+  \sigma e^{-\alpha t} W_t
  \end{eqnarray}
with
\begin{eqnarray}
  W_t &=& \sum_{j=1}^{N_t} \int_{\tau_{j-1}}^{\tau_{j}}  e^{\alpha u}dV^{\nu(j)} _u+ \int_{\tau_{N_t}}^{t}  e^{\alpha u}dV^{\nu(N_t+1)} _u
\end{eqnarray}
where $\nu(j)=\frac{3+(-1)^j}{2}$ and $C_1(t, \alpha) = s_t+e^{-\alpha t}(T_0-s_0)$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

