{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.528211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5701654c0b2604087ff21b4a8239d57e77309872df1ccf3cfe544fb2e7927c66","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 (The associated Vaisman metric) of arXiv:2608.30638, 'On compact steady pluriclosed soliton surfaces'] Let $(M,g,J,f)$ be a compact non-K\"ahler steady
pluriclosed soliton surface. Then $(M,J)$ admits a Vaisman metric.  More precisely,
\begin{equation}
 \widehat\omega
 :=\tau\wedge(J\tau^\#)^\flat
  +\frac{|\theta|}{2}\omega_\perp=\tau\wedge(J\tau^\#)^\flat
  +\frac{|\theta|}{2}\left(\omega-\tau\wedge(J\tau^\#)^\flat\right)
\end{equation}
is the fundamental form of such a metric, whose parallel Lee form is
$2\tau$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.744777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_570ad6c52aba04349bae2b3963a910ac305ab9379a1fc1cec7222dfc016fb99c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2605.13727, 'Stochastic evolution equations\\ driven by arbitrary cylindrical Lévy processes'] Let $L$ be a cylindrical L\'evy process in $U$, and let $\Psi$ be a predictable, $L_2(U,H)$-valued process that is integrable with respect to $L$. Define the integral process $(Y(t):\, t\in [0,T])$  by $Y(t):=\int_{(0,t]} \Psi\,{\rm d}L$. Then, for every uniformly bounded, real-valued, non-negative, adapted c\`agl\`ad process $Z$, the following identity holds:
	\begin{equation}
		\int_{(0,t]} Z(s)^2\;{\rm d}[Y](s)=\left[\int_{(0,{\cdot}]} Z(s)\Psi(s)\,{\rm d}L(s)\right](t)
		\qquad\text{for all }t\in [0,T].
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

