{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.718782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57333469eb272560ba4f37fc1ef676c73deaf800a61e038d9fe93f17ec1bd0e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:covariance_inequality of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] For each $m\geqslant 2$, there exists a constant $C_m$ such that if  $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, $\left(X_i\right)_{i\in\mathbb Z}$ is a strictly stationary sequence taking   $h\colon S^m\to \mathbb R$ is a canonical kernel such that $\sup_{x_1,\dots,x_m\in S}\left|h\left(x_1,\dots,x_m\right)\right|\leqslant R$ and $N\geqslant m$, then 
 \begin{align}
     \E{\pr{U_{m,N+a}\left(h\right)-U_{m,a}\left(h\right)}^2}&
     \leqslant C_{m} \left(N+a\right)^{ m-1 } N\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^{N+a}k^{m-1} 
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2,\\
     \E{\max_{m\leqslant n\leqslant N}\pr{U_{m,n}\left(h\right)   }^2    }
     &\leqslant C_mN^{m }\left(\log  N\right)^2\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^Nk^{m-1}
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2.
 \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

