{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.685198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57396817caede005c040b13b7f63bcf0e188561fffccc8ca06793f91e506e83f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:loca3 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] There exists $C^\star>0$ such that for $t\in [0,1)$  and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$ satisfying \begin{equation*}
