{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.956167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57521e65796d0c0a5de8218babf8fb11bc7640692dbd43535ffca785a3d4bcac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2512.01483, 'Scaling Limits of Line Models in Degenerate Environment'] For $\mathbb{P}$ a.e. environment, when $T \to \infty$, the process $(Y^{(T)}(t))_{t \geq 0}$ converges in law, in $D([0,\infty), \mathbb{R})^2$, to the process $(\mathcal{Y}_1(t), \mathcal{Y}_2(t))_{t \geq 0}$, where 
