{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:02:28.580435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_575accd47699513929ff2ebbb9dc5aa83bc5226e5bc4a91b6f925b994b2da252","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.01296, 'Asymptotic safety regions for Gabor frames generated by Hermite functions'] For every $\varepsilon>0$ and $0<\rho<\frac{1}{2}$, there exists $n_{\varepsilon, \rho} \in \N$ such that, whenever $n\geq n_{\varepsilon, \rho}$ and a pair of parameters $a,b>0$ satisfies
