{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:25:55.459870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57d73761e7f9c6160bef9078df77fdb0bb82dc80c58e339b48b12adff6fb5194","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2607.28238, 'Well-posedness and large deviations for the obstacle problem of first-order stochastic con'] Let $M_\psi:=1+\Vert\psi\Vert_{L^\infty(Q_T)}$. For every $p\geq2$, there exists $C_p>0$ independent of $\alpha$ and $n\in\mathbb N$ such that
\begin{align}
&\E\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}(t)-M_\psi|^p\dd x+\alpha\E\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}-M_\psi|^{p-2}|\nabla u_{\alpha,n}|^2\dd x\dd s\\
&+\E\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}-M_\psi|^{p-2}n|(u_{\alpha,n}-\psi)^-|^2\dd x\dd s +\E\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}-M_\psi|^{p-2}n(u_{\alpha,n}-\psi)^-\dd x\dd s \nonumber \\
&\leq C_p \Big(1+\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u^0_{\alpha}-M_\psi|^p\dd x\Big),\nonumber
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&\E\bigg[\bigg|\alpha\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}-M_\psi|^{p-2}|\nabla u_{\alpha,n}|^2\dd x\dd s\bigg|^2\bigg]+\E\bigg[\bigg|\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u_{\alpha,n}-M_\psi|^{p-2}n|(u_{\alpha,n}-\psi)^-|^2\dd x\dd s\bigg|^2\bigg]\nonumber\\
&\leq C_p \Big(1+\int_{\mathbb T^N}|u^0_{\alpha}-M_\psi|^{2p}\dd x\Big),
\end{align}
and
\begin{equation}
\E\bigg[\bigg|\int_0^T\int_{\mathbb{T}^N}n(u_{\alpha,n}-\psi)^-\dd x\dd s\bigg|^p\bigg]\leq C_p.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.187634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57dc465acd423633e09d0a723dfe1675b45c504e0eec6bc2f421c31a921d9a98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 137 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Let $u,f,f_{i}$,
