    \item $\mu_p$ has bounded density with respect to Lebesgue measure.
    \item $I[\mu_p] \longrightarrow I[\mu]$ as $p \to +\infty$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.482718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_592efc0bc0da2dab0b7d4f72aa2b827232e26a734771f3160778ebb87b300c22","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 34 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] With the notations above,
