{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:23:37.802356+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5949b6a0e2b6aa16504d2602df7909a942abd20dd254cdb97f224a3c5f134e6f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Strichartz estimate) of arXiv:2609.03558, 'Local well-posedness of the higher-order nonlinear Schr\"{o}dinger equation on the half-li'] Let $s\in\mathbb{R}$ and $(\mu,r)$ be higher-order Schr\"{o}dinger admissible, i.e. 	$\mu,r\geq 2,$ and $\displaystyle \frac{3}{\mu}+\frac{1}{r}=\frac12.$ Then, the solution of the homogeneous Cauchy problem \eqref{cauchy1} satisfies the Strichartz estimate
