{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.058686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_596330833ff5bc770538caed541e4ca76da628a0e358d319d9e14eeea9206b8d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 45 (One-species formula for balanced models) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Assume that $\xi$ is balanced with respect to $\lambda$. Then, for every $t\geq0$,
