{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:23:25.634380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5977b6d4b539e540e8c60232268972ac09d85dfaf6fd156e30bfbc44914a903d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Inverse2 of arXiv:2609.01350, 'New classes of trace-form permutation polynomials and their compositional inverses'] Let $q=2^m$ with $m$ odd, and let $f_1$ be as above a permutation
polynomial of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$. By Theorem~(Result1 of the paper), one of the
following holds, and in each case the compositional inverse is:

