{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:27.032786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59d2c229721a861bf220a11ac1fd8317de568fa24d0bb5955369bcd0178b6287","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Muckenhoupt of arXiv:2505.14012, 'Ergodicity for stochastic neural field equations'] The weight $\rho\in L^1_{\operatorname{loc}}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ is called an \emph{$A_2$-Muckenhoupt weight}, denoted $\rho\in A_2$, if
