	\end{equation}
	Then, there is an $\epsilon(i,j)>0$ such that, for any $t\in(0,\epsilon(i,j))$, (equation eq:DCM-w-et(T-Da) of the paper) holds for every $\ell\in S$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.048739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5aa4844f2e78b7831ab65aeef07799d711bbac920596f1432cb9671a8bb5dc90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.16083, 'Eyring--Kramers asymptotics for infinite-dimensional stochastic gradient systems'] Under Assumption \ref{Ass_for_theorem_I}, the number $k_0$ of local minima of $F$ is finite and non-zero. Moreover  
