{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:22:21.906882+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ae5ef5a4706718330a6737d767859f605cc7c23ec4bdaa7946c2e22ddb15ab3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Reference point of arXiv:2411.11429, 'Functional Central Limit Theorem for topological functionals of Gaussian critical points'] For a compact connected component $ C$ of $ \mathscr 	C(A;W;\partial W)$, call $ x(C;F) = x(C)\in W \setminus \partial W$ the critical point of $ C$ lowest with respect to the lexicographic order, called {\it reference point of $ C$}, and define
