{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.873911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b1d8c12de4cc76d19a7660861d0792422d91eaf433a8212632389801600f621","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:char. for ergodic of arXiv:2411.00663, 'Ergodicity and Mixing of invariant capacities and applications'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mu,T)$ be a capacity preserving system. If $\mu$  is subadditive and continuous then the following three statements are equivalent:
