{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.054464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b763b548252d6caa1349b33c98e78143be7b070a2b4e43530d682b76211350b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lema_pomocna_za_pomocnu_dzamic of arXiv:2607.13302, 'Extending an Order-Statistic Characterization of the Exponential Distribution'] For $1\leq m\leq N$ and all feasible real $x$, it holds that
    \[
\sum_{i=0}^{N-m}
\binom{N-m}{i}m^{\overline{i}}
\frac{x^{i}}{\prod_{q=1}^{m+i}(1-qx)}
