\mathbb{P} \left( Y_{\tau_k} = Y^{(\epsilon)}_{\tau_k} \text{ for all } k = 1, \dots, m \right) \ge 1 - C m \Delta_{\epsilon,\gamma,q}.
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.829996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5bcb5e917b54523fc3b7b28c30be9bd6595bd4cd8f0c02237a113e673b2cd193","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:area-odd of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For
