{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.062129+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c23c9d4c99d1128284fef889e5e1e1de7cec50e8b5764b790b0ea27d204b5bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 11 of arXiv:2606.27078, 'Semimartingale Optimal Transport with Jumps: A General Framework and Equivalent Formulatio'] Let $\Theta \subseteq \mathbb{R}^d \times \mathbb{S}_+^d \times \mathcal{L}$ be closed, convex, and satisfy Assumptions \ref{B} and \ref{J}. Moreover, let $\ell$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{ellcontinuous}. Then the function 
