{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.297060+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c3e055b11510e0881648109736b8218143bef19858d405469f81b458572f185","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thmProb9 of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] For any given $\widehat{G} \subset \subset G$ and $\varepsilon \in (0, \frac{T}{2}) $, there exists a constant $\mathcal{C}>0$ such that for some generic constant $ \gamma \in (0,1) $,
