{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.196589+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cfcf0247845e570bab9b524cbe1eb11d1294d4d08c30b71f4955804d1d2278f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 30 (digit profile) of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Recall the definition of $\mathsf Q$ in \eqref{eq:P-Q-def} and definition of $T$ in \eqref{def:set-t}. For $y\in \mathcal A_{\rmleft}$ and $z\in \mathcal A_{\rmright}$ and $x\in A_{y,z}$, the \textbf{digit profile} of $x$ is
