{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.719299+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d4dd375c61fe2849987ff298faf3807b2906365392f591792b5e5e4eba9aa7b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Mollified population regression) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] Let \(\bm v^{z,\varepsilon}\) be the Doob control of \(Q^{z,\varepsilon}\), and let \(\bm u^{\beta,\varepsilon}\) be the Doob control of \(P^{\beta,\varepsilon}\). Then
