{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.783689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d6dba1c252ffa16db84daa197135287acb0629a90ae873bda3aba29222ee159","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 26 (Total-variation principle for dissipated-energy Einstein--Navier--Stokes flows) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Under the conditions in \autoref{proposition-JJJ-NS}, the following total variation bound holds for sufficiently regular solutions: 
