{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.335653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f6dfa94af514cd3625e222679d69103616f0c73a6b4926070cab310f1467451","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=\left(V,E\right)$ be a locally finite weighted graph satisfying the $CD\psi\left(n,-K\right)$ condition with $K\geq0$ where $\psi\in C^{1}\left(0,+\infty\right)$ is a concave function with $\psi^\prime \left(1\right)>0$. Assume that $g\le0$ is a $d$-Lipschitz function. Then for any $\tau,\lambda>0$, there exists a constant $C\left(\lambda,d,\psi,D_{\mu}\right)>0$ depending only on $\lambda,d,\psi,D_{\mu}$ such that 
