{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.680559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f6e668e2cdda33fe5863a0753c5e625ba460e23b6a51ffc729554d883e03404","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] We fix $c_0 \in L^\infty(\R^2)\cap L^1(\R^2)$ and $\theta>0$, $\lambda>0$.
There exists a constant $A$ such that for all $t> 0$, all $x\in\R^2$, all $\e\in [0,1]$,
\begin{equation}
|K^{\theta,\lambda}_t(x)|\leq A (t+|x|^2)^{-1} \quad \text{and} \quad 
|(\phi_\e \ast K^{\theta,\lambda}_t)(x)|\leq A \int_{\R^2} (t+|x-\sqrt \e y|^2)^{-1} \phi(y)\dd y.
\end{equation}
For any $\alpha>0$, any $t>0$, any $x\in \R^2$, any $\e\in [0,1]$,
\begin{align}
|\nabla K^{\theta,\lambda}_t(x)|\leq &
C_3(\theta,\alpha)(t+\alpha |x|^2)^{-\frac{3}{2}}, \quad \text{where} \quad C_3(\theta,\alpha)=\frac{\sqrt \theta C_0\big(\frac{4\alpha}{\theta}\big)}{4\pi}, \\
|\nabla (\phi_\e \ast K^{\theta,\lambda}_t)(x)|\leq& 
C_3(\theta,\alpha)\int_{\R^2}(t+\alpha |x-\sqrt\e y|^2)^{-\frac{3}{2}}\phi(y)\dd y.

\end{align}
There exists $A>0$ depending on $\theta$, $c_0$ and $\phi$ such that for any $t>0$, any $\e\in [0,1]$,
\begin{equation}
||\nabla (\phi_{\e}\ast b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_t) ||_{L^\infty(\R^2)}\leq  A (\e+t)^{-\frac 1 2}.
\end{equation}
For all $t\geq 0$, it holds that
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\e\to 0}\int_0^t ||\nabla \phi_{\e}\ast b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_{s} - \nabla b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_{s}||_{L^\infty(\R^2)} 
\dd s=0.
\end{equation}
For all $s>0$, if $x_n\to x$ and $\e_n\to 0$, then
\begin{equation}
(\nabla \phi_{\e_n}\ast b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_{s})(x_n)\to \nabla b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_{s}(x).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:02:34.821612+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f73edff046edfe4aaf3df0b4802cc52bf5243ff7cb51241ba67353eb2c14c01","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 17 (Uniform small-$r$ boundary entry estimate) of arXiv:2607.19752, 'Weak Equilibrium Measures and Capacity--Hitting Identities\\ for the Hypoelliptic Third-Or'] Let $\Sigma\in\{\partial A,\partial B,\partial\calD\}$, $M<\infty$, and
