{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.670778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f7a1be7136e758252cf15be159355826250f526b0dbac4b096350ec7cb4f5fb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.24392, 'Numerical approximation of Markovian BSDEs in infinite horizon and elliptic PDEs'] When the generator of the BSDE \eqref{eq:BSDEinfinitehorizon} does not depend on the $Z$ process, that is $f(x, y, z) = f(x, y)$, the conclusions of Proposition \ref{pr:Lpestimate} remain true under the same assumptions and with the following contraction constants:
