{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.906806+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f80836d1dd0a6c74cdfbbd594d3018b85ce4b6ed5e52cf9ed09fa9e5950e72d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:many-codim-L of arXiv:2608.26707, 'An Exponential Lower Bound for the Permanent\\of Random Bernoulli Matrix'] Let $L\geq1$, let $k\leq n-3L$, and condition on $\mathcal{F}_k$.
Suppose that $A_0\in\binom{[n]}{k}$ is $\lambda$-heavy, and set $q=\floor{\frac{n-k}{2L}}.$ Then, after exposing rows $k+1,\dots,n-L$, with conditional probability at least $1-Ce^{-cL}$ there exist at least $\left\lfloor q/2\right\rfloor$ $\lambda$-heavy sets
