{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.726446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f914ce3a492f902eeb716dfce7a0abb922e07ff2c327057519b9abe3b912e33","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:BP of arXiv:2411.19163, '\bfseries Random polytopes in convex bodies:\\ Bridging the gap between extremal container'] Let $f:(\mathbb{R}^d)^{d}\to\mathbb{R}$ be a non-negative measurable function. Then,
