{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.686157+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fd0b1c7e7c4cca21b0502f1f662803a48720c7f782c0a06731dcd7c46162a52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor degree-times-uniform of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Let $\set{\left(\mathscr{E}_{j,k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}:j\geqslant 0}$ be \emph{iid} copies of $\left(\mathscr{E}_{k-1\leadsto k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}$ and $T_1$ be an exponential random variable of rate $1$ independent of $\set{\left(\mathscr{E}_{j,k}\right)_{k\geqslant 1}:j\geqslant 0}$. Then 
