{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.786173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_601ce14c6d8a02c31fae58e58912ed3b1c54b1ab17c1d5c3f4fbed310ae4ee9b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 21 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $p \in \mathbb{R}[z_1, z_2]$ be a real polynomial with bidegree $(n,m)$, without zeros in the right bihalfplane $\RHPtwo$. Then $p$ admits a determinantal representation 
