{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:55:18.920663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_607140eaa1d336025c0ec96ccf303f43816d0488194c7f73cd66b27db83ba61e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:FH10.5 of arXiv:2601.21762, 'Navier-Stokes with a fractional transport noise as a limit of multi-scale dynamics'] Let $(X,Y)=(X^i,Y^i)_i$ be a centered Gaussian process on $[0,T]$, such that $(X^i,Y^i)$ is independent of 
    $(X^j, Y^j)$ when $i \neq j$. Assume that there exists $\rho \in [1,2)$, and $\{M_i\}\in \ell^1$, such that 
    \begin{align*}
        \norm{R_{X^i}}_{\rho,[s,t]^2} &\leq M_i |t-s|^{\frac{1}{\rho}}, \qquad
        \norm{R_{Y^i}}_{\rho,[s,t]^2} \leq M_i |t-s|^{\frac{1}{\rho}}, \quad 
        \norm{R_{X^i-Y^i}}_{\rho,[s,t]^2} &\leq \epsilon^2 M_i |t-s|^{\frac{1}{\rho}},
    \end{align*}
for all $i\geq 1$ and $0\leq s \leq t \leq T.$ Then
    \begin{itemize}
        \item [a)] For every $q\in [1,\infty)$ and for all $0\leq s \leq t \leq T$,
       $$
            \mathbb{E} \left[\norm{Y_{s,t} - X_{s,t}}^q \right]^{\frac{1}{q}} \lesssim \epsilon \sqrt{\left\| M \right\|_{\ell^1}}
            |t-s|^{\frac{1}{2\rho}}, \qquad 
            \mathbb{E} \left[\norm{\mathbb{Y}_{s,t} - \mathbb{X}_{s,t}}^q \right]^{\frac{1}{q}} \lesssim \epsilon \left\| M \right\|_{\ell^1}
            |t-s|^{\frac{1}{\rho}}.
$$
        \item [b)] For any $\alpha < \frac{1}{2\rho}$ and $q\in [1,\infty)$, one has
        \begin{align*}
            \mathbb{E} \left[\left\| Y-X \right\|_\alpha^q\right]^{\frac{1}{q}} &\lesssim \epsilon \sqrt{\left\| M \right\|_{\ell^1}}, \qquad
            \mathbb{E} \left[\norm{\mathbb{Y}-\mathbb{X}}_{2\alpha}^q\right]^{\frac{1}{q}} \lesssim \epsilon \left\| M \right\|_{\ell^1}.
        \end{align*}
        \item[c)] For $\rho \in [1, \frac{3}{2})$ and any $\alpha \in (\frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{2\rho})$ , $q<\infty$ one has 
       $$ \mathbb{E}\left[\rho_\alpha(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})^q \right]^{\frac{1}{q}} \lesssim \epsilon. $$
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.674161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6072baee99818c0387fb0699d620decc9fb14fc20d7c4f1d1a8ae37dd01703ce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 40 (Equivalence of intrinsic and fixed-chart norms) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Fix \(n\), \(m\geq2\), \(\sigma\in(0,1)\), \(\Lambda\geq1\), and \(L>0\).
Suppose that
\(\PBG_m(s;\Lambda;[a,b])\) holds and \(b-a\leq L\).  Let
\(\|\cdot\|_{X_{s,{\mathrm{fc}}}^m[a,b]}\) and
\(\|\cdot\|_{Y_{s,{\mathrm{fc}}}^m[a,b]}\) denote the suprema of the Euclidean
component norms in the fixed lifted atlas supplied by
Lemma~\ref{lem:uniform-parabolic-atlas}.  Then there is
\(C=C(n,m,\sigma,\Lambda,L)\) such that every deck-invariant tensor \(U\)
satisfies
\begin{align}
 C^{-1}\|U\|_{X_s^m[a,b]}
 &\leq \|U\|_{X_{s,{\mathrm{fc}}}^m[a,b]}
 \leq C\|U\|_{X_s^m[a,b]},                                      \\
 C^{-1}\|U\|_{Y_s^m[a,b]}
 &\leq \|U\|_{Y_{s,{\mathrm{fc}}}^m[a,b]}
 \leq C\|U\|_{Y_s^m[a,b]}.                                      
\end{align}
The analogous comparison holds for every spatial
\(C^{k,\sigma}\)-norm with \(0\leq k\leq m\).  For tensors on the universal
cover that are not deck-invariant, the same local comparison holds with the
fixed-chart side interpreted as the uniformly local norm.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:59:45.565621+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6079c680287d538599fc7f99e34f628eec7eb475e3c065ca8f9422f22d2de4e5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: Yu replace sum by min of arXiv:2411.17109, 'On the maximal correlation of some stochastic processes'] Let $X_1,X_2,\ldots,X_n$ be i.i.d. real-valued random variables. Let $1\leq \ell+1\leq m\leq n$. Then we have that
