{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.582319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6205323520a110e485824a9e5e10c1f6a5ff95e71e05481bcfb17ff5c5eeae52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop intro of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $1<p<2$ and $\varphi(x)=|x|^{-s}$. Then, $(X^a_p,\mathscr W_{gap,p})$ is a complete geodesic metric space. The free energy $\mathcal F_\beta$ is weakly $\lambda$-geodesically convex on $(X^a_p,\mathscr W_{gap,p})$ with $\lambda=\beta a^{-\frac{2-p}{p}}>0$, i.e.\ for $\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1\in X^a_p$ there is a constant speed geodesic $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t\in[0,1]}$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq 1$
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_t)\leq (1-t) \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_0)+t \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_1)-\lambda \frac{t(1-t)}{2} \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.722518+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62076cf0d81b055301f9e23197ec3400975f5a03dab1dbf3354585121969b5e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma finitepoments of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Consider a subset $\mathcal V$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \{p|_S\text{  for some polynomial }p:\mathbb R^d\to \mathbb R\}\subseteq \mathcal V\subseteq \mathcal O(S)
    \end{align}
    and let $X=(X_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ be an $S$-valued $\mathcal{V}$-holomorphic process. Then $\int_{\mathbb R^d}\|\xi\|^k \ K(x,d\xi)<\infty$ for all  for all $k\geq 2$ and $x\in S$, and the characteristics $(b,a,K)$ of $X$ satisfy
 \begin{align}
        &b_i(\cdot)\in \mathcal{O}(S), \quad \text{for all }i\in\{1,\dots,d\},\\
        &a_{ij}(\cdot)+\int_{\mathbb R^d}\xi_i\xi_j K(\cdot,d\xi)\in\mathcal{O}(S), \quad \text{for all }i,j\in\{1,\dots,d\}^2,\nonumber \\
        &\int_{\mathbb R^d}\xi^\beta  K(\cdot,d\xi)\in\mathcal{O}(S), \quad  \text{for all }\beta\in \mathbb{N}^d_0,\ |\beta|\geq3. \nonumber 
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_620a4076e0a21b94bac02298eb5db06791fe03c003c5b1f8511294598646396e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 18 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d \geq 2$.  
	There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $G$ subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$, every $\beta\geq \beta_c/2$, every $x\in V(G)$ and $zw\in E(G)$, 
\begin{equation}
	\frac{1}{C}\langle \sigma_x \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta} \leq \langle \sigma_x \sigma_z \rangle_{G, \beta} \leq  C \langle \sigma_x \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta}.
\end{equation}
Similarly, for any $\mathsf{h}\in (\mathbb{R}^+)^V$ and $zw \in E(G)$,
	\begin{equation}
		\langle \sigma_z \rangle_{G, \beta, \mathsf{h}} \leq C \langle \sigma_w \rangle_{G, \beta, \mathsf{h}}
	\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.187685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6210e7e6620becbb225c3ceab5ec06c6333e4e5d77482c6ffcac647d82070b31","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:freezing-ising of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] For any $B\in \R$, the ferromagnetic Ising measure on $T^\k$ with freezing temperature and 
         plus/minus boundary condition are defined as follows: 
    \begin{equation}
        \ising_\k^+(\infty,B)=\ising_\k^+(\infty)\coloneqq \delta_{T^{\k,+}},\quad \ising_\k^-(\infty,B)=\ising_\k^-(\infty)\coloneqq \delta_{T^{\k,-}}.
    \end{equation}

         In the antiferromagnetic regime, for any $B\in \R$, extend the definition of the unique $\TIS$ Ising measure $\ising_\k^\sharp$ to the following antiferromagnetic Ising measure on $T^\k$ with freezing temperature: 
    \begin{equation}
        \ising_\k^{\sharp}(-\infty,B)=\ising_\k^{\sharp}(-\infty)\coloneqq \frac{1}{2}\delta_{T^{\k,\pm}}+\frac{1}{2}\delta_{T^{k,\mp}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6218aae5a8b461735cf01889c29d68e1f0ad20d4209cfde76337e9e3bfc4b8e5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 52 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $x\in \Lambda_n$ and $y\sim x$. One has
\begin{equation}
	\mathbf P^{\emptyset}_{\beta_c}[y\connect{\mathcal M_n\:}\mathbb H_n]=\langle \sigma_y\sigma_{\mathcal R_n(y)}\rangle_{\beta_c},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
    \mathbf E^{\emptyset}_{\beta_c}\Big[\mathds{1}\{0,x\in \mathcal{S}_n,\: y \xleftrightarrow[]{\:\mathcal M_n\:} \mathbb H_n \}\langle\sigma_0\sigma_x\rangle_{\mathcal{S}_n,\beta}\Big]
    \leq
   \Big(\langle \sigma_0\sigma_x\rangle_{\beta_c}-\langle \sigma_0\sigma_{\mathcal{R}_n(x)}\rangle_{\beta_c}\Big)\langle \sigma_y \sigma_{\mathcal{R}_n(y)}\rangle_{\beta_c}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

