{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.700562+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62245600834837fd013768bde4b07a720769c78df85fd2b43559b75a68290e04","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem asympdisc of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma > 0$ is chosen small enough then, for any $\eta > 0$ small enough (depending only~on~$\gamma$) we have that, for all $k$ sufficiently large and $T \in [2k,{\rm e}^{\frac{1}{2}k^\gamma}]$, 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{P} \Big( \Big\{ \sqrt{ \widehat{T}_{(v)}(1)} = u \Big\} \cap \mathcal J^{\eta,[1,T-1]}_{(v)} \setminus \Big( \mathcal L_{(v)}^{\eta,[1,T-1]} \cap \mathcal T_{(v)}^{\eta,[2,T-1]}\Big)
		\Big) = r_{k,T}(\widehat{u},\widehat{v})o_k(1)
	\end{equation} holds uniformly over all $u \in \mathcal R^{\eta}_k(1)$ and $v \in \mathcal R^\eta_k(T)$, where $r_{k,T}$ is as in (equation eq:funcfg of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.773951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62282c722c8b9e15ab919e04228a9c84f5a9158372f067d7ab87c9f158c7c4d1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 72 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation from Definition \ref{Def.AuxLE2}. Define the $\llbracket 1,2k_1 + 2\rrbracket$-indexed geometric line ensemble $\tilde{\mathfrak{L}}^{\mathrm{bot},N} = \{\tilde{L}^{\mathrm{bot},N}_{i}\}_{i = 1}^{2k_1 + 2}$ on $\llbracket 0, \hat{B}_N\rrbracket$, by
\begin{equation}
 \tilde{L}^{\mathrm{bot},N}_{i}(s) = L^{\mathrm{bot},N}_{i}(s) = L_{i+1}^N(s) \mbox{ for } i \in \llbracket 1, 2k_1 + 2 \rrbracket, s \in \llbracket 0, \hat{B}_N \rrbracket.
 \end{equation}
Then, for any sequence of measurable sets $A_N \subseteq C(\llbracket 1, 2k_1 + 2\rrbracket \times [0, \hat{B}_N])$, we have
