{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.780368+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_623b424d9c3bb498f978efe2d0be1bbbc8bdd8320daf53b0c2684d6efb0413fc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 1 of arXiv:2603.29549, 'Multitype PCR branching processes'] For given $K>0$, vector $\bar v$ such that for some $1\le d_0\le d$, 
\begin{equation}
1\ge v_1=\ldots=v_{d_0}>v_{d_0+1}\ge \ldots\ge v_d>0,
\end{equation}
and initial state
 $\bar  Z(0)\in\mathbb N^d$,
 define a Markov chain  
 $\bar  Z(0), \bar  Z(1), \bar  Z(2), \ldots$,
 by the recursion
\begin{equation}
Z_i(n)=Z_i(n-1)+\sum_{j=1}^{Z_i(n-1)}\xi_{j}\big(v_i,K,Z(n-1)\big), \quad n\in \mathbb N,\quad i=1,\ldots, d,
\end{equation}
where the summands, conditioned on $Z(n-1)=z$, are independent Bernoulli random variables with success probabilities
\begin{equation}
\P(\xi_{j}(v_i,K,z)=1)=\frac{v_iK}{K+z}.
\end{equation}
Such a Markov chain $\bar  Z(n)$ will be called a multitype PCR (MPCR) branching process with parameters $(K,\bar v)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.981371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_623f5788450462bce7f93330a56abc00a74c964a4270cce64de24d7ffce0a419","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lm:connected of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Fix $k \geq 1$ and suppose $S = (\bm e_1, \bm e_2, \ldots, \bm e_k)$ be a collection of hyperedges (not necessarily distinct) of size $r \geq 2$ such that the hypergraph formed the union of the edges in $S$ is connected and $|\bigcup_{j=1}^k \bm e_j| <  b r-b+1$, where $b$ is the number of distinct hyperedges in $S$. Then there exists an ordering (permutation) $\sigma: [k] \rightarrow [k] $ such that the following hold: 
\begin{itemize}
\item for every $i \in [2, k]$, $t_i(\sigma)  \geq 1$, and  

\item for some $i \in [2, k]$, $t_i(\sigma) \in [2, r-1] $, 
\end{itemize} 
where 
$$t_i(\sigma) = \left|\bm e_{\sigma(i)} \bigcap \left(\bigcup_{j = 1}^{i-1}\bm e_{\sigma(j)}\right) \right| , $$ 
for $i \in [2, r]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.289875+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_624021662d55a7296ce435015d70927151858a30419a91fab67eee8e79d96be9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] For each $n \in \N$, let $X^n$ be a weak solution of
    \begin{equation*}
        X^n(t) = X^n(0) + \int_0^t \overline{b}^n(s,X^n) \, ds + \int_0^t \overline{\sigma}^n(s,X^n) \, dW^n(s), \quad t\in[0,T],
    \end{equation*}
    where $\overline{b}^n : [0,T] \times C([0,T],\R^d) \to \R^d $ and $\overline{\sigma}^n : [0,T] \times C([0,T],\R^d) \to \R^{d\times m}$ are continuous non-anticipative functionals satisfying the linear growth Assumption~\ref{LG-Condition} with a common constant $C_{LG}$.
