{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.357192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62411ff8b285ec221a4bf009e8b39604e669b5604f684229b95381e7d71c8899","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(\beta\in (0,1/6)\). There are \(c,n_0,\lambda_0, r_0\geq 0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), any \(\lambda\geq \lambda_0\), and any \(r_0 \sqrt{\lambda}n^{2/3}\leq k \leq n-r_0 \sqrt{\lambda} n^{2/3}\),
    \begin{equation*}
        P\bigl( W_{k}\geq \lambda n^{1/3}\bigr)
        \leq
        \begin{cases}
            e^{-c\lambda^{3/2}} & \text{ if } \lambda \leq n^{\beta},
            \\
            e^{-c\lambda } & \text{ if } \lambda > n^{\beta}.
        \end{cases}
    \end{equation*}
     In particular, for any \(p\geq 0\), there is \(C_p\in (0,+\infty)\) uniform over \(n,k\) as above such that \(E(W_k^p) \leq C_pn^{p/3}\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:42:39.074300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6243de32751d7f7ff4a47a277d0cca58f385b04694892f6c494ddb1188a7a293","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6. lem: distance between original and trace of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Fix $(F, R, \rho, \nu) \in \mathbb{F}$.
  Assume that, for some $\lambda > 1$, $r>0$, and $\delta > 0$,
  \begin{equation}
