=\frac{m\beta}{4(m\beta-1)(2m+1)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.033755+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62c617ae327e27a9cfb9b090bf04d1b60b1591a4e26eb0b2e5b3c1e512d561fd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Long-time bounds for the propagated test functionals) of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Assume Assumption~\ref{ass:coeff-level-new}, and let $ \varphi \in C_b^7\left( \R^d \right) $.
