	\end{equation*}
	The value of $s_F$ is not assumed to be optimal.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.917943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62dedc3c5b1fc56a6553f59975b3fc2d45092134e630b3e59e1854048a0c52e1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $G$ be a finite group, let $n\geqslant2$, and let $w$ be as in \eqref{eq:intro-weight}.  Then
