{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.289624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62f6055599c86ea8523790ab17daecffd39e892028561776f659af018e4f7750","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 21 of arXiv:2604.25725, 'What is The Probability That A Random Graph With A Given Degree Sequence is Connected?'] For any $m$ large enough, $0<\gamma<1$, $0<\epsilon<10^{-6}$, $n_1<\eps m$, $n_2 \le 10^{-6}m$, $0<C \le m^{\gamma /20}$,  $i \ge 1$, and $0\leq r\le C(\log m)^2$, the following holds: if $2|E(H_{i-1})|+X_{i-1} \le \epsilon m$ then, conditioned on $H_{i-1}$,
