{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863272+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_62fb33e10ba2278028c8b63c446e11c5922d788dc2091b0b35b6040076a0b0df","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $a_0,a_1,b_0,b_1>0$ be positive numbers and let $\delta \in (0,1)$. Assume that there is some $0<c\le 1\le C<\infty$ such that
