{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.299498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_636ee5a3ffdf32cdd4a74943237b6421dbed8a59ab976ec78b058fe08f329212","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7463 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ ( X, U ) $ be a $ ( c, q ) $-regular innovation
on a measurable set $ \mathcal V $ and let $ ( \theta_n ) $ be an \RMSprop\ algorithm
with arbitrary parameter tuple $ ( \beta, \varepsilon, (\gamma_n), \theta_0 ) $ as in the introduction.
Let $ n_0 \in {\mathbb N}_0 $ and let $ \tau $ be the stopping time given by
