\end{align}
where \(\rho_{p,G}(\Sigma)\) is as in Theorem~(thm:main1 of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.116007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_639468c3a81c9c6d4a259d0c3a1c1531c37f560be2ebbe408a0a50f8223d5e7b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] On ${\mathbb{R}}^d$ ($d\ge 3$),  we say a function $h: {\mathbb{R}}^d\rightarrow {\mathbb{R}}$ is in Kato class $\mathbf{K}_{d,k}$ (for $k=1,2$) if
