{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.645664+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6398878165237e528dcf40028a14bf94867441b1fabf439c768f910b1273c0c1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Two-valued sets of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $a,b\in \mathbb R$ and let $u$ be a harmonic function in $D$. Let $\phi$ be a GFF with boundary condition $u$ in $D$.  We say that a random closed set $\mathds A_{-a,b}^u$ is a two-valued set with boundary condition $u$ if
\begin{itemize}
    \item $(\phi,\mathds A_{-a,b}^u)$ is a local set,
    \item there exists a random function $h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}$ such that 
    \[
        (\phi_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u},f)=\int_{D\backslash \mathds A_{-a,b}^u} h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}(z) f(z)dz
        \quad \text{a.s.}
    \]
    for all $f \in C_c^\infty(D)$,
    \item the function $h_{\mathds A_{-a,b}^u}-u$ takes values in the set $\{-a,b\}$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

