{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.276894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_643094e6fa1d01383a7be3ebdedb9b72c0d9e29bb845125cfa9fb1f151ec1e4a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2604.24664, 'Absolute continuity of Rosenblatt measures'] Let $\alpha > 0$ and $f \in L^1([0, T])$. The \emph{left} and \emph{right  Riemann--Liouville fractional integrals of $f$ of order $\alpha$} are defined by
