{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:58:38.146921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6457dccd31fded4588f4a0a88bd48c9953b7292e42cc2112a999122bfc1f2202","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:optimal of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For each $\alpha>0$, there exists a constant $c_\alpha$ such that for any label-invariant estimator $\widehat{\sigma}$, and any $n\ge 2$,
