{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.752028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_645f262324604036e06e1ed74adc2afd34f478ab379d48ed2bf4d0743e838559","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] If $x\ne 0$ is not an eigenvalue of $\mathcal Q_1$, then it is an eigenvalue of $\widetilde{\mathcal Q}_1$ if and only if
