{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:13:21.258428+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d668062d5d6fc364171e0336120b1781d97609a6287c77f7bb13c10daaa4da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2609.01473, 'Keller sequences of exact $\infty$-categories'] Suppose that the localisation $p^l\colon \cal{C} \to \cal{B}^l$ sends cocartesian squares in $\cal{C}$ with parallel maps inclusions to cocartesian squares in $\cal{B}^l$.
