{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.668559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64dca6d92c2fd1efe475f74b002584ee82e078a390c587dad5c9f5c4c2427994","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 16 of arXiv:2604.24189, 'Malliavin calculus and densities for chaos-driven stochastic differential equations'] Let $d$ be a positive integer and let $\mathbf{Y}=\left(Y_1, \ldots, Y_d\right)$ be a random vector satisfying the following two conditions:
