{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.679767+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64f50d6d1f1a29d3a9635ff74dfea5b1664f8f4ac65647509c8e16df9e6fb736","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2607.25986, 'Asymptotics of a two-species particle system associated to the doubly parabolic Keller-Seg'] Consider the process $(U^{1,N,M,\e}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ defined by
\begin{align*}
U^{1,N,M,\e}_t=&(\nu^{1,N,M,\e}_t\ast \nabla \phi_{\e})(X^{1,N,M,\e}_t)-(\nabla \phi_{\e}\ast b^{c_0,\theta,\lambda}_t)(X^{1,N,M,\e}_t)\\
&-\frac1{N-1} \sum_{j \in I_N,j\neq 1}\int_0^t (\nabla \phi_\e\ast K^{\theta,\lambda}_{t-s})(X^{1,N,M,\e}_t-X^{j,N,M,\e}_s)\dd s.
\end{align*}
For any $\sigma\in (0,\frac12]$, any $T>0$, there exists a constant
$A_{\sigma,T}$ (also depending on $\lambda,\theta,c_0$) such that for all $N\geq 2$, all $M>0$, all $\e\in (0,1]$,
