{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.049608+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_657711e3004e509c1b0825430409ddf8d18567bc29f9915bc8ca9b3b5e780383","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mylem 8 (Corollary 1.4 in \cite{RV_imrn}) of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] Consider a random vector $X = (X_1,...,X_n)$ where $X_i$ are real-valued independent random variables. Let $t, b \ge  0$ be such that
