{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.457001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_659568cb1225aa4a333c7f4f84e53f396d7944474a4685dce789e45ce6ba1d7f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 23 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma >0$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$ and $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$. Then
\begin{align} 
 \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ \frac{\Theta(n) K_n}{\sqrt{n}} \int_s^t \dd r \sum_x \sum_{y=x+1}^{\infty} [  H ( \tfrac{y - r v_n }{n}  ) - H ( \tfrac{x - r v_n }{n}  )  ] a(y-x)   \bar{\xi} _x^{\alpha}( \eta_s^n ) \bar{\xi} _y^{\beta}( \eta_r^n ) \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq \widehat{C} (t-s)^{2} f_1(n),
 \end{align}
where $f_1:\mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ is given by
\begin{align*}
\forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad f_1(n):= \begin{dcases}
	 1/n, \quad & \gamma \in (0 , \; 1/2), \\
