holds for some $c_0,C_0>0$, which do not depend on $j$ and $n$, and all $n\in \N$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.576801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6661814f8d7037cd7bcd01e4f12031057a760d1f39c05db82238232110764b0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm2ch5 of arXiv:2512.09308, 'On asymptotic behavior of solutions to random fractional Riesz-Bessel equations with cycli'] Let $u(t,x)$, $t > 0$, $x \in \mathbb{R}$, denote the random field defined by equations~{\rm ((modch5 of the paper))} and~{\rm((modCch5 of the paper))} with the random initial condition $\xi(x),$ which covariance function satisfies Assumption~~{\rm (Asumptionmain of the paper)} with $A_0\neq0$. Then, for $\alpha>\kappa_0/2$, if $\varepsilon \to 0$, the finite-dimentional distributions of the random fields
\[
