    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.383066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66ca5967542686bb8c8fa7edb5deca367f0da8b476f23a2c9bb80a70d4026cd1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:local_hajek of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] As in (equation eq:hatngrhovdef of the paper), let us write
\begin{equation}
    \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(x) = \mathsf{N}_G^{\rho \to v}(x) - \mathsf{d}_\rho p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \mathsf{deg}_v(x).
\end{equation}
Then for all $\zeta \in (0,\frac{3}{4})$, there is some $c > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ \mleft| \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(X) - \mathbb{E} \mleft[ \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(X) \mright]\mright| > n^{\mathsf{v}-1.75+\zeta} \mright]
    \leq \Exp{-c n^{\frac{4}{3} \zeta}}.
\end{equation}
In particular, for all $\xi > 0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Var} \mleft[
        \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G^{\rho \to v}(x)
    \mright] \lesssim n^{2\mathsf{v} - 3.5 + \xi}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.321648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66cbbc2716b0c62a2b9e282c618023c17fb578249ea6c5997b4a3ccef38eb368","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 36 (Laplace benchmark) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] The standard Laplace variable $\Lap$ has density
