{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.777354+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6709a6d3e2b25efe4d91c21550161bab603b4e0a222d0a3ef759ba5a174bcb65","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 10 of arXiv:2603.25459, 'Cram\'{e}r-type moderate deviation for double index permutation statistics'] Let $(W,W^{\prime})$, $\Delta$, $D$ and $D^{*}$ be defined as in Theorem \ref{thm-general-MD}. Assume that there exits a constant $\tau_0>0$ such that for all $0\leq t\leq \tau_0$,
\begin{itemize}
    \item [$(B_{1}):$] $\mathbb{E}\{\big|1-\frac{1}{2\lambda}\mathbb{E}\{D\Delta|W\}\big|e^{tW}\}\leq \kappa_1(t)e^{t^2/2}$,
    \item [$(B_{2}):$] $\mathbb{E}\{|R|e^{tW}\}\leq \kappa_2(t)e^{t^2/2}$,
\end{itemize}
where $\kappa_{1}(\cdot)$ and $\kappa_{2}(\cdot)$ are nondecreasing functions satisfying that $\kappa_{1}(\tau_0)<\infty$ and $\kappa_{2}(\tau_0)<\infty$. Then, for $0\leq z \leq \tau_{0}$
\begin{align}
    \left|\frac{\mathbb{P}(W>z)}{1-\Phi(z)}-1\right|\leq 31\left[(1+z^2)(\kappa_{1}(z)+\delta(1+\delta_{3}(z)+\kappa_{2}(z)))+(1+z)\kappa_{2}(z)\right]
\end{align}
where 
\begin{align}
    \delta_{3}(z) = [z(1+z\delta+2\delta_{1}(z))+(2+z\delta)\delta_{2}(z)](1+3e\delta)e^{\frac{z^2}{2}(z\delta+2\delta_{1}(z))+3z\delta_{2}(z)}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.389221+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6711d2615e170fccbed7a328b747de2f8b12d33a44d43434f17396d542ba437c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:dynamic_margulis_russo of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] Given any Boolean function $\mathfrak{f}: \{0,1\}^{n} \to \{0,1\}$, the functional $Q_{\varepsilon}(\mathfrak{f})$ is differentiable in $\varepsilon$ and
