{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.570599+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_672b554f8dcd4339f9cf58272866d02ea861aae5ae8ef59b594085034a4d6767","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 2 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>4$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
