where the constant $C_3>0$ is the same one as in (2) of Lemma \ref{Lemma-2-2}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.587948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_674a73d9e68cf3069b28e9c4c54575e27616a9e9a40706059c4602c230c6c50a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition StoFubiniThm of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] Let $T\geq 0$, $m(dt)$ be a $\sigma$-finite measure on $\mathbb{R}_+$ and $h$ be a measurable function on $\mathbb{R}_+$ such that
 \begin{eqnarray*}
  \int_0^T \big|h(T-t)\big|  \cdot \bigg( \int_0^t |f(s)|^2\, ds +\int_0^t  \int_0^\infty \big| g(s,y) \big|^2\, \mu(dy)\,ds \bigg)\,m(dt)  <\infty .
 \end{eqnarray*}
 If $\sup_{t\in[0,T]}  X(t)  <\infty$ a.s., we have
 \begin{eqnarray}
  \int_0^T h(T-t)  B(f,t)\, m(dt) 
  \!\!\!&=\!\!\!&  \int_0^T \int_0^{X(s)} \bigg( \int_s^{T} h(T-t)f(t-s)\, m(dt) \bigg)B(ds,dz) 
 \end{eqnarray}
 and 
 \begin{eqnarray}
  \int_0^T h(T-t)   \widetilde{N}(g,t)\, m(dt)  
