 \end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.424288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_674f9fb3680d9d71b19c76cacc1ed3b1cb5b103e536765cfcdcb7a33fc272d59","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:J-edge of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:GOE-mean-LDP}
Let \(\rho_N(x)\,\mathrm d x\) be the normalized expected empirical measure of the \(N\)-dimensional GOE in the normalization used in [ABAC].  These probability measures satisfy a large-deviation principle at speed \(N\) with good rate function
\begin{equation}
 J_{\rm edge}(x)=
 \begin{cases}
 0,&\left\lvertx\right\rvert\le\sqrt2,\\[1mm]
 \displaystyle\int_{\sqrt2}^{\left\lvertx\right\rvert}\sqrt{z^2-2}\,\mathrm d z,
 &\left\lvertx\right\rvert>\sqrt2.
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
Consequently, if \(W\) is continuous and \(W(x)\le C-c_0x^2\) for some \(c_0>0\), then
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \int_\mathbb R e^{NW(x)}\rho_N(x)\,\mathrm d x
 =\sup_{x\in\mathbb R}\{W(x)-J_{\rm edge}(x)\}.
\end{equation}
For every compact interval \(K\) with nonempty interior, the same conclusion holds with both the integral and supremum restricted to \(K\).","status":"unverified"}

