{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.545043+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67f34965ddd49f4190f5f6c014ee6ffadcc4c218ffd4d741fe57d45449ce7144","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 45 (Property~\ref{prop:digits}: Matching digits) of arXiv:2603.28734, 'Free energy analyticity of the disordered XY model and Debye screening in the 2D Coulomb g'] Consider fixed constants $\epsilon\in[0,1]$ and $k\in\Z_{\geq 0}$.
    We say that a Glauber dynamic $R$ \emph{matches digits up to $(\epsilon,k)$}
    if we may find an event $M\subset\Sigma$ of $\diff\iota$-probability at least $1-\epsilon$ such that:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item For any $u\in V$ and $\iota\in M$, we have
        \[
            \big\{
                \{R_{u,\iota}(\tau)_{1,u}\}_k=\{R_{u,\iota}(\tau')_{1,u}\}_k \text{ for all $\tau,\tau'\in \Pi_G$}
            \big\}
        \]
        \item For any $u\in V$ and $\tau\in\Pi_G$,
        the event $M$ and the random variable $\lfloor R_{u,\iota}(\tau)_{1,u}\rfloor_k$
        are $\diff\iota$-independent.
    \end{itemize}
    The event $M$ is called the \emph{matching event}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.477527+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67f4d3399c811a20ccbc6de6f5e54cb4c47cfa4aa1a06058cfc5b02626a56159","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Wedge expansion) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] At $p=\pc$, the wedge rate and its derivative are given by
\begin{gather}
 \Kn:=I_H(\pc)
 =-3\log\left(\frac{\taud}{1-\taud+\taud^2}\right),
 \\
 \kappa_\delta:=I_H'(\pc)
 =\frac{(1-\taud)^3(1+\taud)(1-\taud+\taud^2)}{\taud^3}>0.

\end{gather}
On some neighborhood $U$ of $\pc$, the high-centered wedge probability has the strong expansion
\begin{equation}
 H_n(p)=n^{-1}e^{-nI_H(p)}\{A_2(p)+o_{C^2(U)}(1)\}.

\end{equation}
Here $A_2(p)$ is smooth and positive. In particular,
\begin{align}
 H_n(\pc)
 &=A_{2,\delta}n^{-1}e^{-n\Kn}\{1+o(1)\},
 \notag\\
 H_n'(\pc)
 &=-\kappa_\delta A_{2,\delta}e^{-n\Kn}\{1+o(1)\},
 \\
 L_n(\pc)&=H_n(\pc),
 \qquad
 L_n'(\pc)=-H_n'(\pc),

\end{align}
where
\begin{equation*}
 A_{2,\delta}:=A_2(\pc)
 =\frac{1+\taud^2+\taud^4}
 {6\pi\sqrt3\,\taud(1-\taud)^2}.
\end{equation*}
Moreover, uniformly for $|p-\pc|\le n^{-1}$,
\begin{equation}
 |H_n''(p)|+|L_n''(p)|=O(ne^{-n\Kn}).

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.365492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67f5752dc399cf6c4038fc695a6ef81eacf25abef0049f0998d490f1b5829ecb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sepstatdetconP of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Under the setup of Lemma~(lem:sepstatdetcon of the paper), assume that (item:kcentralstat of the paper) and~(item:kcentdegsmall of the paper) hold, and, in addition, that the following holds. 
