{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.738460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_680a160f68bb6a522cfe272218b164a733ae2190c72dd189c7d6f4f2e1de7a6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:fourthcumu2 of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (lemma_G_large_2 of the paper), let $B$ be an arbitrary deterministic matrix with $\|B\|\le 1$. Then, we have that
