{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.988786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6870cab5199ea3960acc0f69ff77227e60a6cddc6a5bfdc16503aab21c37803e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:decomp_loc_integral of arXiv:2607.04514, 'Boundary-layer asymptotics for Gaussian-smoothed singular measures'] Assume (ass:standing:measure of the paper), (ass:standing:chart of the paper), and~(ass:standing:density of the paper) of
  (ass:standing of the paper) with \(r\geqslant 2\). Let \(A>0\). There exists \(\sigma_0>0\) and a function
