    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.443511+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_690a652aca6d99435fba40ff6370c6831e6c1af39f0025e9eb67d5a2476d3989","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:V=U of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] If  $t_N \ll n_j = O(N^{1/3})$ and $  \theta\gamma  n^2t_N \ll N$,  then 
