{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.409235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a71daf963de88693e2e1fb46e2f154f977cc19cda2e998b52945c8a37838661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop branchmodel of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Let $B$ be either real half-branch. After reparametrizing $B$ and passing to a finite real Puiseux extension $K/\mathbb{R}((u))_{\mathrm{conv}}$ with residue field $\mathbb R$, there exist $\rho_B: \pi_1(M) \to SL_2(K)$ and $C_i \in SL_2(K)$, $i = 1, 2$ such that:
