{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:00:30.488739+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6be158b4e8a2182220ea46f5993c03a756e27b8630338fe912be736153269c7a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 8 of arXiv:2607.03924, 'Tree Coordinates and Range Martingales for Positive Operator-Valued Measures'] For a finite word $w$ and any $n\geq\left|w\right|$,
let $P^{\left(n\right)}_{w}$ be the orthogonal projection of $K_{n}$
onto 
\[
\bigoplus_{\left|u\right|=n,\,u\succeq w}H_{u}
\]
where $u\succeq w$ means $u$ extends $w$. Then 
\begin{equation}
P^{\left(n+1\right)}_{w}J_{n}=J_{n}P^{\left(n\right)}_{w},\qquad n\geq\left|w\right|.
\end{equation}
Hence there are projections $P_{w}\in B\left(K_{E}\right)$ such that
\begin{equation}
P_{w}U_{n}=U_{n}P^{\left(n\right)}_{w},\qquad n\geq\left|w\right|.
\end{equation}
Moreover, there is a unique PVM 
\[
P:\mathcal{B}\left(\Omega_{m}\right)\to B\left(K_{E}\right)
\]
such that 
\begin{equation}
P\left(\left[w\right]\right)=P_{w}
\end{equation}
for every finite word $w$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.634061+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6be4a3041a92c8ad7d9bcbdcee23af41d779117118546fe1624b51f904bd7332","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:log.likelihood.local.region.bounds of arXiv:2607.02013, 'Resolution of the Detection Threshold Conjecture for Random Geometric Graphs in the $d>n$ '] Fix $r\ge2$ and $N\ge1$. For $\Lambda_\theta=\log L_\theta$ as defined by ~((eq:logL-explicit of the paper)), we have the bounds
