{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.769683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c125b132970d3c4bfba3d2bc31f28da6d170a2622f7955cbe0a25a167f59851","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $b > 0$,  $\vec{y} \in \weyl_2$, and $f,g \in C([0,b])$, such that $f(b) \ge y_1 > y_2 \ge g(b)$, and $f(t) > g(t)$ for $t\in[0,b]$. For any $\varepsilon > 0$, there exists $\delta > 0$, depending on $\varepsilon, b, y_1, y_2 ,f,g$, such that
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}_{\mathrm{pin}}^{b,\vec{y}}\left(g(t) - \varepsilon \leq \mathcal{Q}_2(t) \leq \mathcal{Q}_1(t) \leq f(t) + \varepsilon \mbox{ for all }t \in [0,b] \right) &\geq \delta.
\end{align}
Now fix $M>0$ and assume in addition that $f(t) = y_1+m(b-t)$ and $g(t) = y_2+m(b-t)$ for some $m\in\mathbb{R}$ with $|m|\le M$. Then the lower bound $\delta$ in \eqref{Eq.StayInCorridor} may be taken to depend only on $\varepsilon,b,M$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.521201+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c1d2bf1ac5c6447bc78683d8ad59b978174b2a616b5f5c2e0bf158b0440cc03","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:PTASEP-seed-linear of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] Let $H = \ell^2(\mathbb{Z})$.  The seed functions
$\psi_{t,r,n}$ and $\phi_{t,r,n}$ defined in
\S(sec:PTASEP-kernel-reform of the paper) satisfy the linear
problem (equation eq:Linear-Psi-3 of the paper) and the adjoint
linear problem (equation eq:Linear-Phi-Prob of the paper) on
$\mathcal{V}$ with edge weights
$(c_k, \lambda_k)$.  Explicitly, for each fixed
$r \in \mathbb{Z}$:
\begin{align}
\psi_{t+1,r,n+1}
&= (q{+}p\theta)(1{-}\theta)^{-1}
   \psi_{t,r+1,n}
   - \theta(q{+}p\theta)(1{-}\theta)^{-1}
   \psi_{t,r,n},
 \\
\psi_{t+1,r+1,n}
&= q\psi_{t,r+1,n}
   + p\theta\psi_{t,r,n},

\end{align}
and
\begin{align}
\phi_{t,r+1,n}
&= (q{+}p\theta)(1{-}\theta)^{-1}
   \phi_{t+1,r,n+1}
   - \theta(q{+}p\theta)(1{-}\theta)^{-1}
   \phi_{t+1,r+1,n+1},
 \\
\phi_{t,r+1,n}
&= q\phi_{t+1,r+1,n}
   + p\theta\phi_{t+1,r+2,n}.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.299316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c25a8ea47a5c4aadae162eca3b2f0054da2c713f836651358ae841a1dee758d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] Fix $t > 0$ and let $\mu = \cN(0,1)$; it holds that
