{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.828086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c58d796d7019317c7c01347e3a2db57f1212ca52cf02c132ce6db9bdf84a96f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:marcus-correction of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] Let $X:[0,T]\to\mathbb{R}^d$ be a finite-variation c\`adl\`ag{} path. The forward or It\^o{} level-two lift is
\begin{equation}
\mathbb X^{I}_{s,t}
=
\int_{(s,t]}(X_{u-}-X_s)\otimes\,\mathrm{d} X_u.
\end{equation}
The Marcus level-two lift is
\begin{equation}
\mathbb X^{M}_{s,t}
=
\mathbb X^{I}_{s,t}
+\frac12\sum_{s<u\le t}\Delta X_u\otimes\Delta X_u.

\end{equation}
Equivalently, the Marcus lift replaces each jump by a straight chord traversed over an auxiliary interval and then takes the ordinary geometric signature of the completed path.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.243665+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c5abf784bf13b27c6f453e35f1c58fe870f63c7f61384371cf8bc408ec9b11c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 (fractional null-form estimate) of arXiv:2609.01093, 'Ideal MHD below the classical well-posedness threshold'] Let $n\ge2$, $\breg\in(\frac12,1]$, $s>\frac{n+1}2$ and
