for any fixed $p\in\N$, $p\ge 3$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.720902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cb10f916eb1ac889adc2d8eba3a5da0d00288e5b701867dde821a118e437c93","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: a prioiri of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] Suppose (equation path of the paper) and (equation degree of the paper) in Assumption (ass: graph of the paper) hold. Let $\bar m^\varepsilon_0,\bar m^\varepsilon_1 \in {\mathcal P}({\mathcal X_{\varepsilon}})$. Then
