{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:47:32.874634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cd8a927dc039b72726a88f49b083204b5f023460304bb243687873893ed48f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Euler support reduction) of arXiv:2609.02449, 'Finite Directional Coefficient Modules over Euler Fibers of $A$-Hypergeometric Systems'] Let $\Lambda\in\mathfrak{L}_{\bm{\beta}}$, and let
\[
\varphi_{\Lambda}=\sum_{\bm{\gamma}\in\widetilde{\Lambda}}\bm{x}^{\bm{\gamma}}r_{\Lambda,\bm{\gamma}}(\log\bm{x})\in\mathscr{F}_{\widetilde{\Lambda}}^{\log}.
\]
