{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.067080+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d25e98f42af4fbad1553fe9ea7b6070629c9a5bd04a4099bcffec63ab479b0b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Polynomial duality with dual process \eqref{generatory}) of arXiv:2606.00781, '2606.00781'] Let $\Lambda$ be a finite measure on $[0,1]$. Furthermore, let $r:=(r_n)_{n\in\nz_0}$ be a given sequence of real numbers. Then there exists a unique duality kernel $D=D_r:[0,1]\times\nz_0\to\rz$ (depending on the sequence $r$) satisfying the following three properties.
