{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:49.835211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6da3164af6e4cbe7ea9122f98d4c52c08f090a6ca94ae95aae10df1e624f0e13","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6 of arXiv:2506.12755, '{\bf Stochastic intrinsic gradient flows on the Wasserstein space}\footnote{Supported in p'] We assume $(C_1)$, $(C_2)$ (see Sections \ref{ssec:indT} and \ref{sec:EF}) with $G_\D(\D_2\cap \D_1)=1 $  and $\ll\in \ppac$ such that $\rho_\lam$ is strictly positive and Lipschitz continuous. Then:

