  \item For every $\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\delta > 0$ so that $d_n(x,y) < \delta$ implies $d_Y(f_n(x),f_n(y)) < \varepsilon \vee r_n$ for every $n$.
 \end{enumerate}
 Then there is a subsequence $(K_{n_k},f_{n_k})$ that converges in the $d_\infty$ metric. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

