\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.952705+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6dd4bccfd58d2dd7aea3b286b35315aea1344304ba3963c7468c6004a5e59606","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 13 (Pathwise Sobolev space $\mathcal{W}^{2, \pi}_{\omega}$) of arXiv:2608.07365, 'A pathwise Ito formula \\for weakly differentiable functions'] Define   $\mathcal{W}^{2, \pi}_{\omega}$ to be the space of functions $F\in W^{2,1}(\Rr^d)$ for which there exists a sequence $(F_m)_{m\geq 1}$ such that
