{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.302955+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e956b8e7ad5fee6973afba6035055a2ba8aaffa6cf19ca48bca9e2946e33f18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary downright_path of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] For every down-right path $\mathcal{Y} = \{\mathbf y_i\}_{i\in \mathbb{Z}}$, every choice of $\rho_1,\dots,\rho_n \in (0,1)$, and every $t_1,\dots,t_n \in \mathbb{R}$, we have
