{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:56:11.143613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f95bccc755112276add979520b1f7e2b7e77275439c21d791ccdb055f9e4713","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2608.11071, 'Scaling Laws for Majority-based Opinion Dynamics in the Presence of Stubborn Agents'] Let $r_1$ and $r_2$ denote the smallest and largest real roots of $\Delta_k$ in $\mc S$, respectively, with the possibility of $r_1=r_2$ in case $\Delta_k$ has a unique root in $\mc S$.
