{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.818007+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fa5595ae72cdddb912c8e4f3a4dfdc06fe116ca875c6ff5f6955f6591ecfca7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2608.12804, 'Scaling Limits for Ising Models on Inhomogeneous Random Graphs and Applications'] For every $1\leq p<\infty$, we have:
    \begin{equation*}
