{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.115938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6fee6d22d5000399d70273fd621e491dff0f6bf9aca3014ced0c7f23391aba7b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 6.1 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Let $D\subset {\mathbb{R}}^n$ be a convex domain that satisfies (equation RBM-regular-DF-condition of the paper), and let  $d$ denote the Euclidean distance. Let $(X_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be the reflected Brownian motion on $\overline{D}$. For any   $x\in E$ and nearly Borel set $B\subset \overline{D}$,
\begin{equation*}
