{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.382109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_706d5ad276bddf069e2234541cebb6f3c356a42ac21432796ea7b7b75e72094a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2609.03238, 'Representation Defects and Cassels Pairings for Congruent Number Curves'] With respect to the basis \eqref{eq:basis4}, the Cassels matrix is
\begin{equation}
C_{pq}=
