{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:09.903179+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_708998b13b4d354cc4fa7a9f2c33a1cf91d645e64c529e883ed6ab96aaf5c5fb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def CPS of arXiv:2607.19511, 'A Conditional Probability Hierarchy for Stochastic Choice\footnote{We thank Samson Abramsk'] A \textbf{conditional probability space} (\textbf{CPS}) (relative to $\cal G$) is a map $p : {\cal G} \rightarrow \Delta(\Omega)$, which we will also write as $G \mapsto p_G(\cdot)$ for $G \in {\cal G}$, satisfying:
