{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.814876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70b8d25c591a23c0e4f29dbe1de245d8a0e8a412cc796d535cfc3f4d1b31412c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:connection_under_truncation of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] Assume all the conditions of Proposition (prop:non_neg_conn_prob_randomvertices of the paper) and the uniform boundedness assumption (equation assump:unif_bdd_degs of the paper). With $o_1$ and $o_2$ as before random vertices from $\mathcal N^{(s_0)}$, we have
