{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.346928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70c51204087da8779fdd9bdf36f5f71ef0d3502e08b513b307eaa244316c33a3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main_theorem of arXiv:2609.02491, 'Generalised Random Parking for Trapeziums on a Strip'] Assume that $0 \le b \le a <\infty$ such that $a >0$, and let $\eta$ be defined as in~(equation eq:defn_eta of the paper). Then, it follows that $\lim_{x \to \infty}\eta(x)/x = \lambda(a,b) \in (0,\infty)$, where
\begin{equation}
    \lambda(a,b)\coloneqq \frac{1}{2} \int_0^\infty (2+e^{-tb}-e^{-ta})\exp \bigg( \int_0^t \mleft(-2+e^{-s(a+b)/2}+e^{-as}\mright) \frac{\,\mathrm{d} s}{s}\bigg) \,\mathrm{d} t.
    \end{equation} 
    Moreover, as $x > 2a(e+1)$, it holds that
    \begin{equation}
    \bigg|\eta(x) -\lambda(a,b) x +1-\lambda(a,b) \frac{a+b}{2}\bigg| 
    \le\begin{dcases}
      \mleft(\frac{2e}{x/a}\mright)^{x/a-3/2} \frac{e^{3/2} K_1}{\sqrt{\pi}}, &\text{ if }a=b,\\
      \mleft(\frac{2e}{x/a}\mright)^{x/a-5/2} \frac{3e^{5/2}(2K_1+K_2)}{\sqrt{\pi}}, &\text{ if }a>b.
    \end{dcases}
\end{equation} where $K_1 \coloneqq 1 + 2a(2/(a+b)+\lambda(a,b)) + \lambda(a,b)\cdot  (a+b)/2>0$ and $K_2 \coloneqq (2/(a+b)+\lambda(a,b))(a-b)/2\ge 0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

