{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:17:13.075880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70f67538fc619bb341a504a415cd5cd78be62d17d0b4050ca4f17159fc5e7e83","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Lipchitzness-random-environement of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] Let $F^{(t)}$ be an $s$-holomorphic function on the $s$-embedding $\mathcal{S}^{(t)}(\Lambda_{n})$ obtained via Lemma (lem:SDE-embedding of the paper). Then, with $\mathbf{P}$-probability at least $1-O(n^{-4})$, there exist a constant $C(\omega)>0$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq t^{(\alpha)}_n$, the function $F^{(t)}$ is Lipchitz at every scale, meaning that for any  $z_{1,2}\in B(u,d)$ one has 
