{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.766399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71e7005244447c89a72d7a937c51f757540b5edea2d3733ed912d6a3f8b8a406","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2609.03003, 'Causal Foundation Models'] Let $\mathcal{P} \subset \mathcal{P}_{\text{DGP}}$. A causal estimand $g$ is \textbf{identifiable given} $\mathcal{P}$ if it is constant on observational equivalence classes of $\mathcal{P}$, i.e. for any $P_1, P_2 \in \mathcal{P}$,
