where $\lambda(s)$ denotes the best $L^2$ concentration in $PW^2$ on $[-s/2,s/2]$, i.e.,
$$\lambda(s):=\sup_{\substack{f\in PW^2\\ \lVert f\rVert_2=1}}
 \int_{-s/2}^{s/2}|f(x)|^2 dx.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:06:39.329057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72209881de27780adaebf93e5297798ad1cf78ff3a10d52bc9e1addeb3db9643","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:regularity_v_u of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Let $Q$ be a parabolic cylinder with side length $\varrho\in (0,1/2]$ and center $(t_0,x_0)\in {\mathbb R}_+\times {\mathbb R}^d$. Fix $r\in (1,\infty)$, $N\geq 1$ and $\delta\in (0,1]$. 
Let $(v^{N,\delta},\pi^{N,\delta},(\widetilde{\pi}_{k,\alpha}^{N,\delta})_{k,\alpha})$ be a local solution to (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_quantitative of the paper). Let $\mathrm{Err}^{{\rm det}}$ and $\mathrm{Err}^{{\rm sto}}$ be as in (equation eq:def_error_det of the paper) and (equation eq:def_error_sto of the paper), respectively. Then, the process $z^{N,\delta}$ is well-defined with paths
$$
z^{N,\delta} \in L^2(I;H^{1}_0(B;{\mathbb R}^d))\cap L^\infty(I;\mathbb{L}^2(B)) \ \text{a.s.,}
$$
and moreover,
\begin{align*}
\big({\mathbf E}\|z^{N,\delta}\|_{L^\infty(I;L^2(B))}^r \big)^{1/r}
+
\big({\mathbf E}\|z^{N,\delta}\|_{L^2(I;H^1(B))}^r\big)^{1/r}
\lesssim\big( {\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^2(Q)}^r\big)^{1/r}\qquad \qquad\qquad&\\
+\big({\mathbf E}\|\nabla v^{N,\delta}\|_{L^2(Q)}^r\big)^{1/r}
 +\big({\mathbf E} \|(\nabla \widetilde{\pi}^{N,\delta}_{k,\alpha})_{k,\alpha}\|_{L^2(Q;\ell^2)}^r\big)^{1/r},&
\end{align*}
where the implicit constant depends only on $\mu,r,\varrho$ and $d$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:20:15.624052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7221b7d918bb5f44df2f37dd10be2d54b17e2565ad9c36a94c5a4ae5ec327513","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:no-additive-intro of arXiv:2609.00889, 'Dominant-Degree Conditions for Ramsey--Tur\'an Factors of Non-Directed Cycle Orientations'] For every fixed integer $s\ge2$ and every real constant $C$, there are arbitrarily large multiples $n$ of $2s$ and $n$-vertex oriented graphs $D$ such that
