\]
in the positive-label interval convention.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.651865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73405f270064fd0acddd660fdf119e87eaf2883b9cf30bd036749d3287220ae6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 (Finite-network well-posedness) of arXiv:2608.16701, 'Order-Sensitive Fast-Synapse Limits in Sparse Excitatory--Inhibitory Threshold--Reset Netw'] For every finite graph, every $\varepsilon>0$, and every regularization
