\end{equation}
where the infimum runs over all neighbourhoods of $\phi$ in $\B(\A,\rmM_k)_+$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.923541+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_735cec15b24dd808677e0db90317b2dff42c5783643f102ad9a69022e2cfabfd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 25 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $A$ be a finite abelian group of order $r$.  Every minimal gap-determining family for $A\wr\Sn_n$ has cardinality
