law alone need not determine the grading or the support. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.373560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73788535eabb5c4af02397561970996d0e393ec0f35d3ad36beb0562b73d8ab0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 6 (Stopping Time Criterion) of arXiv:2606.04245, 'Properties of a Special Type of Filtration and its Martingale Criteria'] Let $(T_n)_{n\geq1}$ be an increasing sequence of stopping times with respect to $\FF$ such that $T_n\to\infty$ almost surely as $n\to\infty$. 
