{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:15:46.794307+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73aef3f1b128c23a310303a9903bd5e0b06f7f99f9a5b305e82e33e4567a7913","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2609.00974 (conj environment labelled conj: alg int conj).] Let $K/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(x_1,\ldots,x_n)$ be an algebraic extension of fields. Let $\F$ be a foliation on $K$, which admits a model over the ring of integers $\cO_L$, where $L$ is a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$.

