{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_73e325504c6d8b47d499c52ed4ff5f40e219801c35a0929c7166c6e7343bedea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:8.3n of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let ${\rm A}$, ${\mathbf A}$ be as in Lemma~(l:8.3 of the paper), $z \in {\mathbf A}$ and $x \in {\rm B}(z;r_n)$. Then,
