{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.459972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7475d75cdd8ab65e1b4b725ae2d67d1d4a3a2a54f353c041ff5825f7f1a45e88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 47 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $(\alpha^{(i)}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}_+}$, $i=1,2$, be two sequences of 
diverging sequence of constants such that~\eqref{e:seqConst} holds. 
Let $T>0$ and let $\{\mcb P^n_s\colon s\in[0,T]\}$ be a 
real--valued stochastic processes on $[0,T]$.  
Assume that there exist $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $C=C(T)>0$, such that uniformly in $n$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{0\leq s\leq T}\E\left[ |\mcb P_s^{n}|\right]&\leq C\,,\\
\E\left[|\mcb P_t^{n}-\mcb P_s^{n}|\right]&\leq C(t-s)^{\alpha}\,,\qquad \text{for all $s,t\in[0,T]$.}
\end{align}
Then, for any $t\in[0,T]$, and Lebesgue-a.e. $k_1,k_2\in\R$
we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty} \E\left[\left| \int_0^t\mcb P_s^{n} e^{-2\pi \iota  \frac{k_1\alpha_n^{(1)}+k_2\alpha_n^{(2)}}{n}}\dd s\right|\right]=0\,. 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.684617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747c7c53d0734b3ede6f36c4c67f5b1698210d28235d72f21f02afe78f59cf29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Finite-dimensional spectral-growth theorem) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $q\geq1$ and let $A:\C\to M_q(\C)$ be entire, with $A(0)=0$, and suppose
\begin{equation}
\norm{\e^{A(z)}}\leq C\e^{\tau\abs{z}}
\qquad (z\in\C)
\end{equation}
for constants $C\geq1$ and $\tau\geq0$, where $\norm{\cdot}$ is an operator norm. Then $z\mapsto\sigma_k(A(z))$ is a polynomial of degree at most $k$ for $1\leq k\leq q$.

If, in addition, $A(z)=zH+O(z^2)$ as $z\to0$ for some $H\in M_q(\C)$, then
\begin{equation}
\det(\zeta I-A(z))=\det(\zeta I-zH)
\end{equation}
for all $z,\zeta\in\C$. Consequently,
\begin{equation}
\tr(A(z)^p)=z^p\tr(H^p)
\qquad (p\geq1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.192360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747cc8c07b6561b4fcad68b186e3b57bf7732f76a56988d6ce51527f694b74f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Let $W$ be an $N\times N$ GUE matrix. For any $n_1,n_2\in\N\cup\{0\}$ and multi-indices $\bm{k}\in\N^{n_1},\bm{l}\in\N^{n_2}$ it holds that    
