{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.617168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75090fd5a7f9c83d9f72b6a4cff79c0c8eb95da937f8d506c742d4391048bd90","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:face-integral of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] We say that a vector $\vec\ell\in \mathbb{R}^s$ is \emph{of convergent type} for the face $\cal F$ if the integral
