{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.413663+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75a53a3b580353bd0ecfeeb7eacf04b9a47abcdf04bdcacfe73d5db1b3c8b284","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] Let $M$ be a compact orientable 3-manifold, and let $\mathcal{C} \subset X(M)$ be an irreducible algebraic curve. Let $\widetilde{\mathcal{C}}$ be the smooth projective model of $\mathcal{C}$, and let $x \in \widetilde{\mathcal{C}} \setminus \mathcal{C}$ be an ideal point. Let $H \subset \pi_1(M)$ be a finitely generated subgroup, and let $r: X(M) \to X(H)$ be the restriction map. Following Tillmann [tillmann], we say that $x$ \emph{has a limiting character on $H$} if the induced rational map $\widetilde{\mathcal{C}} \to X(H)$ is defined at $x$. Since the character ring of the finitely generated group $H$ is generated by finitely many trace functions, this is equivalent to requiring that every $I_\gamma$, $\gamma \in H$, have a finite value at $x$. In this case, the value $\chi_{x, H} \in X(H)$ is called the \emph{limiting character of $x$ on $H$}. Equivalently, if $\nu: (\Delta, 0) \to (\widetilde{\mathcal{C}}, x)$ is a local analytic parametrization with $\nu(0) = x$ and $\nu(t) \in \mathcal{C}$ for $t \neq 0$, then the limiting character on $H$ is the character
\begin{equation*}
	\chi_{x, H}(\gamma) = \lim_{t \to 0}I_\gamma(\nu(t)) \ \ \ \ \ \gamma \in H
\end{equation*}
where the limit exists and is finite for all $\gamma \in H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.480499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75b7e3f1d6a7f5d74c8c0a70160435f9dc19b0d558771bd190928844d21f8a1b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] For every $z,w\in\C$ and $\varepsilon, \varepsilon'\in (0,1]$,
\begin{displaymath}
G_{D,\varepsilon,\varepsilon'}(z,w)
\leq\Big(\dfrac{1}{2\pi}\log (\varepsilon^{-1}) + c\Big)^{1/2}
\Big(\dfrac{1}{2\pi}\log (\varepsilon'^{-1}) + c\Big)^{1/2},
\end{displaymath}
where
\begin{displaymath}
c = \dfrac{1}{2\pi}
\int_{\C^{2}} 
\log (\vert y-x\vert^{-1})
\rho(x)\rho(y)
\,d^{2}x\,d^{2}y
+
\dfrac{1}{2\pi}
0\vee \log(\diam(D))
< +\infty.
\end{displaymath}
Moreover, for every $\varepsilon, \varepsilon'\in (0,1]$,
and $z,w\in\C$ such that $\vert w-z\vert\geq 2\,\varepsilon\vee\varepsilon'$,
\begin{displaymath}
G_{D,\varepsilon,\varepsilon'}(z,w)
\leq
\dfrac{1}{2\pi}
\Big(
0\vee\log \dfrac{2}{\vert w-z\vert}
+
0\vee\log(\diam(D))
\Big).
\end{displaymath}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.359140+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75bdca6336a1272e5cb2c26f3c74d65df7d79fda9f0d6f93a549ad0905eccb22","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition definition-property-star of arXiv:2609.00794, 'On operators whose adjoints or second adjoints attain their norms'] Let $X$ and $Y$ be Banach spaces. The pair $(X,Y)$ is said to have \textit{property $(P^\star)$} if there is a relatively $\operatorname{WOT}$ compact set $K \subseteq \mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*)$ such that 
