\end{equation}
then $x=y$ as c\`adl\`ag{} paths. Moreover, the forward It\^o{} lift of a path with at least one nonzero jump is not a geometric signature lift of the same completed graph.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.761033+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75e5962537fafe9956f2feb0c8fe7fd04491f5c0c7e26e9ade3f0601e1617e3e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop c2-1 of arXiv:2609.02682, 'LDP for tensor forms'] Suppose $c=v=2$, $\int_0^1 W_\infty (., y) dy = 1$ $\lambda$-a.e., $W_\infty>0$ $\lambda$-a.e., $\mu(\{1\})=p_1=p\in(0,1)$, $\mu(\{2\})= p_2=1-p$, and $\boldsymbol{\alpha}= (\alpha_1,\alpha_2)$ where $\alpha_1,\alpha_2\geq 0$.
