{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.316377+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_75eb921de2c1841f5a7b3430258a1b7e7b87a09af71f3eb03260a6f338e4f3f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ;ph of arXiv:2604.12462, 'Stochastic analysis of Beckner's and related functional inequalities'] It holds that, for every $0\le t\le 1$, 
