{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.357719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76b0da983e8d806b00714d57433e0a31b6fa758bbff4a71390cd6c7a7dec3fcd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] Let $m\in C^2(\bb T)$ be the density of a probability measure
($m\ge 0$, $\int_{\bb T} m(x)\, dx =1$). Suppose that there exists
