{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.512048+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76dc71438de15d6451af442282d308b54835d838a6b90e8ea0fc6bb0efd3b569","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 (Opposite-jump monotonicity) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] Let $X$ and $Z$ be independent variables in the standing class.

