{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.117277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7710ce34fdbce3bc1d7f239f66b04f9b18af3a3416e654fe168c19244aadb343","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $\mathcal{A}_0(\iota)$ denote the collection of pairs $(h,\gamma)$ such that \begin{equation}
