	for almost all $x,x' \in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.060390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_771fe0d23b0ecd5c11811aebfdfe5223c450397e11ee9b69fddcc9604e57650f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thKM of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $\eta$ be an offspring distribution such that $\eta(0) >0$ and $\eta(1) >0$ and denote by $F$ its generating function. Let $(S_n)_{n\geq0}$ be a random walk started from $S_0=0$ with step distribution $\eta$. Assume $k_n=o(n)$ and $k_n\rightarrow \infty$. Then
    \begin{equation}
    \sup_{k\geq -k_n} \left| \sqrt{k_n} \frac{b_n^{k_n+k}}{F(b_n)^{n-k_n}}\mathbb{P}\left(S_{n-k_n} = k_n+k\right) - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}e^{-\frac{k^2}{2k_n}}\right| \xrightarrow[n \rightarrow \infty]{} 0,
\end{equation}
where $b_n$ is defined by
 \[b_n\frac{F'(b_n)}{F(b_n)}=\frac{k_n}{n-k_n}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.244633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7724e094f1dc46d773a722e3136b19166c7d89e7ab524e9fe4ecf8dda55f5b52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $\delta>0$, there exist constants $\kappa > 0$ and $C = C(\delta)>0$ such that the mixing time of the single-flip Glauber dynamic on tilings of the hexagon $\mX$ satisfies
          \begin{eqnarray}

