where $(x_{,1}, x_{T,2},x_{T,3})$ are the ordered set of vertices of $T$ between $g_1$ and $g_2$ and $d_\infty$ is a metric on the ideal boundary of $\tilde{S}$ that is the standard metric on the circle.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.645405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7792e57d70d70ded96a438886e4381245f9fb6945b28b9913d31158e119b2697","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 (Simplex cap) of arXiv:2607.23980, 'Sharp small-deviation inequalities for sums of independent\\nonnegative random variables'] Let $y=(y_1,\ldots,y_n)\in[0,\infty)^n$, and write $s(y)=\sum_i y_i$. If $s(y)>0$ and $0\le t\le s(y)/(n+1)$, then
