{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.956044+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78bcf05e630a729cc344e376704c504ffff0ee24869d83b022c089b87fc2c5b3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tmin of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:ci of the paper), we fix a desired accuracy (or tolerance)
$\varepsilon>0$ at a confidence level $1-\alpha$, with $\alpha\in(0,1)$, and define
\begin{align}
  t_{\textrm{min},A}(\varepsilon,\alpha)
  \equiv
  \frac{1}{2\varepsilon^2}
  \left(\sqrt{\tilde\sigma_A^2}+ \sqrt{\tilde\sigma_A^2 + 2 c_A \varepsilon}
  \right)^{2}
  \log\left(\frac{2N_\nu}{\alpha}\right).

\end{align}
Then $r_A(\alpha,t) \leq \varepsilon$ if and only if $t \geq
t_{\textrm{min},A}(\varepsilon,\alpha)$.
In particular, for every $t \geq t_{\textrm{min},A}(\varepsilon,\alpha)$, it holds that
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left( -\varepsilon \leq \overline{A}_t - \E^\mu[\overline{A}_t]\leq \varepsilon\right)\geq 1 - \alpha.

\end{align}
Moreover, the minimal time $t_{\textrm{min},A}$ admits the simple two-sided estimate
\begin{align}
  \frac{2\tilde\sigma_A^2}{\varepsilon^2}\log\left(\frac{2N_\nu}{\alpha}\right)
  \leq
  t_{\textrm{min},A}(\varepsilon,\alpha)
  \leq
  \left(\frac{2\tilde\sigma_A^2}{\varepsilon^2}+ \frac{2 c_A}{\varepsilon}\right)
  \log\left(\frac{2N_\nu}{\alpha}\right),

\end{align}
and the corresponding one-sided guarantees of Eq.~(equation eq:ci_onesided of the paper) hold at
tolerance $\varepsilon$ for all $t \geq t_{\textrm{min},A}^{(1)}(\varepsilon,\alpha)$, where
$t_{\textrm{min},A}^{(1)}(\varepsilon,\alpha)$ is obtained
from Eq.~(equation eq:tmin of the paper) by replacing $2N_\nu$ with $N_\nu$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.321920+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78bebb788e61a7991101f1e0a9ed85d33ceeecb0fdb36e18705adbafb4faccc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 38 (Exact constant) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\sigma, \alpha > 0$. Every $X \in \SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$ satisfies
