{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.478020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_793dadbfc004e5718e340f7eab2f428702905df08606d91370907334298fbfaf","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 10 (Worst PCS and the cost of using the symmetric center) of arXiv:2609.03466, 'Least-Favorable Location for Binomial Top-$t$ Selection'] Fix $k\ge2$, $1\le t<k$, and $\delta\in(0,1)$. Then, as $n\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
