{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.359716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79825b378dc9d4e87c2b1f8ee144e8cb4b450ec68870faf8fd4f06389fe5d9b2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2511.09517, 'From Cannings model to Brownian motion conditioned on local time profile'] Let $X,Y,Z$ be random elements on the same probability space, with $Y$ independent of $(X,Z)$. For any test function $f(x,y)$ on the value space of $(X,Y)$, define
\[
g(x) := \mathbb{E}[f(x,Y)].
\]
Then
\begin{align}
    \mathbb{E}\big(f(X,Y)\mid Z\big) = \mathbb{E}\big(g(X)\mid Z\big).
\end{align}
In particular, if there exists a random element $W$, independent of $Y$ and distributed as $(X \mid Z)$, then
