{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.361584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a7e7dde9a2e5a6280fa9f361421f757d214834fd3accbcde5f5f7ef17e263a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] Fix a continuous function $f\in C(\bb T)$. Then, there exists a positive constant
$\mf h^*>0$, independent of $\epsilon$ such that
