{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.663351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa458233043015f4683c55b27abd499c128da973ce2d490a3fec98aebea7e9a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:nointersectAT of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}$ denote the event that at least two different odd CLE$_4$ gaskets of the family of CLE$_4$ gaskets constructed in Theorem (thm:twopointAT of the paper) intersect both 
$\mathbb{D}(z_1, \varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2, \varepsilon_2)$. Then
\begin{itemize}
    \item Let $E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)$ denote the event that the $k$-th odd nested CLE$_4$ gasket intersects 
    $\mathbb{D}(z_1,\varepsilon_1)$ and $\mathbb{D}(z_2,\varepsilon_2)$. Then there is a constant $C > 0$
    such that for all $k \geq 1$,
    $$\mathbb{P}(\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2} \cap E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}(z_1,z_2)) \leq C(\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{1/4}\left(\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k}) + \1_{k \geq 2}\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm{odd},k-1})\right).$$
    \item Further, for some $\widetilde C > 0$, 
    for all $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2 > 0$ sufficiently small, 
$$\sum_{k \geq 1}\mathbb{P}(E^{\rm{odd},k}_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}(z_1,z_2)) < \widetilde C\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm odd}(z_1,z_2)).$$
    \item In particular, $\mathbb{P}(\widetilde F_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2})$ is bounded by $C(\varepsilon_1\varepsilon_2)^{1/4}\mathbb{P}(E_{\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2}^{\rm odd}(z_1, z_2))$ for some $C > 0$ as $\max(\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2)\to 0$. 
\end{itemize}
Further, the same holds when we replace odd by even everywhere. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.771087+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aaa6dbed73d567bb52ba6bf1a9e06270642b7b0b82a7b3c10019304f2709472","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 45 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $m \in \mathbb{N}$,  $t_1 < \cdots < t_m$, and set $\mathcal{T} = \{t_1, \dots, t_m\}$. If $\nu = (\nu_{t_1}, \dots, \nu_{t_m})$ is an $m$-tuple of locally finite measures on $\mathbb{R}$, we define the (locally finite) measure $\mu_{\mathcal{T},\nu}$ on $\mathbb{R}^2$ by
\begin{equation}
\mu_{\mathcal{T},\nu}(A) = \sum_{t \in \mathcal{T}} \nu_t(A_{t}), \mbox{ where } A_{t} = \{ y \in \mathbb{R}: (t,y) \in A\}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.122042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aacf2dc62a94b28398cfb0c6e565f95d15bfdcdad754072642286b398a7dbe9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:radial-qf of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Under (equation eq:base-assumptions of the paper) and (equation eq:critical-scaling of the paper), there exists a deterministic sequence $\varepsilon_n\to0$ such that for every deterministic complex $p\times p$ matrix $A$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}\left|
  \frac{x^{\mathsf T}Ax}{p}
  -R_n\frac{\operatorname{Tr} A}{p}
  \right|^2
  \le \varepsilon_n\|A\|_{\mathrm{op}}^2.

\end{equation}
For all sufficiently large $n$, one may take
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{\quad
  \varepsilon_n=\bigl(\sqrt{\delta_n}+\sqrt{\kappa_n}\bigr)^2,
  \quad}

\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  \delta_n=\frac{vd}{n-d}e^{vd^2/(n-d)},
  \qquad
  \kappa_n=
  \frac{8d(n-d)}{n(n-1)}
  \exp\!\left(\frac{2vd^2}{n-d}\right).

\end{equation}
Both terms tend to zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.788465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab31dea35268499d44ff42fcb05af18f94b9d01325c06f3a7dfb61c06848d97","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:tailrl-binary-recovery of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] Suppose $r_i\in\{0,1\}$ and let
$M:=\sum_{i=1}^N\mathbbm{1}\{r_i=1\}$. If $M>0$, then every successful
rollout receives weight $1/M$ and every unsuccessful rollout receives weight
zero. Hence the uncentered TailRL{} estimator reduces to
\begin{equation}
g_{\mathrm{TailRL}}^{(N)}(x)
=
\frac{1}{M}
\sum_{i:r_i=1}S_i,

\end{equation}
which is the MaxRL estimator. After mean-centering, successful rollouts have
weight $1/M-1/N$ and unsuccessful rollouts have weight $-1/N$. If $M=0$,
all uncentered and centered weights are zero.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.780509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab63bd25dc8667f14254e9937df378d3536996116d57b1430890ccf2d9e3fac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma limlo of arXiv:2411.18359, 'Large systems of symmetrized trapped Brownian Bridges and Schr\"odinger processes'] If $\phi:{\mathcal X } \to \mathbb{R}$ is lower semi continuous and the Large Deviations lower bound holds with $I:{\mathcal X } \to [0,\infty]$ then
