{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.049797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ab989b0a129862866acec6886f571be40ca73d336e668610ca6a88385bfcfd9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:transfer of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Fix $\kappa>1$ and OBABO parameters $h,\gamma>0$ with $h<2/\sqrt\kappa$, and set $\beta=e^{-\gamma h}$, $s=h^2(1+\beta)/2$, and $\tau^2=h^2(1-\beta^2)$. Suppose $U\in\mathcal U_\kappa^d$ for $d\in\{1,2\}$ satisfies Assumptions~(ass:cycle of the paper) and~(ass:monodromy of the paper) with these parameters $(s,\beta)$ and that, in addition, there are $\lambda_\ast\in[1,\kappa]$ and $b_\ast>0$ with
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x)=\lambda_\ast x+w(x),
 \qquad \sup_x\lvert w(x)\rvert\le b_\ast.
\end{equation}
Then for $U_R(x)=R^2U(x/R)$ and $Q_R=Q_{h,\gamma}^{U_R}$ there are constants $c_0,C_0>0$, independent of $R$, such that $Q_R$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$ and, for every $R\ge1$ and every $j\in\mathbb Z$, there exist two initial states $z_R^{(j)},z_R^{(j+1)}\in\mathbb R^{2d}$, constructed explicitly in (equation eq:cyclepair-general of the paper)-(equation eq:cyclevelocity-general of the paper) below from the cycle points with indices $j$ and $j+1$, such that at least one of them, denoted by $z_R$, satisfies
\begin{equation*}
 W_2(\delta_{z_R},\pi_R)\le C_0(1+R),
\end{equation*}
and
\begin{equation*}
 \norm{\delta_{z_R}Q_R^n-\pi_R}_{\mathrm{TV}}\ge\frac38,
 \qquad
 0\le n\le N_R:=\left\lfloor\frac1{16}e^{c_0R^2}\right\rfloor.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:21:06.854915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7abbcdab6272cd98c77fd509028952fd460c9b94bcea76c1b754a15654164155","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Strong solution) of arXiv:2608.21014, 'The stochastic Cahn--Hilliard equation in critical spaces'] Suppose that Assumption~\ref{Assumption:semilinear:evolution:equation} is satisfied for some $p\in[2,\infty)$ and $\kappa\in [0,p/2-1)\cup\{0\}$. For $T<\infty$, a pair $(u,\sigma)$ is called an $L^p_\kappa$-strong solution of~\eqref{eq:semilinear-stochastic-evolution} if $\sigma\colon\Omega\to[a,T]$ is a stopping time and $u\colon [a,\sigma]\to X_0$  is strongly progressively measurable, 
    \begin{equation*} u\in L^p(a,\sigma, w_\kappa^a;X_1)\cap C\big([a,\sigma];X_{1-\frac{1+\kappa}{p},p}\big),
    \end{equation*}
    and a.s.\ for all $t\in [a,\sigma]$ it holds that 
    \begin{equation}
        u(t)-u_a +\int_a^t Au(s)\,\dd s = \int_a^t F(s,u(s))\, \dd s +\int_a^t\1_{[a,\sigma]}(s) G(s,u(s))\, \dd W(s).
    \end{equation}
    For $T=\infty$, $(u,\sigma)$ is called an $L^p_\kappa$-strong solution of~\eqref{eq:semilinear-stochastic-evolution} if $\sigma\colon\Omega\to [a,\infty)$ is a stopping time and $u\colon[a,\sigma]\to X_0$ is strongly progressively measurable with $u\in L^p_{\loc}(a,\sigma,w_\kappa^a;X_1)\cap C([a,\sigma]\cap[a,\infty);X_{1-\frac{1+\kappa}{p},p})$ and~\eqref{eq:def:semilinear:strong:solution} holds a.s.\ for all $t\in [a,\sigma]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:40:21.312940+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7abd397c15e4e8a165eb90214802016c43c2941dd575bced879abfce8c7d2fd1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2604.08127, 'Asymptotics of Brownian occupation measures \\ with unusually large intersections'] The distributions of $Z_t = (\widetilde{L}_t , t^{-1}\| \ell_t \|_q)$ satisfy an LDP in $\widetilde{\mathcal{X}}_{\le 1} \times [0, \infty]$ with rate function
