{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.116892+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ac5975e8d6e30e35d61199be351d05f9f1c39498925d25122220ac1b801302c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 144 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] With the notations  of \Cref{prop:AI}, set  $Q = \mathfrak{d} q / 2$ and $M = \mu/\gamma''$. Define 
                \begin{equation}
                \Phi_{M,Q}({\hat x}):={\hat x}+Q(M{\hat x}+ {\hat x}^2),
              \end{equation}
              so that the change of variables \eqref{eq:C138} from $(X,Y)$ to $({\hat x},{\hat y})$ is $(X,Y)=(\Phi_{M,Q}({\hat x}),{\hat y})$. Define $G_{M,Q}({\hat x},{\hat y}):=\mathtt H_{\gamma''}\bigl(\Phi_{M,Q}({\hat x}),{\hat y}\bigr).$ Given $h>0$ and ${\hat x}$ such that ${\hat x},\Phi_{M,Q}({\hat x})>-\sqrt{2h/\gamma''}$, let $U_h({\hat x})$ and $U_{h;M,Q}({\hat x})$ denote the unique values such that
              \begin{equation}
                \mathtt H_{\gamma''}({\hat x},U_h({\hat x}))=
                G_{M,Q}({\hat x},U_{h;M,Q}({\hat x}))\Bigl(=\mathtt H_{\gamma''}(\Phi_{M,Q}({\hat x}),U_{h;M,Q}({\hat x}))\Bigr)=h.

              \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.305112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ac6cd15ea4eabfc2c656a255a9e9fd090b96264235508f6f06af04817da02b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:good_scales_merging of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Suppose that $h$ is a GFF on $D$ with some bounded boundary values. For any $b>0$ and $q \in (0,1)$ there exist $M,p>0$ so that the following is true. 
Let $z \in D$ and $r>0$ such that $B(z,r) \subseteq D$. Let $\widetilde{h}_{z,r}$ be as defined in Section~(se:gff of the paper) with the same boundary values as $\widetilde{h}$ above (after scaling and translation). Let $G_{z,r}$ be the event that
\begin{itemize}
 \item the scale $(z,r)$ is $M$-good for $h$, and
 \item the event $G$ above occurs for the (scaled and translated) field $\widetilde{h}_{z,r}$.
\end{itemize}
For $k\in\mathbf{N}$ let $E$ be the event that the fraction of $1 \leq j \leq k$ so that $G_{z,2^{-j}r}$ occurs is at least $q$. Then $\mathbf{P}[E^c] = O(e^{-bk})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.211809+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7acd83e2e695b615d757413eb6c1208109a8573611e35f3015e18b1304a74700","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma partialt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] For any $\lambda, t > 0$ and any finite set $\Lambda \subset V$, we have
