{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.534399+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bd13cc5aeebfb5d345c504addbc13c0aa4f9bc31a0767e0f67413ae8f830b3c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro pro2.02 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let the assumptions of (pro2.01 of the paper) hold. Then there exists a constant $C_{\bar{p},\theta}^2 >0$ depending only on $\bar{p}$ and $\theta$ such that for each $0\leq r\leq t< +\infty$,
