{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.076915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bd2a5892ad9a3ce95ea6b564d7aaf054a1828bc13cc1238aeac9328aa382aaa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Trace bound with modular constants) of arXiv:2608.27657, '\bfseries Stein Kernels and Normal Approximation\\ for Log-Concave Bilinear Forms'] Suppose that, for some \(C_q,C_{\rm en}\geq0\), one has
\[
  \Var(Y^{\mathsf T}AY)
  \leq C_q\Tr(A^2),
  \qquad
  \E\Tr(AHAH)
  \leq C_{\rm en}\Tr(A^2)
\]
for every \(A\in\mathsf S_n\).  Then
\begin{equation}
  0\preceq\Gamma_{\rm tr}
  \preceq
  \left(\frac{C_q}{4}+C_{\rm en}\right)I_{\mathsf S_n}.
  \tag{3.14}
\end{equation}
More precisely, the full slack has the positive decomposition
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  \left(\frac{C_q}{4}+C_{\rm en}\right)I_{\mathsf S_n}
  -\Gamma_{\rm tr}
  ={}&
  \frac14\left(C_qI_{\mathsf S_n}-\Gamma_{\rm quad}\right)\\
  &+\left(C_{\rm en}I_{\mathsf S_n}-\mathsf U\right)
  +\frac34\mathsf D.
\end{aligned}
  \tag{3.15}
\end{equation}

Under the estimates in \cref{thm:letwin}, \(C_q=8\) and
\(C_{\rm en}=2\).  Hence
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  4I_{\mathsf S_n}-\Gamma_{\rm tr}
  ={}&
  \frac14\left(8I_{\mathsf S_n}-\Gamma_{\rm quad}\right)
  +\left(2I_{\mathsf S_n}-\mathsf U\right)
  +\frac34\mathsf D
  \succeq0,
\end{aligned}
  \tag{3.16}
\end{equation}
and, for every deterministic symmetric \(A\),
\begin{equation}
  \boxed{
  \Var\!\left(\Tr(AH)\right)
  \leq4\Tr(A^2).}
  \tag{3.17}
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}
  \Var(\Tr H)\leq4n.
  \tag{3.18}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:23:58.628174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bd6951ae831d602fc1adfbf730cfe5b78187e168ae762ba1c478cc192d2e322","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 219 (The system of integral inequalities satisfied by the energy controlling quantities) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] Let $\varsigma_0$ be the constant featured in Lemma\,\ref{L:PRELIMINARYBELOWTOPORDERL2ESTIMATESFOREIKONALFUINCTIONQUANTITIES} (see also Remark\,\ref{R:SMALLNESSCONSTANTFORBELOWTOPORDERACOUSTICVARIABLES}). If $\varsigma_1 \in (0,1]$ is sufficiently small, then there exist constants
$C > 0$ and $C_* > 0$ 
that are \textbf{independent} of $\varsigma_0,\varsigma_1$ 
such that the following estimates hold
for $(\ubar,u) \in [\leftubar,\ubarboot) \times [\moreinterestingu_1,\moreinterestingu_2]$: 

\medskip

\noindent \underline{\textbf{Top-order integral inequalities for $\mastercontroltop$}.}
We have the following estimates for the $L^2$-controlling quantity $\mastercontroltop(\ubar,u)$
defined in \eqref{E:MASTERCONTROLLINGQUANTITY}:
\begin{align}
		\begin{split}  
			\mastercontroltop(\ubar,u) &\le \boxed{2.81 + 5.18} \weakspacetimetransvelocitycontrol_N(\ubar,u)  + \boxed{2.33 + 1.01} \totalbulkcontrolprecisefullymodifiedchi(\ubar,u) \\
			& \ \ +  \boxed{1.02 + 2.07} \weakspacetimeangularvelocitycontrol_N(\ubar,u) +  \boxed{4.13}  \totalbulkcontrolpartialmodifiedchi(\ubar,u) \\
			& \ \  + \boxed{\frac{2}{3}} \totalfluxcontrolvelocity_N(\ubar,u) + \boxed{\frac{3}{4}(1.01)} \totalfluxcontrolpartialmodifiedchi(\ubar,u) \\
			& \ \ + \Errortoparg{N}(\ubar,u),
		\end{split}
	\end{align}\noindent where we define $\Errortoparg{N}(\ubar,u)$ to be any term that satisfies the following estimate,
