{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:24:20.646900+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bf6c8255ce8f000975dbfe9e961a2ae066d640aa904d451604d8c43a9056dc3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary CorGroundStateVisitation of arXiv:2608.11178, 'A submartingale for the probability of avoiding the origin in one-point interaction ground'] Fix \(d\in\{2,3\}\), \(T,\gamma>0\), and \(x\in\mathbb R^d\setminus\{0\}\). The following hold.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item The probability that the ground-state diffusion does not hit the
origin by time \(T\) is given by
\begin{align}
\mathbb P_x^{T,\gamma}[\tau>T]
=
\frac{
K_{d/2-1}\!\left(
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}\,|x|,
\lambda_\gamma T
\right)
}{
K_{d/2-1}\!\left(
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}\,|x|
\right)
}.\nonumber
\end{align}

\item Conditionally on the event \(\{\tau\le T\}\), the first hitting
time \(\tau\) has density on \((0,T]\) given by
\begin{align}
\frac{
\mathbb P_x^{T,\gamma}
\left[
\tau\in dt
\,\middle|\,
\tau\le T
\right]
}{dt}
=
\frac{\left(
\frac{|x|}{\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}}
\right)^{d/2-1}}{
K_{d/2-1}
\left(
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}|x|
\right)
-
K_{d/2-1}
\left(
\sqrt{2\lambda_\gamma}|x|,
\lambda_\gamma T
\right)
}\,
\frac{1}{2t^{d/2}}
e^{-\lambda_\gamma t-\frac{|x|^2}{2t}}
,
\qquad
0<t\le T. \nonumber
\end{align}
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:15.351688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7bf701d0e343573c3da6bba56b9c124ae6de7c25e4a8b4e40e7744088260740a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2506.15736, 'Coming down from infinity for coordinated particle systems'] Suppose a coordinated particle system $(X(t))_{t \geq 0}$ on a finite set of sites $V$ has no death and no reproduction. Assuming that $|X(t)| < \infty$, the expected rate of change in total number of particles at time $t$ is given by

