{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.680893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c512f8386bba152b0f9542ce58ff5174f09e6b804afc2ef167d73ff3c108127","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn d:stabilizing-graph of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] We say that a family of graphs 
    $(\Psi(\mathcal{P}_n))_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$  (where each graph is generated by the same rule \(\mu \mapsto \Psi(\mu)\) represented by the marking neighborhood $\bar N$) forms a {\em stabilizing interaction graph} \(\Psi\) on finite windows with respect to a point process \(\mathcal{P}\) if   for every \(p \in \mathbb{N}\), there exist a fast decreasing function $\varphi_p'$ (see~(equation varphibd of the paper)), such that the  interaction range satisfies:
\begin{equation} 
\sup_{1 \leq n < \infty} \sup_{x_1, \ldots, x_p \in W_n} \mathbb{P}_{\bk x1p}
\bigl(S_n(x_1, \mathcal{P}_n) > s\bigr) \leq \varphi_p'(s), \quad s > 0.
\end{equation}
Without loss of generality, we assume that $\varphi_p'(\cdot)\le \varphi_{p+1}'(\cdot)$ for $p \in \mathbb{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.633325+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c5ba570e9822099a3e5d70ed3c3b2cfd1f87fe39e9b4f1ebeeb2d16ee12948e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma hitting3dLERW of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] There exist $C,\alpha>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon>0$, there exists $\delta_0$ such that for all $\delta\leq\delta_0$ and for all $n$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\left(\max_{z\in B(\eta[0,n],\delta n^{1/\beta})}\mathbb{P}^W_z(W[0,\infty)\cap \eta[0,n]=\varnothing\mid \eta)>\varepsilon\right)< C\varepsilon^{1/\alpha}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.000841+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c72f897fc0fa73057b2a9260674a095311ab70f17b2419f2734716b2f5d15cd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Signed threshold coordinate) of arXiv:2609.02788, '\textbf{Quantized Einstein Metrics on \(S^7\) with \(SU(3)\)-Symmetry}'] After orienting $a$, the function $a(c)$ changes sign at $c_*$.  More
precisely, for some finite odd integer $m\ge1$,
\begin{equation}
 a(c)=\kappa(c-c_*)^m+O((c-c_*)^{m+1}),
 \qquad \kappa\ne0.
\end{equation}
Consequently $a$ is a strictly monotone local coordinate and its inverse is
continuous, though it need not be differentiable when $m>1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.301771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c797841794311bb31e78e0d6b9d807923d77cf8a97fbe34ffd0439e249b85b5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:results:convergence of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption  (as:results:strongCoercivity of the paper) and Assumption (as:results:fixedPoint of the paper), and $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ satisfy $\mathbb{H}_\kappa(\lambda) < \infty$.       Let $(\mu, \gamma)$ be a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, \infty)$ with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda$.
