{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.964815+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c94eae769f6d1a26d4800bd1c1a05fbf27076389cfea3972992adea2785b312","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem regularity of arXiv:2412.03560, 'Non-asymptotic entropic bounds for non-linear kinetic Langevin sampler with second-order s'] Under Assumption~(assu:regularity of the paper),  $\nabla U_N$ is $L_1$-Lipschitz continuous for all $N\in\mathbb N$ with $L_1 = M_{1,x}+M_{1,m}$ and there  exist $L_2,L_3>0$  such that, for any $N\in\mathbb N$, $\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb X^N$ and $\mathbf{y},\mathbf{z}\in\mathbb R^{dN}$,
