{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.718147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7ca5b9421dde21cba7dc75d3c906054c7807173007ec6a81eabec164b1daf8f8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 (Nesterov label-noise contribution) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] Assume the stable small-step condition \(\eta\lambda_1\le c_{\rm st}\), where \(c_{\rm st}>0\) is a
sufficiently small universal constant.  There exist constants \(C,c_-,c_+>0\) such that if
\[
