{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.472202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fe53039113d7ff0551dd84b95e4506e6c7f3046c1e2f138430bd98dba0b7655","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:lowerbound of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $P_t$ be a hypocoercive $C_0$-semigroup on $\mathcal{H}$ with the decay function $r(t) = C e^{-\nu t}$ in (equation eq:exponentialconverge of the paper), and $P_{t,O}$ be a symmetric coercive $C_0$-semigroup on $\mathcal{H}_O$ that satisfies (assp:locoercive of the paper). Suppose that $P_t$ is a lift of $P_{t, O}$ and 
        the constant $\widetilde{s_{\rm m}} := \inf_{x \in \mathcal{H}_O^\perp \backslash \{0\}} \frac{\norm{\Pi_1 \mathsf{S} \Pi_1 x}_{\mathcal{H}_O}}{\lVertx\rVert_{\mathcal{H}_O}}$ is positive, where $\Pi_1$ is the projection from $\mathcal{H}_O^\perp$ to $\overline{\ran(\mathsf{L}|_{\mathcal{H}_O})}$. 

        Then, there holds
