{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.564361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8067310126f1a51dece2a3a4841d85cd9181a3f19fa608fed9747ce6808098cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $K \in \mathcal{C}^n$ and $L \in \mathcal{B}(\R^n)$. Define $M(K,L) = \sup_{x\in K, y\in L} \langle x, y \rangle$. Then,
