{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:25:41.599020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81161b2c2bab17027ef782e7f9fe867dbe33b9a85a7c77934cdeb4d1d09389d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:S-Z-liouville of arXiv:2608.11931, '\texorpdfstring{Nonlinear parabolic characterizations of stochastic completeness at infini'] Assume $\kappa=0$.  A graph $G$ satisfies \hyperref[def:SC]{\textup{(SC)}}{} if and only if for one (equivalently, all) strictly increasing $\psi\in\mathcal I$, the only $0\le h\in\ell^\infty(X)$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
    -\Delta h=\Psi h
\end{equation}
pointwise on $X$ is $h=0$.  In particular, if $G$ does not satisfy \hyperref[def:SC]{\textup{(SC)}}{}, then for every strictly increasing $\psi\in\mathcal I$ there exists a nontrivial $0\le h\in\ell^\infty(X)$ satisfying~(equation eq:nonlinear-liouville-eq of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.392152+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8120b31d5bec1811c1fe31fd090d40f164952a298c704dd5fa9d5e7695240c41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:diffeo_conjugation of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] Let $U, \tilde{U} \subset \mathbb{R}$ be open sets and consider a $C^{k+1}$ diffeomorphism $f:U \to \tilde{U}$, for some $k \geq 1$. Assume there exists $u_{\star} \in U$ such that $f(u_{\star}) = u_{\star}$ and such that $\zeta = f'(u_{\star})$ satisfies $|\zeta| \neq 1$. There exists a $C^{k}$ diffeomorphism $h: V \to \tilde{V}$ between open neighborhoods of $u_{\star}$ and the origin such that $h(u_{\star}) = 0$ and such that
\begin{equation}
f(x) = h^{-1} \Big( \zeta h(x) \Big), \quad \text{for all } x \in V.
\end{equation}
Furtheremore, the diffeomorphism $h$ is unique up to multiplication by constants. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.576927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8124b1cda49dbd1a11db3112e53933e079aefb888aac6a8778c0a32e0239409c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2512.09308, 'On asymptotic behavior of solutions to random fractional Riesz-Bessel equations with cycli'] [seneta2006regularly]
A function $L(\cdot)$ is slowly varying at infinity if it is real-valued, positive, and measurable on $[A,\infty)$ for some $A>0$, and satisfies the following condition for every $\lambda >0$:
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{x\to \infty} \frac{L(\lambda x)}{L(x)}=1.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.313649+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_812b35a2c954d2d119f550a191ef11bb5b1443424f76396696cb04a78a95fb3c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For all $p \in (0,1)$,
