{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.856531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_814dc065e14c1039e3202477e29cfdfbebd5198cd6fc6a9d08b913f6c968835a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:LehnerFormula of arXiv:2510.01021, '\Large Random Matrices, Intrinsic Freeness, and Sharp Non-Asymptotic Inequalities\relatedv'] [Lehner's formula~[LehnerFormula1999] (see also~[bandeira2023free])]

Let $A_0,A_1,\dots,A_n$ be self-adjoint matrices and $X_{\mathrm{free}}$ as in Definition~(def:Xfree of the paper):
\begin{equation}
\big\| X_{\mathrm{free}} \big\| = \max_{\varepsilon\in\{\pm1\}} \inf_{Z\succeq 0} \lambda_{\max}\left(Z^{-1} + \varepsilon A_0 + \sum_{k=1}^n A_k Z A_k \right).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.098136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_815373576c123783240dedf36a6ced16c4dd8d713ef949ef4061aa7bdced4a8c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.28198, 'Performative Privacy: When Differential Privacy Maximizes Utility'] Given the aggregated empirical mean mechanism, the exact probability that a specific individual data point $z$ is purged (i.e., its log-likelihood ratio breaches the threshold $\tau$) conditioned on $Z_t$ is given in closed form by:
\begin{equation*}
    \Pr(\Lambda(o_t|z) > \tau\mid Z_t)
    =
    1 - \Phi\left(
    \frac{\tau (N_t-1)\gamma}
    {\sqrt{N_t}\|z-\mu_z\|}
    -
    \frac{\sqrt{N_t}\|z-\mu_z\|}
    {2(N_t-1)\gamma}
    \right)
\end{equation*}
where $\Phi(\cdot)$ denotes the cumulative distribution function of the standard normal distribution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.116328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81548918d9e57fbe9916ca25f63859fdd9f4579393391286185a67138d83d1a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:B2 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] There exists $p^-_\sigma(\cdot, \cdot,\cdot)\in \mathrm{p} \mathscr{B}((0,\infty))\times \mathscr{B}^*(E)\times \mathscr{B}(E)$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}^x\left[f(X_t);t\leq \sigma \right]=\int_E p^-_\sigma(t,x,y)f(y)\mu(\mathrm{d} y),\quad \forall t>0,x\in E, f\in \mathrm{b}\mathscr{B}(E). 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.194101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_815ced3660bd3913939fb692cf90fb3927fe26b25d715c4c638bd6c533ced52b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 19 of arXiv:2605.03851, 'The Relay Random Tree:\\A stochastic geometry approach of multihop relay in an urban visib'] \textbf{Users being relayed by a given building.}

Let $(\alpha, \beta)\in \Half$ be a given point such that $\mathcal{L}([\beta,  +\infty[)>0$, and consider the landscape $\tilde{\landsc} := \landsc\cup \{(\alpha, \beta)\}$. 

Then, the expected length of the zone of eventual relaying of $(\alpha, \beta)$ is equal to 
$$\e[\ell(\zone(\alpha, \beta))] =\left\{
    \begin{array}{ll}
        \displaystyle\int_{0}^{\beta} -\frac{1}{\lambda}\frac{\primi(\beta)}{\primi(u)^2}du & \mbox{if } \beta<S \\
        +\infty & \mbox{if }\beta=S,
    \end{array}
\right.$$
where $S$ denotes the supremum of the support of $\mathcal{L}$. 
In particular, under the Palm measure, the average length of the zone of eventual relaying for a typical building is infinite. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.736161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8178415c524b119f02549f1e8690b02850adbe3673489467e717d49b9b8f6e4c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def_wtM of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Define the spectral domain $\mathbf D(\tau):=\{z=E+\mathrm{i} \eta\in \mathbb{C} :|z|\le \tau^{-1}, |\eta| \ge N^{-1+\tau}\}$ for an arbitrarily small constant $\tau>0$.
For $z_1,z_2\in \mathbf D(\tau)$, we define the $D\times D$ matrices $\widehat M$ and $L$ as
\begin{align}
    \widehat M_{ab}(z_1,z_2,\Lambda):=D\langle M(z_1) E_{a} M(z_2) E_{b}\rangle ,\quad L_{ab}(z_1,z_2, H, \Lambda):= D\langle G(z_1)E_{a}G(z_2)E_{b}\rangle , 
