{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.474147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81915de2fbd35f0eefb27ea0e8c3048a35f7d84d0c4aa79ffb0b52be4d03e30f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:intertcond of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Suppose that $\mathcal{P}_t$ is a $\sigma$-KMS detailed balanced with generator $\mathcal{L} = - \sum_{j \in \mathcal{J}} \partial_j^\star \partial_j$ that satisfies the $\kappa$-intertwining condition for $\kappa \in \mathbb{R}$. Then there holds 
