{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.617468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81bb2ed89149ab94d2fb9b1347a24d033beef030a198cc29b1db1024e49ec69f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem maintheorem of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $f \colon \mathbb N^s \to \mathbb C$ be a function that satisfies (mainassumption of the paper) and that is furthermore real and non-negative or satisfies (upperboundassp of the paper). Assume that the polytope $\cal P$ is bounded, that $\cal F$ is of dimension $d$ and not contained in a coordinate hyperplane, and that $\vec\ell$ is of convergent type for the face $\cal F$.

