with some constants \(C_i>0\), \(i\in\{1,...,5\}\), and \(c_M\) defined as in Lemma~\ref{lem:full-truncated-kl}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.140734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_822821d9d4165484b668260ea512aacdee40849f59cf7ce432b238f08c526e61","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:dd main of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let $\mathfrak{X} = [0, 1]^D$ be the unit cube in dimension~$D$, endowed with the $\ell^{\infty}$ metric $d$ and its Borel $\sigma$-field,
and let~$\mu$ be an absolutely continuous probability measure on~$\mathfrak{X}$ with density $f$ satisfying
\[
c\leq f(x)\leq C\mbox{\rm \ for every $x \in \mathfrak{X}$},
\]
where $0<c\leq C<\infty$. Given $\alpha \in (0, \infty)$, let
\begin{equation}

  r(n)\equiv r(n,D,c,\alpha) := c^{-1/D}(4 \cdot 3^{D - 1})^{1/D} (2 + \alpha)^{1/(2D)} \left( \frac{\ln n}{n} \right)^{1/(2 D)}.
