{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:01:25.573978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_836a05775ed00db1e48b36998391d09a2118198cb07b9a23385de1f9c2df2b86","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem TH1-*_nocutoff of arXiv:2605.15742, 'Turbulent stretching of FENE dumbbell polymer model via special stochastic scaling and sin'] \textbf{(Existence without cut-off.)} Assume $\kappa /(2+ k_T \beta) >1$. There exists $\eta>0$ such that if $k_T\beta \le \eta$ then there exists  at    least   one     solution $f_N$ to  (equation Ito-FP_eps-V2 of the paper) with $\varphi_\varepsilon\equiv 1$ in the sense of  (rmk:def_sol_nocutoff of the paper). Moreover,  it holds 
