{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.302906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_83ed75eec7f2e4021d1a36e888214438e0f4c7a0c9530160746a14056d93dd16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem2.4 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<1$, for any $z=(x,0)$ or $z=(0,x)$ with $x$ positive and large,
