{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:53:00.813342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84224ab2b31b423e1201c3e6746b869a5abcf7b3abd1ac942d60ebea8b81c6b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:giants_MCMs of arXiv:2607.16911, 'Multipartite random graphs with given degrees: local limit, revisiting the giant, distance'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:loc_lim of the paper), consider the branching process $(\mathcal T_\infty,\varnothing)$ that arises as the local limit of the graph sequence $(G_n)_{n \geq 1}$, and let $\eta$ denote its extinction probability.     
