{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.744290+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8468424d636b724f0b57c727adec365ae96d791ea6a9aa29dd053d9db6d1cc93","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2506.10511, '2506.10511'] For all $d\geq 1$ and all $\beta>0$, there exists a constant $c_2=c_2(d,\beta)>0$ {\rm(}depending only on $d$ and $\beta${\rm)} such that for each $k\in [1,K]_{\mathds{Z}}$ and each $S=\{i_1,\cdots, i_k\}\subset [1,K]_{\mathds{Z}}$ in the ascending order, we have
