{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.728976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_853a790991f528185dba292ea63947225cc8592ef66bf41a652e995695d55bfa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hitting-time of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] Suppose that $\alpha>1$ and $\theta>\theta_{0,L}$, and let $C_E$ denote the lower bound obtained from Corollary (coro:m_easy of the paper) for the region $|m(x)| < \mathsf{m}_{3}$. Fix any initialization $X_0$ and let $\tau_{m,\varepsilon} $ denote the first time $|m_t| \geq \varepsilon$, then for any $r>0$ we have 
