{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.068553+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85a11c76aa6de7e2065d89340d2c472ef04eb290e25719c712f90a3de60d3dd0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2606.27774, 'Variational Formulas for the Spectrum of\\ Block Wishart Matrices'] Fix integer $k \ge 1,$
let $\alpha \in (0,\infty)$, and $\nu\in\cuP_0(\sa{k}{\C})$.
 For any $\bZ \in\bbH_+^k$, 
 $\hat\bS_\up{\alpha,\nu}(\bZ)$ 
 of Eq.~\eqref{eq:free_ST_def}
 is the unique solution of
