{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334524+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85ccbdeeedd655e2ecda8a815e71a0b3c5dd91eaeab782b10698033c17d3af23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=\left(V,E\right)$ be a locally finite weighted graph and let $\psi\in C^{1}\left(0,+\infty\right)$ be a concave function. Then for every $0<f\in \ell^{\infty}\left(V\right)$ with $R_{f}<\infty$, 
