{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.315999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85eef1c1b47bca327a2251fd29a5076568d000bdc1f4748bbc6ef0f60eec8b2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] Each point process $\widehat{\rm R}_{n,r}, r\in {\mathbb Z}_{>0},$ is  Poisson, with the  intensity measure
