{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.668731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_86192d16ecb6e31b1bc97fb89478f7d7ecb731dfc43ca879300ee1410e9ce48b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (Finite \(n\) enumerative convergence) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] Fix \(\lambda\in\mathbb R\), let \(p_n\) be given by
\eqref{eq:pn-intro}, and let \(\Xi_n\) be given by \eqref{eq:Xi-intro}.

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2.2em]
\item For every fixed \(q\ge1\), the factorial moment measures satisfy
\begin{equation}
  \alpha_{\Xi_n}^{(q)}\xrightarrow{v}\alpha_\lambda^{(q)}
  \qquad\text{on }E^q.
\end{equation}
In fact, the stronger uniform local asymptotic in
Proposition~\ref{prop:local} holds.

\item There is a unique point process
\(\Xi_\lambda^{\mathrm{enum}}\) on \(E\) whose Laplace functional is
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  \mathbb E e^{-\langle f,\Xi_\lambda^{\mathrm{enum}}\rangle}
  =\sum_{q=0}^\infty\frac{(-1)^q}{q!}
  \int_{E^q}\prod_{i=1}^q(1-e^{-f(z_i)})
  \,\mathrm d\alpha_\lambda^{(q)}(\mathbf z)
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
for every \(f\in C_c^+(E)\), and
\begin{equation}
  \Xi_n\Rightarrow\Xi_\lambda^{\mathrm{enum}}
  \qquad\text{in }M_{\mathrm p}(E)
\end{equation}
under the vague topology.
\end{enumerate}
In \eqref{eq:enum-Laplace-theorem}, the \(q=0\) term is one: by convention
\(\alpha_\lambda^{(0)}\) is unit mass on the singleton \(E^0\), and the empty
product equals one. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.019509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8620caf699563748cdec895692c3286d5f2ca50f6eab2175e55841ba7d0ead91","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2-l07 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] For all $N\ge 1$, 
\begin{equation}

L^*_N {\mathbf 1}\; =\;  U \;+\;  K\, \Upsilon \;,
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

\begin{gathered}
{\color{blue} U (\eta)} \,:=\,
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N} \big\{  (\Delta_N \varrho) (x)\,
+\, K\, G_0(x)\, \big\}  \, \zeta_x 
\\
{\color{blue} \Upsilon (\eta)} \,:=\,
\sum_{j=1}^d \sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N}  G_{1,j}(x) \, \omega_{x} \, \omega_{x+e_j}
\,+\,
\sum_{x\in {\mathbb T}^d_N}  G_2(x) \, \omega_{x-e_1} \, \omega_{x} \,
\omega_{x+e_1} \;,
\end{gathered}
\end{equation}
and $\Delta_N$ stands for the discrete Laplacian, $(\Delta_NG)(x) =
N^2 \sum_{1\le j \le d} [ G(x+e_j) + G(x-e_j)  - 2 G(x) ]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:58:10.026056+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8622d03afd14ebb723bdc6ae4c38fb5fded51ea3e4faa08fbaad5550ebba74aa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2607.19844, 'Binomial probabilities at a fixed distance from the mode:\\ size-biasing and the complete '] Fix $R\in\mathbb N$.  As $N\to\infty$, uniformly for $p$ in a compact subset of $(0,1)$ and for
	integers $r$ with $|r|\le R$, with $\nu=\lceil Np\rceil$ and $h=h_N=\nu-Np$,
	\begin{equation}
		\Pr\{X=\nu+r\}
		\sim\frac{Np}{Np+h+r}\cdot\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi Npq}}\;
		\exp\left(\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{1}{N^{k}}
		\left[\widetilde A_k(h;p)-\frac{\Xi_k(p)}{k}\,S_k(h,r)\right]\right),
	\end{equation}
	and equivalently
	\begin{equation}
		\Pr\{X=\nu+r\}
		\sim\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\,(\nu+r)(N-\nu-r)/N}}\;
		\exp\left(\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{1}{N^{k}}
		\left[\widehat A_k(h;p)-\frac{\Xi_k(p)}{k}\,T_k(h,r)\right]\right).
	\end{equation}
	Equivalently, after either exponential is re-expanded multiplicatively and truncated after
	the term $N^{-M}$, the relative remainder is $O(N^{-M-1})$, uniformly in $|r|\le R$ and in
	$p$ on the chosen compact subset of $(0,1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.246622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_862926e82066b958c1415efb14ed0c988ecbd4212c54de88ee8930149a320bf1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition gcmeasure of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] Fix any $\sigma\in\R$. Consider the product probability measure below on {\small$\R^{\Z}$}:

\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}^{\sigma}[\d{\boldsymbol{\phi}}]:=\prod_{\x\in\Z}\mathcal{Z}_{\upsilon_{\sigma},\mathscr{U}}^{-1}\exp\left[-\mathscr{U}[{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\x}]+\upsilon_{\sigma}{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\x}\right]\d{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\x}.
\end{align}

Here, {\small$\mathcal{Z}_{\upsilon_{\sigma},\mathscr{U}}$} is a normalizing partition function, and {\small$\upsilon_{\sigma}\in\R$} is chosen so that {\small$\E^{\sigma}{\boldsymbol{\phi}}_{\x}=\sigma$} for all $\x\in\Z$, where {\small$\E^{\sigma}$} is expectation with respect to {\small$\mathbb{P}^{\sigma}$}. (Well-defined-ness of {\small$\mathbb{P}^{\sigma}$} will follow from Assumption (assump:potential of the paper).)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.313378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_862b3c25e917d9c8193c41d508bfcf63c87c26971103db6fcdf2286870b9033d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 7 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For all $p \in (0, 1/2]$,
