{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.499798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8647b7534747e0b07860f9e959ceac7c66103b0143dc034502c899866e549cae","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:IBJ-scalar of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The one-point Fredholm determinant
$F_{t, a, n} = \det(I - K_{t, a, n})$ satisfies
