{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.650623+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8664492c62fc33535a1a9023d69d71f225072286e48db6e0263056c8b1ec4a3d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma representation of arXiv:2411.04590, 'Singular stochastic delay equations driven by fractional Brownian motion: Dynamics, longti'] We have the following pathwise identity on a set of full measure:
		\begin{align}
			\int _{s}^{t}B^{\epsilon}_{s-r,u-r}\otimes \mathrm{d} B_{u}^{\epsilon}=\int_{0}^1\rho(z)\int _{s-\epsilon z}^{t-\epsilon z}B^{\epsilon}_{s-r,u+\epsilon z-r}\otimes \mathrm{d}B_{u} \mathrm{d}z=\int _{0}^1\rho(z)\int _{s-\epsilon z}^{t-\epsilon z}B^{\epsilon}_{s-r,u+\epsilon z-r}\otimes \mathrm{d}^{\circ}B_{u} \mathrm{d}z.
		\end{align}
		\begin{proof}
			Note that the integrals in (equation eqn:pathwise of the paper) are defined pathwise, since \(B^{\epsilon}\) is smooth and \(B\) is a Hölder continuous path (almost surely for \(\gamma < H\)). Using integration by parts, we obtain:
			\begin{align*}
				\int _{s-\epsilon z}^{t-\epsilon z}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,u+\epsilon z-r}\mathrm{d}B^{j}_{u}=(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,t-r}B^{j}_{t-\epsilon z}-\int_{s-r}^{t-r}B^{j}_{u+r-\epsilon z}\mathrm{d}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{u}.
			\end{align*}
			Consequently,
			\begin{align*}
				\int _{\mathbb{R}}\rho(z)&\int _{s-\epsilon z}^{t-\epsilon z}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,u+\epsilon z-r}\mathrm{d} B^{j}_{u} \mathrm{d}z\\&=\int_{\mathbb{R}}\rho(z)(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,t-r}B^{j}_{t-\epsilon z}\mathrm{d}z-\int_{\mathbb{R}}\int_{s-r}^{t-r}\rho(z)B^{j}_{u+r-\epsilon z}\mathrm{d}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{u} \mathrm{d}z\\
				&=(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,t-r}(B^{\epsilon})^{j}_{t}-\int_{s-r}^{t-r}(B^{\epsilon})^{j}_{u+r}\mathrm{d}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{u}.
			\end{align*}
			From integration by parts,
			\begin{align*}
				(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,t-r}(B^{\epsilon})^{j}_{t}-\int_{s-r}^{t-r}(B^{\epsilon})^{j}_{u+r}\mathrm{d}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{u}
				=\int _{s}^{t}(B^{\epsilon})^{i}_{s-r,u-r}\mathrm{d} (B^{\epsilon})_{u}^{j},
			\end{align*}
			which implies the claim.
		\end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.984540+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8672ba5f25e5adc3ec2e941372d4cdb0a9660f5e320e5c3ea7edd571564bfad3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Exact orthogonal replica identities) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $E$ and $H$ be real Hilbert spaces, let
