{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.770890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8743ae9636dcbd6ccc24e1cd4f1e11930352387519498af332a945fc1d618111","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 of arXiv:2512.05340, 'The rate of convergence of the critical mean-field $O(N)$ magnetization via multivariate n'] Let $V$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{assumption: assumptions on V}, let $P_t$ denote the semigroup corresponding to~\eqref{eq: overdamped langevin},
  and let $h \in \smoothlip$. For any $x, u, v, w \in \RR^{d}$ the following hold:
    \begin{align}
        \left|D P_{t}h(x)[u]\right| &\leq C_{1}\, e^{-\theta t}\, |u|,
        \\

         |D^{2} P_{t}h(x)[u, v]| &\leq S(t)\, e^{-\theta t/2}\, |u||v|,\\

        |D^{3} P_{t}h(x)[u, v, w]| &\leq Q(t)\, e^{-\theta t/4}\, |u||v||w|, 
    \end{align}
    where $S:(0,\infty)\to(0,\infty)$ and $Q:(0,\infty)\to(0,\infty)$ are given by
