{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.858168+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87d53e93b2c1c93d434fc8d3b2015abb78060be671debbe9172db58d73a26a1a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:ProcDecomp of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] There is an $\mathcal{E}^{a}$-exceptional set $S^a \subset L$ s.th.\ for all $z \in L\setminus S^a$ under $P_z^a$ there exists an $\mathcal{M}_t^a$-cylindrical Wiener process $W^{z,a}$, s.th.\ the sample paths of the associated distorted Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process $M^{a}$ on $L$ satisfy for all $l \in D(A) \cap H_0^1$ that
    \begin{multline}
        \langle l, X_{t}^a-X_0^a\rangle = \int_0^{t} \langle l, dW_s^{z,a}\rangle + \frac{1}{2} \int_0^{t} \langle l, n_{\sigma^{(a)}} (X_s^a) \rangle dL_{s}^{\var{\sigma^{(a)}}} - \int_0^{t} \langle l'', X_s^a \rangle ds \\ \forall \, t \geq 0 \, \text{$P_z^a$-a.s.}
    \end{multline}
    In this equation, $L_{t}^{\var{\sigma^{(a)}}}$ denotes the real valued PCAF associated with $\var{\sigma^{(a)}}$ by the Revuz correspondence.

    The analogous statement holds for $\rho$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.334831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87d7a5aba46bb27944eee45a99ab24d4d4c368168299b22eb42c96c8ff8cf52a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.30409, 'Gradient estimates and volume doubling for locally finite weighted graphs with $CD\psi(n,-'] Let $G=\left(V,E\right)$ be a locally finite weighted graph satisfying the $CD\psi\left(n,-K\right)$ condition with $K\geq0$, where $\psi\in C^{1}\left(0,+\infty\right)$ is a concave function. Let $b>\frac{1}{2}$ be a constant. Then for any $0<f\in \ell^{\infty}\left(V\right)$, 
