{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.926329+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87eca108473aaede8a2943858431f9170e642bd3e26cf88971cd21282811b134","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2609.00988, 'Covering Projective Height Balls by Subspaces in Rigid Adelic Spaces'] There are constants $c_4>0$ and $C_4\ge1$, effectively computable from $d,r_2, |D_K|$, such that for every $T\ge0$:
