{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.567852+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87f24f14e06665aabb2be888a265f467cdc84ef448d3a5ee536cc4d8cb9a0e2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem t:proba of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Let the family $\widetilde{\xi}_{a;n}$ satisfy the assumptions~((a:center of the paper))--((a:growth of the paper)). Then there exist constants $C_1,C_{2}$ and a number $n_0$ such that for every $n>n_0$
