{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.665096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87f97224f3f09b9b0f29301b60e48dbbff49c1fe001b47f4320b05be03d254cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm clt-from-var-lb of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] Here $n$ denotes the length of the segment; the statement will be applied with $n$ replaced by other lengths $m$ with $m\asymp n$.
Assume $1\ll\ell\ll n$ and
$\go_e\stackrel{\mathrm{d}}{=}\mathrm{Exp}(1)^{1/\theta}$. Suppose that,
for some constants $c>0$, $\ga\geqslant0$, and $A\in\mathds{R}$,
\begin{align}
 \var(T_{[n]})\geqslant c\frac{n}{\ell^\ga(\log\ell)^A}

\end{align}
for all sufficiently large $n$. Suppose further that there exists an integer sequence $b=b_{n,\ell}$
such that $b>2\ell$, $b=o(n)$, and
