{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.074159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88212d9a1680567b66093f38bc76bd2aa235e1290f3ec52d25a196eaedd3636d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:GKS of arXiv:2411.14111, 'Stochastic processes on preferential attachment models'] Consider two Ising measures $\mu$ and $\mu^\prime$ on graphs $G = (V, E)$ and $G^\prime= (V, E^\prime)$, with inverse temperatures $\beta$ and $\beta^\prime$, and external fields $\underline{B}$ and $\underline{B}^\prime$, respectively. If $E\subseteq E^\prime$, $\beta \leq \beta^\prime$, and $0 \leq B_i \leq B^\prime_i$ for all $i \in V$, then, for any $U \subset V$,
