{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.500212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88798eeacb2fcc9d6da09ea299b0a59bb9493a72b6759f1c5c1c1982b6475061","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:S_rary of arXiv:2607.22291, 'Rare subtree patterns in size-conditioned Bienaymé trees: Poisson approximation and declum'] Let $(k_n)$ be such that $s_{r,k_n}+\ell_{r,k_n}=n^{o(1)}$. Fix $\eta\in(0,1-1/\alpha)$ and set $M_n=\lfloor n^{1-\eta}\rfloor$. Then:
