{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.258108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891433a07638277a1f0d136841654687b4d11b60583b0c33948f74b6957c4211","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 5 (Feldman--H\'ajek) of arXiv:2609.01105, 'Obstruction to quasi-invariance of Gaussian measures under transport flows on Riemannian M'] \cite[Theorem 2.25]{DaPratoZabczyk2014}\\
Let~\(\nu_1\) and~\(\nu_2\) be two centered Gaussian measures over a Hilbert space $H$ with covariance operators~\(Q_1\) and~\(Q_2\). Then $\nu_1$ and $\nu_2$ are either mutually singular or mutually absolutely continuous with respect to each other. The latter happens if and only if 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item measures~\(\nu_1\) and~\(\nu_2\) have the same Cameron--Martin space $Q_1^{\mez}(H)=Q_2^{\mez}(H)=:H_0$;

    \item $Q_1^{-\mez}Q_2^{\mez}(Q_1^{-\mez}Q_2^{\mez})^* - \mathbf{1} \in \mathfrak{S}_2(\bar H_0)$. 
\end{enumerate}
In the first item, $Q_i^{\mez}(H)$ is the range of the operator $Q_i^{\mez}$, and in the last item, $\bar H_0$ stands for the completion of $H_0$ under the $H$ norm, and the adjoint is understood with respect to $H$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.302096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891a07840c23b70d97d28d4f1406d95f5f449f4883f109129cc1b1a311a89fc1","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:fun_convergence of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] Let $\mathcal T_\Phi$ denote the topology on the space $\Phi$ such that $\varphi_n \to \varphi$ if the following two conditions hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  For every $R\in\mathbb{R}$ there exists $I(R,\varphi)\subseteq\mathfrak{X}$ compact and $N_0(R,\varphi)>0$  such that\ 
    \begin{equation}
        \frac{\varphi_n(\xi)}{\mathcal P(\xi)^2}\leq R, \qquad \forall \xi\in I^c, n\geq N_0.
    \end{equation}
    \item $\text{hypo}(\varphi_n)\xrightarrow{\operatorname{PK}}\text{hypo}(\varphi)$,  as $n\rightarrow \infty$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.799333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891a5b45e6b3b8443b59f0f67daeffba7ac0138ea7b51ed6f52f5878f8c3a709","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cc-gaussian-flip-probabilities of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Recall \(x_t^{\gR},x_t^{\gB}\) from
    (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper). Fix \(c_0>0\)
    and \(M<\infty\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and suppose that
    \begin{align}
    |\gR_t|\ge c_0N,
    \qquad
    |\gB_t|\ge c_0N,

    \end{align}
    while $x_t^{\gR}$ and $x_t^{\gB}$ in (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper) satisfy
    \begin{align}
    |x_t^{\gR}|\le M,
    \qquad
    |x_t^{\gB}|\le M.

    \end{align}
    Then, uniformly over such configurations,
    \begin{subequations}
    \begin{align}
    p_t^{\gR}
    &=
    \Phi\left(
    x_t^{\gR}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{v_t^{\gR}}}
    \right)
    +O\left(\frac1{\log N}\right),
    \\
    p_t^{\gB}
    &=
    \Phi\left(
    x_t^{\gB}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{v_t^{\gB}}}
    \right)
    +O\left(\frac1{\log N}\right).

    \end{align}
    \end{subequations}
    For \(\Delta_t\ge1\), there are constants \(c,C>0\) such that
    \begin{align}
    c\frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}
    \le
    p_t^{\gR}-p_t^{\gB}
    \le
    C\frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}.

    \end{align}
    Furthermore, for every fixed \(C_0<\infty\), when
    \(0\le\Delta_t\le C_0\sqrt{N/\log N}\), we have
    \begin{align}
    p_t^{\gR}-p_t^{\gB}
    =
    \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi}}
    \frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}
    +O\left(\frac{p\Delta_t}{\log N}\right).

    \end{align}
    All implicit constants and the constants \(c,C\) depend only on
    \(b,c_0,M\), and additionally on \(C_0\) in
    (equation eq:cc-gaussian-critical-flip-difference of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.211161+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891f92728758f6a97a8b7ec829f3eb5b7ff6b0d0b9ea54ba7c12ab9cb9b551cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem head-controls of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] Let $1\ler_{\star}\le d$, let $A\in\operatorname{rip}(\delta,k)$
with $\delta<\delta_{\mathrm{sharp}}(k/r_{\star})$, and let $\lambda>\lambda_{0}\ge0$.
 Suppose $\sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\frac{1}{2}\normtwo{A\sigma}^{2}+\lambda\bigl(\normone{\sigma_{\mathrm{tail}}}-\normone{\sigma_{\mathrm{head}}}\bigr)\le\lambda_{0}\normone{\sigma}.
