    \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.862340+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_893ad0264984c9716a7dc8fc61d550cc5512cf49ed1a0ffbc1f5bcd5726b90de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lower-bound-prob-2 of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper) is satisfied, with $C' > 0$ satisfying Item~(item:non-persistence-two of the paper) of Assumption~(ass:non-persistence of the paper). Suppose that $(X_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ and $(X'_{i})_{i \in \mathbb{N}}$ are independent sequences of random variables, with $X_{i} \sim X'_{i}$. Suppose, moreover, that $n, \phi_{n} \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ are given such that
    $n < \phi_{n} - 1$, and  
    \begin{equation} 
    \frac{\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \E{X_{i}}\right)^2}{\sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n} - 1} \var{X_{i}}} \leq \frac{1}{2}.
    \end{equation}
    Then, 
    \begin{equation} 
        \Prob{\sum_{i=1}^{\phi_{n} - 1} X_{i} < \sum_{i=n}^{\phi_{n}-1} X'_{i}} > \frac{1}{96 + 4C'}. 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.737359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_893ce67196b933f54740d44b0a773c4f8e6c474e140447dfa143a54ac53d6598","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] Let \(E\sim\operatorname{Exp}(1)\) be independent of \(B\).  For \(T>0\),
let \(\mathbb Q_T\) be the product law of \((B,E)\) conditioned on
\(\{M_T\leq E\}\).  Equivalently,
\begin{equation}
  \mathrm d\mathbb Q_T(B,x)
  :=\mathcal Z(T)^{-1}
    e^{-x}\mathds1_{\{M_T\leq x\}}\,\mathrm d\PP(B)\,\mathrm dx.

\end{equation}
This is a probability law whose path marginal is \(\widehat{\PP}_T\).  Put
\begin{equation}
  F_T(x):=\PP(M_T\leq x),
  \qquad
  \beta_T(\mathrm dx)
  :=\frac{e^{-x}F_T(x)}{\mathcal Z(T)}\,\mathrm dx,
  \qquad x\geq0.

\end{equation}
Then \(\beta_T\) is the barrier marginal.  For every \(x>0\), a regular
conditional law of the path given \(E=x\) is
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb P_{T,x}:=\mathcal L(B\mid M_T\leq x).

\end{equation}
Under \(\mathbb Q_T\), the overshoot \(E-M_T\) is
\(\operatorname{Exp}(1)\) and is independent of \(B\).  Moreover, for
\(A\geq0\),
\begin{equation}
  \beta_T([A,\infty))=\mathbb Q_T(E\geq A)
  \leq2p_*^{-m_H}e^{-A/2}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.193938+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89407a8ef373aab0857f879ba694a3a973bc905d26b57bc99696f7fd069f32e2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 (Dynamic master inequalities for expectations) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] For any fixed $n,S\in\N$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
\Upsilon_t(n,S)\lesssim \Upsilon_0(n,S) + &\int_0^t \left(\Upsilon_s(n,S-1) + \sum_{S'\le S-2} \frac{1}{\eta^{S-S'+1}_s}\Upsilon_s(n-2,S')\right)\dif s\\
+&\frac{1}{N}\int_0^t \left(\Upsilon_s(n+1,S+2) + \sum_{S'\le S}\frac{1}{\eta^{S-S'+2}_s}\Upsilon_s(n-1,S')\right)\dif s,
\end{split}

\end{equation}
uniformly in $t\in [0,T]$. The implicit constant in~\eqref{eq:dynamic_master} does not depend on $N$ and $z=z_T\in\mathcal{D}$, but it may depend on $n$ and $S$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.884942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8944c64c56e775965c3e6628e806ab9034e7b4b2860011a0756ebd9898f7c80f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:cycles of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] The space of the cycles of a chemical system  $(\Omega, \mathcal R, \mathcal R_s,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ is defined as
