{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.041347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89488d3a9f1ffa7ee83a788cab5cba65e2a02838fffada963bd9da17136cbd04","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] $2\leq h\leq n$. Let $C_1,\dots,C_h$ be a partition of $\hat V$ and $T^h=T^h(C_1,\dots,C_n)$ defined as after \eqref{peRk}. Then:
