{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.714593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a3c098a428086fa4fba6d89abf551830cfb75fab221a8b9a0a57e23b84062fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma repl_lemma_ave of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] For every $H \in C([0,T])$, for any $t \in [0,T]$ and $z=\epsilon_N$, it holds
\begin{equation} 
\lim_{\epsilon\to 0}\lim_{N\to+\infty}\mathbb{E}_{\nu_N} \left[\Big | \int_0^t [\eta_{sN^2}(z) - \overrightarrow{\eta}^{\lfloor \epsilon N\rfloor}_{sN^2}(z)] H(s)ds\Big| \right] =0,
\end{equation}
where, for every $L\in\mathbb N$ and $\eta \in \Omega_N$,
\begin{equation} 
\overrightarrow{\eta}^L(z) :=\frac{1}{L\epsilon_N}\sum_{y= z+\epsilon_N}^{z+L\epsilon_N}\eta(y).
\end{equation}
The same result holds for $z = \tau_N$ by replacing the average to the right, i.e. $\overrightarrow{\eta}^{\lfloor \epsilon N\rfloor}_{sN^2}$, by an average to the left, i.e. $\overleftarrow{\eta}^{\lfloor \epsilon N\rfloor}_{sN^2}$, which is defined, for every $L\in\mathbb N$ and $\eta \in \Omega_N$, as
\begin{equation}
 \overleftarrow{\eta}^L(z) :=\frac{1}{L\epsilon_N}\sum_{y=z-L\epsilon_N}^{z-\epsilon_N}\eta(y).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.161145+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a4f043b705f5720ea7ad30d931867620d9974237410ef24193775aac28ca8bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2604.16795, '2604.16795'] Under Assumption {\rm\ref{A0}} and \eqref{ass},  the probability measure $\nu$ defined by
	\begin{align}
		\nu(\d x) = \frac{\va_0(x)}{\displaystyle\int_{\R^d} \va_0(y) \,\mu(\d y)} \,\mu(\d x)
