	is the unique quasi-stationary distribution for the Feynman-Kac semigroup $(P_t)_{t\ge 0}$ associated with the branching-diffusion process $(Z_t)_{t\ge 0}$ $($see \eqref{E:FK} below$)$. 
 That is, for any $t>0$ and any bounded measurable function $\phi$, it holds that
	\begin{align}
		\int_{\R^d} \mathbb{E}_x \left[ \exp\left(-\int_0^t K(X_s) \,\d s\right) \phi(X_t) \right] \nu(\d x) = e^{-\lambda_0 t} \int_{\R^d} \phi(x)\, \nu(\d x).\end{align}
