{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.557281+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a516eb0043e4d5a6e46fb873c626d812032b7d984342cadf49f6e4abef8bb81","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Push-TASEP-propagator of arXiv:2608.02772, 'Non-Abelian Hirota-Miwa Equations for the KPZ Universality Class'] The propagator $B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}$ satisfies:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)},
leftmargin=*]
\item For all $i > j$ and $r, r' \in \mathbb{Z}$,
\begin{equation}
[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1}}]_{ij}(r{+}1, r'{+}1)
= [B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r').
\end{equation}

\item For all $i > j$ and $r, r' \in \mathbb{Z}$,
\begin{equation}
[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1}}]_{ij}(r, r')
- [B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r')
= \sum_{j < \mu < i}
[B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{i\mu}(r, a_\mu{+}1)[B_{\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{1}}]_{\mu j}
(a_\mu{+}1, r').
\end{equation}

\item The propagator is $t$-independent and
invariant under uniform shifts of the particle
labels: replacing each $n_i$ by $n_i + 1$ leaves
$[B_{\mathbf{a},\mathbf{n}}]_{ij}(r, r')$ unchanged.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.915825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8a564b49394a04c30b96d809cb6452206e105ea553306029c4872bf9964ce23e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:reweight_by_two of arXiv:2506.10765, 'A General Coupling for Ising Models and Beyond'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite  graph. Let $A\subset V$ with $|A|$ even (could be $0$). Then, $\forall \omega\in\{0,1\}^E$,
