{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:18:13.247750+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ad0cd5f65ea9291b477f213c4760eab4c9a71c3716c0ad6de268c257d17f050","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition admissible of arXiv:2507.10545, 'KPZ equation from a class of nonlinear SPDEs in infinite volume'] \fsp We say that a local function {\small$\mathfrak{q}:\R^{\Z}\to\R$} is \emph{admissible} if:

\begin{enumerate}
