 >
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_N^G(B).
\end{equation}
Both conclusions, as well as the local-maximum and local-minimum
versions of (equation eq:coexistence-exact of the paper), remain valid for the standard
symmetric-coordinate model (equation eq:symmetric-coordinate-model of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b536a0fbf12d7900f5b4d0b354bcb2c55c06d3f0312299640d98060dce4d545","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 4$. There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $n\geq 1$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_n$ containing $0$ which satisfies the following properties:
