{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:31:20.577519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6486954731c46e4be7098b6449ae7998d430413b0883691397e8c8e510391c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] In the setting of Section \ref{sec:ou-diff}, let $\mu = N(0,1)$ and $\nu = N(0,\eta^2)$. Then $P^{T}$ and $Q^{T}$ can be explicitly computed, and setting $\pi^{T} = (x_0,x_{T})_{\#}P^{T}$ and $q^{T} = (x_0,x_{T})_{\#}Q^{T}$ we compute
