{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.766116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6aa9c1364d37db7ec350c2fe7863a50011ab913c16f7844a0bb8da8a555be5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2512.04807, 'Existence and uniqueness of the canonical Brownian motion in non-simple conformal loop ens'] Let $F_1,F_2$ be two sets such that $F_1 \cap F_2$ is a non-empty finite set. For $i=1,2$, let $(\CE_i,\CF_i)$ be a resistance form on $F_i$, and let $(\CE,\CF)$ be the resistance form on $F_1 \cup F_2$ defined by
 \begin{align*}\begin{split}
  \CF &= \{ f : f|_{F_1} \in \CF_1,\, f|_{F_2} \in \CF_2 \} ,\\
  \CE(f,f) &= \CE_1(f|_{F_1},f|_{F_1})+\CE_2(f|_{F_2},f|_{F_2}) .
 \end{split}\end{align*}
 Then the following holds. Let $A \subseteq F_1 \cup F_2$ be a finite set containing $F_1 \cap F_2$, let $A_i = A \cap F_i$ for $i=1,2$, and let $w_A, w_{A,i}$ be the weight functions associated with $\CE|_A, \CE_i|_{A_i}$, respectively.
 Then
 \[
  w_A(x,y) =
  \begin{cases}
   w_{A,1}(x,y)+w_{A,2}(x,y) ,& x,y \in F_1 \cap F_2 ,\\
   w_{A,1}(x,y) ,& x,y \in F_1 ,\, \{x,y\} \nsubseteq F_1 \cap F_2 ,\\
   w_{A,2}(x,y) ,& x,y \in F_2 ,\, \{x,y\} \nsubseteq F_1 \cap F_2 ,\\
   0 ,& \text{otherwise.}
  \end{cases}
 \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.778352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b6cff83f309b8faa5ea37517c736cd06d43b07f02d3476d8c91fc5cf177bae7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 (Uniform local and local-maximum bounds) of arXiv:2609.02257, 'Aperiodic random walks: uniform estimates, local limits and invariance principles'] There are constants \(C,c>0\), independent of \(N,L,z,R\), such that
for all sufficiently large \(N\), \(L,R\in\Z_{\ge0}\), and \(z\in\Z\),
\begin{align}
 \Pp(S_N(L)=z)
 &\le \frac{C}{\sqrt{L+1}}
 \exp\left\{-c\frac{z^2}{L+|z|+1}\right\},       \\
 \Pp\left(S_N(L)=z,
       \max_{0\le j\le L}|S_N(j)|\ge R\right)
 &\le \frac{C}{\sqrt{L+1}}
 \exp\left\{-c\frac{R^2}{L+R+1}\right\}.         
\end{align}
Moreover, for some sufficiently large \(N_0\), the uniform lattice
local central limit theorem holds:
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{L\to\infty}\sup_{N\ge N_0}\sup_{z\in\Z}
 \left|
 \sigma_N\sqrt L\,\Pp(S_N(L)=z)
 -\frac1{\sqrt{2\pi}}
  \exp\left\{-\frac{z^2}{2\sigma_N^2L}\right\}
 \right|=0.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.908615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b706847f91903ae86c6ff8f296abd1a65ad873c3a089cfaf31cb79e99a3f203","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop:iteration of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Let $f:[0, \infty)\times [0, \infty) \to [0, \infty]$ be a non-negative function. Suppose it holds, that for all $l>k \geq 0$ and $ \sigma>\sigma' \geq 0$
         \begin{align*}
             f(l, \sigma')\leq \frac{C_{\mathrm{DG}}}{(\sigma - \sigma')^\alpha(l-k)^\beta} f(k, \sigma)^\gamma, 
         \end{align*}
         for some constants $C_{\mathrm{DG}}, \alpha, \beta >0$ and $\gamma >1$. Then, there exists a constant $K\equiv K(C, f, \sigma', \alpha, \beta, \gamma)$ such that 
         \begin{align*}
             f(l, \sigma')=0, \quad \forall l\geq K. 
         \end{align*}
         In particular, we may choose
         \begin{align}

             K = f(0, \sigma)^{\frac{\gamma-1}{\beta}}C_{\mathrm{DG}}^{\frac{1}{\beta}}2^{\frac{(\alpha+\beta)}{\gamma-1}+1}(\sigma-\sigma')^{-\frac{\alpha}{\beta}}, 
         \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.423470+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b726597c9a71f1e25fb64d2bb0262c399cc76f23fd477b4676e747214810d4c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop maypoletwist of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a $C^0$-foliation on $M$ with a $\mathbb{T}^3$-type planar exceptional minimal set $\Lambda$. For any $\varepsilon > 0$, and after an arbitrarily $C^0$-small isotopy of $\mathcal{F}$ whose size is independent on $\varepsilon$, there exists a maypole green $\mathfrak{G} = (N, \gamma, P)$ for $\Lambda$ of size $\leq \varepsilon$ (with a smooth framing of $P$) such that for every $\delta > 0$, there exist two $C^0$-foliations $\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ on $M \setminus \interior P$ such that
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ coincide with $\mathcal{F}$ away from $N$ and near $\partial M$,
    \item $T\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ is $\varepsilon$-close to $T\mathcal{F}$ everywhere, and $\delta$-close to it near $\partial P$,
    \item $\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ has \emph{positive} (resp.~\emph{negative}) slope along $\partial P$ in the chosen smooth framing.
\end{itemize}
In particular, for $\varepsilon$ small enough, the minimal sets of $\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ disjoint from $P$ correspond to minimal sets of $\mathcal{F}$, and $\mathcal{F}^\pm_\delta$ coincide with $\mathcal{F}$ near those.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.652660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b73eff7f043e8ca79ad008082abfe437c2f6ac72353f7135548194eca729813","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2607.24533, 'Colored Markov-Modulated Brownian Motion for Preemptive Workload Stacks'] {Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{assump:intensity} and~\ref{assump:stability} hold, and fix a depleting color $\ell$.} Then $\vect U_\ell$ solves
\eqref{eq:layer-qme}, has a simple zero eigenvalue with right
eigenvector $\e$, and has all remaining eigenvalues in the open left
half-plane.
Let $\vect V_\ell$ denote the complementary solution of
\begin{equation}

\tfrac12(\vect\Delta_\sigma^{(\ell)})^2\vect V_\ell^2
+\vect\Delta_\mu^{(\ell)}\vect V_\ell
+\widetilde{\vect T}^{(\ell)}
=\vect 0,
\end{equation}
whose eigenvalues lie in the open right half-plane. Standard MMBM
Wiener--Hopf theory gives this complementary solution and the
nonsingularity of $\vect V_\ell-\vect U_\ell$
\citep{Asmussen1995,AhnMeini2020}. Define
\begin{equation}

\vect W_\ell
:=2\big[(\vect\Delta_\sigma^{(\ell)})^2
(\vect V_\ell-\vect U_\ell)\big]^{-1}.
\end{equation}
Then, the Green kernel appearing in \eqref{eq:launch-op-correct} is
\begin{equation}

\vect G_\ell(y,x)=
\begin{cases}
\big(e^{\vect V_\ell y}-e^{\vect U_\ell y}\big)
e^{-\vect V_\ell x}\,\vect W_\ell,
& 0\le y\le x,\\[4pt]
\big(e^{\vect U_\ell(y-x)}
-e^{\vect U_\ell y}e^{-\vect V_\ell x}\big)\vect W_\ell,
& y\ge x>0.
\end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.562218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b744e82ea61da0aba05a1a239b97f3c4096ec0fdd8b2e384acc007c4b034bec","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:primitive-up of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[proposition]{prop:primitive-dereg}
For the point-incoherent version,
\begin{align}
 \delta_{L,\mathrm{dr}}^{J,\mathrm{up}}(V)
 &\le
 \liminf_{(\varepsilon,\eta)\to(0,0)}
 \Gamma_{L,+}(\varepsilon,\eta),\\
 \delta_{L,\mathrm{dr}}^{J,\mathrm{low}}(V)
 &\le
 \liminf_{(\varepsilon,\eta)\to(0,0)}
 \{\Gamma_{L,-}(\varepsilon,\eta)+\Sigma_{L,0}(\eta)\}.

\end{align}
The identical statement holds for the frame-weighted direct defects.
Thus the exact upper bound uses only one side of the gradient-slice
comparison.  The lower bound uses the reverse side and the near-zero
determinant defect; no remote spectral-tail condition is present.","status":"unverified"}

