{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.787991+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b9ef3b34da33e865b58614fb5dd3447838b13d21d082410c982cd499fd92c0f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop horizontal-splitting-beta-uniform of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $C,c_1,c_2,s_0>0$ (independent of $\beta$) such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$ the following holds. If $R$ is an $\ell \times e^{ - \beta} \bar \alpha \sqrt{\ell}$ rectangle with $\sqrt{C \log \ell} \le\bar \alpha \le (1/ s)\sqrt{\ell}$, and $\Delta$ has length $s \bar \alpha^2$ for $s \ge s_0$, we have 
