{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.811347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8bcf8d3acbff11d51268d545ac69fc030c3c8234490b7fadc1a31e66171b31fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2608.17509, '2608.17509'] Fix \(0<\theta_*<\pi\), and let \(K\subset S_{\theta_*}\) be compact. Then each \(D_{a,L}\) is holomorphic on \(S_{\theta_*}\), and
