{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.446207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c50a69fc838cff24a3eda064fba330512ef8883da7526d96aa38ba65f8bc546","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm finite N surface sum of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] {cao2023random};} {\textsc{$\mathrm{U}(N)$ Wilson loop expectations as surface sums}}]
Recall that $\Lambda$ is a finite subgraph of $\mathbb{Z}^d$ for some $d \geq 2$, $N\geq 1$ and $\upbeta\in \mathbb{R}$.
Let $s=\{\ell_1,\dots,\ell_n\}$ be a string. Then
\begin{equation}
	\phi_{\Lambda,N,\upbeta}(s) = Z_{\Lambda,N,\upbeta}^{-1}\sum_{K:\mathcal{P}_{\Lambda}\to \mathbb{N}}\sum_{M\in \mathcal{M}(s,K)}\upbeta^{\area(M)}
	\cdot
	w_N(M)
	\cdot
	N^{\eta(M)},
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{M}(s,K)$ is introduced in (defn:embedded-maps-bound-plaq-ass of the paper),
\begin{equation*}
	\eta(M):=2(c(M)-g(M)-b(M))=\chi(M) -b(M),
\end{equation*}
is the generalized Euler characteristic (recall (equation eq:chi-gen-relation of the paper) and the notation introduced above) and
\begin{equation}
	w_N(M):=\prod_{e\in E_{\Lambda}^+(s,K)} \nWg_N(\mu_e(M)),
\end{equation}
with $\nWg_N(\mu_e(M))$ denoting the value of $\nWg_N(\sigma)$ for any permutation $\sigma$ with the same cycle structure as $\mu_e(M)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.613467+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c5106498c414b083ab6e0db4994449ca22c2ac43e9f79b81c6c8d06fed5d7bc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] A random adjacency measure $\xi$ on $S$ is a graph process on $S$ if it admits a representation \eqref{EqRandomAdjacencyMeasure} in which, for some connection kernel $W$ on $S$,
    \begin{equation*}
        A_{ii} = 0, \qquad
        A_{ij}\mid \bigl( N,(S_k) \bigr) \;\overset{\textnormal{ind.}}{\sim}\; \mathrm{Bernoulli}\bigl(W(S_i,S_j)\bigr), \qquad 
        i < j,
    \end{equation*}
    the remaining entries being given by symmetry, $A_{ji}=A_{ij}$. We call \eqref{EqRandomAdjacencyMeasure} an i.i.d.\ representation of $\xi$ if, in addition, the $(S_k)$ are i.i.d.\ according to some probability measure $\hat\mu$ on $S$ and $N\indep(S_k)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.430082+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c55d69b66a6712ded4199e2a08730f377a663d30eccd24d8e5ad38cc0069208","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 203 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] If $\amsmathbb{O} \subset \amsmathbb{C}$ is an open set, we denote $\mathscr{O}(\amsmathbb{O})$ the linear space of holomorphic functions on $\amsmathbb{O}$. If $m \in \amsmathbb{Z}_{> 0}$ we denote
