    \chi_{\mathrm{tan}}^2(D,S,x;\Omega).

\end{equation}

Moreover, consider a compact orientation orbit and compact interior
coefficient set $\mathcal X_{\mathrm{orb}}$ for which physical target
separation is of order $s|\phi-\phi'|$ and the coefficient-profiled deployment
mean separation is of order $s\chi_s|\phi-\phi'|$.  Under the precise
regularity conditions stated in Supplementary
Section~(sec:supp-task-orbit of the paper), the minimax physical diameter on this
restricted orbit satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathcal R_{N,T}^{\mathrm{task}}
(s,\mathcal X_{\mathrm{orb}},\sigma)
\asymp
s
\wedge
\frac{s}{
\sqrt{
    Ns^6
    +
    T\chi_s^2s^2/\sigma^2
}}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.561603+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8e88ca47c39488d050cdb753e19b6c18c8b422c5e83f4f13cfff26739b4fe24e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:explicit_sol of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Fix $\bm{\sigma} \in T(\mathbb{C}^2)$. A solution of (equation eq:heat_eq_coef_sig of the paper) with the terminal condition $\bm{u}_T = \bm{\sigma}$ is given by
    \begin{equation}
