{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.268998+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ec5ea3405ded3bcd2184db179ce70351e4586968a91bf6406689c093b451d7e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 of arXiv:2604.20435, 'Stochastic Extinction with Relaxed Boundedness Conditions'] Let 
	$$v(t):=\Lambda|1+U(\BX(t))+U(\wdt \BX(t))|^{2\wdt d_0+2}[G_I(\wdt \BY_1)]^{-1}(\BX_1(t),0)(\BY_1(t)-\wdt \BY_1(t)),$$
	where
	$G_I$ is the diffusion part of $\wdt\BY_1$.
	One has
	\begin{equation}
		\PP\left\{\int_0^{t\wedge\xi_\delta}|v(s)|^2ds\geq \frac{|\by_1-\wdt \by_1|^2+\delta^2}\eps \forall t\geq 0\right\}\leq \wdt h_1(\eps),
