{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.583601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f3bfa7b68cad422b797979eaecb0b4d716ec161b6f1ffb7c27cf09a85289148","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Main.Thm01 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $\zeta\geq 0$, the process $L^\xi_\zeta$ equals in distribution to the unique non-negative continuous solution of the stochastic Volterra equation
 	\begin{eqnarray}
 	X_\zeta(t) \!\!\!&=\!\!\!& \zeta\cdot c \cdot W'(t)  
 	+  \int_0^\zeta\int_0^\infty \big( W(t)-W(t-y) \big) \, N_0(dz, dy)   + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)}   W'(t-s) \, B_c(ds,dz) \cr
 	\!\!\!&\!\!\!& + \int_0^t \int_0^{X_\zeta(s)} \int_0^\infty  \big( W(t-s)-W(t-s-y) \big) \, \widetilde{N}_\nu(ds,dz,dy), \quad t\geq 0,
 	\end{eqnarray}
 	where $N_0(dz, dy)$ is a  Poisson random measure on $(0,\infty)^2$ with intensity $\bar\nu(y)\,dz\,dy$, $B_c(ds,dz)$ is a Gaussian white noise on $(0,\infty)^2$ with intensity $2c\cdot ds\, dz$ and $\widetilde{N}_\nu(ds,dz,dy)$ is a compensated Poisson random measure on $(0,\infty)^3$ with intensity $ds\, dz\,\nu(dy)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

