{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.446076+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fb7e355789e6ba0ec501e0ec1205429ced1ace3a3f99ba6eb1b2b689b4051e4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn embedded-maps-bound-plaq-ass of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] For a balanced  pair $(s,K)$, we say that  $M=(m,\psi)$ is an \textbf{embedded map with boundary $s$ and plaquette assignment $K$} if $M$ is an embedded map (Definition~(defn:embedded-map of the paper)) which satisfies the following three additional conditions:
