{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.551268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_903832df3cb400198b35b987b207fe371a1cb4a380320074701e341b7eb51f98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] {\cite[Thm 6.2.1]{vershynin2018high}} 
Suppose $X\in \reals^{n}$ is a random vector with independent, mean-zero, subGaussian coordinates and $B \in \reals^{n\times n}$. Then for every $t\geq 0$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\P\left(\left|X^{\sT}BX-\E\left[X^{\sT}BX\right]\right|\geq t\right)
\leq
2\exp\left(-c\min\left\{\frac{t^{2}}{M^{4}\left\|B\right\|_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}},\frac{t}{M^{2}\left\|B\right\|_{\op}}\right\}\right),
\end{equation*}
where $M=\max_{i}\left\|X_i\right\|_{\psi_2}$ and $c>0$ is a universal constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.540859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_903aecb690a32ffab8925b5e3fb1a7a27c8980add806d78f1bd69fd014f7071e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:zeros_disc of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] Let~$\operatorname{Disc}_w(P)$ be the discriminant of the polynomial~$P$ in the variable~$w$, and let~$p(z)=z^{2\ell}\operatorname{Disc}_w(P)$. Then
\begin{equation}
p(z)=\left((z-1)^\ell \Tr \Phi(z)\right)^2-4(z-1)^{2\ell}.
\end{equation}
The function~$p$ is a degree~$2\ell-1$ polynomial with zeros
\begin{equation}
