{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909143d1e0ac8af78e79eb400d70dfee6ef0de300983d3648137ed19808d987a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Assume that $\{\delta_{i}, 1\le i\le n \}$ and $\{\zeta_{i}, 1\le i\le n \}$ are two independent sequences of random variables, where $\delta_{i}\sim\textnormal{Bernoulli}(p_{i})$ are independent and $\zeta_{i}$ are independent centered $\alpha$-sub-exponential random variables.
	Consider a random vector $\xi=(\xi_{1}, \cdots, \xi_{n})$  with $\xi_{i}=\delta_{i}\cdot\zeta_{i}$. Let $A=(a_{ij})_{n\times n}$ be a symmetric diagonal-free matrix. Then for $0<\alpha\le 2$ and $t\ge 0$, 
	\begin{align}
	\mathbb{P}\{\vert \xi^\top A\xi\vert\ge t  \}
		\le 2\exp\Big(-c(\alpha)\min\Big\{ \frac{t^{2}}{L(\alpha)^{4}\sum_{i, j}a_{ij}^{2}p_{i}p_{j}}, \big(\frac{t}{L(\alpha)^{2}\Vert A\Vert_{l_{2}\to l_{2}}}\big)^{\alpha/2}  \Big\}      \Big),\nonumber
	\end{align}
	where $L(\alpha)=\max_{i}\Vert \zeta_{i}\Vert_{\Psi_{\alpha}}$ and $c(\alpha)$ is a positive constant depending only on $\alpha$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:23.315914+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909492d9e09fc29d2b698ee88464eb20489b93f4c8a7b4db57d1dd3c9c881494","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2506.20411, 'Maximal Counts in the Stopped Occupancy Problem'] Let\/ $\tb_n$ be given by \eqref{bt}.
