{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.738855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_909a7963ae3a80ee3733aa4bea0e2e290c64c985ce9f9f28b9fa4e31970db2bb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem mostlytrans of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{G}$, $\mathcal{G}'$ be two mostly-transverse $C^0$-foliations on $\mathbb{T}^2$. Then, for every $\varepsilon>0$, there exist $C^0$-foliations $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}'$ such that
