{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:46:00.392395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90b571fa83a74c473f9145eb97748e0a8d80a77691b05cbb6d085cd8ba634171","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lim_moments of arXiv:2607.21443, 'The critical KPZ scale for the averaging process'] Fix $k\ge2$, $t\ge0$, and $\phi_1,\ldots,\phi_k\in\ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b(\mathbb{R})$. Set $\lambda=7/8$ and $\beta_N\coloneqq\beta_{\lambda,N}$. Let $\mathbf x^N=(x_1^N,\ldots,x_k^N)\in\mathbb{Z}^k$ be such that $N^{-1/2}\mathbf x^N\to\mathbf z=(z_1,\ldots,z_k)\in\mathbb{R}^k$. Then,
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{E}\bigg[
		\prod_{j=1}^k
		\mathfrak H_{\beta_N,N}(t,x_j^N,\phi_j)
	\bigg]
	\xrightarrow[N\to \infty]{}
	\mathbf E_{\mathbf z}^{{\rm BM}^{\otimes k}}
	\bigg[
		\exp\bigg\{\frac12\sum_{1\le i<j\le k}L_t^{W^i-W^j}\bigg\}
		\prod_{j=1}^k\phi_j(W_t^j)
	\bigg]\; \text{.}
	\end{equation}
	In particular, when $\mathbf x^N=\mathbf 0\in \mathbb{Z}^k$ and $\phi_1=\ldots=\phi_k=\phi\in \ensuremath{\mathcal C}_b(\mathbb{R})$, this gives the $k$-th moment asymptotics of $\ensuremath{\mathcal Y}_{7/8,N}(t,\phi)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.675035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90b831db2e4f491727926252927ba4d6141552220605e4cf31bcac4fa6d0618b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 47 (Uniform lifted Ricci--DeTurck continuous dependence) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Fix \(N\geq2\) and \(\sigma\in(0,1)\).  Let \(s(t)\), \(a\leq t\leq b\),
be a Ricci flow satisfying \(\PBG_N(s;\Lambda;[a,b])\) for some \(\Lambda\geq1\).
There are constants \(\eta_{\mathrm{cd}}>0\) and
\(C_{\mathrm{cd}}<\infty\), depending only on these data and an upper bound for
\(b-a\), with the following property.

\medskip
\noindent\textbf{Hypotheses.}
If \(v(a)\) is a smooth Riemannian metric and
\[
 \|v(a)-s(a)\|_{C^{N,\sigma}(M,s(a))}<\eta_{\mathrm{cd}},
\]

