{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.086134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90be913e9b2a8bd9ebce2d23ccb639426ad0ed117170f7744434be2ea5297908","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 4 of arXiv:2609.03819, 'Stochastic damped wave and Euler-Bernoulli equations with singular locally H\"older contin'] Assume \ref{H0}, \ref{H1} and \ref{H3} hold. For every $t>0$, the operator $e^{tA}\mathcal V$, a priori defined on $D(\Lambda^\beta)$, extends to a linear bounded operator from $U$ into $H$ which we still denote by $e^{tA}\mathcal V$. For every $u\in U$, the function $t\mapsto e^{tA}\mathcal V u$ is continuous from $(0,\infty)$ with values in $H$ and there exist positive constants $C_1,C_2$, independent of $t\in(0,\infty)$, which fulfill
