{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.650595+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_912ea554dbe0dded2b00fca898a517830349747c0b5979bf13ad5d7362e0db44","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop TVS-meas of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] {dim-TVS}}] 
    Fix $a\geq\lambda$, $u\in\mathbb R$. Denote $\mathds A=\mathds A_{-a,a}^u$. For $\eta>0$, define the random measures
