{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.306269+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91aa2a8a8cead7695f1801437d936fc991f0279fb9beb470a9bcb1e85fb4f71b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Markov of arXiv:2411.14818, 'Scaling limits of solitons in the Box-Ball system'] If $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}_{\mathrm{AM}}$ and $k \ge K\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$, then for any $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$, (equation def:step_M of the paper) converges weakly to the Brownian motion with variance $G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$ under {$\mu_{\mathbf{q}}$ and} $\nu_{\mathbf{q}}$, where $G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$ is given by 
                \begin{align}
                    G_{k}\left(\mathbf{q}\right) &= 4\rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)\left(1 - \rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)\right)\left(1 - 2 \rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)\right).
                \end{align}
           For any $i \in {\mathbb{Z}}$ and $\lambda \in {\mathbb{R}}$, the limit $\Lambda^{M{,i}}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right)$ exists {and does not depend on $i$}. In addition, $\Lambda^{M}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right) {:= \Lambda^{M{,0}}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right)}$ is a smooth monotone convex function, which is explicitly given by 
                \begin{align}
                    \Lambda^{M}_{\mathbf{q},k}\left(\lambda\right) &= \log\left( \frac{1 - 2\rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)}{2\left(1 - \rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)\right)} \left(e^{\lambda} + \sqrt{e^{2\lambda} - 1 + \frac{1}{\left(1 - 2\rho\left(\theta^{k}\mathbf{q}\right)\right)^2}}  \right)\right). 
