            In particular, the assumptions of Theorem (thm:main of the paper) ((item:1 of the paper)) and ((item:2 of the paper)) are satisfied with $\mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}_{\mathrm{AM}}$ and $k \ge K\left(\mathbf{q}\right)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.724576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91b1b1fa72058db7787649d52d31d66f594a84d46f92deebc151e1894d91b459","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:affine-holomorphic process of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\in [0,T]}$ be an $S$-valued jump-diffusion with extended generator $\mathcal{A}$ and fix a  subset $\mathcal{V}\subseteq \mathcal{O}(S)$.  We say that $X$ is an $S$-valued $\mathcal{V}$-\textit{affine-holomorphic process} if there exists an operator $\mathcal{R}:\mathcal V\rightarrow\mathcal{O}(S)$ such that for each  $f\in\mathcal V$ it holds that $\exp(f)\in\mathcal D(\mathcal A)$, 
