{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:28:31.999654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91cb0aa9209878cd2b23bbfc36bfcd5381048f057afda36dda6732a76f08c930","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 20 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $c_1,c_2>0$ such that the following holds.
	Denote $R \de c_1\min\{1/\kappa, 1/\lambda_{\max}, \rho \}$ and $C\de (R \lambda_{\min})^{\Delta/R}/\Area(D)$.
	Then, for every $T\geq c_2 \Delta^2$, initial condition $x_0\in D$, and measurable $E\subseteq D$,
	\begin{align}
		\bbP(X_{T}\in E \mid X_0 = x_0) \geq C \Area(E).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.213180+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91ce5965b62fd32a8b0ef033b6c48994a81ffd5d6974e197b754104d5d5f685f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2608.13687, 'Multiplicative chaos from random multiplicative functions'] Let $(A_p)_p$ be as in Case \caseS or Case \caseR, and fix a collection of scalars $(c_p)_p \subset \C$ in Case \caseS or $(c_p)_p \subset \R$ in Case \caseR satisfying
\begin{align}
    \sum_{n\in\N} \Big( \sum_{p\in I_n} |c_p|^2\Big)^{1/2} <\infty\,.
\end{align}
Fix $j\geq 1$.  Then the series 
\[
    F_{N,\ep}(x) \coloneqq \sum_{p \leq N} \frac{c_p}{p^{j\ep}}  A_p p^{-ijx}
\]
satisfies
\begin{align}
    \E \exp \, (\lambda \sup_{N,\ep \geq 0 } \|F_{N,\ep}\|_\infty)<\infty
\end{align}
for all $\lambda \geq 0$. Additionally, $F_{N,\ep}$
converges uniformly over $\cI$ almost surely as $\min(N,1/\ep)\to\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.498726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91cf9f749d3d8ff68880db94b5d4225a20b742ec04b7fca7b799d848ab2ef3e2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:defncLmet of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Fix $\rho\in\mathbb{R} \cup \{-\infty\}$. For a  continuous path $\pi:[s,t]\to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, its \emph{length in $\mathcal{L}^\rho$} is
		\begin{equation}  
	\|\pi\|_{\mathcal{L}^\rho}=\inf_{k\in \mathbb{N}} \inf_{s=t_0<t_1<\cdots < t_k=t} \sum_{i=1}^k \mathcal{L}^\rho(\pi(t_{i-1}), t_{i-1}; \pi(t_i), t_i).
		\end{equation}
		A path $\pi$ is a \emph{geodesic} from $(\pi(s), s)$ to $(\pi(t), t)$ if $\|\pi\|_{\mathcal{L}^\rho} = \mathcal{L}^\rho(\pi(s),s; \pi(t),t)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.657369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91e710e3a7e6f781c56456b8f6588bfc27c0a21b0ad6a9ae643e691556416772","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 21 (Tree-graph inequality; Aizenman and Newman
\cite{AN84}) of arXiv:2607.24561, 'Range convergence and sharp one-arm asymptotics\\for the critical percolation cluster in h'] For all $m\ge1$ and \emph{all} $x_1,\dots,x_m\in\Z^d$ (not necessarily
distinct, and not necessarily distinct from $0$),
\begin{equation}
\tau_{m+1}(0,x_1,\dots,x_m)\;\le\;
\sum_{T\in\T_m}\ \sum_{(z_v)_{v\in V_{\mathrm{int}}(T)}\in(\Z^d)^{V_{\mathrm{int}}(T)}}
\ \prod_{\{a,b\}\in E(T)}\tau_2(w_a,w_b),
\end{equation}
where $w_0:=0$, $w_i:=x_i$ for leaves and $w_v:=z_v$ for internal vertices.
The bound holds verbatim when some of the points coincide: with the
convention that a repeated point is not repeated in the connection event,
$\tau_{m+1}(0,x_1,\dots,x_m)$ is then a connection function of the distinct
points among $0,x_1,\dots,x_m$, which is still dominated by the displayed
sum (the right-hand side only grows when leaves are placed at coinciding
positions). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

