{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T07:38:10+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91f6917ae26f92fbd15a4ddb5a47350ce53715fe58f9cbe2aaf38043c418759f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 2.4 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] For any $t>0$ and any $0<a\le b\le1$, the probability distribution $P^\varepsilon_c( \cdot \, : \, t,a,b)$ over $\mathbb N_0$ converges in law to a Poisson distribution with parameter 
