{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.066965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923816e880badd3c35634f0b799058026ce0a59f75121b86a73b7b5e4a8af725","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2606.27520, 'Critical curve of loop percolation on the $d$-regular tree'] Let $\alpha > 0$ and $\kappa \geq \kappa_c$. There exist $\lambda = \lambda(\alpha, \kappa)$ and $\psi = \psi(\alpha,\kappa) > 0$ such that for all $r \geq 1$,
    \begin{equation}
        \P_{\alpha,\kappa}( 0 \leftrightarrow x_r) = \psi\lambda^r\, (1 + o_{\alpha,\kappa}(1)). 
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, $\lambda$ is monotone increasing in $\alpha$, and it is the unique solution in $(\tau^2_\kappa, 1)$ to
    \begin{equation} 
         (\lambda^{-1} -1) \sum_{n \geq 0} \big( (1-\tau_\kappa^{2(n+1)})^{-\alpha} -1 \big) \lambda^{-n}  = 1.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.888432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923bad3f0bfd5d4d448267451ab6eb0f8207c3a27efc4b424e0937427f3c2d95","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.17087, 'Transportation-cost inequalities for invariant measures of stochastic reaction-diffusion e'] Let $p_{t}(x,y)$ be the heat kernel of the operator $\frac{1}{2}\partial_{xx}$ on $[0,1]$ with the Dirichlet boundary condition, and
\begin{align*}
 P_t f(x) := \int_{0}^{1} p_{t}(x,y) f(y)dy, \quad x\in [0,1].
\end{align*}
Then for any $p> 1$,
\begin{align}
  \sup_{x\in [0,1]} |P_t f(x)| \leq C_{p\rightarrow\infty} t^{-\frac{1}{2p}}\Vert f\Vert_{L^p([0,1])},
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty}:= (2\pi)^{-\frac1{2p}} \left(\frac{p-1}{p}\right)^{\frac{p-1}{2p}}.
\end{align}
The constant $C_{p\rightarrow\infty}$ can be bounded by
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty} \leq \left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:28.465207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923c0227c97ee32c1fa4cc1c6558b845b61fb8da150e490660a7888b599e81c5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2606.29131, '2606.29131'] Suppose that \eqref{t1-1-1} holds for some $\beta>0$. Let $\Upsilon_\e^1 f(x,y)$ be defined by \eqref{l2-1-3a}. Then there exists a positive constant $C_7:=C_7(\beta)$ such that for every $f\in \M_\beta$, $x\in \R^d$ and $y\in \T^d$,
\begin{equation}
|\Upsilon_\e^1 f(x,y)|\le C_7\left(\sum_{i=0}^2\|f\|_{\M_{\beta},i}\right)(1+|x|)^{-d-\beta_0}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.713707+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923cc84990db54efe048179b575f7d4a812f099ee0be9ad1d149e9270eb87b4b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:1104.3 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Let $\widehat{\eta}_{\rm D}$ be limit of $\{\widehat{\eta}_{n,r_n}\}$ along some subsequence, with $\{r_n\}$ as in~(equation e:1.11i of the paper). Then, there exists a coupling between $\widehat{\eta}_{\rm D}$, the random measure $\eta_{\rm D}$ from~(equation e:1.10i of the paper), and $h_{\rm D}^\psi$ from~(equation e:1104.13 of the paper), such that $\widehat{\eta}_{\rm D}$ and $h_{\rm D}^\psi$ are independent and 
\begin{equation}

\widehat{\eta}_{\rm D} \circ \tau^{-1}_{h^{\psi}_{\rm D}} = \eta_{\rm D} \,,
\end{equation}
where $\tau_{\psi}: {\rm D} \times \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2} \to {\rm D} \times \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$ is the translation operator
\begin{equation}
	\tau_{\psi}(x,s,\omega) =(x,s + \psi(x), \omega) \,.
\end{equation}
Moreover, along the above subsequence we have
\begin{equation}
	 \big(\eta_{n,r_n}, \widehat{\eta}_{n,r_n}, h_n^\psi\big) \Longrightarrow \big(\eta_{\rm D}, \widehat{\eta}_{\rm D}, h^\psi_{\rm D}\big) \,.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.245146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923df2cca1a03a7fb2492a2692006dfaa67c8deda6a39e371a2573ef7cae0627","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq: short first row of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] For all $\lambda=(\lambda_1,\lambda_2,\ldots)\vdash n$, we have
\begin{equation}
-\frac{\lambda_1'}{n}\le\frac 1n+\frac{n-1}{n}\frac{\chi_\lambda(\tau)}{d_\lambda}\le\frac{\lambda_1}{n},
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
-1+2\frac{\lambda_1}{n}\le\frac 1n+\frac{n-1}{n}\frac{\chi_\lambda(\tau)}{d_\lambda}\le1-2\frac{\lambda_1}{n}+2\left(\frac{\lambda_1}{n}\right)^2.
\end{equation}
In particular, when $\lambda_1\ge n-n^{o(1)}$, set $r:=n-\lambda_1$. Then, we have
\begin{equation}
\frac 1n+\frac{n-1}{n}\frac{\chi_\lambda(\tau)}{d_\lambda}=1-2\frac{r}{n}+O(n^{-2+o(1)}).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.550641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923e54303387905389ced97914c9fef794ae3a4f26de7b917ddd7b7463be755c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Under Assumption \ref{ass:high_order_short}, there exist $C_1,C_2>0$ independent of $\alpha, \eta, L$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
