{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.898493+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93b76df8c97d1816ab8ffa403d25205133d47bbd857481ceb10117b369e2389c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 10 (Central limit theorem for fixed filling fractions) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] For the ensemble \eqref{eq_Hahn_cut_2} with fixed filling fractions and under the off-criticality assumption, there exist holomorphic functions $W_{1}^{[1]}(z)$ and $W_1^{[2]}(z)$ of $z \in \amsmathbb{C} \setminus \amsmathbb{A}$ such that, as $\N\rightarrow\infty$ uniformly over $z$ away from $\amsmathbb{A}$
