{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.559720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93c354a8bab3ec5deb33a1c0a1ae0b6cbab01c44aa3457a193f92ed3f439df46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] For every $n\in\mathbb N$, $\lambda>0$, and $\theta\in(0,1/2)$, the functions
    \begin{align}
