{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.288474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93ed36d88e4d39e4d7f5109c4140dbd33b9c62cffeadd02c8892320ddef1e238","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] An $\R^d$-valued stochastic process $X$ 
    is called a $d$-dimensional \emph{path-dependent process}, if it is a continuous semimartingale and there exist continuous $b : \ccC_T^d \to \R^d$ and measurable $\sigma : \ccC_T^d \to \R^{d \times m}$, such that $a(t,x) := \sigma(t,x) \sigma(t, x)^\top$ is continuous and $X$ satisfies
    \begin{align}
        X(t) & = X(0) + \int_{0}^{t} b(s,X_{[0,s]}) \, ds + \int_{0}^{t} \sigma(s,X_{[0,s]}) \, dW(s), \quad 0 \leq t \leq T,
    \end{align}
    with deterministic initial value $X(0) \in \R^d$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.094367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93fe484b374c12d0701783c6e1e006b2804b0eba0ab6e90e359905b42b95e61f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 36 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Let $\mathfrak{v}\in \Gamma(A_U)$ be a local section, and let $\LXu[v]$ be its complete lift. 
Then, if we denote by $\LB[\mathfrak{v},\mathfrak{u}]^V_A$ the vertical lift of  $\LB[\mathfrak{v},\mathfrak{u}]_A$, 
\begin{align} 
\LXu[v](\mathfrak{u}(x)) = T_x\mathfrak{u}(\rho(\mathfrak{v}(x))) + (\LB[\mathfrak{u},\mathfrak{v}]_A(x))^V_{\mathfrak{u}(x)}. 
\end{align}
Let $c$ be admissible, $\gamma=\pi\circ c$, and let $b$ be a section along $\gamma$. If $\mathfrak{v}_t$ satisfies $\mathfrak{v}_t(\gamma(t))=b(t)$, then 
\begin{align}
\mathcal{T}_c(b)(t) = \mathcal{X}_{\mathfrak{v}_t}(c(t)) + \left(\frac{\partial \mathfrak{v}_t}{\partial t}(\gamma(t))\right)^V_{c(t)}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.741022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9406e9eceaad9080a4fb27f65061f5e3e83885ba103d13acc3a697875fbf4333","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:eigenvalues of arXiv:2603.24803, 'Critical Spectral Invariants in Random Walks with Geometric Resetting'] The operator $\widetilde{P}$ has eigenvalues
