{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.007082+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9408fbbb774b550756920448ebabd0d0d33237afca7c1cf3c791dc71572e21f1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ex1 of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Let $\textbf{M}$ and $\textbf{E}$ be the controlling functions introduced above. Then we have:
