{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.051689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9432c8745951e96c79427d27ba7cd3ab2f10c5f785a9e0b479f7fb5a816ed58a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop thm:exact-identity of arXiv:2608.30847, 'An Almgren-type formula for planar $p$-harmonic functions'] Let $u$ be a nonconstant planar $p$-harmonic function in $B_R(x_0)$, and suppose that $u$ is not locally constant at $x_0$.  For all sufficiently small admissible radii, define
