and $\Theta_{t}^{k, \ell}(s)=0$ if $s>t$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.149943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94525ee15c58fdb9a64f94c91f6e54f0751b012c2a3b4e5f8b918c6a24901e24","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] The set $L^{\infty}_{loc}([0,\infty);\ell^{2\theta}_{\rho}(\mathbb{Z}^{+})])\bigcap\Omega_{Spin}$ is a Borel set in $\Omega_{Spin}$. Moreover, 
