{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.503499+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_946686873346b92f0c12eca1f02fdaa52be59683f08fafee880041e587e82001","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem limits of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] {(Limits of foliations)}
    Let $B$ be a $\Phi$-horizontal branched surface and $(\mathcal F_i)_{i \geq 0}$ be a sequence of foliations carried by $B$. Let $\bm{s}^i$ be the generalized boundary multislope of $\mathcal F_i$. Suppose $\lim_{i\to \infty} \bm{s}^i = \bm{s}^{\lim}\in \mathbb{R}^n$. Then $B$ carries a limit foliation $\mathcal{F}_{\lim}$ with generalized boundary multislope $\bm{s}^{\lim}$, possibly with some entries in $\mathbb{R}$ replaced by $\aleph$.

    Moreover, we have the following control over the boundary type of $\mathcal{F}_{\lim}$:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item If $s^i_k \to s^{\lim}_k$ strictly from above, then $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_{\lim}$ has $\sharp$, $\natural$, or $\aleph$ type.
        \item Similarly, if $s^i_k \to s_k^{\lim}$ strictly from below, then $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_{\lim}$ has $\flat$, $\natural$, or $\aleph$ type.
        \item If $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_i$ has generalized fine slope $(s^{\lim}_k)^\natural$ for all $i$, then $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_{\lim}$ has $\natural$ or $\aleph$ type.
        \item If $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_i$ has $\aleph$ type for all $i$, then $\partial_k \mathcal{F}_{\lim}$ also has $\aleph$ type.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.918371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_946bef9279e26d3f0efb93347f2b8d286a58edd4b7c1692f8a9c668d84cdb1d5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Algebraic integrability only depends on the field of definition) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $K'/K$ be a finite extension of fields of characteristic zero. 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Any foliation $\F$ on $K$ over $k$ uniquely extends to a foliation on $K'$ over $k$, where $k$ is a subfield.
        \item If $\F$ is of rank $1$, and $D$ is a basis of $F$, then if there exists $F\in K'$ non-constant such that $D(F)=0$, then there exists $G\in K$ non-constant such that $D(G)=0$.
        \item If $\F$ is algebraically integrable over $K'$, then it is algebraically integrable over $K$.
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.736749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_946d068cd271a66391c8ad9c28361b849bf4ba86417f82b09bd413029979d353","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For every \(a>0\),
