{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.816579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94864cd66b44d51a37fe3ad2de18ec5c2b24e753628079ffdf1cdae489aad955","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:family of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Under (equation eq:familyhyp of the paper), put $\alpha=q+s-p+r-1$.  The toric ideal $I_A$
is generated by
\begin{align}
 f_1&=x_1^p-x_0^{p-q}x_2^q,\\
 f_2&=x_2^{q+s}-x_0^\alpha x_1^{p-r}x_3,\\
 f_3&=x_1^r x_2^s-x_0^{r+s-1}x_3.
\end{align}
Its Hilbert series is
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{HS}_{S/I_A}(t)=
 \frac{1-t^p-t^{q+s}-t^{r+s}+t^{p+s}+t^{q+r+s}}
 {(1-t)^4}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, if
\[
 \widetilde M_j=\begin{cases}
 \binom{j+3}{3},&j\geq0,\\
 0,&j<0,
 \end{cases}
\]
then, for every integer $h\geq0$,
\begin{equation}
 |hA|=\widetilde M_h-\widetilde M_{h-p}
 -\widetilde M_{h-q-s}-\widetilde M_{h-r-s}
 +\widetilde M_{h-p-s}+\widetilde M_{h-q-r-s}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

