{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.642688+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b081d17ccde35b0165777f39270ab2c237eb24563a36bec3b6ffc1a6eeb7f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l32 of arXiv:2411.13875, 'Large deviations at the origin of random walk in random environment'] Fix $\kappa > 0$, $j\ge 1$ and $\mathcal S:=\{\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_j\} \subseteq \mathcal P_{\mathbb V}^{(\kappa)}$ with all $\sigma_i$'s distinct. Assume that there exists some $u \in \mathbb Q^d$, with $|u|_2=1$,  such that
\begin{equation}

