\end{equation}
for all $1\le i\le j$, where $\mathrm d(\sigma_i)$ is the drift of $\sigma_i$ as defined in (equation eq:defdrift of the paper). Then, given $\varepsilon > 0$, for any $\overline{\lambda}=(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_j) \in \Delta_j$  

there exists some periodic environment $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}$ with $\mathbf p=(\vec{p}(x)) \in \mathcal S^{\mathbf{B}_\mathbf n}$ such that $P_{0,\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}}$-almost surely, for every $1 \leq m \leq j$,
