\end{equation}
where $S_m$ is the set of sites $x\in \mathbb Z^d$ such that $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}(x)=\sigma_m$. As a matter of fact, $\omega_{\mathbf n,\mathbf p}$ can be chosen as a $(u;r_1,\dots,r_j)$-strip periodic environment generated by the $\sigma_1,\ldots,\sigma_j$ for some $r_1,\dots,r_j$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483211+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94b4a6884c68f1cd2c7f2663d5445f2975dcdc3d60af6c9ec68e6aeefe12a0d4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 40 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let be $\eta>0$, $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $b\geq (2v)\vee(2\lambda)$. Then
\begin{equation}

