    \item there exists $c > 0$ and $\delta > 0$ such that  $\theta(\gamma(t)) \geqslant c (t - t_c)$ for all $t_c \leqslant t \leqslant t_c + \delta$.
  \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94caaaf5e0d929f185767816988d2313557cfcb979bb74d3db3ae698ab8c1e69","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (Exact Skellam regimes) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] For the centered Skellam law \eqref{eq:centered-skellam}, the right scale has
