{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.534164+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_959c60ddacde35b30dab134b0fee41bc9e42a59650afaee95bbab962bcec7fb1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro pro2.01 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Assume that the generator $g$ satisfies assumption (A) and $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in [0,\tau]}$ is an adapted solution of BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) such that $y_\cdot\in S_\tau^{\bar{p}}(\bar{\rho}_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^k)$. Then $z_\cdot\in M_\tau^{\bar{p}}(\bar{\rho}_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$, and there exists a constant $C_{\bar{p},\theta}^1>0$ depending only on $\bar{p}$ and $\theta$ such that for each $0\leq r\leq t< +\infty$,
