{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.581525+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_95b6a21de32fc609ddcef53e1ee9504fbb59af249c20a1cc70ae40ded995e08e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 510 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For any $\beta\geq \beta_0$, there exist two constants $C>0$ and $n_0\geq 1$ such that for any  $\delta \geq 0$,
