{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:37:20.357644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_962b20b0d1fa90c976d11ca57e6ca75660f8c536547d485f0acdcfa6360d6d2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2411.13062, 'Graphon-Theoretic Approach to Central Limit Theorems for $\epsilon$-Independence'] Let $(g_n)_{n \ge 1}$ be a sequence of finite simple graphs where $V(g_n)=[n]$. Assume that $g_n \to w$ in the graphon sense. Let $a_1^{(n)},\ldots,a_n^{(n)} \in \mathcal{A}$ be $g_n$-independent identically distributed centered (self-adjoint) random variables with variance one, for every $n \ge 1$. Then 
