{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.881188+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_966eeda1229f5650565a1d8ee5a7819faf149aa862775b04c9d098066fc92dfe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:upper-gradient of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $K \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be a compact $C(v,\theta)$-cone null set and $f \in C^1(\mathbb{R}^n)$, for some $v \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1}$ and $\theta \in (0,\pi/2)$.
		Then,
		\[
		g = {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex \nabla f \kern-0.25ex\right\vert} \mathds{1}_{\mathbb{R}^n \setminus K} + \sup_{w \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1} \setminus (C^\circ \cup( -C^\circ))} {\left\vert\kern-0.25ex \langle \nabla f, w \rangle \kern-0.25ex\right\vert}
		\]
		is an upper gradient for $f$, where $C=C(v,\theta)$ such that
		\begin{enumerate}[(a)]
			\item $g$ is lower semicontinuous;
			\item For any closed ball $B$ such that $B^\circ \supset K$, there exists a non-decreasing sequence of  continuous functions $g_k: \mathbb{R}^n \to [0,\infty)$ such that $\lim_{k \to \infty} g_k(x)= g(x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{R}^n$ and $g_k(x)=g(x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{R}^n \setminus B, k \in \mathbb{N}$.
		\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.861559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9672deca7feb5ae57911290a0bb09e51bd6ec1f4db2e6bb19f3e992036f94188","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2609.03084, 'Convergence rates to traveling waves for an FKPP model with nonlinear advection'] Suppose $0 \leq \chi < 1$ and $u_0$ satisfies the conditions of \Cref{main_result_theorem}. Then there exists positive constants $C$ and $T$ so that
