\mathbb E|f_N(z)|^s\le C e^{s|y|/2}.
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E|\xi^{\beta,\delta}(z)|^s\le C e^{s|z|/2}.
\end{equation}
In particular, both expectations are uniformly bounded when $z$ ranges over a fixed compact set.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.203331+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_968d3cdb106c91135e91a2b28e778e7b7c460df44cf6d7293e28a9f168c7e631","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main:existence of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $G = (V, E)$ be a fixed graph. Then
