{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.135350+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_980831c8e0a0427e4a0b213daa4cee0e64956d63d4903b169884b4a4a8890e95","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 1 of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any simple path $\gamma = (x_t,y_t)$, if $\gamma|_{[0,1]}$ has infinite radius of convergence for its log-signature and $x_t\in[-1,1]$ for all $t\in[0,1]$, then looking at any fixed horizontal level $y=a$ of the image $\gamma([0,1])$, we only have the following two cases: 
\begin{itemize}
       \item The right street copies the left street. In the sense that for any $x\in(0,1)$, $(x,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x-1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$. For any $x\in(-1,0)$, $(x,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$ we have $(x+1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$.

       \item Both capture the missing points of the other. In the sense that for any $x\in(0,1)$, $(x,a)\notin\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x-1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$. For any $x\in(-1,0)$, $(x,a)\notin\gamma([0,1])$, we have $(x+1,a)\in\gamma([0,1])$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.659522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9809148171d19c9f9ee8cde7d730a882d60f214a913b6c3415c163a6b9394c71","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem uniform-lln-horizon of arXiv:2604.07183, 'Stopping on the last success with unknown odds: asymptotic minimax optimality of the plug-'] Let~$(p_n)$ be a sequence in~$(0,1)$ such that~$p_n\to 0$ and~$np_n\to\infty$.
Consider
\begin{equation}
I_n:=\Bigl\{t\in\{1,\dots,n\}:\ t\ge t_n \Bigr\},
\end{equation}
where~$t_n\in\{1,\ldots,n\}$ for any~$n$ and~$n/t_n=O(1)$. 
Then, there exist positive constants~$C,c$ such that
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P
\bigg[
\sup_{t\in I_n}\Bigl|\frac{\hat p_t}{p_n}-1\Bigr| > \varepsilon
\bigg]
\le

C
e^{-c\varepsilon^2 np_n}
\end{equation}
for all~$\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and all~$n$ large enough. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.298853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9812cd3ed1c3a0d87fa7a9f5fdaa8fa53b741ededdaaf3e5c62f300015d72e5c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ denote the set of probability measures equipped with its weak topology and the corresponding Borel $\sigma$-algebra.
	We say that $(L_n)$ satisfies the full LDP (resp. weak LDP) in the weak topology if there exists a lower semicontinuous function $I$, called the rate function, such that all open subsets $O$ and all closed subsets $F$ (resp. compact subsets $F$) of $\mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ satisfy
	\begin{align}
		\liminf_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n\log \mathbb P(L_n\in O)&\geqslant -\inf_{\mu\in O}I(\mu),
		\\\limsup_{n\to \infty}\frac 1n\log \mathbb P(L_n\in F)&\leqslant -\inf_{\mu\in F}I(\mu).
	\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:47:07.702922+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9815036a71f9496d6aa2d9cd69947ea385ba3e788ec0e8d58614b3edfb7197da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.06038, 'Efron type identities\\ for stopping sets and Poisson hulls'] Let $B\in\cX_0$ and let $f\colon \bN\times\R_+\to\R_+$ be measurable
