  \end{displaymath}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.329124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981840435c564e114b5bbfc99c6572f30a6dd1313237a2e4003b5651cffdde46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:cf_tempered of arXiv:2412.06374, 'Stable and tempered stable distributions and processes: an overview toward trajectory simu'] Let $(X_t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}$ be a CTS Lévy process with Lévy triplet $\left(b_\nu, 0,\nu\right)$ where $\nu$ defined as in (equation eq:levy_measure_tempered_stable of the paper) and $b_\nu=\int_{|x|>1}x \nu(dx)$. For $t\in \mathbb{R}_+$, the characteristic function exponent can be expressed for $u\in \mathbb{R}$ as 
\begin{align}
\log(\phi_{X_t}(u))= \begin{cases} 
tP\Gamma(-\alpha)\left((A-iu)^\alpha - A^\alpha + iu\alpha A^{\alpha-1} \right) + tQ\Gamma(-\alpha)\left((B+iu)^\alpha - B^\alpha + iu\alpha B^{\alpha-1}  \right) & \alpha \neq 1,\\
iut(P-Q) + tP(A-iu)\log\left(1-\frac{iu}{A}\right) + tQ(B-iu)\log\left(1-\frac{iu}{B}\right)& \alpha = 1.
\end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.214406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981a5fdb2886062fd443948705ddde17193053e7befc0842603ec013907054c3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:covreperror of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] Assume the system properties described by (equation eq:realhidden of the paper) for the true hidden state, (equation eq:asshidden of the paper) for the assumed hidden state and (equation eq:obs of the paper) for the observation model.  Given $r,s$ such that $r <s, r >0$, we have the following evolution equations for the  error covariance $P_t$ and expected squared error $\tilde{P}_t$,
\begin{align}

	\frac{dP_t}{dt} &= (G -(r-s)K_tH) P_t  + P_t (G -(r-s)K_tH)^\top  + \Sigma   + (r-s)^2 K_t \Xi K_t^\top   \\

	\frac{d\tilde{P}_t}{dt} &= (G -(r-s)K_tH)\tilde{P}_t  + \tilde{P}_t(G -(r-s)K_tH)^\top  + \Sigma  + (r-s)^2 K_t \Xi K_t^\top   - \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t]b^\top  - b \mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t^\top]  
\end{align}
where $K_t$ is the continuous time Kalman gain matrix as defined in (equation eq:kalmangain of the paper).  For the special case $s=0,r=1$, it holds that $P_t = C_t, \enskip \forall \enskip t > 0$ if $P_0 = C_0$ where $C_t$ is the solution of the covariance equation of the replicator-mutator.\\
\\
Furthermore, for any p.d. $C_0$,  the evolution of the mean squared error $E_t$ satisfies the following inequality 
\begin{align}


	\frac{dE_t}{dt} \leq \alpha(A_t(r,s) + A_t(r,s)^\top)E_t - 2\text{Tr}[\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_t]b^\top] + \text{Tr}[\Sigma] + (r-s)^2 \alpha(H^\top \Xi^{-1}H) \|C_t\|_F
\end{align}
where $A_t$ is defined in (equation eq:defnAt of the paper) and $\alpha(A)$ denotes the largest eigenvalue of $A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.298395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981bfa8341a4d7d9051005d66cb3f7637ab2aa2a6a7f111bd4ed9207aee95545","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.23242, 'Correction to ``The stepping stone model in a random environment'' - limit theorems for th'] For any bounded and measurable $ f : \Omega \to \R $, for any $ T > 0 $ and for $ \mu $-almost every environment $ \omega \in \Omega $,
