{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.942173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_985263737fd755f4f39a593e3290f9576291ab0edb3a0a9c2913ca500ec906aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LemmaErgodicity of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Let $K$ be a Markov kernel on $(\mathbb{R}^d, \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d))$ with invariant measure $\mu$ and let $\mathbf{Z} = (\mathbf{Z}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ be a homogeneous Markov chain with kernel $K$ and initial distribution $\mathbf{Z}_0 \sim \mu$. Then $\mathbf{Z}$ is ergodic if and only if
\begin{equation}

