\end{equation}
In particular (as $\lambda\downarrow0$),
$NE_{\cF_{\tau}}\theta_{\tau}\tau_{\rho}(x_{\tau})\geq \nu \rho^{2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.328907+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98dd907a28db925322fe8d2ca973303660be4f83e79271c2011812386fe79a7e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] A scalar fractional Brownian motion $\left(W^{H}_t\right)_{t\geq 0}\subset \R$ with Hurst index $H\in(0,1)$ is a centered Gaussian process with covariance 
