{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.886988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9906db3debe4b37778d0a8669ef4fcdcfaa60f546ef99b046f1d4121c69b8f66","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:spectral_gap_lower_bound of arXiv:2607.02410, 'Polynomial mixing for polygonal side matchings'] Let $g > 0$, let $n > 2g$, and let $\gamma_{n,g}$ be the spectral gap of the fixed genus chord swap chain on $\chorddiagrams{n}{g}$. There exists a constant $C_g > 0$ depending only on the genus such that 
