{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.568483+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_998f172352fe9bd0ffa3c5d733f9daf88f63828ed1b67cbca93edef7f3e375db","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 6 of arXiv:2605.30779, '2605.30779'] Let \(\beta\in\{1,2\}\) and \(\{\xi_{\beta,j}\}_{j\ge1}\) be i.i.d.\ random variables, independent of \(\{a_{\beta,j}^{\Theta}\}_{j\ge1}\), with \(\xi_{\beta,j}^2\sim\chi_\beta^2\). Define the Airy-Green function
