	Assume further that $u(t,0,x)\le0$ for $t\in [ t_*,i_\dagger+t_*]$ and $x\ge X(t,0)$, that\footnote{For this boundary assumption, it will be sufficient to assume: $u(t,i,x)\le 0$ for $t\ge i+t_*$, $i\in[0,i_\dagger)$ and $x\in[X(t,i)-R,X(t,i)]$.}  $u(t,0,x)\le 0$ for $t\ge t_*$ and $x\in[X(t,0)-R,X(t,0)]$, and $u(t,i,X(t,i))\le 0$ for $t\ge i+i_\dagger+t_*$ and $i\in[0,i_\dagger)$, then $u(t,i,x)\le 0$  for $t\ge i+i_\dagger+t_*$, $i\in[0,i_\dagger)$ and $x\ge X(t,i)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

