{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.851516+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a74ad2eda7b6972fdc264b761447344cbbf1a5a4299dc42ba36bd8fde541c78","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 13 of arXiv:2605.18751, '\mytitle'] Let \((Q_\nu)_{\nu\in\mathcal I}\) be a family of probability measures on \(\N_0\) with common support \(S\subseteq\N_0\), so that \(q_\nu(n)\coloneqq Q_\nu(\{n\})>0\) for \(n\in S\). Denote the density of the compound law \(C_\nu\) by
