{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.530242+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ab1135ba2438a78743b3cd2613d4c12e0dedef599f3579bc656270c4455446f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{M}_F(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and let $\gamma >0$. Let $(\mathcal{X}_r)_{r \geq 0}$ be an $\text{SBM}(\gamma)$ started from $\mu$ on a probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F}, \mathbb{P}_\mu)$. For each $a>2$ there $\mathbb{P}_{\mu}$-a.s. exists $\delta>0$ such that if $s$, $t \geq 0$ satisfy $0 \leq t-s<\delta$ then
    \begin{equation*}
        \text{supp}(\mathcal{X}_t) \subseteq \text{supp}(\mathcal{X}_s)^{aH(t-s)}
    \end{equation*}
    where $H:[0,\infty) \rightarrow [0, \infty)$ is the function given by $H(0) = 0$ and for $x>0$ we have
    \begin{equation*}
        H(x) \coloneqq \sqrt{x((\log 1/x) \vee 1))}.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:09:34.462749+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ab98cfb4c7f9678773d1972802243e854cd532fdbfee3052a4fc50777ebd605","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:characnf of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{P}_t = \exp(t \mathcal{L})$ be a QMS with an invariant state $\sigma \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M})$, and $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L})$ and $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})$ be the subalgebras defined in (equation def:fixedpointspace of the paper) and (equation def:decoherence of the paper). Then,
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Any purely imaginary eigenvalue $\lambda = i \mu$ with $\mu \in \mathbb{R}$ of $\mathcal{L}$ is simple, namely, the associated Jordan block is of size one. 
        \item Define $V_0 := {\rm Span}\{X \in \mathcal{M}\,;\ \mathcal{L}(X) = i \mu X \ \text{for some $\mu \in \mathbb{R}$}\}$, and let $V_-$ be the direct sum of generalized eigenspaces of $\mathcal{L}$ associated with eigenvalues $\lambda$ with $\mathfrak{Re}(\lambda) < 0$. 
        We have 
        \begin{equation*}
            V_0 = \mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})\,, \quad V_- = \{X \in \mathcal{M}\,;\ \lim_{t \to \infty} \mathcal{P}_t(X) = 0\}\,,
        \end{equation*}
        and the orthogonal decomposition with respect to both $\sigma$-GNS and KMS inner products:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{M} =  V_0 \oplus V_-\,.
        \end{align*}
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

