{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.365318+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b11edfae6dab96b07d26199c00fe53688587c72dd4ba75b2f2830dc4038db20","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem eq:bound-holder-prob-two of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Given any $\nu\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha'$, for all $R$ large enough depending on $\nu,$ and $p$ small enough depending on $R,\nu$ there exist parameters of events $F,G$ (depending only on $R,\alpha',\nu$) and a constant $C_1=C_1(R)$ such that for all $K$,
