{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:06.982496+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b4896e9283cee1cd9fa5cd1925c74740a228893c6eb8867cf2ec71827f5596d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Gordonpos1 of arXiv:2607.26551, 'An RDT based confirmation of Lehner's formula for Kronecker-Gaussian matrices'] ([Gordon85,Slep62])
 Let $X_{i}$ and $Y_{i}$, $1\leq i\leq n$, be two centered Gaussian processes which satisfy the following inequalities for all choices of indices
\begin{enumerate}
\item ${\mathbb E}(X_{i}^2)={\mathbb E}(Y_{i}^2)$
\item ${\mathbb E}(X_{i}X_{l})\leq {\mathbb E}(Y_{i}Y_{l}), i\neq l$.
\end{enumerate}
 Then
\begin{equation*}
{\mathbb E}(\min_{i} X_{i})\leq {\mathbb E}(\min_i Y_{i}) \quad  \Longleftrightarrow \quad {\mathbb E}(\max_{i} X_{i})\geq {\mathbb E}(\max_i Y_{i}).
\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

