{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:52:17.588708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9be9fae15ee43a13248b48284d7547f9f3eb1d9b100bda9b1e70a6ea0e5afcb4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 604 of arXiv:2411.15485, '\bf\Large Stochastic Volterra Equations for Local Times of Spectrally Positive L\'evy Proc'] For each $p \geq 1$ and $\beta >0$, there exists a constant $C>0$ such that for any $\zeta, t\geq 0$ and $0\leq t_1<t_2\leq t$,
