{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.665351+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c16f3c70f66aac955fe30edcd2138c12853213eec252333386b12afcd72ec1f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop cmj-speed of arXiv:2609.00110, 'Phase Transition and Fluctuation Results for First-Passage Percolation on Spread-Out Cycle'] For the continuous CMJ branching random walk,
\begin{align}
\frac{\mathsf{M}_t}{t}\to \mathsf{v}^\star
\text{ a.s.}

\end{align}
Consequently,
\begin{align}
\frac{\tau(f)}{f}\to \frac1{\mathsf{v}^\star}
\text{ a.s. and in }L^1,
