{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:37:08.313610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c72696844659e50706a0cbf6a7776f46934c11e3d1bee570b54a40d3506fcbf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorema WPHs of arXiv:2608.30777, 'Inhomogeneous nonlinear Schr\"odinger equation \\ in Fourier-Lebesgue and modulation space'] Let $s\geq 0 $ and  $0<b< 1-s$. 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (subcritical) If 
        \begin{align*}
            1< \alpha < \begin{cases}
            1+ \frac{4-2b}{1-2s}\quad &\text{if} \quad s<1/2 \\ 
            \infty \quad &\text{if} \quad s \geq 1/2
        \end{cases},
         \end{align*} 
         then (equation INLS of the paper) is locally well-posed in $H^s.$ 
        \item (critical) If $s> 1/2$ and $\alpha=1+\frac{4-2b}{1-2s},$ then (equation INLS of the paper) is locally well-posed in $H^s$ and globally well-posed for the small data.
        \item (mildly ill-posed) If $s>0,\quad 0<b<1 \leq b+s<5/2, \; \alpha-1 \in 2\mathbb{N} \quad \text{and,\; if}\quad b+s \geq 1,\quad b+s \not \in \mathbb{N},$ then  (equation INLS of the paper) is mildly ill-posed in $H^s.$ 
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.812560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c74844758cfe02afaa7a7bba144079ea8cec61def9d3f8fff72f7b6326ff543","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 3 of arXiv:2608.12804, 'Scaling Limits for Ising Models on Inhomogeneous Random Graphs and Applications'] Let $T$ be a trace--class operator with eigenvalues $\lambda_i$, counted with algebraic multiplicity. Then the \emph{Fredholm determinant} of $I+T$ ($I$ being the identity operator) is defined as,
