{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.529220+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9cd43594833016e1ac0ac7484a261eb8c6a64a9c4379d81332e08ce80d2bae80","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 13 of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] There exist continuous modifications of the processes $(\mathcal{Z}^{(\rm d)}_s, \mathcal{Z}^{(\rm a)}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ and $(\Tilde{\mathcal{Z}}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ from Theorem \ref{theorem ooSBM ffd convergence} and Proposition \ref{proposition damped sbm} which we denote by $(\mathcal{Y}^{(\rm d)}_s, \mathcal{Y}^{(\rm a)}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ and $(\Tilde{\mathcal{Y}}_s)_{s \geq 0}$ and which are $\text{ooSBM}(4, c, \Tilde{c})$ and $\text{DSBM}(4, c)$.
