{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e12adeb6c239982e6ea6e2bc99e0ee142cccaf1bd1a3ae0f553559a74cecb76","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2506.10817, 'On the Weak Error for Local Stochastic Volatility Models'] Let $(\alpha_k)_{k=1}^n,(\beta_k)_{k=1}^n,(\gamma_k)_{k=1}^n$ and $(\Delta_k)_{k=1}^n$ be positive sequences and assume that $\alpha_k \le A$ as well as $a\le \gamma_k \le b$ for some $a\le 1\le A,b$. 

    Let $\delta > 0$ and assume that $|\alpha_k-\beta_k|\le C \max\bigl\{\alpha_k^p,\beta_k^p \bigr\} \Delta_k$ for some $C>0$ and $1/2\le p\le 1$. Then it holds that
   {
    \begin{align*}
    \Bigl|\frac{\frac1n\sum_{k=1}^n \alpha_k +\delta}{\frac1n\sum_{k=1}^n \alpha_k\gamma_k +\delta}-\frac{\frac1n\sum_{k=1}^n \beta_k +\delta}{\frac1n\sum_{k=1}^n \beta_k\gamma_k +\delta}
        \Bigr|
        \lesssim C \max_{j=1,\dots,n}\max\{\alpha_j,\beta_j\}^{p-\frac1{2}} \delta^{-1/2} \sqrt{\frac1n \sum_{k=1}^n \Delta_k^2}
        \end{align*}
    }","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.777535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e165c7dd89cddc24ece016fcd792a58032463b25d348bfceffcc60e86a0d22c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 18 of arXiv:2608.17493, 'Integrals of some compound processes'] Let $N$ be a renewal process with waiting times $X\sim F$ and $\{A_n\}_{n\ge1}$ be a sequence of real random variables independent of $N$ (and its waiting times),
	\begin{itemize}
		\item[($i$)] with $\gamma\in\mathbb{R}$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathbb{E} \exp\Biggl( i\gamma \sum_{k=1}^{N(t)} X_k A_k \Biggr) = \sum_{n\ge0}\mathbb{E} \Biggl[\conv_{k=1}^n \Big( e^{i\gamma A_k\sbullet} F(\sbullet) \Big)\ast 1 (t)- \conv_{k=1}^{n} \Big( e^{i\gamma A_k\sbullet}F(\sbullet) \Big)\ast F \ast 1 (t) \Biggr],
		\end{equation}
		where $hF\ast g (t)= \int_0^t g(t-x)h(x)F(\dif x)$ for suitable functions $h,g$ and distribution $F$.
		\item[($ii$)] If $X$ is absolutely continuous with density $f$ and $\mu>0$,
		\begin{equation}
			\mathcal{L} \left\{ \mathbb{E} \exp\Biggl( i\gamma \sum_{k=1}^{N(t)} X_k A_k \Biggr) \right\} (\mu) = \frac{1-\mathcal{L}f(\mu)}{\mu}\sum_{n\ge0}\mathbb{E} \prod_{k=1}^n \mathcal{L}f(\mu+i\gamma A_k).
		\end{equation}
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:19:46.227645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e1c96ce4a2c7be3a08e8331d412350f92c22fe1b8b8a120a065a52c647a595b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm 2 of arXiv:2507.08909, 'Annealed almost periodic entropy'] The random positive definite function $\Phi^{\pi_n}_V$ obeys the large deviations principle in the space $\S^\rm{u}_k(\G)$ with rate function equal to
