{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.954100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e1d01bdabab46743cfd6926f0b1454cdf9685446737088a5825aaef5f486fec","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 (Four-moment replacement path) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] For $0\le r\le M_N$, define the centered hybrid $H_N^{(r)}$ by
\begin{equation}
 H_N^{(r)}(e_q)
 :=N^{-1/2}
 \begin{cases}
 Y_{e_q},&q\le r,\\
 \widehat Y_{e_q},&q>r,
 \end{cases}
\end{equation}
and set
\begin{equation}
 M_N^{(r)}:=A_N+H_N^{(r)}.
\end{equation}
For the replacement of edge $e_r=(a,b)$, let
$\mathring H_N^{(r,e_r)}$ be the centered hybrid with the $(a,b)$ and
$(b,a)$ entries set to zero.  Put
\begin{equation}
 M_N^{(r,e_r)}(u)
 :=A_N+\mathring H_N^{(r,e_r)}+N^{-1/2}uV_{e_r},
 \qquad
 V_{e_r}:=E_{ab}+E_{ba}.
