\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:49:17.502144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e3c7f7bed96cbcb552c1f374761e318340b7ed3ad6f0bb736f0c29bd3b985d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 22 of arXiv:2605.30030, 'Critical exponents for planar random-cluster model with cluster-weight~$q=4$'] For every~$x,y \in \bbR^2$ and~$\eps \geq \delta > 0$ satisfying~$|x|/16 \geq |y| \geq 4\delta$,
    \begin{align}

    \frac{\widetilde\Delta^\delta(x,y,\eps)}{\pi_1^\delta(\eps,|y|)^4}\asymp \Delta^\delta(|y|,|x|)^2+o_{\eps,\delta}(1)
    \end{align}
    where~$o_{\eps,\delta}(1)$ is a quantity that satisfies~$\lim_{\eps\to0}\limsup_{\delta\to0} \Ll|o_{\eps,\delta}(1)\Rr|=0$. 
	The constants in~$\asymp$ are uniform in~$x$,~$y$,~$\delta$ and~$\eps$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.185613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e3fea86967cfd561ac4c103743c87fa0eabca88c239922dbcb47792d86cfe39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] Assume that $N,v,v'$ satisfy the conditions in Theorem \ref{thm1}. There exist constants $\cl(d),\cl(d)\in (0,1)$ and $\Cl(d)>1$ such that for any $1\le M\le \cref{const_thm3_volume_1}N$, 
