{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:31:57.881075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e4d7060bb3e2e47b12592630267c0d7a9b49f5af92a4bc1ca9f34bfc55bf75b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l:conenull of arXiv:2510.13659, 'On the energy image density conjecture of Bouleau and Hirsch'] Let $K \subset \mathbb{R}^n$ be compact $C$-cone null set, where $C=C(v,\theta) \subset \mathbb{R}^n, v \in \mathbb{S}^{n-1}, \theta \in (0,\pi/2)$ is a cone. Let $\gamma:I \to \mathbb{R}^n$ be a Lipschitz curve. Then 
