{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852629+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e504878a9b6db0dc741f7b7508a3b3d422baac05bbd16d72741edb88f58b37a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition e:QalphaY of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. The generator of  $Y$ is given by

\begin{equation} 
  \begin{split}
    Q^\alpha f(n, \lambda)
    =& -\lambda f(n, \lambda) + \alpha(\beta-\lambda)f_\lambda (n, \lambda)\\
    &+\lambda \int\mathds{1}_{\{u < A-\lambda\}} f(n+1,u+\lambda) \,dG_{\ell}(n+1, u)\\
    &+\lambda f(0,{\lambda^o}) \bar{G}_{\ell}(n+1, (A-\lambda) \textrm{-}),
  \end{split}

\end{equation}
  where  $G_{\ell}(n, \cdot)$ is the distribution function defined in (equation e:Gell of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.353407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e52f5de88ef3ed9f35343ce7c3b40cdae2655446765fa73e7f6be7bf84e87e8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.follmervalue of arXiv:2605.14149, 'The mean-field limit of online stochastic vector balancing'] Fix $p\geq 2$. The function $\mathcal{U}_p^\mathrm{F}$ is upper semicontinuous on $[0,1]$. In particular, it is bounded and
