{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:58:40.873880+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e550d279bcefaf1a65f7db6d5cefa40cddb9aa4fde603a9a779067f41a5baa7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma logfluc0 of arXiv:2605.10617, 'Logarithmic scaling of selective sweep curves:\\ from tents to houses'] For $w \in \mathbb W$, write
    $S(w):= \max\limits_{0\le n \le \tau_0(w)} w(n)$ for the maximum of the path $w$ before it first visits $0$, and abbreviate
    $k(N):= \lfloor \tfrac N{\sqrt{\log N}} \rfloor$. Then with $\sigma_k$ defined in (equation defsigma of the paper) 
    \begin{align}
       \max_{0\le n <  \sigma_{S(W)}(W)}(\log_N (S(W)) - \log_N(W(n))\to 0 
        &\quad \mbox{ in } \mathbb{P}_{k(N)}^{p(0,N)}\mbox{-probability as } N\to \infty 
    \intertext{and}

         \max_{S(W)\ge k > 0}\,\max_{\sigma_{k}(W)\le n <  \sigma_{k-1}(W)}(\log_N (k) - \log_N(W(n))\to 0
          &\quad \mbox{ in } \mathbb{P}_{k(N)}^{p(0,N)}\mbox{-probability as } N\to \infty.
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.922630+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e56d956e38aba9dab49dc41de7074ceec820202d01b48c160822b9dab9a652d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $A$ be a finite abelian group, let $n\geqslant2$, and let $w$ be as in \eqref{eq:intro-weight}.  Then
\begin{equation}
\psi_{A\wr\Sn_n}(w)
=
\min\left\{
