\end{equation}
with the non-negative constant $u_{I} := \liminf_{t\uparrow\infty} \beta_{1}^{+}(t)N(t) - \beta_{1}(t)\E\big[I_{t}\big]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.875075+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ed34977c10d15c152642edab162dd3f343a33646546c3dc63df22e4f8f7e2ca","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop gamma_rate of arXiv:2605.07920, 'Primitive Sequences for Probability Measures on Compact Intervals'] Assume there exist constants $\kappa>0$ and $C>0$ such that, for all $u\in[0,1]$,
