{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.270072+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f84fb8d980c667bcc9459fecb7139b12fdac77049f0ec03fa553282820c77d0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mytheo Theo_uniform_hansonwright of arXiv:2411.08430, 'The Restricted Isometry Property of Block Diagonal Matrices Generated by $\varphi$-Sub-Gau'] Let $\xi=(\xi_{1},\cdots, \xi_{n})$ be a random vector with independent centered $\alpha$-subexponential variables ($0<\alpha\le 2$) and $\mathcal{A}$ is a family of $m\times n$ fixed matrices. We have for $t\ge 0$
