{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.909832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f8bae80d306bca6ca88d6f62a3cfad574451fa0e8cd99a315bfa7a91c160467","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cubic-expansion of arXiv:2608.26745, 'Moderate Deviations for the Largest Eigenvalue of a Randomly Deformed Gaussian Unitary Ens'] There are constants $c_0,c,C>0$ such that, on $\mathcal G_N$ and uniformly for
