and such that~\eqref{e.limDelta_N(x_N)=02} and~\eqref{e.lim|dF^x=dF^x|=02} hold with $(x'_N,y'_N)$ in place of $(x_N,y_N)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.511444+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a001c484cd7997ef8b291819de8257ca61643ed6abd248b454dcfc1b8c373d2f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (An interior-control criterion) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] Suppose that the L\'evy measure is supported in a bounded interval and charges
