=\ensuremath{{\mathbb P}}(\emph{\text{Bi}}(n-1,1/2)\leq d-1 ). $$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.445248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a032af171a23e7cc677a1a2fe4eb95de2bebfc2efc4aec7344a67a11719fd1ba","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5. lem: sub-aging fucntion, smaller parts of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Fix $l \in \mathbb{N}$.
  The following statements hold.
  \begin{enumerate} [label = (\roman*)]
    \item 
      For every $r>0$,
      \begin{equation}
        \lim_{\eta \to 0} 
        \limsup_{n \to \infty}
        \limsup_{(s,t) \in T_{3}(l)}
        \int_{D_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, r) \times \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \times (0, \eta]} 
          e^{-ws/v} P_{\rho_{n}}^{\nu_{n}}(X_{n}^{\nu_{n}}(t) = x)\, 
        \dot{\pi}_{n}(dx dw dv) 
        = 0.
      \end{equation}
    \item 
      It holds that 
      \begin{equation}
        \lim_{r \to \infty} 
        \limsup_{n \to \infty}
        \limsup_{(s,t) \in T_{3}(l)}
        \int_{D_{R_{n}}(\rho_{n}, r)^{c} \times \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \times \mathbb{R}_{>0}} 
          e^{-ws/v} P_{\rho_{n}}^{\nu_{n}}(X_{n}^{\nu_{n}}(t) = x)\, 
        \dot{\pi}_{n}(dx dw dv) 
        = 0.
      \end{equation}
    \item 
