{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.068254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05cae5cb584e3accd361f75ae913fa048c7ea1636e01ff5e16d27a2f7b8951b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem elemlemma of arXiv:2506.15500, 'On extinction and survival of the Bak-Sneppen model on arbitrary graphs'] Let $X_n$ be an ergodic Markov chain on a finite state space $\mathcal{S}$ with the stationary distribution $\pi$; assume that $0$ is one of the states. Suppose there is a non-negative function $f:\mathcal{S}\to{\mathbb R}$ such that 
\begin{align}
\begin{split}
f(0)&=0;\\    
\max_{x\in\mathcal{S}: \ p_{0x}>0} f(x)&=c_0;\\
|f(X_{n+1})-f(X_n)|&\le C;\\
{\mathbb E}(f(X_{n+1})-f(X_n)\mid X_n=x)&<-\varepsilon,\quad x\ne 0,
\end{split}
\end{align}
for some $\varepsilon>0$, $c_0>0$, and $C>0$.
Then for some $c_1,c_2>0$ depending on $c_0,C,\varepsilon$ only,
\begin{align}
\pi(A_k)\le c_1 e^{-c_2 k},
\quad\text{where }A_k=\{x\in\mathcal{S}:\ f(x)>k\},\ k>0.  
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.706265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a05e817c1233c6a13a4b540016e9053597e31d60a9d14132435c02bae7d43081","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem l:8.2 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For all $n$ large enough, $x \in {\rm D}_n^\circ$ and $y \in \partial {\rm B}(x; r_n)$, 
