\Op_{h_1}\left[\frac{\sqrt{(* - \alpha_{h_2})(* - \beta_{h_2})}}{2(*- z_2)^2}\boldsymbol{e}^{(h_2)}\,;\,\boldsymbol{\kappa} = \boldsymbol{0}\right](z_1),
\end{equation}
where $*$ is a placeholder for the variable in which this tuple is seen as a function on which the operator $\Upsilon_{h_1}$ is applied, and $\boldsymbol{e}^{(1)},\ldots,\boldsymbol{e}^{(H)}$ is the canonical basis of $\amsmathbb{R}^H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.317548+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a106b20abc5fb8f1531a30101e84a85ec2d09e63e160ecf985d64031fe539b18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma flowuniq of arXiv:2411.06131, 'Non-Markovian dynamics: the memory-dependent probability density evolution equations'] The flow $ \Phi_t $ associated with the RDEs ((RDEvec of the paper)) is given by the formula
