{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.405427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1097a2096ec79d1bd44ab7403a8a9fc23893a839bfc1b9e6d4f8db48e116968","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] For almost every $a_0\in \R$, we have
