{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.326042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a121ce97057a590fefb3fe5f904e2f47544dfc1b7dd2cf1035e5b4401fb0c8cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:sslongrange of arXiv:2606.01866, 'Phase Transition of a Semiflexible Membrane in Two Dimensions'] \label[proposition]{thm:sslongrange}
    Let $\lambda\in[0,2]$ and $\delta\in (0,1)$ be fixed. For any $x,y\in V_N^\delta$, if $\|x-y\|\gtrsim N^{\lambda/2}$, then 
    \begin{equation}
        \bar{G}_N(x,y)=G^0_N(x,y)+O(1),
    \end{equation}
    uniformly in $x,y\in V_N^\delta$. Moreover, the $O(1)$ error term improves to $o(1)$ if $\|x-y\|\gg N^{\lambda/2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.374199+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a122abddbcdaacd857ded99c629751adfce81c8839c163fa4d84a84fd318354b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2606.04245, 'Properties of a Special Type of Filtration and its Martingale Criteria'] Assume $P(\gamma=+\infty)>0$, $\EE[\sup\limits_{t\in[0,+\infty)} |F(t)|]<+\infty$ and $\EE[|L|]<+\infty$. 
