Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \Phi_{p,n}'(t)
 =
 -C_{p,n}\sqrt{v_{p,n}}\,\frac{n-1}{2}\,\E|Z|^p\,t^{p/2-1}
 +O_{p,n}(1).
\end{equation}
In particular, $\Phi_{p,n}'(t)<0$ for all sufficiently small $t>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.319949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1341f00ae797767f86f3f0d56703efc221b89ef686b98a11142076336d31b29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:integrate-one-spin of arXiv:2411.06195, 'Restrictions of some reinforced processes to subgraphs'] Let $1\in\Lambda$ and set $1^c=\Lambda\setminus\{1\}$.
