{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591243+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a148cef2b7379a443ac94044ce5f4e489411fbc5862bc46a8d9d4323365dcfcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma WPD-NHS-HUD-BB-3 of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $N \in \left\{ {0,1, \cdots ,10} \right\} $ and $t \in \mathop  \cap \limits_{j = 0}^{q} \left[ {0,{\mathfrak{t}_j}} \right] \cap \left[ {{t_k},{t_{k + 1}}} \right)$, the intermittent building block ${\mathbb{W}_\xi } \left( {t, \cdot } \right)$ defined by (equation IBW-GJI-A-2 of the paper) satisfies
