{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.856804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a173aca04a6ee6bc0051da898125b86499a5bd4a64a029bbf76b18c12c37faa2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:independence of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $x\in (0,1)$. Then it holds that $\beta_x$ and $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}$ (as introduced in Definition (def:l_and_bb_pin of the paper)) are independent. Further, the integration formula
    \begin{align}
    	\mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta) \psi (\beta_x) \right]
    	&= \int_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}+y l^x)\right] \psi (y) \, \mathcal{N}(0,x(1-x))(dy) \nonumber\\
    	&= \int_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{E}\left[ F(\beta+(y-\beta_x) l^x)\right] \psi (y) \, \mathcal{N}(0,x(1-x))(dy)
    \end{align}
    holds for any $\psi \in C_b(\mathbb{R})$ and any bounded Borel-measurable map $F \colon L \to \mathbb{R}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.116162+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a17b1757d4a6e424835ca5f9757a1e85cb2588640168675e14dcfba1c552417b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop PRO73 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Assume that the assumptions of Theorems~(THM61-2 of the paper) and (THM61 of the paper) are both satisfied, and that the transition density function of $X$ satisfies the two-sided sub-Gaussian estimate (equation eq:71 of the paper). Let $x\in E$ and $B\in \mathscr{B}^n(E)$ satisfy $\tilde{d}(x,B)>0$. Then
 \begin{equation}
     \lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{\mathbb{P}^x[\sigma_B\leq t]}{\exp\left\{-\gamma_1 t^{-\frac{1}{\beta -1}}\right\}}=\lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{\exp\left\{-\gamma_2 t^{-\frac{1}{\beta -1}}\right\}}{\mathbb{P}^x[\sigma_B\leq t]}=0
 \end{equation}
 for any constants $\gamma_1,\gamma_2>0$ such that
\[
    \gamma_1<c_2\cdot \widetilde{d}(x,B)^{\beta/(\beta-1)}\leq C_2\cdot \widetilde{d}(x,B)^{\beta/(\beta-1)}<\gamma_2.
\]
In particular, if $x_1,x_2\in E$ and $B_1,B_2\in \mathscr{B}^n(E)$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
    c_2\cdot \widetilde{d}(x_1,B_1)^{\beta/(\beta-1)}>C_2\cdot \widetilde{d}(x_2,B_2)^{\beta/(\beta-1)},
\end{equation}
then
\begin{equation}
    \lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{\mathbb{P}^{x_1}[\sigma_{B_1}\leq t]}{\mathbb{P}^{x_2}[\sigma_{B_2}\leq t]}=0. 
