{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:49:05.472258+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1aa688a294c50aaa2b5d6a476d84de153c9ea0c77edbb6973a58c23acb03336","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor H-in-L1 of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] For any $\mu \in P_{inv}(\mathcal{M})$ we have $\mu |H| \leq A$, where $A$ is as in (muH-converge of the paper).  In addition, $\mu \mapsto \mu H$ is a continuous 
