{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.779763+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a29be06c9646c0fc4c4c468365568c11741199bf9d23865eed16337e4037776e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Stationary Radial Ornstein Uhlenbeck process SDE of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] The normalized stationary radial Ornstein--Uhlenbeck process $\mathrm{ROU}_d(m)$, is the unique solution to 
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        &dR(t)=\bigg(\frac{m(d-1)}{R(t)}-mR(t)\bigg)\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{t} +m \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}{W(t)} \\
        &R(0) \sim \chi_d
    \end{split}
\end{equation}
for a standard one dimensional Brownian motion $W(t)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.013450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2a30a325726866f305cbd670e196aa033e13110d22a764d4cd55bccdb685790","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Let $Y=\left(Y^1,Y^2,\cdots,Y^n\right)$ be an adapted $n$-dimensional process with regulated trajectories of the form
	\begin{equation}
		Y_t=Y^{\ast}_t+\sum_{0 \leq s <t} \Delta_{+} Y_s,\quad \forall t \in [0,T],

	\end{equation}
	where $Y^{\ast}=\left(Y^{\ast,1},Y^{\ast,2},\cdots,Y^{\ast,n}\right)$ is an RCLL adapted $n$-dimensional semimartingale and $\sum_{s <t} \left|\Delta_{+}  Y_s\right|  <\infty$  a.s. Let $F$ be
	a twice continuously differentiable function on $\mathbb{R}^n$. Then the process
	$\left(F\left(Y_t\right)\right)_{t \leq T}$ also has the form \eqref{form of the process for Ito}. Moreover, almost surely, for each $n \geq 1$ and all $t \leq T$,
	\begin{equation*}
		\begin{split}
			F\left(Y_t\right)
			&=F\left(Y_0\right)+\sum_{k=1}^n \int_{0}^{t} D^k F\left(Y_{s-}\right)dY^{\ast,k}_s+\dfrac{1}{2}\sum_{k,l=1}^n  \int_{0}^{t} D^k D^l F\left(Y_{s-}\right) d\left[Y^{\ast,k},Y^{\ast,l}\right]^c_s\\
			& \quad+\sum_{0 < s \leq t}\left\{ F\left(Y_s\right)-F\left(Y_{s-}\right)-\sum_{k=1}^n  D^k F\left(Y_{s-}\right)\Delta_{-}Y^{\ast,k}_s\right\}\\
			&\quad+\sum_{0 \leq s < t} \left\{F\left(Y_{s+}\right)-F\left(Y_{s}\right)\right\},
		\end{split}
	\end{equation*}
	where $D^k$ denotes the differentiation operator with respect to the $k$-th coordinate,and $\left[\cdot,\cdot\right]^c$ denotes the continuous part of the quadratic variation $\left[\cdot,\cdot\right]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.921620+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2a8a146847f4f9db07cc40396e5fc30f70ead6eda4a777e4e6853cc260c3810","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $(X_{t})_{0 \le t \le T}$ be the Poisson F\"ollmer process. Then, we have
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $X_{t} \sim P_{T-t}f \dd \pi_{t}$ for all $0 \le t \le T.$
        \item Denote the compensated process $(\tilde{X_{t}})_{0 \le t \le T}$ as 
        \begin{displaymath}
            \tilde{X_{t}} := X_{t} - \int_{0}^{t} \lambda_{s} \dd s.
        \end{displaymath}
        Then, $(\tilde{X_{t}})_{0 \le t \le T}$ is a martingale.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.141607+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b635c354577fc4827c591b81d991bf4ed78512823f58d8ed02b87e14f83f79","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma kernel-growth of arXiv:2609.00425, 'Individual and Uniform Eventual Positivity of Self-Adjoint Semigroups'] For each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $h_n\colon[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}$ be given by $h_n(t)\coloneqq\mathrm{e}^{-(n-\delta_n)t}-\mathrm{e}^{-nt}$. Then one has
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\sup_{t \geq 0} h_n(t)}{u_n} \longrightarrow 0
    \end{align*}
    as $n \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.922693+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2b9489d6e5ba9fe75a08759a0d70a716178cdd554f9409eacc0773eaa366375","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2608.29914, 'Fixed points in abstract provability structures'] For each one-variable meet APS term $\triangle v$, we define $\mu(\triangle)\in\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$ recursively as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mu(v)=\infty$, 
    \item $\mu(\Box\triangle)=\mu(\triangle)+1$, 
    \item $\mu(\boxtimes\triangle)=0$, 
    \item $\mu(\triangle_0\land\triangle_1) = \min\{\mu(\triangle_0), \mu(\triangle_1)\}$.
\end{enumerate}
Here, $\infty+1=\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:56:37.657881+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2bb4ab5b21341729e321a8587de3870c00365f8697a0519d1440587eb03bfe3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:vertical of arXiv:2608.24830, 'Motion helps the contact process: survival below\\ the percolation threshold on Poisson Br'] There is $c=c(d)>0$ such that the following holds. Let $\eta>0$, $\epsilon\in(0,1)$,
$0<\Delta\le\Lambda$ and $W>0$, and let $\ell$ satisfy
\begin{equation}

  \Delta\ge c_0\ell^2(\epsilon/3)^{-4/\kappa}\qquad\text{and}\qquad\eta\ell^d\ge1 .
\end{equation}
Let $\mathsf G\ge\max\{c_1\Delta^{1/2}(\epsilon/3)^{-1/d},\,12r\}$, and put $K'=W+2\mathsf G$ and
$K=K'+2\mathsf G$. Let
$B\subseteq Q_W\times[0,t_0]$ and $B'\subseteq Q_W\times[t_0+\Delta,\Lambda]$, and let $A,A'$ be
increasing events determined by $B$ and $B'$ in the sense of (lem:Hprops of the paper). Then
\begin{equation}

  \mathbb{P}_\eta(A\cap A')\le\mathbb{P}_\eta(A)\Big[\mathbb{P}_{\eta(1+\epsilon)}(A')
  +\Gamma\,e^{-c\eta\epsilon^2\Delta^{d/2}}\Big]
  +\Big(\tfrac K\ell\Big)^de^{-c\eta\epsilon^2\ell^d}
  +C_d\,\eta\,(K+\Lambda^{1/2})^de^{-\mathsf G^2/(8d\Lambda)} ,
\end{equation}
where $\Gamma=C_d\,\epsilon^{-d}\big(K\Delta^{-1/2}\big)^{d(d+1)}$ is the factor
(equation eq:Gamma of the paper) of (thm:mixingupper of the paper) at mixing parameter $\epsilon/3$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2c6768429f320cfc463b28045f2fe74d360457c3ceea1c32b07fec273391018","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
\begin{align}

\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t;x,y)=p_t(x-y)\mbf E_B\left[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^{x,y}_t)>t\}}\exp\left(-\ka\int_0^t\xi_\eps\big(B^{x,y}_t(r)\big)\d r\right)\right],\qquad x,y\in D,
\end{align}
where we assume that $B^{x,y}_t$ and $\xi_\eps$ are independent, and we use $\mbf E_B$ to
denote the (conditional) expectation with respect to the randomness in $B$ only.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.693347+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2c9d2c767284a04e78c8ae93c4f55c00f6d284f68e691a161771edc49fe4188","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro_crdata of arXiv:2609.00645, 'Global persistence of nearly radial concentrated vortices in a bounded domain'] Under the assumptions of (thm:main of the paper), suppose in addition that
\[
  \mathbf a_\varepsilon=\mathbf a_*,
  \qquad
  \omega_{\varepsilon,0}(\mathbf x)
  =\omega_{\varepsilon,0}^*(\mathbf x-\mathbf a_*).
\]
Then, for all sufficiently small $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\left\{
  \mathcal D(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})
  +\kappa^2\sup_{\mathbf b\in\mathsf C(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})}
  [H(\mathbf b)-H(\mathbf a_*)]\right\}
  \leq C\varepsilon,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\mathcal A(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})
  \leq C\varepsilon^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
If $D^2H(\mathbf a_*)$ is positive definite, then, after possibly decreasing
$\rho$,
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{t\in\mathbb R}\ \sup_{\mathbf b\in\mathsf C(\omega_{\varepsilon,t})}
  |\mathbf b-\mathbf a_*|
  \leq C\varepsilon^{1/2}.
\end{equation}
Here $C>0$ depends only on
$D,\mathbf a_*,\rho,\kappa,M$, and $R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.782337+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2cf738128bf6ad09a03d147b8eb335d651d0fb2791b0ddabd2e63b0e767f38c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main-general of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Fix $d\ge 2$. Suppose Assumption~(assump:uniform-mixing-time of the paper) holds. There exists $p_0(d)<1$ such that for all $p>p_0$ and all $\beta > \beta_0$, if $X_t$ is continuous-time Glauber dynamics on $\mathbb T^d_n = (\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^d$, with probability $1-o(1)$, $x_0 \sim \bigotimes_{\mathbb T_n^d}\text{Rad}(p)$ is such that 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\mathbb P_{x_0} (X_t \in \cdot) - \pi^+_{\mathbb T^d_n}\|_{{\textsc{tv}}} \le n^{-10} \qquad \text{ for all $t\in [n^{o(1)}, e^{ \Omega(n^{d-1})}]$}\,.
    \end{align*}
    If $X_t$ is the infinite volume Glauber dynamics on $\mathbb Z^d$, with probability going to $1$ as $R\to\infty$, $x_0\sim \bigotimes _{\mathbb Z^d} \text{Rad}(p)$ is such that for $\Lambda_R = \{-\frac{R}{2},...,\frac{R}{2}\}^2$, once $t \ge R$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \|\mathbb P_{x_0}(X_t(\Lambda_R)\in \cdot) - \pi^+_{\mathbb Z^d}(\sigma(\Lambda_R)\in \cdot)\|_{{\textsc{tv}}} \le \exp( - \Omega((\log t)^{10}))\,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.644652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2d53c0a68712030fe434d7221f5f61b171b116dfaf965e59b579e6e0a5b3379","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Vlassis--Thomas) of arXiv:2607.23980, 'Sharp small-deviation inequalities for sums of independent\\nonnegative random variables'] If $Y_1,\ldots,Y_n$ are independent nonnegative random variables with $\E Y_i\le1$, then
\begin{equation}
 \Pp\left(K_n(Y_1,\ldots,Y_n)\le\alpha\right)\le\alpha,
 \qquad 0\le\alpha\le1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.328825+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2ec308f2995f3e9524f1eda2edee8026ea1b0c6f534ca07c127ffbe269a5977","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] {\em (Wiener-Khintchine)}
    Let $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a (weakly) stationary process. Then,
    $AC(\tau)$ is a autocorrelation function of some (weakly) stationary process $\mathbf{x}_t$ if and only if there exists a function $F(\omega)$ having the properties of a distribution function on $(-\infty,\infty)$ such that for all $\tau\in\R$
\begin{align*}
    AC(\tau)=\int_\R e^{i\omega\tau}~\txtd F(\omega),
\end{align*}
where $F(\omega)$ is called the spectral distribution of $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$. Moreover, if 
$$\int_\R AC(\tau)~\txtd \tau<\infty,$$
we have
\begin{align*}
    F(\omega)=\int_{-\infty}^\omega \frac{S_\mathbf{x}(\theta)}{V(0)}~\txtd\theta.
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.383265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f4db55d033bdd5d40c43394e11340d5e45408d7b9893e53432ec2b06ae6c42","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local_step_concentration of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For $\alpha \in (0,\frac{1}{2})$ there is some $c > 0$ such that, for all $e \in \binom{[n]}{2}$ with $v \in e$,
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ | \mathsf{N}^{\rho \to v}_G(X,e) - \mathsf{d}_\rho p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} | > n^{\mathsf{v} - 2.5 + \alpha} \mright]
    \leq \Exp{- c n^{2\alpha}}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954522+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2f63eea62cb52d3ac4ac7d51a3a20f60e1095fc0fa1fc40d1d3649fdda0645e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:two_sided_density of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Under the assumptions of
Theorem~(thm:conc_density of the paper),
for all $t>0$ and $a>0$, the left tail is bounded via
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\overline{\rho}_t - \E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] \leq -a\right)
  \leq
  \left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \exp\bigl[-tI^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] - a)\bigr].

\end{align}
Consequently, the two-sided
deviation probability satisfies
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\bigl|\overline{\rho}_t - \E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t]\bigr|\geq a\right)
  \leq
  2\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
  \exp\bigl[-t\min\bigl(I^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] + a),I^\rho(\E^\mu[\overline{\rho}_t] - a)\bigr)\bigr].

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.528276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2fc9a95121c8fe175231fc393279676f5ada4e6e503b99a6f0e4e41dda52dcd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 (Residual lifetime process, Section 4 of \cite{BertoinLeGallLeJan1997}) of arXiv:2604.01852, 'The on/off Brownian snake'] Let $E$ be a complete and separable metric space, let $x \in E$ and let $w \in \mathcal{W}_x$. Consider a Brownian snake $X$ under $\mathbb{P}_w$ (respectively $\mathbb{N}_x$) as defined in Theorem \ref{theorem bivariate brownian snake}. Let $D$ be an open subset of $E$, let $x \in D$ and let $F = E \backslash D$. For $v \in \mathcal{W}_x$, set $\tau(v) \coloneqq \inf(\{t \geq 0, v(t) \notin D \})$. Assume that $P^\xi_x(\tau<\infty)>0$. Then define
    \begin{equation*}
        U_t \coloneqq (\zeta(X_t) - \tau(X_t))^+ \hspace{0.5cm} \eta_r \coloneqq \inf\Big(\Big\{t, \int_0^t \mathbbm{1}_{\{\tau(X_u)<\zeta(X_u)\}} du > r \Big\}\Big),
    \end{equation*}
    and then the process $(U_{\eta_r}, r \geq 0)$ is a reflecting Brownian motion $\mathbb{P}_w$-a.s., (respectively is a stopped reflecting Brownian motion $\mathbb{N}_x$-a.e.). Furthermore, it follows that there exists a local time at level $0$ for $(U_t)_{t \geq 0}$ which is the limit
    \begin{equation*}
        \ell(t) \coloneqq \lim_{\varepsilon' \rightarrow 0}\frac{1}{\varepsilon'} \int_{u=0}^t \mathbbm{1}_{\{\tau(X_u) < \zeta(X_u) < \tau(X_u) + \varepsilon'\}} du
    \end{equation*}
    which exists for every $t \geq 0$ $\mathbb{P}_w$-a.s. (respectively $\mathbb{N}_x$-a.e.) and defines a continuous increasing process. As before, let $d\ell(t)$ denote the Lebesgue-Steiltjes measure associated with $\ell(t)$. Under $\mathbb{N}_x$, for a measurable function $\Phi$ we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{N}_x\Big(\int_{t=0}^\sigma \Phi(X_t)d\ell(t)\Big) = E_x^\xi(\Phi(\xi) \mathbbm{1}_{\tau(\xi) < \infty})
    \end{equation}
    and in particular we have
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{N}_x(\ell(\infty)) = P^\xi_x(\tau(\xi)<\infty).
    \end{equation}
    \begin{proof}
        This result is given in \cite{BertoinLeGallLeJan1997} at the start of Section 4 prior to the introduction of exit measures. In particular, \eqref{equation local time general} is given in \cite[Equation (35)]{BertoinLeGallLeJan1997} and \eqref{equation local time contribution} is a particular instance of this result.
    \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.668108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3058d2ec698f6cf1a50c273b338af02fa8672c3ceb62e5de313ef5ee8eb99b3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2607.20838, 'Long-memory Markov chains with power-law intensities'] Let $I(K) = \int_{K}^{\infty} \bar{F}_{\varepsilon}(u) \D u$. 
	For all $x,c>0$, the inter-arrival time $\tau_n$ satisfies
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{E}_{x,c}[\tau_n] \le \frac{\mu_{\varepsilon}}{\mu + k_p x} + \dfrac{I\left((\mu + k_p x)c\right)}{\mu}, \quad\quad k_p = \frac{1-2^{\,1-p}}{p-1}.
	\end{equation}
	For any $x_* > 0$, the conditional expectation $\mathbb{E}_{x,c}[\tau_n]$ satisfies:
	\[
	\mathbb{E}_{x,c}[\tau_n] \le 
	\begin{cases} 
		\dfrac{\mu_{\varepsilon}}{\mu + k_p x} + \dfrac{I((\mu + k_p x)c)}{\mu}, & x \ge x_*, \\[3ex]
		\dfrac{\mu_{\varepsilon}}{\mu} + \dfrac{I(\mu c)}{\mu}, & 0 \le x < x_*.
	\end{cases}
	\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.872267+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a30652ca5f8d0ae215e48e4039ebb45e1ea8a9cb4f20e1fe3f15f6084dd1ce2c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:link_gat_der_mall_der of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Let $A$ be defined as in (equation A of the paper), let $\Lambda : \mathcal{D} (\Lambda) \subseteq U \rightarrow U $ be a positive self-adjoint operator on a separable Hilbert space $U$. Then for any $h\in K $ there exists $\widetilde u_t$ such that 
\begin{align}

\int_s^te^{(t-r)A} G(r)\widetilde u_t(r)dr= e^{(t-s)A}h, \quad \mathbb P\textup{-a.s.},    
\end{align}
and, for some positive constant $C$ which does not depend on $t\in(0,T]$.
\begin{align*}
\|\widetilde u_t\|_{L^2((0,t);U)}
\leq & C \frac{|h|_{K}}{t^{3/2}};
\end{align*}
moreover if $h=Jb=\begin{pmatrix}
0 \\ b
