{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.829831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a35765bb8bc70f0272afcebb2846ee8c81555b9ac0cc0b2ff252888c3de4d76a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm exponentialconvergence of arXiv:2606.24385, 'Gradient Mean-Field Dynamics with Measure-Valued States: Well-Posedness, Chaos, and Long-T'] Let us suppose that (A4 of the paper),(A7 of the paper)--(A12 of the paper) hold true. Furthermore, suppose that the constants given in the hypotheses satisfy
