{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.149978+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3e79dda7008cad1455978d6563c15061d6cdf19e696665d09097b4634564ad6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 36 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $\gamma\in(0,2)\backslash\{\sqrt2\}$. There is a constant $C_\gamma>0$ such that for every $b>0$, the above boundary length process for 
