{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:51:30.076001+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3f34a3d1c85cd51e540c6c5308ed90e79232271f5f3edaa66a52d48f4809dd3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.02036, 'Self-intersection local times for Volterra Gaussian processes in stochastic flows with int'] The random process $\{\cT_k(t): t \geqslant 0\}$ is a positive continuous square integrable martingale with respect to $\tilde{\cF}_t$ with quadratic variation
