{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:37:28.980146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a3f6295af343cbce9a4971c47110ef40c14208708bdff3e998f96f21a314ba2f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor graph of arXiv:2412.00610, 'Joint Poisson Convergence of Monochromatic Hyperedges in Multiplex Hypergraphs'] Consider a sequence $\bm H_n = (H_n^{(1)}, H_n^{(2)})$ of 2-multiplexes. Suppose the vertices of $\bm H_n$ are colored uniformly at random with $c_n$ colors as in (equation eq:cn of the paper), such that the following hold: 
