{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.587288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4a24e4e0e5a34988e7c171da6a2e6a5f34d11c3657fe2ce1b63e9483da48096","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Thm-generalized KB of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Suppose (Hypo-generalized KB of the paper) holds. Let $\nu_{T}^{x_0}$ be defined by (equation eq:approx_measures of the paper) for the fixed initial point $x_0 \in E$ given in Definition (Locally Feller definition of the paper). Assume the following conditions are satisfied:
