{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.422285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a4a276c76c20a0878e713c174b308179f0f0997d8d37b627984d98d4079e70ce","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma a_binomial_identity of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] We have for all $n\in \tfrac12\mathbb{Z}_{\ge0}$:
	\begin{equation}

		\sum_{i=-n}^n\sum_{j=-n}^n
