{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.581783+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a51ff1992f314c4650038cfc520aba8a404429149650b7513f322eb4380d7eab","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Locally Feller definition of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let $x_0 \in E$ be a given reference point and define the strong closed ball
