\end{equation}
for some constant $C>0$ independent of $z$ and $n$, where $\kappa$ is defined in (\ref{KAPPA}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.755738+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5451b42b49a3582fdef83fd6eade2a48ede32cdc1c9e7afb70d324934ecdab3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:response-realization of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] We say that the response is \emph{potential-realizable} if, for every
