{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.606098+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a54a2de28135694083528fba2eda453878f8c0a0c7c4b031f2de3d1120fb36b3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition xtilde of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] For reaction $\mathcal{R}_{\ell}$, define subspaces $\tilde{\mathbb{X}}^{(\ell)}\subset \mathbb{X}^{(\ell)}$ and $\tilde{\mathbb{V}}^{(\ell)}\subset \mathbb{V}^{(\ell)}$ by removing all particle substrate position and velocity vectors in $\mathbb{X}^{(\ell)}$ and $\mathbb{V}^{(\ell)}$ respectively for which two particles of the same species have the same position or the same velocity. That is
