{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:31.001163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a682b1c3027b25e7fe77060dc71a0c6c682bd7cbcc33a41b78776ec0ccfcb25b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 51 (Counterexample to simultaneous mixed-degree extraction) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $Q=2,d=1$, and let $e,h$ be orthonormal in $\cK_1$.  Consider
\begin{equation}
 x_1=\alpha e+h,\qquad x_2=e^{\odot2},\qquad 0<\alpha\ll1.

\end{equation}
Then $\cN_1(F)=\mathbb Re$, so $h$ belongs to the canonical Gaussian
factor.  Nevertheless the first reduced
promotion is made at weight two and its range contains a nonzero $e\odot h$ component.
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U_2^{-1}M_{2,\mathcal U}^{[J]}
