{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:41:03.269592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a76db47621038414752e8987347bc09ae0ccabbc0d68fb4047ef71a03a546ed5","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mylem Lem_bound_pth_decoupled of arXiv:2411.08430, 'The Restricted Isometry Property of Block Diagonal Matrices Generated by $\varphi$-Sub-Gau'] Let $\{\xi_{i}, i\le n \}$ be a sequence of i.i.d. variables with distribution $\mathcal{W}_{s}(\alpha)$, $0<\alpha\le 2$. Let $A=(a_{ij})_{n\times n}$ be a fixed symmetric matrix and $\{\tilde{\xi}_{i}, i\le n \}$ be independent copies of $\{\xi_{i}, i\le n\}$. Then, we have for $p\ge 2$
