{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.985263+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a7760b72b51b65f65456aacbc6da9fe8e6dc58a7c730120e5af96bd8100ab056","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_lem of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let the polynomials $P_n^{(1)}(r)$ and $P_n^{(2)}(r)$ be as in ((poly_1 of the paper)) and ((poly_2 of the paper)), respectively. Then $P_n^{(1)}(1)<P_n^{(2)}(1)$ for every even integer $n\ge8$, i.e., 
