Furthermore, if $\tau< \infty$ a.e. then  $f_{\tau}(S):=
f_{\tau(S)}(S)$ is defined a.e.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.618627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a807efcaeb59cfe27eac49abdac11ff0ac3ba97aa2c48f394564f891334caf1d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2608.19065, 'Boundedly exchangeable graphs'] Let $\xi$ be a boundedly exchangeable graph process on $S$ directed by $\nu$. For every $B \in \widehat{\Bcal}(S)$ where $\pbb(\nu(B) = 0) < 1$ there exists an infinite jointly exchangeable matrix $A^B \in \rbb^{\nbb \times \nbb}$ such that the adjacency matrix $(A, N)$ of any i.i.d.\ representation of $\xi\vert_B$ satisfies for all $n \geq 1$:
    \begin{equation} 
        A \mid (N = n) \overset{d}{=} A^B[n]
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, the distribution of $A^B$ is unique.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.251349+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8124d00014613a4b41f91c32bc280eb6365cd2a3284d279fa840956edfab02a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2605.23222, 'On global solutions to the semidiscrete stochastic heat equation'] For $\beta$ sufficiently small, there exists a constant $c > 0$ such that 

