{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.781106+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a82e0f1cbded3429971e758fb01302f8e2c32733b74e97ec1f76aa108150e83c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3 of arXiv:2609.03054, 'The classes of bivariate Schur and Herglotz matrix-valued rational functions: realizations'] Let $F\in\mathbb C^{n\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ be a rational matrix valued function. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[\rm (i)]
\item {$F$ has no poles in $\RHPtwo$},  $F(z_1,z_2)$ has nonnegative real part
$($i.e.\ $F(z_1,z_2)^*+F(z_1,z_2)\geq 0)$ for any $z_1,z_2\in\RHP$,
and $\lim_{t\to\infty} F(t,t)$ exists;
\item $F$ admits a realization of the form
\begin{equation} 
F(z_1,z_2)= D+ C(z_1P_1+z_2P_2+A)^{-1}B,
\end{equation}
where the block matrix $\matr{A&B\\C&D} \in\Cmats{(k+n)}{(k+n)}$ is such that
\begin{equation}
\matr{
A+A^*  & C^*- B \\ C- B^* & D^*+ D
} \geq 0,
\end{equation}
$P_1,P_2\in \sqmat{k}$ are positive semidefinite and $P_1+P_2=I_k$.
\end{enumerate}
Additionally, if $F\in\mathbb R^{n\times n}(z_1,z_2)$ then the matrices $A,B,C,D,P_1,P_2$ in {\rm (ii)} may be chosen as real matrices.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:13:31.933745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a84b85520b353483d425e996a5d952f2dde358b97951388c8f0583b98febba6a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:surface_tension of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] The \textit{surface tension} $\sigma: \mathcal{N}(\Lambda)\to \mathbb{R}_+$ is given by
    \begin{equation}
    \sigma(s) := -\lim_{n\to \infty} \lim_{N\to \infty} \frac{1}{N n^d} \log \frac{Z_{n,N}^s}{(N!)^{n^d}}.
\end{equation}
It is straightforward to check that $\log (Z_{n,N}^s/(N!)^{n^d})$ forms as subadditive sequence in $n,N$, so $\sigma(s)$ exists for any fixed $s\in \mathcal{N}(\Lambda)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:41.028392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a84dbce4a6022ca86635e360ef0e11d81f474ba99dbfc6c9f9db4a4674f03753","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2-l14 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] Fix a bounded function $F\colon {\mathbb R}_+ \times {\mathbb T}^d_N \to {\mathbb R}$,
