{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:38:13.641708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a868006db0e85225a1e900f1d410b85b177c6840bf51696f82048bdb0f1dabea","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2609.00702, 'On the Set-Valued Katugampola Fractional Integral: Properties and Regular Selections'] Let $F:I\rightrightarrows \mathbb{R}$ be a set-valued function and $\mathfrak{I}$ be the collection of all integrable selections of $F.$ Riemann-Liouville set-valued fractional integral of $F$ is defined as 
