{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.302876+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8d7faad6143d72c9d28cefa84afa29e8fa64f9b8857e179ed92069b54efe549","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary thm_diffusive of arXiv:2608.07236, 'Negative association of Busemann functions \\in exponential last-passage percolation'] Fix $\varepsilon >0$. 
For any $\rho_1,\rho_2, \dots,\rho_n \in [\varepsilon,1 -\varepsilon]$, any down-right path $\mathcal{Y}= (\mathbf y_i)_{i\in \mathbb{Z}}$, and any $t\ge 0$, we have
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align} 
\mathbb{P}\Big(\sum_{i=1}^n B^{\rho_{i}}_{\mathbf y_i, \mathbf y_{i+1}} - \mathbb{E}\Big[\sum_{i=1}^n B^{\rho_{i}}_{\mathbf y_i, \mathbf y_{i+1}} \Big]\geq t \sqrt n \Big) 
