{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115767+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a8fc29f9b5e788fe06e12fe9c5f4dc15a677ed56e465f13058258715561056b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma-joint-convergence of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] $(W_{\delta}^{h}, \tilde{\mathcal{Z}}_{\delta}^{\pm,\lambda,h}, \theta_L(\delta)S_{L}^{h}(\delta), \theta_{R}(\delta)S_{R}^{h}(\delta))_{\delta}$ under ${\mathbb{P}} \otimes \mu_{\delta}^{\pm}$ jointly converge in finite dimensional distribution to $(W,\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\pm,W,\lambda},S_{L}^{W}, S_{R}^{W})$ under ${\mathbb{P}} \otimes \nu_{\operatorname{SLE}_{3}}^{(D,a,b)}$. Here, $W$ is a two-dimensional white noise, $\mathcal{Z}_{D}^{\pm,W,\lambda}$ is the limiting partition function of Theorem (theorem-cvg-RFIM-partition-function of the paper) and $S_{L}^{W}$ and $S_{R}^{W}$ are defined as
