{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.019189+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a99c73a23052c99b4a2970301f4a04ca567c8509c199f4d6e36c4bc9678dc7cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 of arXiv:2605.05986, '\bf Convergence rate of the occupation measure of { classes of ergodic processes toward th'] Assume that $d=d'$, that $b$ and $\sigma$ are locally Lipschitz functions, that $\sigma$ is bounded and that $\sigma$ is uniformly elliptic\footnote{In fact, the ellipticity assumption must be uniform only on compact sets.}:
