    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.018245+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9cd8a9b866ae5e3cd4fe2eba50551d67bed79259ae434c4a810ba14a9c29a0d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:massive_limit of arXiv:2605.15545, 'Crossover from subcritical to critical decay: \\ random walk, self-avoiding walk, percolat'] Let $d \ge 1$. Suppose $D(x)$ has finite support $\mathcal{U}$.
Let $x \in {\mathbb R^d}$ be on the boundary of $\mathrm{Conv}(\mathcal{U})$.
Then as $z \to 0$, we have
\begin{equation}
\abs x_{z} = \mathrm{rad}(\mathcal{U}) + O(m_z^{-1}) .
\end{equation}
In particular, $\lim_{z\to 0} | \cdot |_z$ defines a norm on ${\mathbb R^d}$, with its unit ball being $\mathrm{Conv}(\mathcal{U}) / \mathrm{rad}(\mathcal{U})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:20:07.907789+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9dbf12e8b6720c5a4ebdaa89687d4c75711143ced21f3bddd528daec8ca7b60","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:NSP:statement of arXiv:2608.23765, '\texorpdfstring{Tight Majorizations and Convergence Rates\\ of Nuclear Norm Minimization I'] A linear operator $\mathcal{A}: \R^{d_1 \times d_2} \to \R^{m}$ is said to satisfy 
	the \emph{NSP} of order $r \in \N$, $1 \leq r < d$ with constant $0 < \eta_r < 1$ if 
	\begin{equation} 
		\sum_{i=1}^{r} \sigma_i(\mathbf{N}) \leq \eta_r \sum_{i=r+1}^{d} \sigma_i(\mathbf{N})
	\end{equation}
for all  $ \mathbf{N} \in \ker(\mathcal{A})$. Here, $\sigma_i(\mathbf{N})$ denotes the $i$-th largest singular value of the matrix $\mathbf{N}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:28:08.664704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a9dd53127b3481d8249f7d93e07f0178d96cd50ef003548a8004c44a4cfda2b8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] Fix integer $q\geq 2$ and $\beta>0$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph and 
$\nu=\nu_{G;q,\beta}$ be the Edwards--Sokal distribution.  Let $\mu=\mu_{G;q,\beta}$ and $\pi=\pi_{G;q,\beta}$ be the Potts and RC distributions. 

Suppose that $\mu$ satisfies
entropy factorisation with constant $C_{\mathrm{spin}}$. 
Then, with $C_{\mathrm{joint}} \coloneqq O(q^3  \emm^{3\beta \Delta}C_{\mathrm{spin}})$, for every function $g\ge0$ on the joint spin-edge space $[q]^V\times \{0,1\}^E$,
\begin{equation}
\Ent_\nu(g) \leq C_{\mathrm{joint}}
        \bigg(
        \sum_{v\in V}
        \E_\nu\left[\Ent^{\circ}_v(g)\right]
        + \sum_{e\in E}
        \E_\nu\left[\Ent^{\circ}_e(g)\right]
        \bigg).
\end{equation}
As a corollary, $\pi$ satisfies
entropy factorisation with constant $C_{\mathrm{joint}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

