{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.772219+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa05e5d1140364d3da82882ec6a9843d53a2610052891ac0a93f908e2de3a0e8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop link-with-compositions-new-2 of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Under the assumptions of Proposition (prop:link-with-compositions-new-1 of the paper), we have for $n\geq 0$ the identity $\PFtrees{\mathbf{w}} {nd+1}=\PFComp{{\mathbf{w}},{\mathbf{b}}}{nd}$, and for $T\in\trees[d]_{nd+1}$ if we write $c(T)=\underline{n}_1 \cdots  \underline{n}_i$ and $\varphi(T)=(T^{[1]},\dots,T^{[i]})$, then
