{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.338754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa09dc799f9ef84f8589f0eb06f903c6046af2e54f8b7c826d7bfc8e1d8386bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 12 of arXiv:2512.05687, '$L^p$-Boltzmann-Gibbs principle \\ via Littlewood-Paley-Stein inequality'] (cf.\ Theorem 5.1 of \cite{BFS})
Let $p\ge 4$ 
and let $f$ be a local $L^{p'}(\mu_{u_0})$ function on $\mathcal{X}_N = \R^N$
for some $p'>p$, depending only on $\eta_{\La_{\ell_0}} = 
(\eta(x))_{x\in \La_{\ell_0}}$, such that 
$\tilde f(u_0) = E^{\mu_{u_0}}[f]=0$ and $\tilde f'(u_0)=0$.  Then,
there exists a constant $C= C(u_0,\ell_0)$ (which is uniform in $u_0: |u_0|\le K$
for any $K>0$)
such that for $\ell\geq\ell_0$ we have
\begin{align}  
\Big\| E^{\mu_{u_0}}\big[f| \eta^{(\ell)}\big] 
 - \frac12\Big\{(\eta^{(\ell)}-u_0)^2- \frac{{\rm var} (u_0) }{2\ell +1}\Big\} 
\tilde f''(u_0)
\Big\|_{L^p(\mu_{u_0})} 
\leq \ \frac{C\|f\|_{L^{p'}(\mu_{u_0})}}{\ell^{3/2}},
\end{align}
where ${\rm var} (u_0)$ is defined below \eqref{eq:3.2-A}.
On the other hand, when only $\tilde f(u_0)=0$ is known, we have
\begin{align}  
&\Big\| E^{\mu_{u_0}}[f| \eta^{(\ell)}]  - (\eta^{(\ell)} - u_0)\tilde f'(u_0)  
\Big\|_{L^p(\mu_{u_0})} \ \leq \ \frac{C\|f\|_{L^{p'}(\mu_{u_0})}}{\ell}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.256830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa11192aa67057dfe2b0af1363ec29e64f46719002576f321ee2b5caa8e3ce1c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 55 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] For any $\delta>0$ and $n\in\N$,
there exists a constant $\g{c}{sle,n}=\g{c}{sle,n}(\delta)\in (0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{align*}
  \g{c}{sle,n}\alpha\leq \inf_{\substack{x,y\in F\\d(x,y)\geq \delta}}E_{x}[1-e^{-\alpha \sigma_{x,y}}]\wedge \inf_{\substack{z,w\in F_n\\d(z,w)\geq \delta}}E_{z}^n[1-e^{-\alpha \sigma^n_{z,w}}],\quad \alpha\in (0,\alpha_n).
\end{align*} 
Here, $\sigma_{x,y}$ and $\sigma^n_{z,w}$ are the commute time of $X$ between $x$ and $y$, 
and that of $X^n$ between $z$ and $w$ (recall its definition from \Cref{resis}, respectively).
Moreover, $\g{c}{sle,n}$ is given by
\begin{align*}
  \g{c}{sle,n}=\int_{0}^{T}(Ae^{-Bs}-1)^2e^{-\alpha_n s}ds.
\end{align*}
The definitions of $A,\;B,$ and $T$ are given below at \eqref{abtdef}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.687846+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa1c583c161f5e92075c7e2f273ffba7704f07c1b860ab7cf0ce92a0a57846cd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 26 (Geometric axis and gate decomposition) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional real normed space, let $0\neq v\in V$, and let $g,a\in\Sl(V)$ satisfy
\[
g=a\e^v a^{-1}.
\]
Equip $V$ with an auxiliary Euclidean norm, denoted by $\norm{\cdot}_{\mathrm{Euc}}$, and set
\[
\mathcal{A}=a\mathcal{A}_v
 =\set{a\e^{tv}:t\in\R},
\qquad L_g(x)=gx,
\]
and let $p$ be the metric projection of $1$ onto $\mathcal{A}$. Then, for every $x\in\Sl(V)$,
\begin{align}
 d_{\infty}(x,gx)
 &=2d_{\infty}(x,\mathcal{A})+\norm{v}_{\mathrm{Euc}},
 \\
 \mathcal{A}
 &=\set{x\in\Sl(V):d_{\infty}(x,gx)=\norm{v}_{\mathrm{Euc}}}.

\end{align}
Thus $\mathcal{A}$ is the unique minimum-displacement axis of $L_g$ and is independent of the chosen factorisation of $g$. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
[1,g]=[1,p]\cup[p,gp]\cup[gp,g],
\end{equation}
where the three pieces meet only at $p$ and $gp$, and
\begin{equation}
gp=p\e^v,
\qquad
g=p\e^v p^{-1}.
\end{equation}
Finally,
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{A}\cap[1,g]=[p,gp].
\end{equation}
The first and third pieces in \cref{eq:conjugacy-geodesic-decomposition} degenerate simultaneously.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.538492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa1c8fd333e9ca0d8764e79247483e4e14d3a3cea9c14921c114f4500f233d29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem gam of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] Let Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)}, \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:lip of the paper)} and \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:super of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:convergence2 of the paper)}  hold with 
   $\bar p\geq \max\{2,\eta/8+1\}(\varepsilon+2)(\eta+1)(\eta+2)/{\varepsilon}\color{black}$
   where $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$.
	 Then,
	\begin{align*}
		&\int_Z E\big|\gamma\big( x_s^{i, N,n},\mu_s^{x, N,n}, z\big)-(\widehat{\Gamma})_{tam}^{\displaystyle n}\big(\kappa_{n}(s),s,x_{\kappa_{n}(s)}^{i,N,n},\mu_{\kappa_{n}(s)}^{x,N,n},z\big)\big|^2\nu(d z)\leq Kn^{-1-\frac{2}{\varepsilon+2}}
	\end{align*}
	for any $s\in[0,T]$ and $i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}$	where $K>0$ is a constant independent of $N$ and $n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:17:17.063249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa2891a2a64a7010e4b7f99bd57e93caabda13ca564fcd0c85033040efded02b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.19744, 'Conditioned Brownian motion and local equivalence of path ensembles'] Let $K\subset\R$ be compact and let $a\in\R$.  Suppose that
\begin{equation}
 \inf_{u\in K}\inf_{\zeta\in\spec(H_{\beta-iu})}\Re\zeta>a

\end{equation}
and that
\begin{equation}
 \Re\mathfrak h_{\beta-iu}[f]
 \geq a\norm f_2^2,
 \qquad f\in\cD, u\in K.

\end{equation}
Then there are $C,\eta>0$ such that
\[
 \sup_{u\in K}\norm{S_u(t)}_{2\to2}
