{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.722742+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aa93d8822bce77df03cc14dbbfce2a33ad6ab5399fa510f5e0c2f482929d6bd8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:kernelholojs of arXiv:2411.04238, 'Holomorphic jump-diffusions'] The jump kernel $K$ is said to have holomorphic jump size if it is of the form
