{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:25:39.115685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aaa7816e08d98e4048d61b22dd56050d027687c4937e4e58873c1acc15387604","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition proposition-uniqueness-law-curve of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] There exists a unique law $\nu_{W,\lambda}^{(D,a,b)}$ such that the following holds. ${\mathbb{P}}$-almost surely, the Radon-Nikodym derivative of $\nu_{W,\lambda}^{(D,a,b)}$ with respect to $\nu_{SLE_{3}}^{(D,a,b)}$ is given by
