{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.051751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aac5c8de91ce9e4222789d073d28ba35961f350bb5be249230869253cb85217c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RT of arXiv:2607.12564, 'Power-law and log-periodic degree tails for a family of probability generating function eq'] There exist $C,c>0$, depending only on $p$ and $j$, such that
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}(D^*_n=k)\le C\lambda^{-n}\exp\!\Bigl\{-c\,\frac{k}{\lambda^{n}}\Bigr\},
  \qquad n\ge0,\ k\ge j .
\end{equation}
Consequently, writing $N_k=\lfloor\log_\lambda k\rfloor$ and $m=n-N_k$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}(D^*_n=k)\le\lambda^{-n}\mathcal D_m,\qquad
  \mathcal D_m=\begin{cases}C\exp\{-c\lambda^{-m}\},& m<0,\\[2pt] C,& m\ge0,\end{cases}
\end{equation}
and $\mathcal D_m$ is weighted-summable:
\begin{equation}
  \sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}}\mathcal D_m\,\lambda^{-(\rho+1)m}<\infty .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:21:56.720734+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aacdb59a7cf8ec40f30858b5e4cd62c6a45fe3b1725a763220a80ac2dfc12fbf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:detect_intersection_left of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Let $z\in D$ and $r>0$ such that $2r < \delta^{1+a_3}$ and $B(z,r) \subseteq D$. Let $e \in \mathcal {E}^\delta_0(\mathcal {L})$ for some $\mathcal {L} \in \widehat{\Gamma}_0^\delta$, and suppose that $U_e \subseteq B(z,r/4)$. Then there exist $z_1 \in \partial B(z,r/2)$, $w_1 \in \partial B(z,r/4)$ such that one of the following is true.
