\item Let $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line of $h$ starting at $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(z,3r/4)$. Let $\eta^R_{w_1}$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting at $w_1$, reflected off $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Then $\partial U_e \subseteq \eta^R_{w_1} \cup \eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$.
\item Let $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line of $h$ starting at $z_1$ and stopped upon exiting $B(z,3r/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting at $w_1$. Then it hits $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ before exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Let $\overline{w}$ denote the first hitting point, and let $\overline{\eta}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting at $\overline{w}$, reflected off $\eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(z,r/2)$. Then $\partial U_e \subseteq \overline{\eta}^R \cup \eta^{\theta_0}_{z_1}$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.795517+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aacf9e538458ca80100dcfd34fc33bccf3dabbc51f3b39696d5b88cd3c15015d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:tailrl-harmonic-decomposition of arXiv:2609.02987, 'Tail Likelihood Reinforcement Learning'] If $J_{\mathrm{TailRL{}}}(\theta;x)>-\infty$, then
