{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.500435+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ab1883a9bf713d87fc3b96cf4a6d4da10bbe0f3c799fd573556c6c404346e720","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:one-point-bds of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] For any $\alpha_0>0$, there exists a constant $c>0$, such that whenever the boundary parameter satisfies $\alpha\ge \alpha_0$ we have the following bounds. 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item (Upper tail) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, n^{-1/3}]$ we have
$$
\mathbb{P}(X(1, 1; n, n) \ge \mu_\alpha(n) + \epsilon n) \le 2\exp\left(-c \epsilon^{3/2} n \left(1 \wedge \frac{\epsilon^{1/2}}{(1/2 - \alpha)\vee 0}\right) \right).
$$
    \item (Shallow lower tail when $\alpha < 1/2$) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, 1]$ such that $\alpha \le 1/2 - n^{-1/3}$ and $\epsilon n \le \mu_\alpha(n) - 4n$, we have
\begin{align}

	\mathbb{P}\Big(X(1, 1; n, n) \le \mu_\alpha(n) - \epsilon n\Big) \le 2\exp\left(- \frac{c\epsilon^2 n}{1/2 - \alpha} \right).
\end{align}
\item (Full lower tail for $\alpha \ge 1/2$, deep lower tail for $\alpha < 1/2$) For all $n \in \mathbb{N}, \epsilon \in (0, 1]$ we have
\begin{align}

	\mathbb{P}\Big(X(1, 1; n, n) \le 4n - \epsilon n\Big) \le 2\exp\left(- c \epsilon^3 n^2\right).
\end{align}	
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

