{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.347073+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abb2e5ef9e9250b3d8dd374456e6c788d796994c392c782ae6103429333b9789","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:variance_asymptotics of arXiv:2609.02491, 'Generalised Random Parking for Trapeziums on a Strip'] There exist finite constants $\lambda_2(a,b)>0$ and $C_{a,b}>0$ such that, 
\begin{equation}
