{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.312823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abd2382cf3a3cad9b3d6f0611b80c2a2db2ed943ef249851556d36079ebd0bf2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 27 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Suppose $U = \sum_{j=0}^\infty u^j$ satisfies Assumption~\ref{asmp:main for refreshing} for some $\beta >0$ and let $\alpha \in (0,1)$ such that $\alpha + \beta/2 > 1$. Let
    \[p >\frac{ \beta}{\alpha + \beta/2-1} \lor \frac{\beta}{\alpha}\]
    and suppose for some $K \geq 1$, 
     we have that for all $j \in \N,$ and  $n \in \{0,1,2\},$
     \begin{equation*}
         \|\nabla^n u^j\|_{L^p_\omega \continuous^0_{t,x}} \leq K 2^{(n-\alpha)j}.
     \end{equation*}
     Then there exist $\delta(\alpha,\beta,p)>0, \gamma(\alpha,\beta,p)>0$, and a random field $M : \T^d \to [1,\infty)$ such that $\gamma \to \infty$ as $p \to \infty$ and
        \begin{enumerate}
         \item almost surely $\sup_{y \in \T^d} |M(y)| < \infty$; in fact $\E \big[\big(\log \log\big(\sup_{y \in \T^d} |M(y)| + e\big)\big)^{\gamma}\big]<\infty$,
         \item $\E \big[\big(\log\big(\|M\|_{L^p_y} + 1\big)\big)^{\gamma}\big]<\infty$,
         \item and for any $y,z \in \T^d$, any $w \in C^{1/2 + \delta}([0,1])$ with $w_0=0$, if we have any solution $X$ to~\eqref{eq:main refreshing ODE 0}, and any solution $\tilde X$ to 
          \begin{equation*}
         \tilde X_t=z+\int_0^t U(s,\tilde X_s)\,ds+w_t,\qquad t\in[0,1],
         \end{equation*}
         then we have the stability estimate on the time interval $[0,1]$,
         \[\|X - \tilde X\|_{C^{1/2 +\delta}_t} \leq M(y)\big(|y-z| + \|w\|_{C^{1/2+\delta}_t}\big),\]
        and, in the case that $w=0$, the expansion/compression estimate for all $t \in [0,1],$
        \[\frac{1}{M(y)} |y-z| \leq |X_t - \tilde X_t| \leq M(y) |y-z|.\]
     \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.117824+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abd9abde2004622293e80b686096e70ee4985a5c468c881a22ea8fdd38d2c56d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2608.17022, 'Sharp hypocoercive convergence estimates for underdamped Langevin dynamics with specular r'] Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^d$ be a bounded convex domain with $C^{2,1}$ boundary, $U\in C^2(\overline\Omega)$, and let $\mu$ be the Gibbs measure (equation eq:gibbs of the paper) on $\Omega\times\mathbb{R}^d$. Assume:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(i)] the position marginal $\mu_x$ satisfies the Poincar\'e inequality
\begin{equation}
\nrm[\mu_x]{g}^2\le\frac1m\,\nrm[\mu_x]{\nabla_xg}^2,
\qquad\text{for all }g\in H^1(\mu_x)\text{ with }\textstyle\int_{\Omega} g\,\mathrm{d}\mu_x=0,
\end{equation}
with constant $m>0$;
\item[(ii)] the Hessian lower bound $\nabla^2U(x)\succeq-K\,\mathrm{Id}$ holds on $\Omega$ for some $K\ge0$;
\item[(iii)] the well-posedness Assumption~(ass:WP of the paper) holds.
\end{enumerate}
Let $f(t)=e^{t\mathscr{L}}f_0$ solve (equation eq:bke of the paper) with the specular boundary condition and $f_0\in\Lmuz$. With the friction coefficient
\[
\gamma=\sqrt{16m+2K},
\]
the following decay estimate holds for all $t\ge0$:
\begin{equation}
\nrm{f(t)}\le\sqrt3\,e^{-\Lambda t}\nrm{f_0},\qquad
\Lambda=\frac16\,\frac{\sqrt m}{\sqrt{2+\frac{K}{2m}}+\sqrt{4+\frac{K}{2m}}}.
\end{equation}
In particular, when $U$ is convex on $\Omega$ (so $K=0$), the choice $\gamma=4\sqrt m$ yields
\[
\Lambda=\frac{2-\sqrt2}{12}\,\sqrt m.
\]","status":"unverified"}

