{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.167400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_abf9a8188f2d07b2d76a89c0d064cfa4fb3809fd99763f2709cb734977231ea6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.17973, 'Schauder estimates and classical solutions of the Dirichlet problem for stochastic parabol'] Let $p,q\in(2,\infty)$, and let $Q_T^+=\R^n_+\times(0,T]$. Assume that \eqref{eq:flat-compatibility} holds. Then the following assertions are valid.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\rm(\roman*)]
