{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.231268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac0c52db37abb921bda3bbc1c87ed915e8f4c605c4eae540c0db517694fac8bd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 26 ({\cite[formula $(2)$ and $(3)$) of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] {BHS:Binfinite}}]  Let $(\omega_v)_{v \in \Z^2}$ be an i.i.d.~environment. There exist constants $c,C,m_0>0$ such that for all $x>0$ and $v=(\np,m\np)$ with $m \in \big( \frac{m_0}{\np},1 \big]$, the last passage times satisfy
