{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.589673+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ac3c55c30d9f5035e98f514dd21d062484e1723f3c805e76356085acb8a91ac8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop approx_hyper of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\mathcal W^{elec}(\mathsf{P})<\infty$ there exists  $(\mathsf{P}^N)_{N\geq 1}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with
    $\mathsf{P}^N\xrightarrow{N\to \infty}\mathsf{P}$ weakly and 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal E(\mathsf{P}^N)\xrightarrow{N\to \infty}\mathcal E(\mathsf{P})
    \end{align*}and \begin{align*}
       \limsup_{N\to \infty}\limsup_{n\to \infty} (nN)^{-1}\left(\mathcal H(\mathsf{P}^N,nN)-B_{nN}\right)\leq \mathcal W^{elec}(\mathsf{P}). 
