        c''\exp(-C''S) 
        \ \leq\ \mathbb{P} \Big( \widehat{\sigma}_{J}(v) \leq \frac{1}{S} v\Big) 
        \ \leq\ C'\exp(-c'S).
    \end{equation}
    The upper bound holds for all $v \in [n]$ and $S \in [1, \sqrt{v}]$; the lower bound holds for all $v\in[n/2]$ and $S\in[1,\delta'v]$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

