{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.210315+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ad5c39f7ebc34ea0721fa63e44316d4e4e26b593c21ec07787850fc220579c64","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2604.27242, 'Statistical Inference for Homogenization Limits Driven by Wiener or Hermite Processes'] The following asymptotics hold as \(N\) grows
\begin{enumerate}
    \item If \(\alpha\in(-1,0)\): \begin{equation}
        \f{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N-1}(1-k/N)(k/N)^{\alpha} \sim \f{1}{\alpha+1} - \f{1}{\alpha+2}
    \end{equation}
    \item If \(\alpha = -1\): \begin{equation}
        \f{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N-1}(1-k/N)(k/N)^{-1} = \log(N) + \gamma - 1 + \frac{1}{2N} + o(N^{-2})
    \end{equation}
    \item If \(\alpha<-1\): \begin{equation}
        \f{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N-1}(1-k/N)(k/N)^{\alpha} \sim \zeta(-\alpha)(1/N)^{\alpha+1}
    \end{equation}
    where \(\zeta(\cdot)\) is the Riemann zeta function.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

