{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.009100+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae18e113b1d35b1818d3afc42a3e9fb5a034aabef9b6a3ae4435fd44a62a0074","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition ESM of arXiv:2605.12777, 'Mesoscopic Rates of Convergence for Complex Wishart Matrices at the Leftmost Spectrum Edge'] Given an Hermitian matrix $H\in M^n(\mathbb{C})$, the ESM of $H$ is defined as:
