{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.822108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae1981f064f5e53f001bdcd3bbff7350797d1ad9298ec141e132238fc4bdd3fb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:homogeneous-monomial-weight-complexity of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For all $k\geq2$ and $h\geq1$,
