{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.038671+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b037f2f5805412417f2d75e889954869846d45ddecf0eeeaeccf9df768dc8f75","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 2 of arXiv:2609.00743, '$L_p$ Brunn-Minkowski inequality for the eigenvalue of generalized Monge-Ampère equation'] Let $u$ be a closed convex function on $\mathbb{R}^n$, and let $u^*$ denote its Legendre transform. Then
\begin{equation}
u(x)+u^{*}(\xi)\geq \xi\cdot x\quad \text{for all }x,\xi\in\mathbb{R}^n. 
\end{equation}
Moreover, the following three statements are equivalent:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] $u(x)+u^{*}(\xi)=\xi\cdot x$;
\item[(b)] $\xi\in\partial u(x)$;
\item[(c)] $x\in\partial u^{*}(\xi)$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.752363+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b03e42ecf49cce97e561e46cc295a6a885c5813f6209b420bad660b509631531","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 35 (Anisotropic local law outside the spectrum) of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Under the assumptions of Theorem \ref{local_law}, fix any constant $\epsilon>0$. Then, for any 
