{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.255520+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b10a42ab1caa0aa0b1d427a20e001a8f6662b89f295da21b9be611867e462646","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 108 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Recalling the definition of $k$ from \eqref{eq:h0new}, set 
	\begin{flalign*}
		x^{\pm} =\bar{x} \pm N^{B\delta/9} \td_{\bar{z}}
	\end{flalign*} 

	\noindent and let ${\bf L}^{\pm}$ denote the line parallel to the $y$-axis and with $x$-coordinate $x^\pm$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.513475+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b10b4a81474f55c76feec091a2dd3b944ac3248c6f3a1ef05985433b4e48a2cf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma: weight of all possible pinchings is 1 of arXiv:2411.11676, 'Surface sums for lattice Yang--Mills in the large-$N$ limit'] Fix a blue face $B$ with disjoint vertices. 
Then
\begin{equation}
	\sum_{B'\in \AF(B)}w_{\infty}(B')=1,
\end{equation}
where if $B'$ has multiple faces $\{B'_i\}_{i=1}^k$, we set $w_{\infty}(B'):= \prod_{i=1}^kw_{\deg(B'_i)/2}$.
As a consequence, if $M\in\mathcal{N}\mathcal{P}\mathcal{M}(s,K)$ is a non-separable planar embedded map and $B$ is one of its blue faces, then 
\begin{equation}
	\sum_{M'\in \AM(M,B)}w_{\infty}(M') = \prod_{f\in \BF(M)\setminus \{B\}}w_{\deg(f)/2},
\end{equation}
where we recall $\BF(M)$ is the set of blue faces of $M$.","status":"unverified"}

