{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.052658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b24f401e05d2787adbbec06fd233daf85184a1ca1f9507023fa5b36ab2a237e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro 31 of arXiv:2606.16164, 'A Low-Regularity Semigroup Sewing Lemma via Quotient Structures'] Let $\alpha\in\mathbb R$ and $h\in Z\hat C^{1}(\Delta^3_T;B_\alpha)$. Assume that $B\in C(\Delta^2_T;B_\alpha)$ and $\hat\delta B = h$. Then, for every $\tau\in[0,T]$, 
