{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.661317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2accb04ddf71d8a4f41c8c540bc57c48cb2d4b2df90e1a7cac123e5d63b783f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm conv-fields of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ be a Jordan domain. For every continuous function $f:D\to\mathbb R$ with compact support in $D$, and any $k\geq1$, 
