{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.566807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b32178ed07b3fddf03658c346a444427453e785ff5de37b70ecc5052fc2ef328","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 31 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Fix $m\in \N$ and a measurable, non-increasing function $\Omega:\R_+\to\R_+$. For $i=1,\dots,m$, let $c_i>0$. Suppose $f_1,\dots,f_{m+1}:\R^n\to\R_+$ are measurable, even functions that satisfy
    $$\left(\prod_{i=1}^{m}f_i(a_i)\right)\cdot f_{m+1}(v) \leq \Omega^{m+1}\left(\sum_{i=1}^mc_i|\langle a_i,v\rangle|\right) \quad \text{for all } a_1,\dots,a_m,v\in \R^n.$$ 
    Then, we have
