{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:22:46.468071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b33780a0499ba5f5526ffdad6990bcb22ff217ce9424f47c36683464184e7688","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 60 (Change of variables maps) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] We define the change of variables map from geometric to Cartesian coordinates as follows:
	\begin{align} 
		\Upsilon(t,u,x^2,x^3) 
		& 
		\eqdef (t,x^1,x^2,x^3).
	\end{align}

	We define the change of variables map from geometric coordinates 
	to rough adapted coordinates as follows:
	\begin{align} 
		\CHOVgeotorough{0}(t,u,x^2,x^3) 
		& 
		\eqdef (\timefunctionarg{0},u,x^2,x^3).
	\end{align}

	We define the map $\CHOVgeotomumuxmu$ 
	from geometric coordinates to ``$(\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3)$-space''
	and its Jacobian 
	$\CHOVJacobiangeotomumuxmu$ as follows:
	\begin{subequations}
		\begin{align} 
			\CHOVgeotomumuxmu(t,u,x^2,x^3)
			& \eqdef (\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3),
			\\
			\CHOVJacobiangeotomumuxmu(t,u,x^2,x^3)
			& \eqdef 
			\frac{\partial \CHOVgeotomumuxmu(t,u,x^2,x^3)}{\partial(t,u,x^2,x^3)}
			=
			\frac{\partial (\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3)}{\partial(t,u,x^2,x^3)}.

		\end{align}
	\end{subequations}

	We define the map $\CHOVroughtomumuxmu{0}$ 
	from rough adapted coordinates to ``$(\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3)$-space''
	and its Jacobian 
	$\CHOVJacobianroughtomumuxmu{0}$ as follows:
	\begin{subequations}
		\begin{align} 
			\CHOVroughtomumuxmu{0}(\timefunctionarg{0},u,x^2,x^3)
			& \eqdef (\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3),
			\\
			\CHOVJacobianroughtomumuxmu{0}(\timefunctionarg{0},u,x^2,x^3)
			& \eqdef 
			\frac{\partial \CHOVroughtomumuxmu{0}(\timefunction,u,x^2,x^3)}{\partial(\timefunctionarg{0},u,x^2,x^3)}
			=
			\frac{\partial (\upmu,\muX \upmu,x^2,x^3)}{\partial(\timefunctionarg{0},u,x^2,x^3)}.

		\end{align}
	\end{subequations}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.984660+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b33815ef659727c2aebeb18a9464b67ec862c6f4aa5354c46732bb74e0c4ba5e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2609.03339, 'Exterior Serrin Rigidity for the Homogeneous \texorpdfstring{$k$}{k}-Hessian Equation\\'] Define 
