{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:26.258533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b35a1279620567feacd625ddfeb6946363c2487e479cd0fbeacbaec570b252d5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prp 81 of arXiv:2605.23308, 'Convergence rate estimates for semigroups and heat kernels associated with resistance form'] Set $r_n=n^{\theta},\;\theta\geq 0$ and suppose that $\kappa\in (1/2,1]$ and $\alpha>1$.
Then, for any $\zeta>\alpha^{-1}$, it holds that
\begin{align*}
  d_{\BL^{\kappa}}(\mu^{(r_n)},\mu_n^{(r_n)})
  \lesssim
  \begin{dcases}
    n^{-\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}}(\log n)^{1+\zeta}, & \theta=0,\;\alpha\in (1,2),\\
    n^{-\frac{\alpha-1}{\alpha}+\frac{2+\alpha}{2\alpha}\theta}(\log n)^{\zeta(1-\alpha/2)}, & \theta>0,\;\alpha\in (1,2),\\
    n^{-\frac{1}{2}}(\log n)^{1+\zeta},& \theta=0,\;\alpha=2,\\
