{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617848+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b401e5d4425c84a364d4f59c5409fac799103a3eca8ef5adf49dc7f90d1ca462","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For each~$s\ge u$ and~$A\in\sigma(h(x_0),\dots,h(x_n))$,
\begin{equation}

