{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:51:12.739126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b56118357133bd72893edce550e5e9086f3a9eb219051fe3e5c20fb39d2dd47a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 of arXiv:2605.02420, '\textbf{Large time behavior of critical marked Hawkes processes with heavy tailed marks an'] a) For any $m\in\N$ and $\theta_1,\ldots, \theta_m, t_1,\ldots, t_m\in (0,\infty)$ we have
\begin{equation}
 E\exp\left\{-\sum_{k=1}^m\theta_k Y_{T}(t_k)\right\}=\exp\left\{-\mu\int_0^\infty g_T(t)dt\right\},

\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  g_{T}(t):=1-Ee^{-\<N^t, f_T\>},

 \end{equation}
 with $f_T$ given by \eqref{e:f_sum} and \eqref{e:fT} and recalling that $N^t$ denotes the empirical measure of a branching particle system starting from a single particle at point $t$ (with no immigration). Moreover, the function $g_T$ satisfies
\begin{align}
  g_{ T}(t)=&1-e^{-f_T(t)}
G\left(1-\int_0^\infty g_{T}(t+s)\varphi(s)ds\right)
 \\
 =& 1-e^{-f_T(t)}+e^{-f_T(t)}\int_0^\infty g_T(t+s)\varphi (s)ds -e^{-f_T(t)}H \left(\int_0^\infty g_T(t+s)\varphi(s) ds\right)
 .
