{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:48:02.407703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b668c71ba6e9c0b6cc48db1b0bb7ab86f0a63cc0285a24fd5a3c03ceb4108641","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop torusgroup of arXiv:2608.26564, 'Real ideal points, Conway spheres, and left-orderable Dehn fillings'] $G_n^{tor}$ is free on $A = x_{n+3}, H = x_2(x_{n+3}x_{2n+4})^{-n}$. Killing the trivial-strand meridian gives the quotient
