{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:38.602191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6a5fcb3c132ddbbe23c5f72fb2e1a46d228d9d718cc6fff8ac8b9f5097e2880","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 35 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] Assume that the Markov renewal kernel is strict, and let $\mathcal E$ and $(R_h)_{h\in\N^d}$ be defined by \eqref{eq:augmented-admissible-set} and \eqref{eq:augmented-transition-kernel}. For every initial law concentrated on $\mathcal E$, the augmented field $Y=(Z_k,U_k)_{k\in\N^d}$ satisfies

\begin{equation}
\Ee\left[f(Y_{k+h})\mid \mathcal G_k^Y\right]=R_hf(Y_k),
\qquad k,h\in\N^d,
\end{equation}

for every bounded measurable function $f$ on $\mathcal E$. Moreover, $(R_h)_{h\in\N^d}$ is a Markov semigroup:

\begin{equation}
R_{\zerod}=I,
\qquad
R_{h+r}=R_hR_r,
\qquad h,r\in\N^d.
\end{equation}

In particular, the coordinate transition kernels $R_{e_1},\ldots,R_{e_d}$ commute.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:38:36.827689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6aafa1ba250e824b75b1754ff2e8d6bbcabc90c9168bb0688a68b8e2b787c5c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:shuffle of arXiv:2606.28869, '\bfseries A General Theory of Paths:\\ \large Signatures, Jump Lifts, and Expected Signatu'] For bounded-variation paths and words $u,v$,
