{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.968747+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6e9e897a6eff13d5592c4d44b930fb153dc82e327df1ab45d2745a15a8421cb","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 32 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] Let $T<\infty$. For any $\varepsilon>0$ such that $\mathcal{I}_\varepsilon:=[t_1+\varepsilon,t_2-\varepsilon]$ has nonempty interior, there exists a $K_\varepsilon>0$ uniformly for all sufficiently large $T$ such that
