{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.561801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b89f3fa324ee1ecd1332b099aff1fb7641b15a0924cb4fb0972322fc5f89c201","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:uncut-trace-derivative-formula of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:uncut-logdet-derivatives}
For \(\eta>0\), \(A,C\in\operatorname{Sym}_n\), and \(r\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\,\mathrm d^r}{\,\mathrm d s^r}
 \operatorname{Tr}\ell_\eta(A+sC)\bigg|_{s=0}
 =
 (-1)^{r-1}(r-1)!\,
 \Re\operatorname{Tr}\!\left\{\bigl((A-i\eta I_n)^{-1}C\bigr)^r\right\}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{align}
 \abs{D\operatorname{Tr}\ell_\eta(A)[C]}
 &\le\eta^{-1}\sqrt n\left\lVertC\right\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}},
 \\
 \abs{D^r\operatorname{Tr}\ell_\eta(A)[C,\ldots,C]}
 &\le(r-1)!\eta^{-r}
 \left\lVertC\right\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}^2\left\lVertC\right\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}^{r-2},
 \qquad r\ge2.

\end{align}
The bounds are uniform in \(n,A,C\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.727028+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b89fb9475e5cd50c64e75d13c5215e20d890d3d12eaed272cf4215b9707dfe4a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemmas2.1 of arXiv:2608.01279, 'Stochastic heat equation with nondegenerate Hölder diffusion coefficient: uniqueness below'] Let \((W,W')\) be two independent cylindrical Wiener processes on \(H\),
and let \(a_t,b_t\) be bounded predictable processes
satisfying \(a_t(x)^2+b_t(x)^2=1\) for all $x\in\mathbb{T}$ (so that both processes lie in $L^\infty(\mathbb{T})$ a.s.) Define

\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
dB^0_t&=a_t\,dW_t+b_t\,dW'_t,\\
dB^1_t&=b_t\,dW_t-a_t\,dW'_t.
\end{aligned}

\end{equation}
Then \((B^0,B^1)\) is a pair of independent cylindrical Wiener
processes in the enlarged filtration.","status":"unverified"}

