{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.955636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9640ffa52b06e7f2fad55b9b7647f9f93a43f57992a4da60c4ab6fa9434f3ef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:two_sided_current_explicit of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let $i\in\{1,2\}$ and adopt the assumptions of Theorem~(thm:explicit_current_1 of the paper)
($i=1$) or Theorem~(thm:explicit_current_2 of the paper) ($i=2$). 
Since $Q$, $\mathrm{Var}_\mu(W)$
and $\|\bar W\|_{L^\infty(\mu)}$ are invariant under sign reversal 
of $\overline{J}_t(U)\mapsto -\overline{J}_t(U)$ (hence $U\mapsto -U$)
the parameters
$\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2, c_{J,i}$ remain unchanged.
Applying the theorems to 
$-\overline{J}_t(U)$ therefore leads to bounds on the left tail with the same constants.
For all $t>0$, $a>0$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\E^\mu[\overline{J}_t] -\overline{J}_t(U)\geq a\right)
\leq
\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
\exp\left[-t\frac{\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2}{c_{J,i}^2}
  h\left(\frac{c_{J,i} a}{\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2}\right)\right].
\end{align}
Correspondingly, a union bound correspondingly gives the two-sided sub-gamma bound, and its simpler Bernstein
form with the additional factor of $2$, i.e.,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{P}^\nu\left(\bigl|\overline{J}_t(U) - \E^\mu[\overline{J}_t]\bigr| \geq a\right)
&\leq
2\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
\exp\left[-t\frac{\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2}{c_{J,i}^2}
  h\left(\frac{c_{J,i} a}{\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2}\right)\right]
\\
&\leq
2\left\|\frac{\mathrm{d}\nu}{\mathrm{d}\mu}\right\|_{L^2(\mu)}
\exp\left[-\frac{ta^2}{2(\tilde\sigma_{J,i}^2 + c_{J,i}a)}\right].
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:04:39.774192+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b964ccef0457269628cd46a5c61d8814615ce6e59e63b09eba48c28d1f3a162e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:measure-data-rigorous of arXiv:2609.01464, 'Removability of non-isolated singularities for Einstein metrics and RCD spaces'] Let $(Y,\mathrm{d},\mathcal{H}^n,y)$ be a pointed
$\operatorname{RCD}(K,n)$ space, with an integer $n\geqslant 2$, and $K\in\mathbb R$. Let $R>0$, and suppose that $\overline{B}_{\frac{3}{2}R}(y)\neq B_{2R}(y)$, and
\[
 f\in W^{1,2}_{\mathrm{loc}}(B_{2R}(y)),\qquad
 \mathbf{\Delta} f=\sigma,
\]
where $\sigma$ is a finite signed Radon measure on $B_{2R}(y)$.  Then,
for every $1\leqslant q<n/(n-1)$,
\begin{equation}
 \|f\|_{W^{1,q}(B_R(y))}
 \leqslant C\left(\|f\|_{L^1(B_{2R}(y))}+|\sigma|(B_{2R}(y))\right).
\end{equation}
The constant $C$ depends on $q,K,n,R$ and geometric data on $B_{2R}(y)$\footnote{From the proof, one can track down precisely the constants on which this $C$ depends on: those are the constants appearing in (equation eq:P-Lq of the paper), (equation eq:gradient-Lq of the paper), (equation eqn:LinftyL1 of the paper), (equation eqn:Caccioppoli of the paper), and (equation eqn:Ebbasta of the paper).} (upper/lower bounds of volumes of balls of radius $\sim R$, upper/lower bounds of Ahlfors constant on $B_{2R}(y)$, Poincaré/Dirichlet inequality constants...).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.962181+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b964eabf8a11cc50e6fa2b2a0081d002221e19a6ab003319c77db3f84168e16b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem.new of arXiv:2411.07103, 'On a connection between total positivity and Bernoulli stopping problems'] Let $I \coloneqq \{m_1, m_2, \ldots, m_N\}$ be a arbitrary collection of positive integers, where $N \in \mn$.  Define 
