If  $\sum_k p_k < \infty$, then $v$ is unimodal.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.676147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9659144d0a5871a902c5bcc1da490a6c9d0426fb21b7156c905b8fe77b77956","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:concentration1 of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] Let $t\in [0,1)$ and $x\in \mathbb{R}^d$, then for all $f\in \mathcal{H}_1^{\beta-\lfloor \beta \rfloor,\theta}(\mathbb{R}^d)$  we have
