{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:56:36.591448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b971a137098ba7d8942835e148fb9aab6896aceff46c0638976d4551d6881d00","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition RSRI-ujdh-main of arXiv:2608.30582, 'The flexible part of intermittent Onsager theorem for the two-dimensional stochastic incom'] For any $t \in \mathrm{supp}_t\ w_{q + 1}^{\left( s \right)}$, the Wiener process ${\mathfrak{W}_{q+1}}\left( t \right)$, the velocity ${u_{q + 1}}\left( {t,x} \right)$ and the Nash pressure ${\mathfrak{p}_{q + 1}}\left( {x} \right)$ satisfy
