{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.044230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b98731a67ea4ef0fa681a7250ed10fd0b7413fead9aefc053af98f94a641338a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 82 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Suppose   that $(\sfd_{0},q,p)$ are properly tight.
 Then 
