{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.661079+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba4722d9a1bc7a2c9f892ae1b737102b935f62d45762fe00f3a64027e219bd61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:uniform_Bound_diam of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] For any $\rho>0$ there exists $c>0$ such that
