{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:47:40.734400+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baa87bb0ac880d7d903b45a72083abae08a0a6b2c0db444048be1a02fd2519bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sobolev of arXiv:2604.20008, 'Mixing times of Langevin dynamics for \\ spiked matrix models'] On the unit sphere $\mathbb S^{N-1}$, for any $g \in W^1_2(\mathbb S^{N-1})$, we have the Sobolev inequality
    \begin{align*}
        \left\lVertg\right\rVert_q^2\leq \frac{q-2}{N-1} \left\lVert\nabla g\right\rVert_2^2+\left\lVertg\right\rVert_2^2\,,
    \end{align*}
    where $q=\frac{2(N-1)}{N-3}$.    
    Switching to $\mathbf{S}_N$, for any $f\in W^1_2(\mathbf{S}_N)$, 
    \begin{align*}
        \left\lVertf\right\rVert_q^2\leq \frac{N(q-2)}{N-1} \left\lVert\nabla f\right\rVert_2^2+\left\lVertf\right\rVert_2^2\,.
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:15.483138+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bab871297b6483a1039cd6158e0c27ff82eb22cbe094b3c544357a38adda12bf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 39 of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Fix $\varepsilon\in (0,1)$ and $z\in D$.
On the event $\{\ell_{0,b}(z) = b,\, 2\pi V_{A_{0,b}}(z)<\vert \log\varepsilon\vert\}$,
\begin{displaymath}
\PP(z\in \Ns_{\varepsilon}(A)\vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}) =
\sum_{k=0}^{+\infty} (-1)^{k}
\dfrac{1}{2^{k} k! (k+1/2)}
\dfrac{\E[\psi_{2k+1, A} \vert A_{0,b},\ell_{0,b}](z)}{\big(\frac{1}{2\pi}\vert\log \varepsilon\vert\big)^{k + 1/2}}.
\end{displaymath}
On the event $\{\ell_{0,b}(z) = b, \CR(z,D\setminus A_{0,b})\in (\varepsilon,\varepsilon^{-1})\}$,
