{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.196495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd6e72a47bc71a323804d7bfc0f9fc09528078c018e9639918f5aec2aa908629","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 29 of arXiv:2510.22783, 'Universality of Cutoff for Riffle Shuffling'] Let $X\sim \Hyp(n_1,n,m)$ and let $\sigma^2=\frac{n_1m(n-n_1)(n-m)}{n^2(n^2-1)}$ be the variance of $X$. There exists an absolute constant $C$ such that for each $k\geq 0$,
