{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.280322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_be15a07aa79e7ec61e00d6437cae439fc78b7799e5e202bc00f21628d18e3765","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemme eq:encoredesrestrictiobs of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Under the allometric setting, suppose that the weight function $\omega$ has an \hyperlink{alloform}{allometric form} with $0 \leq \kappa_{1} \leq \kappa_{2}$. Then, Assumption~(ass:finallejd of the paper) is equivalent to 
