{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.661728+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bef6259ac1bdc4f78e91c485341b289978f4abf7a6a9cf5a302030115e4c94c8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2605.09372, 'Sharp weighted norm estimates for martingale square functions'] Let $1 < p <\infty$ and let $W$ be a matrix weight. There exist a sequence of matrix-valued functions $\widehat W_n$ such that for every $n$, the  entries of $\widehat W_n$ are adapted to $ \mathcal F_n$ and
