{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.457300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bf825385cd75e29799b3fa0d10d70f14ae2c5c2a2a3fbf35e7a813f478a5b810","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 26 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma >0$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $ \widehat{b}_n \in \mathbb{R}$. Moreover, let $(F_x)_{x \in \mathbb{Z}}: \Omega \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ be a sequence of mappings such that 
\begin{align}
 \forall x \in \mathbb{Z}, \; \forall s \in [0,T], \; \forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad & \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \big[ \big\{ F_x(\eta_s^n) \big\}^{2} \big] \leq \frac{C_1}{L^{2}},  \\
 \forall x,y \in \mathbb{Z}: |y-x| \geq 2 K, \; \forall s \in [0,T], \; \forall n \in \mathbb{N}_+, \quad & \mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \big[ F_x(\eta_r^n) \; F_y(\eta_r^n) \big]=0. 
