  where $\mathcal N(x)$ denotes the set of vertices adjacent to vertex~$x$\footnote{Note that $\mathcal N(x) \subset V_1$ corresponds to the set of edges adjacent to $x$ in the original graph.}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:43:53.646335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bfdbf2c7a9856cf8890967efaa8a5f2f97f02bbc23a8001cfd137cad9f36eefb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:W asympt of arXiv:2512.17747, 'On exponentially height-penalized random trees'] Let $\mu=\mu_n$ be such that $1/\sqrt{n}\ll\mu\ll n^{1/4}$.
