{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:22:08.368720+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c05e259b63a857a72b8752c48ff8926885ea9ad333157ce986b121be90a8f30d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:circulantmatrix of arXiv:2607.28817, 'Limiting spectral distribution for the adjacency matrix of the Watts--Strogatz random grap'] For all $n\ge1$ and even integers $K<n$, the eigenvalues of $D_{n,K}$ are
    \[
        \lambda_j = \begin{cases}
            \frac{\sin((K+1)\pi \frac jn)}{\sin(\pi \frac jn)}-1&\quad\mbox{ for } j\in\{1,\dots,n-1\},\\
            K&\quad\mbox{ for }j=n.
        \end{cases}
    \]
    Furthermore, for all sequences $(K_n)_{n\ge1}$ of even integers that satisfy $2\le K_n<n$ for all sufficiently large values of $n$ and a sequence $(p_n)_{n\ge1}$ in $(0,1]$, under the assumption~(equation eq:assumption1 of the paper), there exist two matrices $D^{(1)}_{n,K_n}$ and $D^{(2)}_{n,K_n}$ such that
    \begin{gather}
        D_{n,K} = D^{(1)}_{n,K_n} + D^{(2)}_{n,K_n},\\
        \operatorname{rank}\left(\frac{D^{(1)}_{n,K_n}}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}\right)\underset{n\to\infty}{=}o(n),\\
        \left\|\frac{D^{(2)}_{n,K_n}}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}\right\|\;\xrightarrow[n\to\infty]{}\;0,
    \end{gather}where $\|\cdot\|$ denotes the spectral norm of a matrix. It follows that the empirical spectral measure $\mu_{\frac{D_{n,K_n}}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}}$ of $\frac{D_{n,K_n}}{\sqrt{p_nK_n}}$ converges weakly to the Dirac mass $\delta_0$ as $n \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.314724+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c05f210195ce4aaff64a631499b26bcfcb80ec6700fa69e9c380a3e78e0f2272","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition pro:1 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For all $0<M<\infty$, there exist constants $v_1=v_1(M)>0$ and $a_1=a_1(M)$ such that for each $m\ge1$ and $(\gamma,\gamma')\in\mathcal X_m(M)$, we can couple $X$ and $X'$ in such a way that
    \begin{equation}
        \mathbb P\big(X\setminus\mathcal B_{-m/2}\neq X'\setminus\mathcal B_{-m/2}\big)<a_1\,e^{-v_1m}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.239110+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0633b62538f4d5a80275467a1613d1e43474fcc00c048238eab78a92c0c2548","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cond_prob_crossing of arXiv:2609.04140, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ III:\\ uniqueness'] There exists a universal constant $p \in (0,1)$ such that the following holds for all $\varepsilon \in (0,\varepsilon_0)$,  where $\varepsilon_0$ denotes the constant in the statement of Lemma~(lem:upper_bound_on_width of the paper).  For every fixed $n \in [0,\lfloor \log(1/\varepsilon) \rfloor -1]_{\BZ}$ and $j \in \{1,2,3,4\}$,  and conditional on $U_1,U_2,U_3,U_4$ and on $P_{j,\tilde{n}}$ for $\tilde{n} \neq n$,  we have that the curve $P_{j,n}$ first intersects the right boundary of the rectangle
\begin{align*}
(0,L_j) \times \left(\vert a_{j,n} \vert- \frac{1}{4 \log(1/\varepsilon)} ,  \vert a_{j,n} \vert + \frac{1}{4 \log(1/\varepsilon)} \right)
\end{align*}
before hitting either its top or bottom boundaries,  with conditional probability at least $p$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.364960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c068e0895e14d490d2427e1c7bee91efa8db9913e2c166fd881aba74f12f0a84","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sep1 of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] If $\bclr{ T_n^{1}, T_n^{2}}_{n\in \N}$ is distributed according to the measure $0\text{-CUA}$, then for all $\varepsilon>0$ there exist $m,K,\ell \in \N$ such that for all $n \geq m$
