for any representation $\pi$, recalling the notation from~\eqref{eq:pre-lin-maps-Q}. \qed (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.996731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0c8cf4fd8f609eb7098b148b2189e0836c24f517eee165f7f3398d1c7682848","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem hk est of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Fix $x_0\in M$, $r\in(0, 1 \wedge r_*)$, and $s\in(0, 1 \wedge t_*)$.
We then have
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{(x_1, \ldots, x_k) \in M^k}
  \int_{B(x_0,r)}
  \prod_{i=1}^k p^i_s(x_i,y)\,\mu(dy)
  \leq
  \tilde{c}_1\!
  \left(
    s^{-\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}^*/2}
    \wedge
    r^{d_{\mathrm{f}}}s^{-\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}/2}
  \right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if we set $c_1 \coloneqq \max_i (2 c_{\mathrm{LE}}^{-1})^{d_{\mathrm{w}}^{(i)}} \vee 1$, then, for all $s \geq c_1 r^{d^{\mathrm{min}}_\mathrm{w}}$,
\begin{equation}
  \inf_{(x_1,\ldots,x_k) \in \hat{B}_*(x_0,r)}
  \int_{B(x_0,r)}
  \prod_{i=1}^k p^i_s(x_i,y)\,\mu(dy)
  \ge
  \tilde{c}_2\, r^{d_{\mathrm{f}}}s^{-\hat{d}_{\mathrm{s}}/2}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

